window.AKK_MY_BELOVED_CONCUBINE_ONLY_WANTS_TO_EAT_MELONS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MY_BELOVED_CONCUBINE_ONLY_WANTS_TO_EAT_MELONS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101","paragraphs":["The truth of the matter had finally come to light. Yanshu, remembering her promise to the Empress Dowager, came to the Palace of Benevolent Peace first thing the next morning to share the full story with her.","After hearing Yanshu recite the contents of the novel, the Empress Dowager was naturally furious.","\"No wonder the Shao family had to come begging to me about this matter. It turns out that Nephew Han was the one who started all this trouble! Hmph, what a heartless scoundrel! This is the result of that old lady forcing her son to adopt an heir back then!\"","Yanshu quickly nodded in agreement, \"Exactly, that's what I thought too. Old lady Xing forced her own son into such a situation back then. If she knew about this now in the afterlife, I wonder if she would regret it?\"","The Empress Dowager let out a cold laugh, \"Even if she regrets it, she can only do so in the underworld. It's fortunate she died early, otherwise who knows what state the general's household would be in now?\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously again.","The Empress Dowager was right - it was lucky that Old lady Xing had died seven or eight years ago. Otherwise, with her ways, Madam Shao and her three children probably wouldn't have survived until now.","But now things were better. That ungrateful wolf of a nephew, Han Xing'an, who dared to falsely claim imperial orders and slander the emperor, would likely not escape death.","After he dies, he can be reunited with his biased grandmother. Tsk.","Sure enough, a few days later, the court sentenced Han Xing'an to beheading on charges of slandering the emperor's name, falsely transmitting imperial orders, moral corruption, and being unfilial. It was personally approved by the emperor, and no one dared object. On the day the imperial edict was issued, the man was taken out to Wumen Gate and beheaded.","Thinking back to the Carefree Young Master's novel, that ungrateful nephew had met the same beheading fate. No one expected reality to mirror fiction so quickly. While the common people cheered with satisfaction, they also reached a consensus on their guesses about the Carefree Young Master's identity.","— Who else but someone close to the emperor could know such details about court officials and major events, and predict the outcome so accurately?","So in the future, no one should be foolish enough to try to oppose him, like that fake heir Wei Jingshi from the Eight Corners Bookstore did.","After all, opposing him is the same as opposing the emperor, and there's absolutely no chance of winning.","Thanks to Doctor Jiang's superb medical skills, General Wu An finally recovered after more than half a month.","The first thing he did after recovering was to enter the palace with his beloved concubine Madam Shao to thank the emperor and Empress Dowager for their grace.","Having learned of this news in advance, Yanshu was very excited. She insisted on accompanying the emperor to the Palace of Benevolent Peace, intending to see the heroic figure of this devoted man with her own eyes.","Fortunately, both the emperor and Empress Dowager doted on her, so they indulged her wishes.","Of course, the male and female protagonists of her novel were now in their forties or fifties. General Wu An no longer possessed the youthful vigor of his younger days, and having just recovered from illness, his frame appeared somewhat weak.","However, as a man who had weathered many battles, he still carried an air of heroism about him. Standing next to the slightly frail Madam Shao, they still made a handsome and well-matched couple.","As soon as they entered the hall, the two knelt down in greeting. General Wu An said, \"Your subject Han Gaochu and his concubine pay respects to Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and Consort Yi. We are deeply grateful for Your Majesty's and the Empress Dowager's vast imperial grace in saving this old subject's life. This old subject fears he has no way to repay such kindness and feels extremely ashamed.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"General, you have just recovered from a serious illness. There's no need for such formalities. You have spent half your life bravely serving the country, and the court will not mistreat you. Please rise.\"","General Wu An complied and stood up with Madam Shao's assistance.","The Empress Dowager looked the two over and said, \"Speaking of which, the General should properly thank Madam Shao this time... If it weren't for her coming to plead before me, neither I nor the emperor would have known about the situation in your household.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, Yanshu nodded inwardly in agreement. The Empress Dowager was indeed her number one supporter, saying exactly what she wanted to say!","— Come to think of it, when Madam Shao entered the palace to request the Empress Dowager's decree, she had faced quite a bit of obstruction from that nephew. It was fortunate that the servants were loyal and managed to send her to the palace gates.","Although they had gone through hardships, General Wu An had finally recovered. From now on, the two of them would become even more inseparable, spending the rest of their lives together hand in hand.","Thinking of this, she couldn't help but tear up —","[Wuwu, back then he gave up a fortune just for one person, and now she's risked everything to save him. What a touching love story! It makes one believe in love all over again!]","Yuwen Lan, who silently overheard this, thought: \"???\"","Why would she think this way?","Was his own affection not enough to make her believe in love?","However, just as he was secretly frowning, General Wu An suddenly knelt down again and said, \"The Empress Dowager speaks truly. This old subject has been considering this matter for days. Today, I boldly request Your Majesty's permission to resign from my official post and return to my hometown, so that I may give her the status of a proper wife.\"","What, resign?","When these words were spoken, everyone present was stunned at first, and then they couldn't help but sigh in sympathy.","— As everyone knew, Madam Shao came from a humble background, and current etiquette laws did not allow General Wu An to give her the status of a proper wife. But if General Wu An resigned from his official position and became an ordinary citizen, there would be no obstacles.","However, wouldn't this waste all the battle scars on his body and the merits he had earned through decades of risking his life?","Amidst the shock, before the emperor could speak, General Wu An continued, \"The person this old subject has wronged the most in this life is her. Now that I'm in my twilight years, I only wish to give her proper recognition. Although I will no longer be able to serve Your Majesty loyally in the future, which fills my heart with shame, at least my son will continue to serve the country loyally, to make up for this regret in my heart.\"","As his words fell, everyone inwardly nodded in agreement —","Indeed, General Wu An had risked his life protecting the country throughout his life, living up to his duty to the emperor and the world, and even to his family. After all, the Han family's glory and wealth were earned by him alone, and he had even compromised by accepting his nephew as an adopted heir.","The only ones he seemed to have shortchanged were Madam Shao and their children.","If things continued this way, his son and daughter would still bear the status of illegitimate children, and his daughter might never find a good match. Even after death, the couple might not be able to be buried together...","Perhaps after experiencing this brush with death, General Wu An had finally made the decision he truly wanted.","Thinking this through, everyone more or less understood General Wu An's intentions.","However, Yanshu was very anxious and couldn't help but speak up, \"I can understand that the General is thinking of his wife, but isn't the price of such a decision too high? Isn't there any other way?\"","As she spoke, she glanced secretly at the emperor, urgently thinking, [Hey, can't you see how touching this love story is? Why can't you just bestow a marriage upon them? After all, Madam Shao bravely saved her husband this time, which deserves to be rewarded! Don't be so cold-blooded, please!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","The situation had developed so suddenly that he really hadn't expected General Wu An to make such a request today. How had he become cold-blooded?","He pondered for a moment and was about to speak when the Empress Dowager unexpectedly beat him to it.","\"The General's consideration for his beloved concubine is touching, but if His Majesty were to approve your resignation, wouldn't it make the outside world think that the court deems you too old and is mistreating you? I think there might be another way to handle this matter. Why rush to resign?\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu immediately looked at the Empress Dowager and nodded, saying, \"The Empress Dowager speaks wisely. Who doesn't know that General Wu An has risked his life for the country numerous times in the past, achieving countless merits, and now... has even sent his own son to the battlefield? Such dedication deserves to be well-treated by the court. In my humble opinion, Madam Shao's efforts to save her husband this time are also very praiseworthy.\"","As her words fell, the Empress Dowager inwardly praised her cleverness, then addressed General Wu An, \"Consort Yi speaks correctly. Your nephew falsely transmitted imperial orders, and if it weren't for Madam Shao personally coming to plead with me, if your nephew had succeeded this time, wouldn't it have tarnished His Majesty's reputation? Madam Shao's actions have greatly pleased me. Today, I shall bestow upon you two the right to formally marry as husband and wife.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone was stunned.","Only Yanshu reacted first, quickly saying, \"The Empress Dowager is most wise!\"","Inwardly, she was so excited she could almost cry, [Aww, my number one supporter is indeed reliable! Empress Dowager, I love you!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Wait a moment...","He could have said that too...","He just hadn't had the chance yet...","But at this moment, everyone in the hall had already followed Yanshu's lead, saying, \"The Empress Dowager is most wise!\"","Everyone's faces were filled with excitement.","The General Wu An and Madam Shao finally reacted, and in their joyful surprise, both knelt down again with teary eyes, kowtowing to the Empress Dowager, \"We thank the Empress Dowager for her great kindness!\"","The Empress Dowager nodded with a smile and said to General Wu An, \"General, there's no need for such formality. You should also abandon any thoughts of resigning. Your battlefield experience is valuable, and the court may need you again in the future. Even if you can't go to the battlefield, it would be good to train a few disciples for the court.\"","General Wu An responded emotionally once more, \"Please rest assured, Empress Dowager. As long as the court has use for me, even if it means exhausting these old bones, I will spare no effort and face any danger without hesitation.\"","As his words fell, everyone wished they could applaud.","The Empress Dowager is wise! The Empress Dowager is truly wise!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","The Empress Dowager was indeed very wise.","Of course, the most crucial thing was—","The speed was fast.","The Empress Dowager's marriage decree was sent to the General's mansion on the same day with General Wu An and Madam Shao.","To receive a marriage decree personally from the Empress Dowager was indeed a great joy.","However, as General Wu An and Madam Shao were both over fifty years old and the household had just experienced some turbulence, they didn't want to hold a grand ceremony. So they chose an auspicious date, held a simple ceremony at home, and submitted their marriage certificate to the government office.","It seemed simple and peaceful, but it was something they had waited for more than half their lives.","From then on, a beloved concubine became a beloved wife, and the status of their children changed from illegitimate to legitimate. The couple could finally fulfill their wish to share the same bed in life and the same grave in death.","Due to the groundwork laid by the Carefree Young Master's story, many people had already sympathized with Madam Shao's background. Now, seeing the protagonists of the story finally achieve a happy ending in reality, everyone felt quite gratified.","Although there might still be some gossip behind their backs, after experiencing a life-and-death separation, this meant nothing to General Wu An and his wife.","For the rest of their days, being able to spend time together with a clear conscience was enough.","Having witnessed the happy ending of this story, Yanshu, as a key behind-the-scenes contributor, felt very gratified.","Lying on the bed at night, she stroked her belly while giving prenatal education to the baby inside—","\"As they say, 'Where there's a will, there's a way.' So, my dear, always remember to keep hope in your heart. Although there are still many restrictions in this world, as long as you work hard in the right direction, you can definitely achieve your wishes.\"","As her words fell, Yuwen Lan, who had just finished washing up, also got onto the bed. He embraced her and commented, \"'Where there's a will, there's a way' is indeed true, but in this case, it was mainly your... achievement. If you hadn't discovered the truth in time, those two might not have ended up with such a perfect outcome.\"","He glanced at her swollen belly, his heart filled with longing.","He also wanted to touch it so badly...","Maybe, just a little?","As long as he didn't think about anything inappropriate, it should be fine, right?","However, while he was struggling with this internal dilemma, Yanshu nodded and said, \"Your Majesty is right, I was referring to myself! At that time, I thought I could do something meaningful by writing stories. Now that I've saved one unfortunate family after another and cleared up one tarnished truth after another, haven't I achieved my wish?\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"...That's indeed well said. But are you sure you didn't write stories for money initially?\"","Yanshu choked, \"...Money was one aspect, but I'm also a person with grand aspirations!\"","Then she suddenly looked at him and pouted, \"Speaking of which, the reason I wanted to write stories to earn money in the first place was because I was too poor.\"","[Hmph, since you mentioned money, I won't hold back.]","She raised her eyebrows at him and said, \"I've done quite a bit of meritorious service for Your Majesty lately. Hasn't Your Majesty thought about rewarding me?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Such skill at seizing opportunities was truly rare in this world.","So he smiled and said, \"How should I reward you? Do you still lack money now?\"","Suddenly struck by inspiration, he casually placed his hand on her belly, gently stroking it while thinking to himself, [Silly girl, I've given you my whole heart, isn't that enough?]","As he spoke, he secretly watched her.","He saw her indeed pause, [Huh? How come I heard it again?]","[Is he saying he's given me his heart???]","Yuwen Lan nodded inwardly, desperately wanting to tell her that she hadn't misheard, that this was exactly what he meant.","However, fearing he might give himself away, he quickly removed his hand, pretending it was unintentional.","He cleared his throat inwardly—","Silly girl, do you finally understand his feelings now?","However, her thoughts were not on his recent confession.","Yanshu was now trying hard to solve a problem—why could she suddenly hear his thoughts again?","She kept pondering in her mind, [What happened just now? Is it because he's hugging me?]","[No, that's not it! He's still hugging me now, but why can't I hear anything?]","[Oh right! He was touching my belly just now, could it be... is this belly a signal receiver?]","Yuwen Lan jolted.","Although he didn't know what this so-called \"signal receiver\" was, he could see she was about to figure it out.","Tsk, how did she suddenly become so clever?","To be on the safe side, he immediately said, \"By the way, the Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching. I'll be hosting a banquet for the officials and their families. Do you think it would be better to hold the banquet in the palace, or at Jinming Pool, or perhaps at Jinbo Garden?\"","Oh? A chance to go out of the palace?","Yanshu's attention was finally diverted. She thought for a moment and said, \"I think both Jinbo Garden and Jinming Pool are nice, but Jinbo Garden seems to have a broader water surface? I imagine the atmosphere would be better for the emperor and his officials to enjoy the moon together.\"","—Hehe, actually, moon-gazing was secondary. The main thing was that the roast pig and roast lamb she ate at Jinbo Garden last time were unforgettable. Just thinking about it now made her mouth water!","Yuwen Lan listened silently, then nodded, \"Alright, then let's choose Jinbo Garden. I'll have them prepare more roasted dishes, which I'm sure you'll like.\"","Yanshu, whose thoughts had been completely diverted without realizing it, brightened up and quickly nodded, \"Thank you, Your Majesty. I do really like the roast lamb there. Since there will be many people at the Mid-Autumn night banquet, why not roast a few more?\"","Yuwen Lan hurriedly nodded, \"Roasting five wouldn't be a problem.\"","He then asked, \"What else would you like to eat? Think about it carefully over the next few days so they can prepare early.\"","Yanshu indeed started to consider seriously, \"Besides roast lamb, roast fish is also good. Crabs are at their fattest during Mid-Autumn, so why not let everyone try some crabs? Oh, and crabs are not only good steamed, they're also delicious when stir-fried with spicy sauce or cooked in a meat crab pot...\"","Yuwen Lan nodded repeatedly, \"Whatever you wish.\"","...","Phew, that was close."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102","paragraphs":["As August arrived, the Mid-Autumn Festival was just around the corner.","This year, the capital of Daliang had enjoyed favorable weather overall. By this time, many places had reaped a bountiful harvest. With the festival approaching, various seasonal delicacies were successively transported to the palace. As a result, the Internal Affairs Bureau had been very busy for several consecutive days.","On this day, Yanshu was accompanying the Empress Dowager for tea in the Palace of Benevolent Peace when the Head of the Internal Affairs Bureau came in to report, \"Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, Consort Yi, the fresh lake produce such as green crabs and whitebait offered by Suzhou Prefecture has just arrived. This year's quantity is considerable, and I estimate the imperial family won't be able to finish it all quickly. How should we handle this?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Yanshu's face showed disappointment.","— Pregnant women shouldn't eat too many crabs, and just when she's pregnant this year, there's a bumper harvest of green crabs?","Isn't this deliberately tempting her? Wuwu!","She could only say, \"These lake delicacies are best when fresh. Please ask the Emperor and the Empress Dowager to enjoy them soon. Have the imperial kitchen prepare some for lunch.\"","However, the Empress Dowager shook her head and said, \"I'm getting old, and eating too much might upset my stomach. Keep some for the palace, and as usual, distribute the rest to the court officials.\"","The Head of the Internal Affairs Bureau acknowledged and was about to withdraw.","Suddenly, Yanshu had an idea and quickly added, \"If there are still leftovers, why not distribute some to the teachers and students at the Imperial Academy and its affiliated academies? Although there's a three-day holiday for the Mid-Autumn Festival, some teachers and students from distant places probably can't return home to reunite with their families. It would be nice to give them some green crabs for a treat.\"","— Hehe, most importantly, this way, her idol Headmaster Qi would also get to taste them!","After all, with this year's bumper harvest of green crabs, the market price must be cheap. Those officials don't lack money to buy crabs, so instead of giving them all to the officials, why not let her upright and honest idol Headmaster Qi have a treat?","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager thought, [This is not a bad idea, but just a few green crabs might seem a bit inadequate, wouldn't it?]","Hmm? Inadequate?","Yanshu thought for a moment and quickly added, \"Oh right, just green crabs might be a bit monotonous. Why don't we make some mooncakes to distribute along with them? It would help everyone ease their homesickness.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager finally nodded in satisfaction, \"That's not a bad idea. The imperial kitchen isn't busy anyway, and it's about time to make mooncakes. Let them make some extra. I'm sure the students will like it.\"","She then sighed inwardly, [Ah, that person has been alone for so many years. I wonder if anyone has ever made mooncakes for him? I hope he can taste them this time.]","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"This is the imperial family's care. They will surely appreciate it.\"","Ahem, when the mooncakes are ready, she must instruct the person handling the task to ensure that Headmaster Qi gets to eat the mooncakes. After all, this is the Empress Dowager's heartfelt concern.","Hearing this, the Head of the Internal Affairs Bureau hurriedly agreed and went to carry out the orders.","It was still early, and the system, showing great perception, said, [Speaking of which, the Empress Dowager is actually very skilled at making pastries, especially lotus seed paste mooncakes. She makes them exceptionally well.]","Is that so?","Yanshu had another idea and said, \"Come to think of it, it's been a while since I last made some pastries after learning from Your Majesty. Why don't I try making some mooncakes today? It would be fitting for the season, and if they turn out well, I could help the imperial kitchen.\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded slightly, thinking to herself, [Come to think of it, it's been a long time since I made any...]","Yanshu sensed an opportunity and quickly added, \"Oh right, the lotus seeds harvested from the Taiye Pool have been dried. I remember the Emperor mentioning before that Your Majesty makes excellent lotus seed paste mooncakes. May I have the honor of receiving Your Majesty's guidance?\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow and said, \"I've only made them a few times. The Emperor still remembers?\"","Yanshu, maintaining a straight face, nodded vigorously, \"How could I dare to make this up? Of course, I only know because... the Emperor mentioned it.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and finally said, \"Very well, since we have nothing else to do, I'll personally teach you today. Once you've learned, you can make them for the Emperor in the future.\"","Yanshu quickly smiled and repeatedly expressed her gratitude, \"Then I'm truly blessed today!\"","With that, the two of them went to the pastry room and got busy. By lunchtime, they had made about thirty shortcrust mooncakes.","They tasted a few on the spot, and the flavor was indeed excellent. The Empress Dowager, wary of too much sweetness, had the palace maids accompany Yanshu to send the rest to the Ganlu Palace for her to handle.","Upon returning to the Ganlu Palace, Yanshu set aside a plate for the Emperor and had the rest wrapped in oiled paper and sent to the Internal Affairs Bureau, placing them with the batch to be sent to Songhe Academy.","Hehe, the lotus seed paste in these mooncakes was personally made by the Empress Dowager. This way, her idol would be able to taste the handiwork of his beloved.","Wuwu, as a hardworking CP fan, one must learn to turn passive into active and find sweetness in the most unexpected places!","Of course, she didn't forget to set aside a portion for her maiden family and sent someone with a message asking her mother to come to the palace tomorrow for a chat.","Thus, the next day, her mother, Ms. Zhu, arrived as agreed.","Yanshu first inquired about the situation at home, and seeing that everything was fine, she had Rendong bring out the mooncakes and said softly, \"I learned to make these yesterday with the Empress Dowager. I specially saved some for the family. Please take them back for everyone to taste.\"","Hearing this, Ms. Zhu was naturally delighted, \"You've even learned to make pastries now?\"","Yanshu replied with a bit of embarrassment, \"After being your daughter for so many years, this is the first time I've made something for you to eat. I hope you won't blame me.\"","— As she watched the baby in her belly grow day by day, she increasingly understood the difficulties her parents had faced.","Hearing her say this, Ms. Zhu was also filled with emotion, her eyes reddening as she said, \"We're family, why are you being so formal with us? Now, we don't ask for anything else, we just hope that you and the imperial heir will be safe and sound.\"","Seeing her mother like this, Yanshu also felt her eyes starting to water.","However, it wouldn't do for the mother and daughter to burst into tears over this, would it?","So she immediately changed the subject, \"By the way, did you try the green crabs the palace distributed yesterday? Were they fat and delicious?\"","Ms. Zhu quickly nodded, \"We did, they were excellent. We're truly grateful for the Emperor and Empress Dowager's care.\"","Yanshu smiled and continued, \"I'm glad you enjoyed them. This year, the Internal Affairs Bureau is also distributing some to the academies, so each family probably won't get much. If you like them, just have someone buy them from the southern wharf in the city. The lake produce there is the freshest and cheapest. Don't hesitate to buy them.\"","However, to her surprise, her mother shook her head and said, \"There's no need to buy any. You don't know, but we have plenty of green crabs at home this year. A few days ago, someone sent several large baskets. We didn't want to accept them, but they insisted on leaving one basket. We've been eating crabs every day for the past few days, to the point where we're starting to fear the sight of them.\"","Hmm? Someone sent several large baskets of crabs?","Yanshu quickly asked, \"What happened? Who sent them?\"","Ms. Zhu explained, \"A while ago, Duke Qi celebrated his birthday and sent an invitation to our household. I originally wasn't planning to go, but then the Wife of the Heir of Duke Qi came personally to invite us, so I had no choice but to accompany your father. During the event, the duchess introduced me to many people, including the wife of the Provincial Judge of Suzhou, Lady Xie, who said she had a favor to ask of your father...\"","At this point, Yanshu tensed up and asked, \"You didn't agree, did you?\"","This situation sounded like a trap from the very beginning.","Fortunately, her mother replied, \"Of course not. I don't know her, and besides, she was asking for your father's help. I just said I didn't understand and brushed it off vaguely.\"","Yanshu finally relaxed.","— The capital is not like their simple and honest Andechun. These noble ladies all seem to have countless schemes. She was worried her mother wouldn't be a match for them.","However, her mother continued, \"But somehow, just a couple of days after we returned from that birthday celebration, Lady Xie came to our door personally to deliver crabs. Several large baskets were brought directly to our doorstep. We tried to refuse, but couldn't, so we ended up accepting one bucket and gave her a few boxes of persimmon cakes that your uncle had just sent us in return.\"","Yanshu nodded upon hearing this, \"That's fine then. Our Qingzhou persimmon cakes are valuable too. At least we didn't take her gifts for nothing.\"","— Tsk, after all, her maiden family is now part of the noble circle in the capital. It's impossible not to interact with others. She can only advise her parents to be more cautious and not give others any opportunity to take advantage of them.","Just as she was thinking this, she heard her mother say to her, \"Oh, there's one more thing. I think I should tell Your Highness about it.\"","Yanshu quickly asked, \"What is it?\"","Although there were no idle bystanders in the room at this time, Ms. Zhu still lowered her voice and said, \"The other day when the Provincial Judge's wife came to deliver crabs, she mentioned to me that she was an old acquaintance of Consort Dowager Hui.\"","Consort Dowager Hui?","Yanshu was startled, \"You mean the Emperor's birth mother?\"","She saw her mother nod, \"That's right, that very Consort.\"","This surprised Yanshu somewhat. After thinking for a moment, she asked, \"What's this about? How is the Provincial Judge's wife an old acquaintance of Consort Dowager Hui?\"","Ms. Zhu lowered her voice again and said, \"She said she was best friends with Consort Dowager Hui's sister, and knew Consort Dowager Hui back then as well.\"","Consort Dowager Hui's sister?","Yanshu was taken aback again. She only just learned that Consort Dowager Hui had a sister?","Wouldn't that make her the Emperor's aunt?","But come to think of it, she had never heard any news about this sister of Consort Dowager Hui before.","So she asked, \"Where is this sister of Consort Dowager Hui now?\"","She heard her mother lower her voice once more, \"I heard that Consort Dowager Hui's family has always been in the Songjiang Prefecture area of Jiangnan. From what Lady Xie implied, it seems someone in the capital has been deliberately suppressing them, not allowing them to leave Songjiang. She said that a few years ago, Consort Dowager Hui's Nephew was originally qualified to come to the capital to enter the Imperial Academy, but was replaced by someone else.\"","Could this be true?","Yanshu couldn't help but frown.","Admittedly, thinking about it carefully, this information was quite intriguing—","Someone in the capital deliberately suppressing the family of the Emperor's birth mother, not allowing them to leave Jiangnan?","Tsk, they were close relatives with blood ties to the Emperor after all. Who would have the authority to do such a thing?","So was this Lady Xie implying it was the Empress Dowager?","Hmph, the Empress Dowager was her top-tier ally, whose character was absolutely trustworthy.","She wouldn't easily believe such claims!","Moreover, this person suddenly approached her mother's family to volunteer such information. Wasn't she trying to get her to pass this message to the Emperor?","Thus using her as a pawn to drive a wedge between the Emperor and the Empress Dowager?","She heard the system say, [That's right, this is exactly what that person intends.]","Yanshu immediately asked, [But what's the real story here? Does Consort Dowager Hui truly have a sister in Songjiang? How come we've never heard any news about them all these years?]","The system then explained to her, [The sister is real, but she's Consort Dowager Hui's half-sister. Besides her, Consort Dowager Hui also has a half-brother in Songjiang. The reason you've never heard about them is not because the Empress Dowager suppressed them, but because Consort Dowager Hui had a poor relationship with this brother and sister when she was alive and didn't want anything to do with them.]","[As for why their relationship was bad, it's because Consort Dowager Hui was the eldest legitimate daughter of the family, but her father favored his concubine, which drove her mother to an early death from depression. After that, he elevated this concubine to be the main wife, who then gave birth to this brother and sister. Consort Dowager Hui was old enough to remember all this, so she always hated that side of the family.]","[Moreover, Consort Dowager Hui wasn't actually very favored at first. She was only made a consort because she gave birth to the Emperor. The Empress Dowager helped her gain that title to elevate the Emperor's status. She died not long after giving birth to the Emperor, and before she died, she specifically instructed the Empress Dowager not to let her family benefit from her position. Plus, after the Emperor was taken to be raised by the Empress Dowager, he became the Empress Dowager's child, so it naturally had nothing to do with others anymore. That's why that family has remained in Songjiang Prefecture all this time, without any opportunity to come to the capital.]","Yanshu finally understood.","Tsk, who would have thought that Consort Dowager Hui, even on her deathbed, didn't forget to instruct the Empress Dowager not to let her family take advantage?","It's clear she truly hated them.","Now how dare this sister come and spread rumors saying the Empress Dowager is suppressing them!","No wonder people find them hateful!","She heard the system say, [As they say, men die for wealth, birds die for food. Everyone has a greedy heart. It was one thing when the Emperor wasn't Emperor yet, but now that they see their sister's son has ascended the throne and the empire is stable, they're naturally unwilling to accept their situation! So they've been secretly trying various methods, and after much effort, they found out that you're favored. They planned for a long time before using the opportunity of Duke Qi's birthday to strike up a conversation with your mother. Now they're hoping you'll mention this to the Emperor, giving them a chance to be brought to the capital and given a title so they can live an easy life.]","Yanshu thought, [Haha.]","Keep dreaming! They even dare to smear the reputation of her top-tier ally, the Empress Dowager!","[But speaking of which, what's the story with the nephew trying to enter the Imperial Academy? Was he really replaced by someone else?]","The system replied, [Of course not. That boy didn't study hard himself and was afraid he couldn't pass the Imperial Academy selection exam. So he found someone to take the exam in his place. Unexpectedly, it was discovered by the local education official. The official only held back from reporting it out of consideration for his mother's relation to the Emperor.]","Yanshu thought, [Haha.]","Sure enough, people from such an improper family are always thinking of such crooked schemes.","In this situation, she certainly wouldn't get involved.","So she advised her mother, \"This must be a fabrication. The Emperor and the Empress Dowager are both generous people, how could they mistreat them without reason? Even if such a thing did happen, it must be because they themselves did something wrong to deserve such treatment. You should just listen to this and not mention it to anyone else. In the future, if this Lady Xie comes again, don't see her anymore.\"","Ms. Zhu nodded repeatedly, \"Yes, yes, that's what I thought too, which is why I only told Your Highness about it. I won't mention it to anyone else, and if she comes again in the future, I'll claim to be ill and not see her.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"That's good. I think we should be wary of Duke Qi's household as well. Why would the Wife of the Heir of Duke Qi introduce that Lady Xie to you for no reason? They might have been in cahoots from the beginning, setting a trap for you and me!\"","Ms. Zhu nodded repeatedly, \"Exactly. Duke Qi is the younger brother-in-law of Emperor Gaozu and the uncle of the Former Emperor. With such a prestigious background, there must be something fishy about them sending us an invitation out of the blue.\"","Yanshu nodded as well.","Fortunately, although her parents were kind-hearted, they weren't foolish, which was somewhat reassuring.","However, as her mother said, given Duke Qi's household's high status, why would they collude with Consort Dowager Hui's siblings for no reason?","After sending her mother off, Yanshu got the answer to this question.","The system said, [Latest news, just now, Duke Qi joined with five or six other officials to petition the Emperor, saying that the country cannot go a day without an heir, and urging the Emperor to quickly select consorts and establish an Empress to ease the people's minds.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, although it took some mental effort, she more or less understood.","— The Wife of the Heir of Duke Qi and Lady Xie were setting a trap for her mother, hoping she would tell the Emperor about Consort Dowager Hui's family. Whether or not it succeeded in driving a wedge between the Emperor and the Empress Dowager, the Empress Dowager would certainly dislike her for meddling.","Thus, when the officials pressured the Emperor to select consorts and establish an Empress, the Empress Dowager naturally wouldn't speak up for her anymore.","...","Having figured out the ins and outs of the situation, Yanshu could only laugh wryly.","If they want to urge the Emperor to select consorts and establish an Empress, so be it, but isn't it a bit unfair to set a trap for her?","So she immediately called out to the system, [System, do you have any dirt on Duke Qi's household?]","The system replied, [Oh, they've all got plenty of skeletons in their closets! Tell me, whose dirt do you want to hear about?]"]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103","paragraphs":["What? The whole family has scandalous affairs?","Tsk tsk, what kind of family is this?","Yanshu immediately became excited and said, \"Tell me quickly, what's going on?\"","After all, it was still early, and there was plenty of time today.","However, she heard the system ask her, \"Then who should we start with?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, there were so many juicy stories that it became difficult to decide where to begin.","She thought for a moment and said, \"Then let's start from the oldest to the youngest, beginning with Duke Qi.\"","She heard the system respond with an \"Alright!\" and immediately began to spill the tea:","\"To talk about Duke Qi's scandal, we need to start with Emperor Gaozu's sons, who were the Former Emperor's brothers. As is well known, the Former Emperor had a total of five brothers. Among them, only he and the youngest, the King of Beiliang, were Emperor Gaozu's legitimate sons, and thus Duke Qi's blood nephews. Although both were Duke Qi's blood nephews, in reality, Duke Qi favored the King of Beiliang more. Why? Because the King of Beiliang married the daughter of his brother-in-law, the Marquis of Anding.\"","Yanshu, afraid of getting confused, quickly sorted out the details, \"So you're saying that Duke Qi's wife's niece married the King of Beiliang and became the princess consort? They became even closer relatives, so Duke Qi favored his younger nephew, the King of Beiliang.\"","The system said that was correct, \"Anyway, Duke Qi, the Marquis of Anding, and the King of Beiliang formed an interest group, competing with the Former Emperor behind the scenes for the position of crown prince. But no matter what, the Former Emperor was still the elder brother and ultimately ascended to the throne legitimately. However, the King of Beiliang had already made plans, intending to rebel under the pretext of the Former Emperor's false edict.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu raised an eyebrow, \"As a key member of the interest group, Duke Qi must have known about this, right?\"","The system said, \"Of course he knew, and he even helped the King of Beiliang quite a bit with the plan. However, the Former Emperor and the Empress Dowager weren't pushovers either and had already made preparations. By coincidence, Duke Qi got wind of this early on, and after comparing the situation, he realized the King of Beiliang had no chance of winning. So he immediately went to the Former Emperor and betrayed the King of Beiliang, secretly eliminating all the confidants around him who knew about this matter, and earned merit by presenting himself as a firm supporter of the Former Emperor.\"","Yanshu: \"... So the King of Beiliang died before he could even start his rebellion?\"","System: \"Well, he died, of course. How could the Former Emperor tolerate such a major act of treason?\"","Yanshu: \"... What about the other member of the interest group, Duke Qi's brother-in-law, the Marquis of Anding?\"","System: \"Duke Qi sold him out too. His brother-in-law, along with his father-in-law's entire family, were all sent to accompany the King of Beiliang in death.\"","Yanshu: \"... What a ruthless person! Doesn't that mean Duke Qi's wife must hate her husband to death?\"","Tsk, after all, Duke Qi was the first to discover something was wrong. If he had properly advised his brother-in-law to stop, couldn't he have avoided the death of his father-in-law's entire family?","But the system said, \"You're overthinking it. Duke Qi would never have advised his brother-in-law to stop. After all, the Former Emperor knew he was closer to the King of Beiliang, and after ascending to the throne, he would certainly be wary of him. The title of uncle alone wouldn't count for much. So he had to betray his brother-in-law as well to show enough loyalty and sincerity to make the Former Emperor believe in him. So even if his wife hated him to death, he had to do it.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, the story was over, and the outcome was obvious - Duke Qi finally managed to keep his wealth and status by betraying his teammates and his in-laws' entire family. Now he could even use his status as the emperor's great-uncle to submit memorials meddling in the emperor's affairs.","System: \"That's not just meddling. His own granddaughter has just come of age this year, so she's ready to be married, right? Looking around the capital now, there aren't many families that can match his status.\"","Yanshu: \"Heh.\"","So this old man wants to secure another empress position to maintain his wealth and status? The problem is, if you have the ability to protect it, then do so, but why do you have to dig a pit for others first? Isn't that a bit too unscrupulous?","Oh right, this old man never had any scruples to begin with.","But come to think of it, Duke Qi's betrayal of his teammates is indeed not easy to expose. Firstly, it's a major incident, and secondly, it happened a long time ago. After all, Duke Qi himself is already in his seventies or eighties, so there probably aren't many people still alive who knew the inside story back then.","But that's okay, aren't there other scandals...?","So she asked the system again, \"Tell me about someone else, what other scandals does their family have?\"","Then she heard the system say, \"Then let's talk about Duke Qi's heir. He's about the same age as Duke Cheng'en, and is also a profligate son. His level of lechery is comparable to Duke Cheng'en's. Not to mention the countless concubines and bedmaids in his household, a few years ago when he went hunting in Lu Prefecture, he took a liking to the eldest daughter of Lin Chengxian, the centurion of the Lu Prefecture Right Guard, and forced her to become his concubine.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but slam the table and shout \"Scoundrel!\" \"A perfectly good daughter from an official's family, forced to be a concubine to such an old lecher? Even Duke Cheng'en hasn't gone so far as to force himself on someone!\"","System: \"Who says he hasn't? But that's not the end of it. A couple of years later, when Centurion Lin's second daughter grew up, this old lecher wanted to prey on her too. Naturally, Centurion Lin was unwilling, so he quickly found a marriage partner for his second daughter and got her engaged. Who knew that this scoundrel would hold a grudge, and framed Centurion Lin for embezzling military supplies, getting him locked up in Lu Prefecture Prison. Just a few days ago, Centurion Lin was released, but this scoundrel is feeling disgruntled and is planning to frame him again with another crime.\"","What???","Yanshu was so angry she almost stood up, \"This old lecher is specifically targeting one family to bully! And he's so vindictive, he threw the man in prison because he couldn't prey on his second daughter? This is even more inhuman than Duke Cheng'en!\"","System: \"That's right, after all, his family status is higher than Duke Cheng'en's. As they say, the higher the family status, the more degenerate the prodigal sons they raise.\"","Yanshu: \"... Pfft, that's indeed true. By the way, does his family have any more scandals?\"","System: \"Of course there are! The wife of Duke Qi's heir is also a fierce one!\"","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, \"Tell me quickly, how fierce is she?\"","The system then said, \"This Lady Wei was originally the Second Daughter of the Second Branch of Marquis Yongping's Mansion. When Duke Qi's family was arranging a marriage, they originally had their eye on the legitimate daughter of the main branch, who was Lady Wei's cousin. However, in order to marry into Duke Qi's family, Lady Wei secretly put elm flowers in her cousin's food, causing her allergic cousin to break out in a rash all over her body and become unpresentable. Then she spread rumors saying her cousin's face was covered in pockmarks. As a result, Duke Qi's family chose her as their daughter-in-law instead.\"","Yanshu: \"... Isn't this just sabotage? And she sabotaged her own family member at that.\"","As someone with allergies herself, she naturally sympathized with that cousin.","But come to think of it, after going to such lengths to marry an old lecher, constantly seeing the countless concubines in the mansion, she wondered if Lady Wei regretted it or not?","But she heard the system say, \"Lady Wei doesn't regret it, after all, this was her dream, to be the future duchess! However, there's not a single concubine in the mansion who doesn't regret it, because there's not one who hasn't been drugged by her.\"","Drugged?","Yanshu was startled, \"What kind of drug?\"","System: \"Of course it's a sterilization drug! With Lady Wei's personality, she definitely couldn't allow the concubines in the mansion to give birth to illegitimate children that would be eyesores to her. So none of her husband's concubines can have children, and if any of them get pregnant, once discovered, they would all be given abortion drugs by her. That's why although Duke Qi's heir has many concubines, he doesn't have a single illegitimate son or daughter.\"","Yanshu couldn't help but sigh, \"What sin did those girls like the eldest daughter of Centurion Lin commit, to be treated like this by this couple!\"","But then she heard the system say another sentence, \"Lady Wei not only does this herself, but she also teaches her daughter by example.\"","Yanshu was stunned, and couldn't help but hiss, while instinctively touching her belly.","This... if this daughter really becomes the empress...","No! She absolutely cannot allow anyone to harm her child. Hmph!","Just as she was feeling indignant, she heard the system say another sentence, \"Of course, not all concubines submit to being slaughtered without fighting back. There's a newly entered concubine in their mansion with a fierce temperament. After being drugged by the heir's wife, she harbored resentment and seduced her son for revenge.\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","Damn... It seems this grandson of Duke Qi isn't reliable either.","System: [Like father, like son, as they say.]","Yanshu: [...I have to admit... That's another truism.]","Tsk, this Duke Qi's household could really be called a breeding ground for \"talent\".","Having finished gossiping for now, she thought for a moment. Based on what she'd heard so far, the easiest thing to tackle should be the matter of Duke Qi's heir framing Officer Lin...","However, what she was more curious about right now was how the Emperor had reacted after receiving Duke Qi's memorial.","The System said: [How else would he react? Duke Qi is his great-uncle. Since he personally led five or six high officials into the palace to submit a memorial, the Emperor naturally had to accept it, and even had to exchange a few polite words with the old man.]","Yanshu was somewhat dissatisfied and pouted: [So what is he thinking? Does he also want to hold a selection for Empress?]","System: [This System doesn't know about that. This System can't probe the Emperor's inner thoughts.]","Yanshu: [...]","Fine, if the System couldn't probe then so be it. Anyway, she now had mind-reading abilities, so she could test him out when he came.","Just as she was thinking this, she heard an announcement from outside: \"His Majesty the Emperor arrives...\"","Yanshu was stunned.","— It was only morning, why had he come at this time?","But since he was already here, she got up to go greet him outside the door, bowing and saying, \"Greetings to Your Majesty.\"","In the blink of an eye, he had already come close. He reached out to help her up, saying, \"Rise.\"","Then he lowered his gaze to carefully examine her expression, asking, \"How are you today?\"","Yanshu secretly raised an eyebrow.","— How am I today?","Why would he ask her this? Could it be because of Duke Qi submitting the memorial?","Did he want to see her reaction?","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","That was indeed what he was thinking.","Knowing she had that special ability and that nothing could be hidden from her, he wanted to come quickly to see if she had any wild thoughts.","But then he heard her think irritably: [How else could I be? The mighty Duke Qi's household is digging a pit for me to jump into! I absolutely can't let them off!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Duke Qi's household was digging a pit for her?","What was this about now?","Fortunately, she then spoke up: \"This consort is quite well. However, I just heard something that I was thinking of reporting to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan gave an \"oh\" and said, \"What is it?\" As he spoke, he naturally took her hand and sat down with her on the heated couch.","He then heard her say, \"That case of embezzling rations from two years ago at the Lu Prefecture military camp was actually a false accusation. In fact, it was because Duke Qi's heir went hunting in Lu Prefecture some years back and took a liking to the eldest daughter of Lin Chengxian, the Centurion of the Lu Prefecture Right Guard. He first forcibly took her as a concubine, and then wanted to take her younger sister as well. The Lin family was upright and clean, so naturally they were unwilling to send both their good daughters to that old man in his fifties. Moreover, Duke Qi's wife was vicious and had made all the concubines in the household infertile with drugs.\"","\"To avoid having his daughter fall into the tiger's den again, Centurion Lin quickly found a marriage match for his second daughter. Unexpectedly, this angered Duke Qi's heir, who then framed Centurion Lin with the crime of stealing and selling military rations, and had him imprisoned. I heard Centurion Lin was released a few days ago, but that man still intends to frame him again!\"","\"What?\" Upon hearing this, Yuwen Lan immediately frowned and said, \"It was actually like this?\"","Yanshu nodded vigorously, \"It's absolutely true. In fact, this matter isn't difficult to investigate. As long as Your Majesty sends someone to Lu Prefecture to ask around, the truth can be uncovered.\"","Yuwen Lan of course knew that if she could say this, the matter must be true.","He let out a breath and nodded, \"Very well, I will send someone to investigate right away.\"","As he spoke, he was about to get up.","But she stopped him, saying, \"This consort has one more thing to report.\"","He paused, \"What else is there?\"","Yanshu coughed, \"This consort has a story and would like to ask Your Majesty's opinion.\"","— It's actually about Consort Dowager Hui's family.","She thought for a moment and felt she should still tell the Emperor about this matter.","After all, if Consort Dowager Hui's family members were not content and had designs elsewhere...","If rumors were spread and eventually reached the Emperor's ears, it would inevitably affect his relationship with the Empress Dowager. So it was better for her to proactively tell him the truth now.","Yuwen Lan, who had silently heard her thoughts, naturally already knew she wanted to talk about his birth mother's matter. He became even more curious and patiently said, \"Go ahead and tell me.\"","Yanshu then said, \"There was a story about a great noble family with a kind and benevolent mistress who treated the concubines well, and the concubines repaid her with true loyalty. One day, a concubine gave birth to a child but unfortunately could not survive the birth. On her deathbed, the concubine entrusted her young child to the mistress, who then raised the child with great care and toil until he grew up and inherited the family headship.\"","\"But just when everything seemed peaceful, the concubine's family suddenly appeared. They told a bunch of lies to the young family head's beloved, attempting to drive a wedge between the family head and his foster mother, and frame the beloved as disloyal. Fortunately, the beloved was wise and clever, and discovered the truth in time. It turned out these relatives had actually owed a debt to the family head's birth mother and had never gotten along with her. Now they were fabricating a story of sisterly affection, hoping to use the family head's power for their own gain.\"","\"After learning the truth, the beloved naturally did not let those schemers succeed. But now she doesn't know whether she should tell the family head the truth or not.\"","As she finished speaking, she quickly looked at him.","Yuwen Lan had of course already understood. In this story, the family head was him, the wise and clever beloved was her, the foster mother was the Empress Dowager, and the concubine who passed away early was naturally his birth mother.","He was rather surprised - so his birth mother's relatives had come to find her?","Since he now knew about this, he naturally wanted to ask for the details.","So he said, \"Why don't you explain in more detail - why did the family head's birth mother have a bad relationship with her relatives?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, it seems he has understood.","Alright, since he wanted to know, she might as well tell him everything about Consort Dowager Hui's life.","So she continued, \"It started when this lady was young. Her father favored a concubine over his wife, causing the lady's mother to pass away early. Afterwards, her father elevated the concubine to formal wife status and had more children with her. This lady naturally could never let go of this matter. Later when she first entered the household, she was favored by the old family head for a time due to her beauty. Unfortunately, the old family head was not a constant man. After she became pregnant, he was no longer as good to her. This lady couldn't accept it and became depressed. After giving birth, seeing that the family head still treated her and her child coldly, she became even more heartbroken, to the point of developing a wasting illness. She soon passed away.\"","\"Before her death, she still hated her family. After entrusting her child to the mistress, she specifically instructed that her relatives were not ambitious people, and in the future to never let them use the child, lest they tarnish the child's reputation.\"","...","Yuwen Lan understood the rest of the story without her needing to continue. His birth mother's family must have been unwilling to accept this and came to her to spread rumors.","— In fact, although he had no memories from when he was young, he had later heard the palace ladies mention that from the time he was born, his father the Emperor had already begun to cultivate the Dao, so even though he was a prince, the Emperor was very indifferent towards him. His sensitive birth mother became depressed because of this and fell ill.","So what she said must be true.","Of course, he would not pay any attention to those relatives who wanted to use him for their own gain.","But at this moment, he couldn't help feeling heavy-hearted.","Such a pitiful woman, to wither away like that in the palace.","Just as he was about to sigh, he suddenly heard Yanshu's inner thoughts:","[Oh my poor baby, your birth grandmother and birth father were both so pitiful! We must both take good care of ourselves, okay? When you're born, Mommy will definitely give you lots of kisses and hugs, my darling child...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","\"Birth grandmother\" was one thing, but what was this about \"birth father\"?","Could it be there would be a father who wasn't the birth father?","But just then, he heard her think to herself again: [Oh baby, when all is said and done, Mommy is just a concubine too! What if Mommy dies one day, will your daddy have to find someone else to raise you?]","Yuwen Lan's heart skipped a beat.","He suddenly couldn't help saying to her, \"I have already lost my birth mother in this lifetime. This tragedy will definitely not be allowed to happen to you.\"","Yanshu was stunned upon hearing this.","How...","Immediately after, she saw him place his hand on her belly.","Yanshu then heard him say in his heart, \"You two are now the most important people to me.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu was stunned once again.","An indescribable warmth spread through her heart, gradually extending throughout her body, even causing her eyes to water and her nose to tingle.","But wait, who was more important - her or the child?","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Did this even need to be chosen between?","Before he could come to his senses, he saw her take his hand and place it on her belly again, saying, \"Your Majesty, the baby has been moving a lot lately. You should feel it and talk to the baby more.\"","Hehe, she knew it - it must be the belly!","As long as he touched her belly, she could read his mind!","Yuwen Lan: \"!!!\"","Wh-what's going on???"]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104","paragraphs":["Just as his palm was about to rest on Yanshu's swollen belly,","Yuwen Lan was startled at first, but quickly composed himself and forced himself to stay calm.","Yes, what mattered most now wasn't letting her hear his thoughts.","Rather, he couldn't let her discover that he could hear hers.","Otherwise, she would surely be angry...","Having cleared his mind, he cheerfully agreed and placed his hand on her belly again.","Meanwhile, he tried hard to clear his mind of distracting thoughts.","Then suddenly, he felt something move beneath his palm.","Though gentle, the movement was distinct—like a soft rabbit or deer lightly kicking against his heart.","Yuwen Lan was stunned, followed by a rush of wonder and joy.","This was his child.","This was the first time he had felt the little one's presence.","Thinking back to not long ago, when it was only the size of a peanut or taro, and now it could play with him through its mother's belly?","He wondered what movement the little one had just made?","A kick? A wave? Or perhaps a somersault?","...","Having heard all these thoughts, Yanshu said proudly, \"The baby has been moving for quite a while now, but Your Majesty never tried to feel it before.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and hummed in agreement, appearing very good-natured, \"I have been negligent.\"","Then he thought to himself, would the clothing make it harder to feel clearly?","So he tried placing his palm directly on her bare belly, hoping to feel more distinctly.","But the little one stopped moving.","However, the sensation under his hand caught his attention.","Hmm, smooth, just like before.","Well, since she became pregnant, he had strictly followed the doctor's orders and dared not touch her carelessly. Though they still shared a bed, he hadn't touched her like this for a long time.","Now he couldn't help but let his mind wander...","He suddenly missed those nights of intimacy before her pregnancy...","Speaking of which, it had been several months now—could they perhaps...?","Maybe he should ask Doctor Jiang later?","Yanshu, who had been secretly listening to his thoughts, went [???]","Why was he thinking about this?","She finally had a chance to read his mind!","Though, come to think of it, it was actually allowed now.","Doctor Jiang had said it would be fine after the first trimester, ahem.","Hmm?","Yuwen Lan's eyes lit up.","But before he could think further, Fu Hai suddenly announced from the doorway, \"Your Majesty, the Northwest Governor seeks an audience at Qianming Palace.\"","Yuwen Lan snapped back to reality.","Oh right, it was still broad daylight, and he had rushed back from Qianming Palace to see her. There must be a pile of matters waiting for him to handle.","And there was still the matter of the Duke Qi's heir.","He had to withdraw his hand, coughed lightly, and said to her, \"Rest well, I'll return early tonight.\"","Then he stood up and strode out of the hall.","Yanshu raised an eyebrow, pondering—","What did he plan to do by coming back early...?","He wasn't really going to ask the doctor, was he...?","Although... it was quite something to look forward to, ahem.","Of course, it was still early, and how could she be distracted by male beauty when there were important matters at hand?","The Duke Qi family affair couldn't just be told to the Emperor!","After all, their story could fill several novels!","Hehe, she would write it while the iron was hot.","Filled with righteous indignation, her creative juices flowing, Yanshu spent two days writing two novels.","However, she didn't rush to publish them, but first took the manuscripts to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Tsk, with so much gossip about Duke Qi's family, how could she not share it first with her number one fan!","However, when she arrived, before she could present the manuscripts, the Empress Dowager first inquired about her well-being.","\"I haven't seen you for two days, are you feeling unwell?\"","Yanshu was startled, about to speak, when she heard the Empress Dowager's thoughts while examining her carefully, [This girl hasn't visited for two days, could she have been upset by that old Duke Qi? Hmph, that old man has always been scheming, submitting a petition for establishing an heir at this time, his intentions are truly despicable!]","Hearing this, warmth filled Yanshu's heart.","She knew her number one fan cared for her the most.","Of course, this also showed how much the Empress Dowager disliked Duke Qi.","Indeed, as the Emperor's mother, she had the most right to worry about the Emperor's affairs. How could Duke Qi bypass her and submit a petition directly? How could anyone not find that annoying!","She quickly replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Grace. I've been well these past days, just busy writing novels and failed to pay my respects to you, which was truly remiss of me.\"","The Empress Dowager responded with an \"Oh\" and immediately showed interest, asking, \"What novel have you written this time?\"","Since there was no one else in the hall, Yanshu directly explained, \"Actually, His Majesty received news a few days ago that Duke Qi's heir, Guo Zhenghai, had forcibly taken Lin Chengxian's eldest daughter as a concubine several years ago. Lin Chengxian was a commander of the right guard in Lu Prefecture. Within two years, Guo wanted to take his second daughter as well. When Lin refused and hurriedly arranged a marriage for his second daughter, Guo Zhenghai framed him for stealing and selling military provisions, landing him in prison. Now that Lin has just been released, Guo Zhenghai learned of it and wants to use the same trick to harm him again.\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager frowned and said, \"Isn't Guo Zhenghai over fifty? How could he still commit such outrageous acts?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"His Majesty was also quite shocked at first and ordered an investigation. Not only was this incident true, but they discovered other matters in their household that were even more shocking. I felt these things should be made known to the world, so I wrote two novels about them.\"","The Empress Dowager responded, \"You wrote two novels in just two days? Don't exhaust yourself.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Don't worry, Your Grace, I'm not tired. I brought the manuscripts today—would you like me to read them to you?\"","This was something the Empress Dowager enjoyed most, so she naturally nodded, \"Since you've already written them, of course I want to hear them.\"","Yanshu agreed and took out the manuscripts to read to the Empress Dowager.","As she said, she had written two novels about Duke Qi's household. The first focused on Lin and his daughters, portraying a father who truly loved his daughters and protected them against powerful forces, until finally receiving justice from a wise emperor who cleared their names and punished the villains, leading to the family's reunion.","After listening, the Empress Dowager said, \"It seems the Lin family was truly wronged. This Commander Lin is far better than those who use their own flesh and blood to curry favor with the powerful—he deserves praise. But this Duke Qi's heir went too far! Does he think the law belongs to his family? Arbitrarily framing good people for revenge!\"","Yanshu quickly consoled her, \"Don't worry, Your Grace. Since His Majesty has ordered an investigation, he will surely ensure the villains get what they deserve.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"Though that may be true, it's still pitiful that Lin's eldest daughter was violated by Guo Zhenghai!\"","Then she asked, \"What's the second novel about?\"","Yanshu replied, \"The second novel is about the inner court affairs of the Guo family.\" Then she began reading it to the Empress Dowager.","Compared to the first story, this one had more complex plots, starting with how Lady Wei, Guo Zhenghai's wife, had framed her cousin sister while still unmarried, then after entering Duke Qi's household, how she used her position as the main wife to torment the concubines. It thoroughly exposed all her crimes.","The Empress Dowager kept shaking her head in anger as she listened, \"That woman always appears so proper and generous, who would have thought she was so vicious! No wonder the capital suddenly spread rumors about her cousin sister having a pockmarked face—it was her doing all along! Come to think of it, it's fortunate her cousin sister didn't marry into Duke Qi's household. Lady Wei and Guo Zhenghai truly are a perfect match, as they say: birds of a feather flock together.\"","Yanshu nodded repeatedly, \"Indeed, indeed, they're truly a match made in heaven. It's just a pity for those women who were forcibly taken into their household.\"","The Empress Dowager also sighed, saying, \"With such parents, how could they raise any good children?\"","[\"Hmph, that old man has the nerve to petition for an Empress selection! Others must have the worst luck in eight generations to become in-laws with them!\"]","Yanshu silently took in these words, nodding repeatedly in her heart like pounding garlic.","As expected of her number one supporter, even the criticism was so satisfying!","Speaking of which, she hadn't told the Empress Dowager about how Duke Qi's grandson was involved with his father's concubine.","This matter was particularly difficult to bring up, after all, it was an extremely private affair that couldn't be easily investigated.","However, these two incidents were enough.","She then said, \"After thinking it over, the injustice of Officer Lin can be handled well now that the court is involved, but Lady Wei's actions are all domestic matters. I'm afraid they won't be easy to address, given that in their household, it seems no one will stand up for those poor women.\"","The Empress Dowager thought for a moment, then suddenly asked, \"You haven't released that story yet, have you?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"His Majesty just sent people to Lu Prefecture, and the investigation is likely still ongoing. I dare not release it yet, fearing that if it gets out, Duke Qi's heir might silence people, which would be terrible.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Well, let's wait two more days then. The Mid-Autumn Festival is approaching. Last time at the Golden Mirror Pool, the storytelling arrangement was quite good. This time at Jinbo Garden, we might as well have the Court of Imperial Sacrifices arrange another one.\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Of course!\"","Hehe, as expected of her number one supporter, always thinking along the same lines as her!","Two days passed quickly, and soon it was the Mid-Autumn Festival.","To welcome the palace nobles and guests, Jinbo Garden began preparations two days in advance.","As night fell, thousands of palace lanterns illuminated the garden, complementing the bright moon above, casting the pavilions and towers in magnificent splendor.","Seeing this scene, the guests couldn't help but exclaim in admiration, though they dared not linger to appreciate it.","This was because the palace nobles had arrived, and they needed to hurry to pay their respects.","Yanshu had slept well during the day to prepare for tonight's entertainment. Now she sat at the front of the hall with the Emperor and Empress Dowager, watching guests come forward one by one to pay their respects, feeling quite energetic.","Such an occasion naturally included royal relatives like the Grand Princess's family and King Ruyang's family, as well as court nobles such as the Marquis of Guangyang, Linwu Marquis, Marquis of Xuanping, and the Minister of Works.","Speaking of which, having not seen him for a while, that paper-eating Marquis of Guangyang had actually gained quite a bit of weight, with noticeably fuller cheeks and better complexion, quite different from his previously increasingly gaunt appearance.","Seeing this, the Empress Dowager asked, \"It seems the Marquis of Guangyang has recovered?\"","Before the Marquis could speak, the Marchioness of Guangyang quickly replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Grace. The Marquis's appetite has improved greatly, and his meals are now regular.\"","The Marquis hastily nodded along, \"Thank you for your care, Your Grace. I have indeed recovered.\"","Well, ever since discovering the miraculous food called pancakes at the water festival banquet at Golden Mirror Pool, he had found a new hobby.","This food had a texture similar to paper but felt much better in the stomach and was nutritious. It could be wrapped with various fillings, which finally helped him gradually abandon his strange habit of eating paper and return to a normal life.","He was truly grateful to whoever prepared the food at that water festival banquet - they were his savior!","Yuwen Lan silently listened, secretly glancing at Yanshu.","Meanwhile, Yanshu modestly nodded along with the Empress Dowager, saying nothing.","It was a small matter, not worth mentioning.","More familiar faces appeared afterward, and Yanshu recognized many of them from the various palace banquets she had attended over the past year.","However, perhaps due to Duke Qi's recent petition for the Empress selection, many families had brought their eligible young daughters tonight, all dressed in fine silks and looking splendid.","Yet Yanshu paid them no mind, as she was wholly focused on waiting for tonight's main characters - Duke Qi's family - to make their appearance.","Fortunately, it wasn't long before they appeared.","The white-haired Duke Qi led the way, followed by his son Guo Zhenghai, daughter-in-law Lady Wei, and their children Guo Jianguang and Guo Zhaorong.","Duke Qi led his family in paying respects to the Emperor, Empress Dowager, and Yanshu, \"This old subject and family wish Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and Consort Yi a peaceful Mid-Autumn Festival.\"","As he was an elder, Yuwen Lan naturally responded politely, \"No need for such formality, please rise.\"","As soon as he spoke, he heard the simultaneous thoughts of the Empress Dowager and Yanshu in his mind--","Yanshu: [Look, this is that old scoundrel's family! We absolutely can't let them off tonight!]","Empress Dowager: [Hmph! So this is that family, it's not easy to have them all gathered today. If heaven has eyes, a bolt of lightning should strike them down.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, that's a good idea, but it's already August, so the chances of thunder are quite low.","Just as she was thinking this, Duke Qi's family had risen, and Lady Wei took the initiative to say, \"As we entered the garden earlier, we saw the flickering lanterns, truly magnificent. It is our fortune to enjoy such scenery with the nobles today.\"","As she finished speaking, her daughter Guo Zhaorong quickly nodded in agreement.","The Empress Dowager spoke, \"Consort Yi is now carrying the imperial heir, we cannot risk any mishaps. Having more lanterns makes the garden brighter, preventing anyone from accidentally stepping into any pits or ditches, which would be unfortunate.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone paused.","Well, the Empress Dowager's words... seemed to carry some hidden meaning?","Lady Wei also hesitated, only able to nod repeatedly, \"The Empress Dowager speaks wisely.\"","Feeling too self-conscious to separately introduce her daughter for greetings, she quickly retreated to the side.","Seeing that all guests had arrived, the Mid-Autumn banquet began.","Tonight there was again singing and dancing for entertainment. As the music played, guests exchanged cups, and the atmosphere gradually became lively.","Many young noble ladies had prepared performances for tonight, waiting for their chance to show their talents.","However, at this moment, several palace servants brought out a table with a wooden clapper on it, followed by a man who appeared to be a storyteller.","Everyone immediately became curious - there would be storytelling tonight?","This was truly novel.","Then, the storyteller struck his wooden clapper and began to speak.","\"I am honored today to tell you several new stories from the pen of the Carefree Young Master.\"","Oh? New stories from the Carefree Young Master?","Hearing this, everyone's eyes lit up.","Especially the Minister of Works, Yanshu's number one fan, who immediately put down his wine cup and chopsticks, forgetting everything else to listen with full attention.","The storyteller's first story was based on Duke Qi's heir's wife.","Come to think of it, this was the same artist who had performed at Golden Mirror Pool, and after not seeing him for a while, his skills had improved even more. His vivid performance portrayed Lady Wei's malice even more incisively than Yanshu's original story.","When they heard about how the woman had harmed her sisters to marry into a noble family, then after marriage persecuted the concubines, and even disfigured and sold off or drowned in the lake any maids who had been harassed by her lecherous husband, everyone was furious to the extreme, almost wanting to flip their tables on the spot.","Fortunately, the storyteller then took a turn in the narrative, saying, \"Finally, one day, the vengeful spirits of all those she had killed came to claim her life, possessing her son and daughter, making them go mad, smashing things at home, cursing and biting people. In her panic, she had no choice but to send for a Taoist priest to take a look. However, after examining the situation, the priest said that she had committed too many evil deeds, and now could only kowtow before the gods for redemption, for seven times seven, forty-nine days, before there might be a chance to dispel these vengeful spirits' harassment.\"","At this point, the Grand Princess couldn't help but ask, \"Did she do it? Come to think of it, if forty-nine days of fasting and praying could really eliminate this woman's sins, that seems too easy!\"","Everyone nodded, thinking that after this woman had committed so many evil deeds, if she could offset them just by fasting and praying, that would be too unsatisfying!","The storyteller smiled and said, \"Your Highness, don't be hasty. Although the Taoist said this, the woman had no intention of following his advice. After all, doing so would confirm that she had indeed committed these evil deeds, and if word got out, wouldn't she lose all face? So she sent people from her household to search for an even more powerful expert who could suppress the haunting spirits. However, before such an expert could be found, the vengeful spirits in the mansion grew increasingly furious, compelling her own children one dark night - one pushed her into a well, while the other set fire to the residence.\"","The Grand Princess's eyes widened, \"So the woman drowned in the end?\"","The storyteller nodded, \"Indeed. At the time, the house was engulfed in flames, and everyone was frantically trying to escape and extinguish the fire. By the time they managed to put out the blaze and remembered her, they discovered she had already drowned in the well. At that moment, all the vengeful spirits vanished, and peace finally returned to the mansion. However, the buildings had been reduced to ruins and became uninhabitable.\"","\"Serves her right! Absolutely deserved it!\"","The Grand Princess clapped her hands, \"This is what we call karma! What a satisfying ending!\"","As her words fell, everyone joined in the applause, nodding in agreement, \"What a gratifying story!\"","Amidst the chorus of praise, Yanshu glanced at the story's protagonist, Lady Wei.","She saw that Lady Wei's face had turned ashen, looking extremely uncomfortable.","She even seemed to be hesitating, appearing as if she wanted to leave her seat.","Hmph, how she loved seeing the panicked expressions of those who had done evil deeds.","Where was all that energy now, compared to when she had been so determined to set traps for her?","Just then, the white-haired Duke Qi suddenly spoke up, \"Today is the Mid-Autumn Festival. Telling these fabricated ghost stories is rather inappropriate for the occasion.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone was taken aback.","What's inappropriate about it?","This old man was the one being inappropriate - it was just a story, and unless one had done something to trouble their conscience, why fear ghost tales?","Of course, they could only feel angry but dared not speak up, as the old man's status was too high to challenge casually.","Fortunately, Yanshu spoke up promptly, addressing the storyteller, \"In that case, tell us something else. Surely you have stories without ghosts?\"","The storyteller immediately nodded, \"Indeed, I do. Please be patient, everyone.\"","He struck his wooden clappers and said, \"Let me tell you all a second story. In Lu Prefecture, not far from the capital, there lived a family where husband and wife were deeply in love and lived in harmony. They raised two wonderful daughters who were both very well-behaved, earning praise from all their neighbors. As time passed, the daughters grew more beautiful by the day. Soon the elder daughter reached marriageable age, and suitors were practically wearing down their doorstep.\"","\"Just as the parents were carefully considering potential sons-in-law for their elder daughter, a powerful old man from the capital appeared. This old man, apart from his wealthy and distinguished background, had absolutely no redeeming qualities. He regularly bullied others and committed all manner of evil deeds. Despite being several years older than the girl's father, he set his sights on their elder daughter. Using various schemes, threats, and enticements, he eventually forced the good girl to become his concubine.\"","At this point, the storyteller deliberately paused, and a wave of angry voices arose from the banquet.","Perhaps due to the wine, or perhaps due to Duke Qi's earlier forceful interruption, everyone was harboring anger. They couldn't help but exclaim, \"This old man's face is truly as thick as the city walls! He's even older than the girl's father, yet he has the nerve to force her to be his concubine!\"","\"Exactly! He has absolutely no sense of propriety or shame!\"","Amidst the chorus of condemnation, Duke Qi's heir, Guo Zhenghai, appeared extremely uncomfortable, suddenly standing up as if trying to slip away unnoticed.","However, the Emperor spoke up to stop him, \"Where is Lord Guo heading?\"","Guo Zhenghai froze, then bowed his head and said, \"Your Majesty, I suddenly feel unwell and wish to get some fresh air...\"","Before he could finish, the Emperor replied, \"There are imperial physicians in the garden today. Let them examine you.\"","Imperial physicians?","That would be disastrous if they actually examined him!","Guo Zhenghai was startled and quickly said, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty, but I wouldn't dare trouble the imperial physicians. I'm fine.\"","The Empress Dowager watched this exchange and sneered, \"If you're fine, then sit down properly and listen to the story.\"","Guo Zhenghai had no choice but to respond and return to his seat."]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105","paragraphs":["Following the Empress Dowager's words, Guo Zhenghai, the Heir of Duke Qi, had no choice but to sit back down.","The storyteller continued, \"This man already had more than ten concubines in his household, including many virtuous ladies like this young woman, all forcibly taken by this old man. Most critically, the main mistress of the household - this old man's legal wife - was extremely cruel. She would force every woman who entered the household to drink infertility medicine to prevent them from bearing children. This young lady couldn't escape this fate either. Within half a month of entering the household, she was forced to drink the medicine by the mistress and nearly lost her life. In short, her life was truly miserable.\"","At this point, everyone was stunned.","The Princess Consort of Ruyang couldn't help but ask, \"Wait, why does this mistress sound so similar to the evil woman from the previous story?\"","The storyteller nodded and said, \"Your Grace is correct. They are actually the same person - these two stories are about the same family.\"","Upon hearing this, the Princess Consort of Ruyang had a look of sudden realization and nodded, \"So they're from the same family! No wonder they're all so wicked!\"","Others nodded in agreement.","Someone in the crowd cursed, \"So one's a lecherous old man and the other's a cruel woman - what a perfect match this couple makes!\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up when she heard this, almost wanting to applaud! What an accurate summary!","Meanwhile, she glanced toward Guo Zhenghai, the Heir of Duke Qi, and Lady Wei, seeing their faces alternating between pale and flushed, their expressions twisted with panic and anger, yet unable to speak out, appearing extremely frustrated.","Hmph, this was nothing compared to what was coming - after committing evil deeds for so many years, getting cursed at a few times was nothing.","Just then, the storyteller continued, \"Your observations are all correct, my esteemed audience. Let me continue with the story. While this young lady was suffering miserably in this noble household in the capital, she didn't know that the beastly old man was still thinking about her younger sister. After two years, assuming the younger sister had grown up, this old man used hunting as an excuse to visit their family again, intending to use the same trick to forcibly take the younger sister as well.\"","Upon hearing this, the audience became agitated again.","The Grand Princess couldn't help but exclaim, \"The second sister absolutely must not fall into this tiger's den! The parents must quickly think of something!\"","Everyone agreed.","The storyteller continued, \"Your Highness speaks wisely! Fortunately, the parents had sensed the danger, and when someone came to propose marriage to the second daughter, they quickly arranged her engagement.\"","Hearing this, everyone breathed a sigh of relief, thinking the family had finally escaped disaster.","However, the storyteller then said, \"Unexpectedly, the old man became furious and used his influence to frame the father with false charges, forcibly sending him to prison.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone became angry again, exclaiming, \"Does this old man have no respect for the law?\"","\"Indeed! How can he bully people like this!\"","The Grand Princess also angrily said to the storyteller, \"In all my years, this is the first time I've heard of such bullying! Surely such a person can't have a good ending!\"","The storyteller quickly responded, \"Please don't worry, Your Highness. Let me continue. How could common people withstand the oppression of power in the capital? So despite being wrongfully accused, the father went to prison. Fortunately, the local official knew he was innocent and couldn't bear to give him a heavy sentence, so after two years, he was released. However, just when they thought the family could finally reunite and live peacefully, news reached the capital, and the old man became dissatisfied again. He not only wanted to send the father back to prison but also planned to frame the presiding official to vent his anger.\"","At this point in the story, the audience exploded with anger again, crying out, \"Heavens! How can such an evil person exist?\"","\"Indeed! Does he think he rules the world? How dare he act so arbitrarily!\"","The Grand Princess spoke again, \"This person is still alive and well? Haven't the heavens struck him down with lightning? Or rather, struck down his entire family?\"","Hearing this, Yanshu raised an eyebrow, seeing her number one supporter, the Empress Dowager, quickly looking at her sister-in-law and nodding in support.","Yanshu reflected inwardly - no wonder these sisters-in-law got along so well, they shared such excellent values!","Looking at Guo Zhenghai and his wife again, their faces had turned ashen, as if they wished they could crawl under their chairs.","Someone anxiously asked the storyteller, \"What happened next? Such a good family couldn't have been framed by this old man again, right?\"","The storyteller quickly replied, \"Of course not, please rest assured. As they say, heaven's justice prevails and evil deeds cannot go unpunished. Also, as the saying goes, if you want to keep something secret, better not do it at all. Eventually, someone at court discovered this man's intentions and, outraged, immediately reported it to the emperor. The emperor was naturally furious and ordered an immediate investigation into the matter.\"","\"What they discovered was shocking - this man had committed many other evil deeds, all using the power granted by the imperial court to oppress common people and tarnish the court's reputation. Some cases even involved loss of life, and not just one instance. How could the emperor tolerate such a villain? He immediately sentenced him to death! He was executed outside the palace gates that very day to satisfy the people's anger.\"","As these words fell, applause erupted in the hall, with audience members cheering, \"Justice is served! Evil deeds bring evil consequences!\"","\"Wonderful! Thank heavens for the imperial court's justice! Thank heavens for our wise emperor!\"","Amidst the applause, there was a sudden thud, as if something had fallen to the ground.","Everyone turned to look and discovered that Guo Zhenghai, the Heir of Duke Qi who had earlier claimed to be unwell, had collapsed onto the floor.","His face was deathly pale, covered in cold sweat, appearing very unwell.","The audience was puzzled.","Then the emperor spoke, \"If Lord Guo is unwell, let the imperial physician examine you.\"","Though the words showed concern, the tone was ice-cold.","Guo Zhenghai, guilty-conscious, struggled to his feet and returned to his seat, saying, \"Your subject dares not trouble you. Thank you for your concern, Your Majesty. I am fine.\"","The audience, still caught up in the story, quickly asked the storyteller, \"Though this man died, what about all the young ladies he had taken, and what about that evil woman of his?\"","The storyteller replied, \"As his family member who was aware of his crimes, that evil woman couldn't escape legal punishment. She was ultimately sentenced to exile, condemned to wander in the cold frontier regions for life, never allowed to return to the capital. As for the innocent women in their household, the court considered them all victims and granted them their freedom. Finally, that poor eldest daughter was able to return to her parents' embrace, reuniting the family.\"","As these words fell, some in the audience nodded, while others sighed.","Princess An Kang had tears in her eyes, wiping them as she sighed, \"Such a good young woman, what did she do wrong to be treated so cruelly by that evil couple, having her body poisoned, unable to become a mother, probably unable to marry in the future.\"","Hearing this, everyone nodded in agreement, once again cursing the evil couple for treating people so inhumanely.","The Empress Dowager then spoke, \"Regardless, regaining freedom is always good. A family that values loyalty and righteousness must have raised daughters of good character. If she meets a good person, she might still find a good marriage. Even if she doesn't, spending her future days with her parents is still far better than being abused by those evil people.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement to these words.","With this, the story came to an end. The storyteller received his reward and, after paying his respects, withdrew.","Just as Guo Zhenghai and Lady Wei thought this matter had passed and were about to secretly breathe a sigh of relief, the emperor spoke, \"What do you all think about the evil deeds this man committed?\"","The audience was still caught up in the story, and upon hearing this, they immediately shared their thoughts.","Yanshu's devoted supporter number one, Lord Lu, the Minister of Works, spoke first, \"Your Majesty, from the story, this man abused his power to bully people and dishonor the court's dignity. Just the two counts of forcibly taking virtuous women and falsely accusing court officials would be enough to warrant severe punishment.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement.","The Minister of Justice also said, \"Just looking at how this story involves framing an imperial official, this person's methods seem quite skilled. If such a thing happened in reality, this person must have committed more than one such evil deed. We should follow this case to prevent other innocent people from being wronged. In any case, those who damage the court's reputation and aid villains must not be treated lightly.\"","Everyone agreed again, \"Indeed! We must not be lenient.\"","The Emperor nodded, then suddenly turned to Duke Qi and asked, \"What does Duke Qi think of this matter?\"","Duke Qi paused, then immediately stood up and said, \"Your Majesty, this old minister thinks the story is well-written, but fears it's just a story. Your Majesty is wise and mighty, currently maintaining peace and prosperity in the nation, with citizens living in harmony. Such things shouldn't happen in reality.\"","Upon hearing this, Yanshu secretly raised her eyebrows―","This old man sure knows how to speak - by this logic, if this were true, wouldn't that mean the Emperor wasn't wise and mighty?","Fortunately, Yuwen Lan didn't fall for it, but continued asking, \"I want to know, if this were true, according to Duke Qi, how should it be handled?\"","The Duke replied, \"Your Majesty, if this were indeed true, the evildoer should certainly be severely punished.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound of acknowledgment and asked further, \"If this villain were from a noble family, in Duke Qi's opinion, should the law show favoritism and be lenient?\"","At these words, Yanshu could barely contain her internal applause.","What an excellent question from the Emperor!","Everyone knows the principle that nobles who break the law face the same punishment as commoners. If Duke Qi suggested favoritism, many officials would surely oppose him, so he could only say no.","And thus, once the Emperor decided to convict his son, he would have nothing to say!","Sure enough, after the Emperor's words, the old man said, \"Your Majesty, as the saying goes, nobles who break the law face the same punishment as commoners. This old minister believes that regardless of one's status, they should not receive special treatment under the law. However, given the gravity of the matter, we must investigate thoroughly to ensure we aren't deceived by those with ulterior motives.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone raised their eyebrows, thinking that Duke Qi must be getting old and out of touch with current affairs, not knowing that the storyteller's tales all had real-life origins?","And who had been wrongly accused?","However, just then, the Emperor spoke, \"A few days ago, I received reports that the Heir of Duke Qi, Guo Zhenghai, abused his power to force a virtuous woman to become his concubine and maliciously framed Lin Chengxian, the Commander of the Right Guard of Lu Prefecture, for stealing and selling military provisions, causing him to be wrongly accused for two years.\"","At these words, Duke Qi was stunned.","Everyone else was stunned too.","They all turned to look at Guo Zhenghai.","No wonder he had claimed to feel unwell and collapsed when the story was first told - so he was the villain!!!","Under everyone's gaze, Guo Zhenghai immediately knelt and said, \"Please investigate clearly, Your Majesty! This is completely fabricated! This Lin Chengxian is actually a greedy person who, during my visit to Lu Prefecture, forced his eldest daughter to become my concubine and then constantly extorted money from me. He truly did steal those provisions, and when his crime was exposed, he begged me to cover for him. When I refused, he became resentful and started making false accusations against me...\"","Hearing this explanation, everyone raised their eyebrows.","What?","In his version, a mere commander had threatened him, the heir to a duke?","Just then, the Empress Dowager spoke, \"What nonsense is this? Their daughter, probably younger than your own son, was forced upon you as a concubine? And you accepted? What, did they get you drunk and force you?\"","Pfft...","At these words, though angry, the crowd could barely suppress their laughter.","Well said, Empress Dowager!","Yanshu also secretly praised her cleverness, then spoke up, \"I hear you have fifteen or sixteen concubines in your household. Were they all forced upon you as well? If so, you must have suffered greatly.\"","Hearing this, everyone had to stifle their laughter again, all looking at Guo Zhenghai, who was now sweating profusely and could no longer fabricate any excuses, only stammering, \"I... I am ashamed...\"","Just then, Yanshu heard Guo Zhaorong's thoughts, [Hmph! This woman dares to insult my father! I'll make her pay for this in the future!]","Oh my, still daring to threaten her?","Yanshu immediately added, \"By the way, with so many concubines in your household, why haven't we heard of any children from them?\"","At these words, everyone naturally looked at Lady Wei.","Well, since that old lecher was Guo Zhenghai, needless to say, that evil woman must be her.","Tsk tsk tsk, who would have thought she could be so vicious! If what the story says is true, there must be at least ten wrongful deaths by her hand, considering she had disposed of five or six unborn children alone.","The pregnant Princess of Ankang couldn't help but say, \"How could anyone do such things?\"","Everyone nodded, whispering, \"With such a mother, how could she raise a good daughter? And they still have the nerve to aspire to be Empress?\"","\"Indeed, if she really became Empress, wouldn't that spell disaster for the imperial family?\"","Just then, Lady Wei suddenly knelt and cried, \"This is unjust! Please investigate, Your Majesty and Empress Dowager, the storyteller is framing me! I have never done anything unconscionable! If I had, heaven would have struck me down...\"","At these words, Lord Lu, the Minister of Works and the storyteller's number one fan, couldn't help but speak up, \"The storyteller has never wrongly accused anyone since beginning to write!\"","Everyone nodded in agreement.","But just then, there was another thud.","Everyone hurriedly looked over to see their son, Guo Jianguang, suddenly collapse, foaming at the mouth and convulsing violently.","This startled everyone, and Yanshu quietly asked the system, [What's happening now?]","The system replied, [Would that concubine seduce him for nothing? Of course she had poisoned him! Now that he's drunk and nervous, he naturally can't withstand the poison's effects.]","Yanshu: [!!!]","That concubine was truly bold and clever!","It seems this family was providing today's most spectacular show.","Sure enough, seeing this situation, the Guo family members all cried out in alarm, and Yuwen Lan ordered the court physician present that night, \"Examine what's wrong with him.\"","The physician complied, immediately examining him before concluding, \"Your Majesty, Young Master Guo's body is severely depleted, seemingly from excessive sexual activity.\"","Tsk...","Hearing this, everyone exchanged glances, whispering in their hearts―","To be so depleted at such a young age, just how corrupt has this family become?","The Empress Dowager commanded, \"Take him to the side hall and revive him first.\"","The palace servants complied, quickly carrying him out of the hall.","But there were still urgent matters to handle.","The Emperor said, \"The Ministry of Justice has already brought witnesses and evidence back from Lu Prefecture. Guards, arrest the Heir of Duke Qi, Guo Zhenghai, and begin the trial immediately to give the people an explanation as soon as possible.\"","At these words, guards responded in unison and took Guo Zhenghai away.","Of course, as his family members, Lady Wei and her daughter Guo Zhaorong were also \"invited\" out and placed under guard.","Seeing this, Duke Qi hurried to speak, \"Your Majesty...\"","But before he could finish, the Emperor interrupted, \"It's admirable that Duke Qi understands justice so well. As you said earlier, once the crimes are verified, I will certainly punish severely without mercy.\"","Before Duke Qi could say more, everyone praised in unison, \"The Emperor is wise!\"","After the Guo family members were removed, the hall returned to order.","Everyone still wanted more, so the master of ceremonies called the storyteller back up to tell a few more stories.","Everyone enjoyed eating mooncakes while listening to the stories.","In the garden, the Mid-Autumn moon rose high, creating a beautiful reflection in Jinbo Lake.","This Mid-Autumn Festival banquet, though different from others, had its own unique charm.","It was only a pity that those young ladies who had dressed up hoping to perform could no longer find their opportunity."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106","paragraphs":["The day after the Mid-Autumn Festival banquet, the Carefree Young Master released two new stories simultaneously, much to the readers' delight.","Meanwhile, the case involving Duke Qi's Manor was under investigation. When the news broke, combined with the Carefree Young Master's new stories, the common people finally understood how this once-invincible noble family had become so corrupt.","Condemnation spread like wildfire.","As the news spread throughout the capital and beyond, numerous victims who had suffered under Duke Qi's Manor's oppression came forward to file complaints at the government offices. Some had their land and wealth stolen, others had their wives and daughters abused - there were more than ten such cases in total.","At this juncture, local authorities dared not ignore these complaints. They hurriedly documented everything and forwarded the cases to the Ministry of Punishment for review.","As a result, the scope of the investigation continued to expand. The Ministry of Punishment and the Imperial Censorate spent nearly half a month thoroughly investigating the cases before reporting to the emperor.","Upon seeing the verified evidence of crimes involving more than ten lives, the emperor flew into a rage and personally signed Guo Zhenghai's death warrant.","His servants and advisors who were involved in the crimes were all severely punished - the worst offenders were executed, while others were exiled, with none being pardoned.","Guo Zhenghai's wife and children were also convicted as accomplices and sentenced to exile in the harsh frontier regions. However, his son, still suffering from residual poison, died before reaching fifty li outside the capital.","As for Duke Qi, who had betrayed his nephew and brother-in-law, causing the deaths of dozens of his in-laws' family members, he suffered a stroke on the night of the Mid-Autumn Palace banquet after returning home and passed away three days later.","Thus, a noble family that had flourished for decades completely vanished from public view.","Of course, in his mercy, the emperor ordered officials to account for all the concubines and servants in the household. Those who had not participated in the family's crimes were granted their freedom.","As a result, the eldest daughter of the Lin family was finally able to return home to Lu Prefecture and reunite with her parents.","By the time the Duke Qi's Manor incident officially concluded, it was already September in the capital, and the weather had turned cool in the mornings and evenings.","Yanshu's belly had grown noticeably larger, visible even through her thick daytime robes.","It was even more apparent at night in her sleeping garments.","Yuwen Lan had been busy for over half a month, but tonight he came early. When he entered the hall, he saw her just emerging from the bathhouse.","Rendong and Lianxin were supporting their mistress on either side. Upon seeing the emperor, they hurriedly tried to bow, but as they began to curtsy, the emperor said, \"You may leave.\" He naturally reached out to replace them in supporting Yanshu.","The two maids acknowledged and withdrew with lowered heads.","With no one else in the room, before Yanshu could speak, Yuwen Lan looked her over and sighed, \"Your belly seems to have grown larger.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"Well, I am five months along now, and besides, Your Majesty hasn't visited for several days.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan quickly explained, \"The past few days, I finished work quite late. I was afraid of disturbing your rest, so I slept in Qianming Palace.\"","He felt quite guilty as he spoke - how could he have let her sleep alone in this hall for three days while carrying their child?","But she was very understanding and said, \"Your Majesty must take care of your health while attending to state affairs. Please don't overwork yourself.\"","Though in her heart she thought, [Actually, my dear baby's father, no need to be so polite with me. Having the big bed to myself was quite comfortable - I could roll around however I wanted!]","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Did she really not miss him?","And what was with calling him \"baby's father\"?","Also, with her belly so big, could she really roll around as she pleased?","He had many things he wanted to say, but since it wasn't summer anymore, he worried about her catching cold. He first led her to the bed and helped her get under the covers.","Then he went to wash up before joining her in bed.","Hmm, the bedding seemed to have been sun-dried that day, giving off a comfortable smell. More importantly, there was a natural little heater in bed, not only fragrant but also very soft, finally allowing his body to relax after a long day's work.","However, Yuwen Lan still remembered what happened earlier. He pulled her into his arms and asked, \"Is my embrace comfortable?\"","Yanshu nodded without hesitation, \"Of course it is.\"","Yuwen Lan asked again, \"Then, do you prefer sleeping alone or with me?\"","Yanshu naturally replied, \"Of course it's better with Your Majesty.\"","But as soon as the words left her mouth, she felt something was amiss.","Why was he asking such questions?","It was as if he knew what she had been thinking earlier?","No, she'd better check what was on his mind.","So she took his hand and placed it on her belly, saying, \"Your Majesty, feel the baby.\"","Yuwen Lan startled, quickly trying to suppress the thoughts he didn't want her to know.","However, as soon as his palm touched her belly, the little one pushed against it, creating a bump that landed perfectly in the center of his palm, allowing him to feel it very clearly.","Yuwen Lan was stunned, his heart instantly melting.","[Hmm, as expected of my child, just as clever as me.]","Yanshu: \"...\"","So the emperor was this confident too - truly, all men are the same!","However, at this moment, the baby in her belly seemed very excited and started moving again. Yanshu thought, perhaps the little one really did recognize their father and enjoyed his touch?","She was also very happy and said to Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty should talk to the baby more now. Once the baby becomes familiar with your voice, they will be especially close to you in the future.\"","Yuwen Lan found this interesting, \"Is that so?\"","Seeing her nod, he seemed uncertain about what to do and asked, \"What should I say to them?\"","He appeared somewhat awkward.","Indeed, this was his first time being a father. Yanshu couldn't help but smile at his behavior and suggested, \"Your Majesty could start by introducing yourself to the baby.\"","Yuwen Lan made a thoughtful sound, then cleared his throat and tried, \"Little one, I am your father.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the baby actually pushed against his hand again through the belly.","Yuwen Lan was greatly excited.","Yanshu's eyes lit up - so he also called the baby \"little one\"?","Could this be what they call having the same mind?","She couldn't help but sigh, \"Your Majesty is so gentle with the baby.\"","Unexpectedly, he lightly pinched her chin and smiled, \"Am I not gentle with you?\"","Hmm, the touch of his fingertips was smooth and somehow made one's thoughts wander.","However, it had only been half a month since they last...","After all, the imperial physician had said that while it was possible now, it shouldn't be too frequent.","He had to suppress his thoughts and asked her instead, \"How big is our little one now?\"","Yanshu thought for a moment and made a gesture the size of a grape, saying, \"About this big, I suppose.\"","Yuwen Lan was surprised, \"Only that big? Then won't it take a long time before the birth?\"","Being a first-time father, and having rarely seen pregnant women before, he didn't have much common knowledge about this.","Of course, Yanshu was also a first-time mother with no experience. Hearing his question, she gestured the size of a watermelon based on her imagination and said, \"When I'm ready to give birth, my belly will probably be about this big.\"","\"I see,\" Yuwen Lan nodded, then frowned and asked, \"That's so big - how will it come out?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","That was a good question.","All men in the world should understand how arduous childbirth is for women.","But probably not many would think to ask such a question.","Unfortunately, there were no prenatal training classes for expectant fathers in this era. And she wasn't sure either, only knowing it would be very painful.","So she said, \"...Well, we'll cross that bridge when we come to it. I'm sure I'll manage when the time comes.\"","Though she said this, she was already starting to feel nervous. After all, with the limited medical conditions of the time, women often faced the possibility of difficult births!","Oh no, what would she do then?","Yuwen Lan silently took in her words, suddenly pulling her closer in his embrace, saying, \"Don't worry, I will summon all the imperial physicians to ensure your safety.\"","This embrace gave her an inexplicable sense of security, and Yanshu nodded.","She couldn't help but sigh inwardly, thinking that compared to many men nowadays, he was already quite good. At the very least, compared to Consort Dowager Hui's situation back then, she was much happier.","Speaking of which, after eliminating Duke Qi's Manor this time, the emperor had consistently ignored Consort Dowager Hui's so-called family members, making his attitude quite clear.","After witnessing so much drama, it was truly rare to find someone like the Empress Dowager who could raise a concubine's child so well and with such dedication.","The Empress Dowager truly deserved to be called one of the world's finest stepmothers.","Yuwen Lan thought the same, and after reflecting on this, he said, \"The Double Ninth Festival is approaching. We should think about how to celebrate it with the Empress Dowager.\"","Yanshu made a thoughtful sound and began to consider.","Celebrating the Double Ninth Festival in the palace usually meant nothing more than holding a banquet and drinking chrysanthemum wine.","But the Empress Dowager wasn't like her, fond of food and drink, so a banquet seemed meaningless.","Most importantly, there hadn't been any new gossip from their acquaintances lately...","How boring would a banquet be without any drama to discuss, she thought with a click of her tongue.","Oh, if only her idol, Principal Qi, could celebrate the Double Ninth Festival with the Empress Dowager...","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How could that be possible? The Empress Dowager was still the Empress Dowager, and Qi Shuguang was just the principal of Songhe Academy - they were worlds apart...","Of course, Yanshu knew this wasn't possible, so the thought quickly passed.","However, after thinking for a moment, her eyes lit up and she said, \"During the Double Ninth Festival, common people like to go climbing mountains. Perhaps the Empress Dowager would like to get some fresh air too? Your Majesty could take her out for a walk?\"","Yuwen Lan hesitated, \"Would the Empress Dowager enjoy leaving the palace?\"","Yanshu thought to herself, how could she not enjoy it? Even birds in this palace would want to fly out and see the world!","The Empress Dowager had been confined for decades, of course she'd want to go out!!!","But she dared not say these thoughts aloud, and could only suggest, \"Your Majesty often goes out to observe the common people's lives. Putting yourself in her shoes, the Empress Dowager has been in the palace for so many years, surely she'd like to observe the common people's lives too? Like when Your Majesty took me out to eat delicious food- I mean, to experience the common people's way of life, wasn't that enjoyable?\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, he had to admit that sometimes he too felt confined in the palace and wanted to go out for a walk.","However, he glanced at her and said, \"But can you climb mountains in your current condition?\"","Oh, this meant there was hope!","Yanshu immediately perked up and nodded eagerly, \"I'll be fine! The imperial physician said I should exercise moderately, it will help with the delivery later.\"","Before he could respond, she had already started planning, \"I think Osmanthus Mountain would be perfect. The osmanthus flowers are fragrant this season, and the mountain isn't too high with good paths. I heard even carriages can go up there.\"","\"Oh, and there's a temple on the mountain where we can pray. I'll ask the Empress Dowager tomorrow, I'm sure she'll love it.\"","Hehe, another chance to go out!!!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Wait, he hadn't agreed yet...","Was it too late to say no...","...","As Yanshu had predicted, the Empress Dowager was very pleased with the idea of going mountain climbing outside the palace, and agreed immediately when asked the next day.","Yuwen Lan had no choice but to order the imperial guards to make arrangements, and after ensuring safety, they set out early on the morning of the Double Ninth Festival, taking the Empress Dowager and Yanshu to Osmanthus Mountain.","As Yanshu had said, Osmanthus Mountain wasn't very high, with well-maintained paths that allowed carriages to drive almost to the summit.","After they got out of the carriage, they saw layers of red leaves all around, and the breeze carried the sweet fragrance of osmanthus flowers, making everyone feel comfortable.","The Empress Dowager was indeed in good spirits, her words and actions notably lighter.","As for Yanshu, her steps were light, and she truly showed no signs of fatigue.","Of course, Yuwen Lan remained cautious and held her hand the entire way.","There was a White Pagoda Temple on the mountain, and they could see many visitors carrying incense heading there to pray. Since they had come all this way and enjoyed the scenery, they decided to visit the temple as well.","The path to the temple couldn't accommodate carriages, but fortunately, it wasn't far. After walking for about the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, they arrived.","The temple wasn't large but had a charming rustic quality, and was said to be very efficacious. The family of three paid their respects together and made some donations.","After paying their respects, they admired the temple's scenery and rested in a pavilion in the courtyard.","The attending maids promptly served hot tea, and Yuwen Lan asked the Empress Dowager, \"Mother, how do you find today?\"","Under her veiled hat, the Empress Dowager's voice carried a satisfied smile, \"Very good. You've been thoughtful, my son. Along the way, I heard visitors discussing the recent Guo family matter, all praising the emperor's wisdom. You should continue to work hard in the future.\"","Yuwen Lan quickly nodded, \"I understand, Mother. Please rest assured.\"","He felt satisfied in his heart.","Then, as he raised his teacup and casually looked around, before he could take a sip of the hot tea, his gaze froze.","The courtyard wasn't particularly crowded today, though visitors would occasionally enter, pay their respects to Buddha, admire the scenery, and then head back down the mountain.","At that moment, a single person entered the courtyard, particularly noticeable because he was alone.","He appeared to be in his forties, wearing a blue robe, standing as straight as a pine tree. It was none other than Qi Shuguang, the principal of Songhe Academy.","Why was he here too?","Yuwen Lan paused, and before he could think further, a sudden exclamation burst into his ears--","[Oh heavens, isn't that isn't that Principal Qi? To actually meet him here? This must be fate!!!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","At this moment, only two women were sitting beside him.","Needless to say, it was Yanshu screaming in her mind again.","When he first saw Qi Shuguang, he had suspected that she might have arranged this.","But hearing her scream like this, he believed that she truly didn't know about it.","Then he heard the Empress Dowager's thoughts pause as well, [This... why is he here too?]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, apparently the Empress Dowager didn't know either.","Tsk, to meet here by chance, could it really be...","Fate?","At that moment, Qi Shuguang, who had been admiring the scenery, also noticed him. After a moment of surprise, he immediately approached and bowed, saying, \"I didn't know Your Excellency was here. I apologize for the disturbance.\"","Since they had already encountered each other, Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"It's fine, I'm just here to enjoy the scenery today. No need for formalities.\"","Just as he finished speaking, Yanshu coughed slightly under her veiled hat and said, \"What a coincidence, Master Qi is also here to enjoy the scenery today?\"","Qi Shuguang quickly replied, \"Yes, my lady.\"","He thought to himself, judging by the voice, this must be Consort Yi, so the other person... could it be... her?","Yanshu secretly heard this and wanted nothing more than to answer \"yes,\" but reason told her not to say too much, so she only said, \"What a coincidence today. By the way, we sent some blue crabs to your academy recently, did you get to taste them?\"","Her idol replied, \"My lady, all the teachers and students have tried them and are very grateful for your kindness.\"","Yanshu nodded and continued, \"What about the mooncakes? They were all made in our manor, using lotus seeds we grew ourselves.\"","Her idol replied again, \"We all enjoyed them. The teachers and students are truly fortunate to receive such care from you.\"","Yanshu felt relieved, thinking that at least her boss's mooncakes hadn't gone to waste!","Aww, if only she could tell her idol more, but she couldn't say anything else.","As her words faded, she saw her idol Scholar Qi preparing to take his leave.","However, at that moment, the Empress Dowager suddenly spoke, \"You must be tired from climbing the mountain, Master. Why don't you join us for a cup of tea?\"","Yanshu: \"!!!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","In an instant, another scream burst into his ears, [Ahhhhh boss is awesome!!! Please accept, idol, please accept!!!]","Needless to say, it was from his beloved consort again.","Looking at Qi Shuguang, he was already stunned.","After a moment, he bowed his head and said, \"I dare not disturb Your Excellencies.\"","But the Empress Dowager continued, \"We're not in the palace today, why be so formal? It's just a cup of tea, surely better than walking back to the academy thirsty.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","To prevent more screaming in his ears, he finally spoke up, \"Since my mother has spoken, Master, please don't be modest. Do join us.\"","Well, it was just a cup of tea, what's the big deal."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107","paragraphs":["Since even the emperor had spoken, Qi Shuguang had no choice but to acknowledge with a \"yes\" and take a seat in the pavilion.","However, just when Yuwen Lan thought he could avoid trouble, at the moment Qi Shuguang sat down, he heard Yanshu's mental screams again—","[Ahhhhh my idol sat down! He's sharing a table with the boss! They're drinking tea together!!!]","Yet after the screaming, she suddenly became emotional, crying in her heart, [Waaah they have it so hard! Is this the first time in their lives they're sitting together? It's so heartbreaking...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How could someone think so much?","Tsk, would such dramatic mood swings be healthy?","Fortunately, after all the crying and whimpering, Yanshu finally calmed down. Seeing the maid bring tea for Qi Shuguang, she quickly said, \"Oh right, we brought some snacks today. Let's all try them together.\"","The maids responded and brought out the food boxes, arranging various pastries on the stone table in the pavilion - Double Ninth Festival cakes, chestnut cookies, lotus seed cakes, osmanthus pastries, and more. They all looked quite appealing.","Especially the Double Ninth Festival cake, made from glutinous and non-glutinous rice flour mixed with red beans and preserved fruits, looked white, soft, and sweet - absolutely tempting.","Moreover... ahem, these pastries were from the Palace of Benevolent Peace's kitchen, something that outsiders couldn't buy even with money.","Yanshu said, \"Today is the Double Ninth Festival, we must eat Double Ninth cakes. Everyone please try some.\"","Ahem, mainly she hoped her idol Mr. Qi wouldn't be too polite - such opportunities were rare!","However, after she spoke, she saw the emperor and Empress Dowager pick up the cakes, but Mr. Qi still didn't dare to move.","Yanshu felt somewhat disappointed but couldn't say anything more.","Fortunately, at this moment, her cool boss the Empress Dowager spoke again, \"I made these Double Ninth cakes myself. Won't you do me the honor of trying some, sir?\"","Yanshu: [What!!! These were actually made by the Empress Dowager herself??? Mr. Qi absolutely can't miss this opportunity!!!]","Then, she saw Mr. Qi hesitate again before saying, \"Your Grace is too kind. How could I dare?\"","The Empress Dowager laughed softly under her veiled hat and said, \"Since we're sitting at the same table, it wouldn't look right if we eat while you don't. Please don't be so formal.\"","Yanshu: [Ahhh the boss is so awesome! What she said makes so much sense! Mr. Qi, please don't be so polite anymore!!!]","After these words, she saw her idol Mr. Qi finally respond with a \"yes\" and pick up a piece of Double Ninth cake, joining the other three in eating.","Yanshu finally felt relieved and carefully tasted the Double Ninth cake herself.","Yuwen Lan's ears were finally quiet, and he too could properly taste the pastry.","But before he could swallow, he heard Yanshu flattering the Empress Dowager again, \"This cake is so soft and smooth, sweet but not cloying, with just the right amount of red beans and preserved fruits. Your Grace's culinary skills are amazing!\"","This made the Empress Dowager laugh and say, \"You little girl, always know how to please people!\"","Yanshu shamelessly continued, \"Not at all, I'm speaking from my heart! If you don't believe me, ask the Emperor - isn't this cake especially delicious?\"","Yuwen Lan, who was suddenly put on the spot: \"...\"","Wasn't her own flattery enough? Did she have to drag him into it too?","But since he had been called out, he could only say, \"Indeed, it's very good. Mother's cooking has always been excellent.\"","After speaking, he couldn't help but wonder - the Empress Dowager actually made these Double Ninth cakes herself, could it be for Qi Shuguang?","But thinking again, she didn't know they would meet today, so probably not.","Thinking this, he couldn't help but probe Qi Shuguang's thoughts, and heard him silently sigh, [The cake is delicious, and it's rare for her to make it herself. I suppose it's all for His Majesty? At least now mother and son are close - it wasn't all for nothing, those hardships of the past.]","Yuwen Lan secretly raised an eyebrow.","Well, he had to admit, he had never heard anything improper in this man's thoughts.","Of course, he wasn't the only one who could hear Qi Shuguang's thoughts now. Soon after, Yanshu's mental voice came to his ears, [Waaah idol is always thinking about the Empress Dowager, sympathizing with her... is there another man as good as him in this world???]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Was he not considered a good man?","Why did he always rank behind Qi Shuguang in comparison?","Perhaps due to that inexplicable displeasure in his heart, he asked Qi Shuguang, \"Why did you come to Osmanthus Mountain today, sir?\"","Qi Shuguang hurriedly replied, \"In my hometown, we have the custom of climbing heights during the Double Ninth Festival. I heard Osmanthus Mountain isn't very high, so I thought I'd come take a look.\"","After hearing this, Yuwen Lan didn't detect any other thoughts from him.","However, he heard Yanshu secretly grumbling, [How dare he question my idol like that!!! Do you think he deliberately came to encounter the Empress Dowager?!!! My idol is already in his forties, couldn't it just be that he can't climb high mountains anymore so he had to come to a shorter one? So heartbreaking...]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He was just asking a simple question, was there any need to get so angry...","Right after, he heard the Empress Dowager sigh, [He's not young anymore either, probably like me, his legs aren't what they used to be.]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, indeed, just like the Empress Dowager, Qi Shuguang wasn't young anymore, and he might truly be unable to climb other, higher mountains.","Though unsaid, time had passed quickly. He remembered when Qi Shuguang served in court, he had been in his prime.","Unexpectedly, in the blink of an eye, so many years had passed.","Yuwen Lan didn't say anything more, just picked up another osmanthus pastry and started eating.","After a couple of bites, finding it good, he passed one to Yanshu, saying, \"Try this one, it's fragrant and delicious.\"","Yanshu took it and had a bite, immediately starting to flatter the Empress Dowager again, \"Did Your Grace make this too? It's so crispy and has such a lovely osmanthus fragrance!\"","The Empress Dowager laughed and said, \"Well, you're praising the wrong person there - this one's from the kitchen.\"","But Yanshu, without missing a beat, continued her shameless flattery, \"The kitchen staff were trained by you, weren't they? How could any other place compare?\"","This made the Empress Dowager laugh again.","Even Qi Shuguang couldn't help but show a slight smile.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, so this was how she had won the Empress Dowager's favor.","But seeing the Empress Dowager so happy, today's outing hadn't been in vain after all.","As they chatted and laughed, two cups of tea's worth of time had passed.","There seemed to be fewer visitors climbing the mountain now, and few people were coming into the courtyard.","Just as Yuwen Lan was considering whether it was time to head down the mountain, several people suddenly came into view.","Leading them was what appeared to be a mother and son - the son looked about fifteen or sixteen, while the mother seemed not yet forty. Behind them followed a manservant and a maid.","Strangely, though the mother and son's manner and bearing suggested they weren't from a humble background, their clothes weren't as eye-catching as those of wealthy families.","Moreover, all of them had the air of having traveled a long distance.","Yuwen Lan couldn't help but look at them more closely.","Just then, he heard the young man say, \"Mother, let's rest a while.\"","From his accent, he clearly wasn't from the capital.","After speaking, he looked around, and seeing people in the courtyard, led his mother to sit on a stone stool nearby.","The maid then untied the bundle from her shoulder and took out a water flask, seemingly about to serve the two some water. Surprisingly, after taking out the flask, she also retrieved two bamboo cups from the bundle.","Before pouring the water into the cups, she deliberately poured out a bit first to rinse them, only then formally filling them and serving them to the mother and son.","Such manners...","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow - clearly not an ordinary family.","Of course, with few people in the courtyard at this time, not just him, but everyone else had noticed these people too.","Then he heard the Empress Dowager say, \"That woman... looks somewhat familiar? I seem to have seen her before.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu also took a look, confirming that in all the palace banquets she had attended over the past half year, she hadn't seen this mother and son.","However, indeed, judging by their behavior and manners, they didn't seem to be ordinary people.","Just as she was about to ask the system, she saw the young man look around the courtyard, then suddenly fix his gaze on her idol Mr. Qi. After a pause, he unexpectedly came forward to greet him, saying, \"May I ask if you are Mr. Qi Shuguang?\"","Oh?","Yanshu was startled - this young man actually knew her idol?","As the words fell, she saw her idol, Master Qi, also stand up and reply, \"I am indeed Qi Shuguang. May I ask who you are?\"","The young man suddenly became very excited and said, \"I am Ren Kaiji from the Marquis of Yanping's household. Do you remember me, sir?\"","Marquis of Yanping's household?","At these words, everyone in the hall was stunned for a moment. The maid Hong Yu hurriedly whispered to the Empress Dowager, \"This servant remembers now, that lady seems to be the Marchioness of Yanping.\"","The Empress Dowager glanced at her and nodded, \"I remember now too.\"","Yanshu thought to herself, of course, since the boy had already identified himself as being from the Marquis of Yanping's household, and that was his mother, there was a 95% chance she was the Marchioness of Yanping.","However, judging by the title, the Marquis of Yanping's household was probably in Minyue region. Why had this mother and son traveled all the way to the capital?","Yuwen Lan was also puzzled, and moreover, how did people from the Marquis of Yanping's household know Qi Shuguang?","Then they saw Qi Shuguang finally react, hurriedly saying, \"Oh, it's the young master. What brings you here?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the young man suddenly looked grief-stricken and said, \"It's a long story... Please wait a moment, sir, I need to inform my mother.\"","With that, he returned to his mother's side, and Qi Shuguang hurriedly followed.","Then they saw his mother suddenly stand up as well, speaking very emotionally to Qi Shuguang.","Being some distance away, the people in the pavilion couldn't hear clearly, only glimpsing that the lady seemed quite agitated, as if about to cry.","This only made everyone more curious.","Fortunately, it wasn't long before Qi Shuguang returned to the three of them, reporting, \"Your Graces, this humble one had the fortune of being invited to the Marquis of Yanping's household several years ago while passing through Minyue, to tutor the young master. I just now discovered that the lady and young master of the household have come here.\"","After he finished speaking, the Empress Dowager asked, \"Why did they suddenly come to the capital?\"","Qi Shuguang replied, \"According to them, something terrible happened at home. The Marquis wants to kill his son and wife. With nowhere else to turn, they came to the capital seeking justice from Your Graces.\"","What?","Kill his son and wife?","At these words, everyone was shocked.","Yuwen Lan ordered the guards, \"Watch the courtyard gates for now, don't let any outsiders enter.\"","Then he instructed Qi Shuguang, \"Have the mother and son come forward to speak.\"","Everyone went about their tasks.","Soon, the courtyard gates were secured, and the mother and son from the Marquis's household came forward to the pavilion, kneeling in shock to pay their respects.","\"This humble wife Madam Tao of the Marquis of Yanping's household, along with my son Kaiji, pays respects to Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager, and Consort Yi.\"","She was already crying as she spoke.","Before Yuwen Lan could speak, the Empress Dowager had already said, \"Please rise. Why have you two come all the way to the capital? What exactly happened?\"","The Marchioness of Yanping cried, \"Thank you for your grace, Empress Dowager. This humble wife came uninvited because something terrible happened at home, and my son and I were about to lose our lives! Recently my husband fell ill, and we invited a Taoist priest to exorcise evil spirits. But that priest claimed my son Kaiji was an ill omen, and my husband believed him. At first, he would scold our son daily, and when I tried to stop him, he would scold me too. Later he even tried to burn Kaiji to death. I had no choice but to flee the household with Kaiji. But when I sought help along the way, no one in Yanping dared to intervene. With nowhere else to turn, I could only come to the capital to beg Your Graces to help us!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager immediately frowned, \"Such a thing happened?\"","Everyone's eyes widened, finding it incredibly hard to believe.","How could the Marquis of Yanping kill his own son? And not just any son, but his legitimate heir, the court-appointed young master!","How could the noble lady of a Marquis's household be forced to flee to the capital to file a complaint?","It was too absurd!","Yanshu thought the same, and in her disbelief, she quickly consulted the System, [System, is this true or false?]","The System replied, [What the lady says is not exaggerated at all. The Marquis recently contracted a stubborn illness called \"waist-encircling dragon.\" This illness was quite difficult to treat, and after consulting many famous doctors with no success, they happened to hear of a famous Taoist priest and invited him. The priest took one look and immediately said there were evil spirits in the household. He performed a ritual, and the Marquis's condition improved somewhat.]","[But as soon as the priest left, his illness returned and the pain was worse than before. The Marquis had a favored concubine who took the opportunity to bribe the priest to return. Unexpectedly, this time the priest told the Marquis that the evil spirit in the household was his legitimate son, suggesting that the title of heir should be taken from the legitimate son and given to a concubine's son.]","[Didn't the Marquis start looking at his son with disfavor after that? At first it was beating and scolding, then he thought about burning his son alive. How could a mother tolerate such a thing? So she fled with her son, but unfortunately the Marquis had considerable power in the area at the time, and no one dared to intervene. The mother and son had no choice but to come to the capital. Today happened to be the Double Ninth Festival, and they came to pray at the temple, unexpectedly meeting your idol. Speaking of luck, it's fortunate that Qi Shuguang is so honest and sincere, otherwise others might not have believed this story.]","Her idol was indeed honest and sincere, but Yanshu was still incredulous and said, [Is the Marquis an idiot? How could he believe such nonsense?]","The System replied, [On one hand, he might indeed be somewhat foolish, and on the other hand, the illness was truly unbearable. The Marquis had lived in luxury for so many years, he certainly couldn't endure the pain. It's not surprising that he would become desperate and try anything, especially since the priest's first ritual seemed effective. It would be hard for him not to believe.]","Yanshu thought about it - \"waist-encircling dragon\" seemed to be what later generations would call shingles, which was indeed difficult to treat.","But why did the priest's exorcism work?","The System explained helpfully, [Because this priest actually knew medical arts.]","Yanshu: [??? What, the priest knew medicine? If he was so skilled, why not properly treat people as a doctor instead of putting on these supernatural acts?]","The System enlightened her, [Because pretending to be supernatural could earn much more money!]","Yanshu still didn't understand, [??? What does a monk need so much money for? Don't tell me he wants to build a mansion and secretly enjoy a life of luxury?]","The System said, [Now you're being narrow-minded, this priest's ambitions are far greater! By the way, this priest happens to be an acquaintance of the Empress Dowager.]","Yanshu: [??? The Empress Dowager's acquaintance? Who?]","The System: [The \"Baihe Taoist\" who helped the Old Emperor pursue immortality.]","Yanshu's eyes widened, [What??? The same corrupt priest who put drugs in the Qianming Palace bedchamber and made the emperor impotent?]","The System: [That's right, the very same.]","Hearing this, Yanshu nearly coughed blood, [That charlatan actually fled to Minyue? The emperor's men couldn't find him?]","At that moment, Yuwen Lan beside her also tensed up.","Indeed, from Yanshu's thoughts, he had just learned that the Baihe Taoist was behind this.","Ever since discovering the truth back then, he had been sending people to search for him, but they had never found him. Who would have thought he had gone to Yanping?","Yanshu was still confused, but before she could ask the System, she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"How could the Marquis of Yanping be so foolish? To be manipulated to such an extent by a charlatan?\"","The Marchioness of Yanping nodded through her tears and said, \"I dare not deceive you, this priest has gathered many followers in Minyue in recent years. Some have even built temples to worship him, spreading tales of his supernatural powers.\"","\"What?\"","The Empress Dowager immediately furrowed her brow.","For a moment, she couldn't help but think of that foolish man from years ago.","Yuwen Lan also frowned.","Had the Baihe Taoist already achieved such influence?","Why hadn't his men discovered this?","Yanshu quickly asked the System, [System, what's going on? Isn't the emperor trying to catch this Baihe Taoist? How did he manage to build such a large operation? Didn't the Imperial Guards notice?]","The System replied, [Because after fleeing the palace back then, he changed his name. He now calls himself the Yuanchong Taoist. Few of the Imperial Guards had seen him back then, so of course it was difficult to catch him.]","So he had changed his name.","Yanshu still didn't understand, [What skills does this person have that he could actually gather followers!]","However, the system continued, [This person knows medicine, and his medical skills are quite exceptional. Over the years, he's maintained his youthful appearance despite his gray hair. Those wealthy people with time on their hands are always pursuing immortality, so isn't it easy for them to fall for this? This Yuanchong Taoist has been wandering around the Min-Yue regions these years, amassing enormous wealth. Within a few years, he's taken many disciples and established a sect called the \"White Cloud Sect.\"]","Yanshu still didn't understand, [So what does he want to do with all that wealth? Is it just for the feeling of being worshipped by others?]","The system replied, [No, his true purpose is to support the Red Lotus Cult's rebellion.]","Rebellion?","Yanshu was shocked.","Holy crap, this Red Lotus Cult was no small matter.","This had been a nightmare plaguing various dynasties for hundreds or even thousands of years!","Things were getting way out of hand!","She needed to tell the Emperor right away."]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108","paragraphs":["Fortunately, before Yanshu could speak, Yuwen Lan had already sensed something unusual from Madam Tao's words. He immediately suggested to the Empress Dowager and Yanshu, \"We've been out for quite a while today, perhaps we should return first.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, and Yanshu quickly agreed.","He then instructed the accompanying guards, \"Take Madam Tao and the Marquis of Yanping back to the city and arrange for their accommodation. Order the Left and Right Assistants of the Bureau of Revenue to attend the court later.\"","This indicated his intention to investigate the matter. Upon hearing this, Madam Tao and her son immediately kowtowed to express their gratitude. Yuwen Lan ordered them to rise. Then, he stood up, preparing to leave.","The Empress Dowager and Yanshu also stood up, and everyone in the courtyard immediately bowed their heads in silence, showing their respect.","The closest to the three of them at this moment was Qi Shuguang.","Yanshu paused, realizing that this unexpected meeting between her idol Qi Shuguang and the Empress Dowager was about to end...","At this moment, her idol was standing with his head bowed like everyone else, looking very serious, with no visible emotions on his face.","Yanshu felt a deep sigh in her heart.","Unexpectedly, as the Empress Dowager passed by him, she suddenly stopped and said, \"The weather will get colder from now on, please take care of your health, Master Qi.\"","After all, the next time they met, it was uncertain when.","Yanshu was stunned.","Qi Shuguang paused slightly, still bowing his head and said, \"Yes.\"","Then, in his heart, he silently added, \"You too, take care.\"","Yanshu was stunned again, and in that instant, she couldn't help but feel a tingling in her nose.","Oh, how difficult it was for the two of them...","Yuwen Lan, who heard this, also suddenly felt a heaviness in his heart.","Then, he suddenly ordered the guards, \"Assign two men to escort Master Qi back to the academy.\"","The guards acknowledged.","Qi Shuguang was also taken aback and quickly said, \"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan hummed in acknowledgment and then continued walking down the mountain.","Although she felt a deep sigh for her favorite couple, Yanshu, with the current major matter at hand, deliberately squeezed into the emperor's carriage on the way back and quickly reported on the carriage, \"Your Majesty, I have just received accurate information that the Taoist mentioned by Madam Tao is actually the Baihe Taoist who once deceived the late emperor. After escaping from the palace back then, he changed his name and mingled among the wealthy in the Min Yue Region, using his medical skills to deceive and collect money from those wealthy people. He also established a sect called the White Cloud Sect, which was actually using the money to support the Red Lotus Cult, intending to cause chaos in the country.\"","\"Red Lotus Cult?\"","Upon hearing this, Yuwen Lan immediately frowned, \"It's actually the Red Lotus Cult?\"","Indeed, although he had already learned some truth from Yanshu's thoughts and knew that the Taoist was actually the Baihe Taoist, he had never expected that this person would also be related to the Red Lotus Cult?","It is known that this cult was born in the previous dynasty and has been like a tumor attached to the people for hundreds of years. On the surface, it advocates great virtue and righteousness, but in reality, it gathers people to commit rebellion.","Especially at the end of the previous dynasty, the followers of the Red Lotus Cult had already numbered in the tens of thousands, rising up in various places, directly accelerating the decline of that dynasty.","Later, when the founding emperor led the army to start a rebellion and achieved great success, the Red Lotus Cult attempted to continue the chaos. The founding emperor, learning from the lessons of the previous dynasty, immediately dispatched troops to suppress it, which indeed took a lot of effort. However, in the following decades, there was no news of this evil cult.","Unexpectedly, today, the name was heard again.","And this Baihe Taoist was actually related to the Red Lotus Cult?","Yanshu could understand his surprise and quickly further explained to him, \"This person is actually a remnant of the Red Lotus Cult from back then. Due to the suppression of the founding emperor, he has always harbored resentment towards the court. That's why he disguised himself as a Taoist to harm the late emperor and intended to make you childless. Now, he has turned to causing trouble among the people.\"","Upon hearing this, Yuwen Lan finally nodded and frowned, \"So that's how it is.\"","With this, all the actions of this person in the palace could be explained.","It turned out to be the remnants of the Red Lotus Cult causing trouble. It's a pity that he had once suspected the Empress Dowager...","Thinking of those dark three years, he became even more furious with this person.","At the same time, he angrily said, \"If it weren't for you telling me today, I don't know what kind of trouble this swindler would cause? What are these people doing?\"","Yanshu said, \"Your Majesty, please calm down. After all, from the time this person left the palace to when the truth was discovered that night, several years had passed in between. During this period, he was on the run everywhere, not only changing his name but also knowing medicine. Most of the Imperial Guards had never seen him, and even if they had his portrait, he could change his appearance. With such a vast world, it's understandable that he couldn't be caught in just a few months.\"","\"But the officials in the Min Yue Region have an unshirkable responsibility. After all, this person has been collecting money from the wealthy in recent years. According to Madam Tao's words, it has even formed a certain scale. As the local officials, they couldn't have been unaware of this, right? Maybe even some of them have been brainwashed by this swindler and deliberately helped him cover up.\"","Oh, and, afraid he wouldn't understand, she quickly explained, \"By 'brainwashed,' I mean being deceived by this person and completely believing in him.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"This term... is quite vivid.\"","Thinking about it, he added, \"The possibility of disguise is very high. This time, with Madam Tao and her son here, have the painter draw a few more portraits based on their descriptions.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Your Majesty is wise.\"","Then, she sighed in her heart, \"Little Emperor, Little Emperor, what would you do without me?\"","Yuwen Lan, \"......\"","Although he still didn't want to hear this title, he had to admit that what she said made sense.","So, he couldn't do without her.","When they returned to the palace, the Assistants of the Bureau of Revenue who had been summoned earlier had arrived.","However, since this matter had involved the Red Lotus Cult, the Bureau of Revenue alone was not enough. Yuwen Lan then summoned the Vice Minister of War and several university scholars to court.","Seeing this situation, the Empress Dowager was a bit puzzled. The next day, when Yanshu came to pay her respects, she asked, \"Could it be that the Marquis of Yanping's matter has escalated? Why did the emperor summon the military officials yesterday?\"","Yanshu replied, \"Your Majesty is right. It turns out that after investigation, the Taoist mentioned by Madam Tao seems to be the Baihe Taoist who escaped from the palace back then. Moreover, this person seems to have some connection with the Red Lotus Cult. Given the gravity of the matter, the emperor summoned several ministers, probably to investigate thoroughly!\"","\"What?\"","The Empress Dowager was also shocked and said, \"It's actually that person? And he's also related to the Red Lotus Cult?\"","Yanshu nodded, \"It is said that this person is actually a remnant of the Red Lotus Cult. For many years, he has harbored resentment towards the court and has been retaliating against it through his actions.\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager paused and then sneered, \"How ridiculous, so many people were actually manipulated by a swindler.\"","Especially that man, Yuwen Sheng. His father, the founding emperor, had gone through so much trouble to suppress the Red Lotus Cult, and it was through his hands that it reignited?","Back then, in order to seek immortality, he had given a lot of money to that swindler!","Yanshu listened quietly beside her, thinking that Yuwen Sheng was the late emperor. This guy had invited wolves into his home and even funded the enemy. The Empress Dowager's scolding was indeed justified.","She could only nod and say, \"Your Majesty is right. Fortunately, Madam Tao came at a timely moment this time. The Taoist and the remnants of the Red Lotus Cult had not yet gained momentum. At this time, to eliminate them, it should be relatively easy.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"This person is cunning and deliberately causes trouble in the remote Min Yue Region. He is also good at deceiving people. I hope the emperor can eliminate him once and for all this time and not leave any hidden dangers.\"","Alas, speaking of which, it makes one think of those nightmare-like days back then. I hope such things never happen again in the future.","After bidding farewell to the Empress Dowager, Yanshu returned to Ganlu Palace. In the afternoon, she heard that a new portrait of the Taoist had been drawn.","She curiously went to Qianming Palace to take a look and was surprised to find that compared to the previous portrait obtained by the Imperial Guards, this one was completely different.","According to the memories of the palace servants, the first portrait showed the Taoist to be about sixty years old, with sagging corners of the eyes and mouth, not to mention the wrinkles on his face.","Now three years had passed, and this person should have aged even more. However, according to the description provided by the Marquis of Yanping's wife, the second portrait drawn showed that the person did not have droopy corners around the eyes and mouth, and the wrinkles were not as numerous.","Moreover, as the Marquis of Yanping's wife mentioned, this person now, apart from having white hair, looked no older than forty, exuding an ethereal aura, making them appear even more like an old immortal.","Seeing this, everyone was astonished, initially suspecting that the two portraits had been mixed up.","If not, could it be that this person truly possessed some kind of sorcery that allowed them to reverse aging?","Yanshu naturally did not believe in sorcery. She merely suspected that this old man might have mastered some advanced makeup technique?","How could he reduce his age by over twenty years?","Then she heard the system say, **Makeup is one aspect, but mainly this person is skilled in medicine, combined with some Taoist alchemy, and has concocted some pills for themselves, so they appear to be regressing in age.**","Hmm?","Upon hearing this, Yanshu immediately became interested and asked, **What kind of pills are so miraculous?**","If she could master the formula, wouldn't she also be able to stay young forever?","But the system replied, **Don't think about it. You can't use this medicine. It requires the use of purple river carriages, and one every day. Do you know what a purple river carriage is?**","Yanshu, having been a frequent visitor to the medicine cabinet in her previous life, was familiar with various medicinal names. She responded, **Isn't it the human placenta?**","The system confirmed that was correct.","However, she then widened her eyes in shock, **But as a Taoist, where could he find so many purple river carriages?**","The system explained, **Initially, he bought them from people. He wasn't short of money, and now that he has followers, and they are all wealthy, he doesn't have to worry about it himself. Some people, in order to follow him, even went so far as to abort the pregnancies of their concubines to present them to him.**","Yanshu was almost sick to her stomach upon hearing this, **Is this even human? This is clearly a cult!**","The system agreed, **Exactly!**","Yanshu felt utterly disgusted and shivered all over, especially as a pregnant woman, she was particularly outraged.","So, when no one was around, she immediately told Yuwen Lan, \"Your Majesty, I heard that this person actually uses human placentas to refine pills to maintain a youthful appearance. It's truly heartless and terrifying! This time, we must capture him!\"","Yuwen Lan was also shocked and immediately frowned, saying, \"It's utterly inhumane!\"","Then he ordered Fu Hai, \"Have the painter draw more portraits and distribute them. This time, we must catch him!\"","Fu Hai acknowledged and quickly went to arrange the personnel.","Unexpectedly, not long after, he rushed back to report, \"Your Majesty, just now there was news from the Palace of Benevolent Peace that the Empress Dowager's old ailment has flared up again.\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109","paragraphs":["\"How strange - why did the Empress Dowager suddenly have a relapse of her old illness?\"","After their initial surprise, Yanshu and Yuwen Lan immediately rushed to the Palace of Benevolent Peace to check on her.","When they arrived, they found the Empress Dowager lying in bed with her eyes tightly shut and brows furrowed, appearing to be in great pain.","By her bedside, Zhang Shengkang was taking her pulse. Upon seeing the two arrive, he and the others immediately bowed in greeting.","Seeing this scene, both of them felt their hearts sink.","Yanshu and Yuwen Lan were well aware that Zhang Shengkang was not an honorable man, but unfortunately, the Empress Dowager trusted him completely and always summoned him first whenever she felt unwell.","Of course, he wasn't the main concern right now. Yuwen Lan first commanded everyone to rise, then anxiously asked, \"How is the Empress Dowager?\"","Zhang Shengkang replied, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager is suffering from another attack of her chronic headache.\"","Yanshu was skeptical and said, \"Her Majesty was perfectly fine when I visited this morning. How did she suddenly fall ill?\"","In response, Zhang Shengkang quickly explained, \"Noble Consort Yi may not be aware, but Her Majesty's condition is highly susceptible to weather changes. In the past, her attacks were usually triggered by cold weather in autumn and winter, when external wind pathogens affected her. I heard Her Majesty went hiking yesterday, so it's very likely that the mountain breeze triggered another episode.\"","Yanshu remained doubtful.","Really? Yesterday wasn't even cold, and Osmanthus Mountain wasn't very high with barely any wind. Besides, the Empress Dowager had worn a veiled hat after leaving her carriage - how could the wind have affected her?","...Could Zhang Shengkang have poisoned the Empress Dowager?","But just as she was thinking this, she heard Zhang Shengkang's cold laugh in his mind, [What, you think I would poison the Empress Dowager? Hah, would I be that stupid?]","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, it seemed he wasn't behind this after all.","Meanwhile, Yuwen Lan silently took in everything he heard, his brows slightly furrowed.","Ever since learning of Zhang Shengkang's poor character, he had also suspected the man might be responsible for the Empress Dowager's recurring illness. However, after secretly listening to his thoughts several times, he never found any trace of the man plotting against her.","So it seemed he truly had nothing to do with the Empress Dowager's condition.","At this moment, hearing Zhang Shengkang's explanation, he could only say to the Empress Dowager, \"Mother, how are you feeling now? I was too careless yesterday, causing you to suffer like this.\"","After he spoke, Yanshu also said with guilt, \"It was my idea, so I'm the one to blame.\"","Hearing them speak this way, the Empress Dowager finally managed to open her eyes and sighed, \"Don't blame yourselves. It's my own weakness, don't feel responsible.\"","She then tightly furrowed her brows again and closed her eyes, looking very much in pain.","The sight made both their hearts clench with worry.","Yanshu quickly asked Zhang Shengkang, \"What should we do now? How can we help Her Majesty recover quickly?\"","Zhang Shengkang replied, \"Noble Consort Yi, for now, the Empress Dowager should focus on taking medicine and resting. She must stay indoors these few days and absolutely avoid catching cold or wind.\"","As if afraid she wouldn't believe him, he hurriedly explained further, \"This type of chronic headache is very stubborn. For all these years, whenever the Empress Dowager has an attack, this has been the treatment. There's no permanent cure.\"","Yanshu could only nod.","Indeed, in less than a year, she had personally witnessed the Empress Dowager suffer through three attacks. It truly seemed difficult to cure.","But this was her beloved number one supporter! Seeing such a perfect mentor in such pain made her heart ache terribly...","Just then, she heard Zhang Shengkang think to himself, [If it weren't for my intervention, the Empress Dowager would suffer for even longer each year. Little Emperor, you should know that I'm irreplaceable!]","As Yuwen Lan was about to frown at this, he heard Yanshu's explosive thoughts, [What? This old dog dares to call my man that?! Only I get to call him 'Little Emperor'!!!]","Hmph, what does he mean by 'irreplaceable'?","No, this old scoundrel was getting too arrogant. She had to do something about it! She refused to believe that Doctor Jiang couldn't cure the Empress Dowager.","Yuwen Lan thought the same. Based on past evidence, Jiang Nianqi's medical skills were no less than Zhang Shengkang's. He might well be able to cure the Empress Dowager's chronic condition.","But before he could speak, the smell of medicine wafted over - Dan Shuang, a palace maid from the Palace of Benevolent Peace, had arrived with freshly brewed medicine.","Seeing this, Yanshu quickly said, \"Let me do it.\"","She took the bowl of medicine, sat by the bed, and began helping the Empress Dowager drink it.","As she did so, she couldn't help but feel heartbroken, thinking to herself: This medicine smells so bitter, why must her mentor suffer like this after enduring hardship for most of her life? Please get better soon.","After finishing the bowl of medicine, the Empress Dowager forced her eyes open and said to them, \"It's getting late. Your Majesty should go rest, and Noble Consort Yi is carrying the imperial heir - don't exhaust yourself worrying about me.\"","But Yanshu replied, \"I have nothing urgent to attend to. I can't rest easy seeing you like this, Your Majesty. Let me stay with you a while longer.\"","She then turned to Zhang Shengkang and said, \"Doctor Zhang, you must be tired too. Please go have your meal first.\"","Seeing this, Zhang Shengkang could only bow and withdraw.","With the annoying presence gone from the chamber, Yanshu quickly said to the Empress Dowager, \"I understand you've always trusted Doctor Zhang, but different doctors might have different approaches. Why don't we invite Doctor Jiang to examine you as well?\"","The Empress Dowager sighed and said, \"It's all the same. I know my own illness - there's no good solution.\"","Seeing this, Yuwen Lan quickly added, \"Mother, you've seen Doctor Jiang's medical skills yourself recently. He might be even more capable than Zhang Shengkang. Why not let him try? Your health is what matters most.\"","Hearing him speak thus, the Empress Dowager finally agreed.","Soon after, Doctor Jiang arrived hurriedly upon receiving the summons.","After taking the Empress Dowager's pulse for a while, he reported to the two, \"Your Majesty, Noble Consort Yi, from the pulse, it appears Her Majesty is suffering from spleen deficiency, blood and qi deficiency, liver qi stagnation, and poor blood circulation blocking the channels, causing yang energy to fail to rise and nourish the head.\"","This medical terminology was quite technical - Yanshu couldn't really understand it. Looking at the emperor, she saw him slightly furrowing his brows, seemingly not comprehending either.","The Empress Dowager was already drowsy, so after some thought, Yanshu simply had a palace maid stay to attend to her while she led the emperor and Doctor Jiang to the outer chamber to talk.","With no other people around, she immediately asked Doctor Jiang, \"The Empress Dowager's illness is chronic, flaring up every year and causing her great suffering. In your opinion, can it be completely cured?\"","After she spoke, Yuwen Lan nodded, looking at Doctor Jiang.","Both of them were full of hope, truly wanting to help the Empress Dowager.","However, Doctor Jiang bowed his head and said, \"Your Highness, chronic headaches are indeed difficult to cure completely. Most prescriptions can only provide relief.\"","What?","Both were stunned - could even Doctor Jiang do nothing?","Yanshu refused to accept this and pressed, \"How can that be? You could even cure aconite poisoning! How can you not cure a mere headache?\"","Doctor Jiang showed an ashamed expression and said, \"I am inadequate and have disappointed Your Highness. Usually, external injuries and acute illnesses are relatively easy to treat. The Empress Dowager's condition is an internal illness and a long-standing one at that, which truly is difficult to cure completely.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Was there really no way to help her beloved mentor?","Just as she was about to despair, Doctor Jiang continued, \"When I treated the aconite poisoning last time, it was an emergency with only one option - I had to take the risk to save the person. But while others can risk such treatment, how could we casually risk the Empress Dowager's wellbeing?\"","Risk?","Yanshu paused, thinking that this implied there might be a solution after all?","Yuwen Lan had caught on as well. After some thought, he said, \"If you have any ideas, please speak freely. I know you're very knowledgeable, surely more so than others.\"","Upon hearing these words, Doctor Jiang paused before responding, \"Your Majesty, I do know that there was once a famous physician in the capital named Xun Ji. He authored a book called 'Medical Records Collection,' which documented numerous difficult cases and their treatments. Years ago, I had the fortune to glimpse this book, and I vaguely remember it contained methods for treating stubborn migraines. Unfortunately, I only had a brief look and couldn't study it thoroughly. Now I can only recall a few of the medicines mentioned, not the complete prescription, so I dare not rashly treat the Empress Dowager.\"","As his words fell, both Yuwen Lan and Yanshu froze.","Had Doctor Jiang just mentioned his own father?","Then, they heard him sigh heavily in his heart, [If only I hadn't been so playful back then, if only I had been more obedient, I wouldn't have wasted my father's life's work...]","Yanshu, listening quietly, thought to herself that this 'Medical Records Collection' must be the secret manual that Zhang Shengkang had stolen.","Suddenly, the system chimed in, [That's right, it's that secret manual.]","Yanshu drew in a sharp breath, [So you're saying Zhang Shengkang has this manual and could cure the Empress Dowager's condition, but deliberately won't?]","The system replied matter-of-factly, [Well, if he cured the Empress Dowager right away, how else would he maintain her favor?]","Yanshu couldn't help but curse Zhang Shengkang as a scoundrel three times!!!","Damn, this dog of a man was truly despicable!!! To treat her number one supporter this way! He had absolutely no conscience!!!","Hearing her curses, Yuwen Lan felt equally angry.","This Zhang Shengkang was just like how he had been with him - knowing the cure but refusing to treat, only seeking merit and favor. Truly detestable!!!","Such a petty man would always be petty, not worthy of any trust.","Of course, after the initial anger subsided, he understood that the most pressing matter now was how to obtain this 'Medical Records Collection.'","Just then, Yanshu asked Doctor Jiang, \"So if we could find this 'Medical Records Collection,' you would be able to treat the Empress Dowager?\"","Doctor Jiang replied, \"I would be ninety percent confident.\"","Ninety percent?","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. Knowing that physicians rarely made empty promises, Doctor Jiang's confidence was very promising.","At this moment, Yuwen Lan asked Doctor Jiang, \"Does the doctor know how we might find this book?\"","Yanshu was startled, thinking to herself, hadn't he remembered that the book was with Zhang Shengkang?","Before she could react, Doctor Jiang spoke, \"I heard that Master Xun was falsely accused by evil people and died with grievances. The fate of the book remains unknown...\"","Just as he was speaking, she heard him sigh in his heart, [Never mind, saving people is what matters.]","Yanshu was startled again—","From his tone, it seemed Doctor Jiang was about to reveal the matter between Xun Ji and Zhang Shengkang?","But wouldn't he fear exposing his own identity change?","This could be considered deceiving the emperor!","No, although his intentions were pure, she couldn't let his entire family be put in danger.","So she quickly exclaimed, \"I've heard about this too! That Doctor Xun was extremely skilled, able to treat all sorts of difficult conditions. I heard Zhang Shengkang was his disciple.\"","Upon hearing this, Doctor Jiang was dumbfounded, \"...How does Your Highness know this???\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","However, Yanshu didn't answer and continued, \"It seems Doctor Xun's death was related to Zhang Shengkang. Ah, perhaps that book is in Zhang Shengkang's possession right now!\"","Doctor Jiang was stunned again, \"This... this... how did Your Highness hear about...\"","Before he could finish, Yanshu waved her hand dismissively, \"Never mind about that, let His Majesty and I handle this. You just go prepare yourself, and once we find the book, you can properly treat the Empress Dowager.\"","Doctor Jiang: \"???\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Unable to bear seeing Jiang Nianqi's confused expression any longer, he had to say, \"Do as Consort Yi says and wait. Don't ask about the rest.\"","Hearing this, Doctor Jiang finally responded with a \"yes,\" bowed to them both, and took his leave.","Yuwen Lan cleared his throat, about to say something, when Yanshu urgently told him, \"Your Majesty, see how awful Zhang Shengkang is! He has the means to cure the Empress Dowager but won't do it. He's a disgrace to physicians and betrays the Empress Dowager's trust!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, trying to speak, but she continued, \"However, the Empress Dowager trusts him so much. If we move against him now, firstly, we might shock the Empress Dowager, who can't handle any sudden events right now, and secondly, we might alert him and he could destroy the manual. So for now, getting the manual and treating the Empress Dowager is most important.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded again, but before he could speak, she added, \"I've figured it out - the 'Medical Records Collection' is in Zhang Shengkang's study, on the third shelf of the north wall bookcase, second slot from the left. Tonight, Your Majesty should send the Imperial Guard to steal— no, to retrieve what rightfully belongs to others.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...Alright.\"","With his beloved consort around, was there anything in this world that couldn't be accomplished?","Also, he probably wouldn't need to speak at all in the future."]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110","paragraphs":["Given the Empress Dowager's illness, Yuwen Lan couldn't afford any negligence and sent someone to the Zhang residence that very night.","Well, since they had the exact location down to the specific shelf, and with Zhang Shengkang required to stay on duty in the palace due to the Empress Dowager's condition, no one was entering or leaving the Zhang family study. The Imperial Guards obtained the \"Medical Records Collection\" with almost no effort.","So early the next morning, when Doctor Jiang arrived at the palace for his shift, he immediately saw his father's life's work.","While excitement and sighs were inevitable, the urgent matter at hand was treating the Empress Dowager. After reviewing his father's records, Doctor Jiang immediately devised a treatment plan and began the therapy.","Yanshu was already waiting in the Palace of Benevolent Peace, and Yuwen Lan rushed there immediately after the morning court session, anxiously asking Doctor Jiang, who was examining the Empress Dowager, \"How is she? When will the Empress Dowager recover?\"","Doctor Jiang replied with a serious expression, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager's chronic headache is an old ailment. The current treatment should focus on soothing the liver, relieving depression, nourishing the kidneys, replenishing qi and blood, and alleviating pain. All of these require a gradual approach. For now, I propose a course of treatment lasting half a month, repeated for three courses, which should eliminate the root cause of the Empress Dowager's illness.\"","Three courses?","Yuwen Lan frowned and asked, \"So it will take at least a month and a half for the Empress Dowager to fully recover?\"","Doctor Jiang bowed in confirmation.","Seeing this, Yanshu quickly consoled, \"Your Majesty, please don't worry. Having a solution is better than having none at all. Besides, the Empress Dowager has been suffering from this illness for many years. If we can completely eliminate the problem in just a month and a half, that's quite good.\"","That made sense. Yuwen Lan nodded, then watched as Doctor Jiang took out a pack of silver needles and inserted them one by one into the acupuncture points on the Empress Dowager's head.","The scene made him pause, and Yanshu watched with trepidation - heavens, so many needles in the head must be incredibly painful!","Yet looking at the Empress Dowager, she showed no reaction.","This revealed that the headache attacks must be even more unbearable than the needle insertions.","Yanshu was nearly moved to tears with sympathy.","Yuwen Lan understood this too, and with a heavy heart, he asked Doctor Jiang, \"Besides medicine and acupuncture, what else should we be mindful of?\"","Doctor Jiang promptly replied, \"Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager's illness has both external and internal causes. Externally, she must stay warm and avoid catching cold. Internally, we must keep Her Highness in good spirits and relieve her liver stagnation.\"","The explanation was quite straightforward. Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but sigh inwardly—","[After all, isn't the Empress Dowager's current state all because of the late Emperor? Like the Empress Dowager, having an unfaithful husband, losing her child early, and spending years of effort to support her adopted son to the throne? To make matters worse, her family members were troublesome, causing one problem after another, and she couldn't even be with the person she came to know and care for... How could any woman not become depressed and ill under such circumstances? Oh, the Empress Dowager has had such a difficult life!]","Yuwen Lan silently took in these words, and after a pause, he said to the Empress Dowager lying in bed, \"Mother, you have endured much hardship over these years.\"","Yanshu had a point.","Indeed, the palace had never given the Empress Dowager many days of peace and happiness.","As his words fell, the Empress Dowager slowly opened her eyes and said weakly, \"This is a busy time. Your Majesty need not worry too much about me. Please go back.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu quickly added, \"I will stay to keep the Empress Dowager company. Your Majesty should return.\"","Indeed, it was morning, and surely a pile of important matters awaited him in the study. Yuwen Lan could only nod in agreement, bid farewell to the Empress Dowager, and return to Qianming Palace.","Doctor Jiang remained to continue treating the Empress Dowager, with Yanshu staying by her side.","After the acupuncture was complete and she had personally helped the Empress Dowager take her medicine, Yanshu waited until the Empress Dowager fell asleep before going to rest herself.","It must be said that Doctor Jiang's methods were indeed much more effective than Zhang Shengkang's. After two or three days of treatment, the Empress Dowager's symptoms had already lessened. She was no longer constantly dizzy and suffering from severe headaches, and when she felt better, she could even chat with Yanshu.","It was now mid-September, and the weather was growing increasingly cold. Although it was warm inside the palace, one could see through the windows that the trees in the courtyard had already lost all their leaves.","The Empress Dowager was still concerned about palace affairs. As her pain slightly improved, she couldn't help but worry again, asking Yanshu, \"Has the Needlework Bureau finished making all the winter clothes for the palace?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"The winter clothes have all been distributed, Your Highness need not worry.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and sighed, \"You've become more and more capable now, but with a child in your belly, you shouldn't work too hard.\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"I'm fine, please don't worry, Your Highness.\"","She then asked, \"It's almost noon, would you like something to eat?\"","The Empress Dowager shook her head and sighed, \"These days of taking medicine have left such a bitter taste in my mouth, I don't want to eat anything.\"","This troubled Yanshu - one needs food to maintain strength, how could the Empress Dowager recover if she wouldn't eat?","Just then, a palace servant announced from outside, \"Your Highness, Eunuch Fu Hai has arrived.\"","Since Fu Hai must have come on the Emperor's orders, the Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"Let him in.\"","The person outside acknowledged, and soon Fu Hai entered the hall carrying a food box. He bowed to both women and said, \"His Majesty has sent some persimmon cakes for the Empress Dowager.\"","Oh?","Yanshu was startled - the Empress Dowager had just mentioned the bitter taste in her mouth, and now the Emperor's persimmon cakes arrived. Could this be the connection between mother and son?","The Empress Dowager also seemed surprised, letting out an \"Oh\" before asking, \"What made His Majesty think to send these to me?\"","Fu Hai explained, \"His Majesty had just inquired about Your Highness's condition from Doctor Jiang and learned that your appetite hasn't been good these past few days. As it happened, Headmaster Qi from Songhe Academy had just sent some persimmon cakes to the palace. His Majesty, knowing Your Highness's fondness for them, asked me to bring them to you.\"","He added, \"His Majesty specifically checked with Doctor Jiang, and it's fine for Your Highness to have a few.\"","Upon hearing this, both the Empress Dowager and Yanshu were stunned.","Especially Yanshu, who could barely maintain her composure—","Did Fu Hai just say these persimmon cakes were from Headmaster Qi??? Why would Headmaster Qi suddenly send persimmon cakes to the palace?! Could it be for the Empress Dowager?!","At this crucial moment, the system chimed in to explain, [That's right, word has spread outside about the Empress Dowager's illness these past few days, and naturally, Headmaster Qi was even more worried. Unfortunately, being outside the palace meant limited access to information. After much hesitation, he finally gathered the courage to send in the persimmon cakes he made himself. Of course, he didn't dare say they were for the Empress Dowager, only that they were produced at Songhe Academy and sent to His Majesty as a token of gratitude for his care.]","Yanshu was extremely excited and quickly asked, [Then, then, then, how did the Emperor think to send them to the Empress Dowager?]","The system replied, [Because the Empress Dowager truly loves persimmon cakes! They've been mother and son for over twenty years, how could he not know this?]","Yanshu remained very excited, [So Scholar Qi also knew the Empress Dowager likes persimmon cakes? He even learned to make them himself? After waiting for so many years, he can finally let the Empress Dowager taste them?]","She had already imagined Scholar Qi's intense internal struggle between reason and emotion before finally being unable to resist his concern for the Empress Dowager, gathering his courage to personally send the persimmon cakes to the palace!","Though not a word was spoken, these persimmon cakes carried his feelings!","Looking at the Empress Dowager, she too was full of surprise, thinking to herself, [Could he have... deliberately sent these for me?]","Hearing this in her mind, Yanshu wanted so badly to nod and tell the Empress Dowager—","Your Highness, please don't doubt it, Scholar Qi truly did this all for you!!! He really cares about you deeply!!!","Oh, this is pure love moving in both directions!!!","Of course, while she couldn't say these words aloud, she could do other things.","So she quickly responded, \"His Majesty's persimmon cakes have arrived at just the right time. Your Highness was just saying your mouth felt bitter. These persimmon cakes will help with that.\"","As she spoke, she took the initiative to accept the food box, took out the persimmon cakes, and had the palace maid Dan Shuang cut them into small pieces before presenting them to the Empress Dowager.","Seeing this, the Empress Dowager indeed took a few pieces to taste.","Mmm, it was the natural sweetness of persimmons, and as she slowly chewed, she seemed to see his face in her mind.","These persimmon cakes, she suspected, were specially sent by him for her.","Given his personality, he wasn't one to actively try to please others.","With these thoughts, the sweet taste in her mouth gradually spread to her heart, seemingly making the medicinal smell in the room less noticeable.","Yanshu quietly observed from the side. Seeing the brightness returning to the Empress Dowager's eyes, she was delighted and quickly suggested, \"While you're enjoying the sweetness of the persimmon cakes, perhaps Your Highness would like to eat something? We could have the kitchen prepare some porridge and a few small dishes?\"","The Empress Dowager nodded with a smile, \"Now that you mention it, I am feeling rather hungry. Very well, have them bring the food.\"","Yanshu acknowledged and quickly sent Dan Shuang to relay the order.","Before long, when lunch arrived, the Empress Dowager indeed finished a bowl of porridge and two side dishes.","She then drank all of her medicine in one go, clearly showing her improved spirits.","Seeing this, Yanshu felt relieved.","With her idol's encouragement, her number one fan would surely recover quickly.","Yuwen Lan had been constantly worried about the Empress Dowager, but unfortunately, his official duties kept him busy. When he returned to Ganlu Palace in the evening, he asked Yanshu, \"How was the Empress Dowager today?\"","Yanshu quickly replied, \"Your Majesty need not worry. The Empress Dowager was much better today. She particularly brightened up after eating the persimmon cakes you had Fu Hai deliver, and she ate well during both lunch and dinner.\"","In her heart, she thought gleefully, [You really know what you're doing! You even knew to send Headmaster Qi's persimmon cakes to the Empress Dowager. Not bad, not bad, you're learning well!]","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, since Doctor Jiang said the Empress Dowager needed to maintain good spirits, he would have to do his best to ensure that.","After this thought, Yanshu said to him, \"Your Majesty, I was thinking today, now that the Empress Dowager's condition is improving, perhaps we could try telling her about Zhang Shengkang's past deeds. Didn't I write a story before about how Zhang Shengkang betrayed his teachers and ancestors and showed no gratitude? We could read it to the Empress Dowager, laying the groundwork for her to learn about his past misdeeds. Then in a few days when she's recovered, we can reveal the truth about the Medical Records Collection, and she'll fully understand Zhang Shengkang's true nature.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"That would work.\"","Speaking of which, these past few days, seeing that the Empress Dowager was being treated by Doctor Jiang, Zhang Shengkang must be getting quite anxious, and might try something despicable again.","But it didn't matter, as he had already ordered his secret guards to follow the man. If he attempted any wrongdoing, he would be caught immediately.","Still, Yanshu's arrangement was quite good. Preparing the Empress Dowager mentally first would help avoid too much shock and disappointment when they eventually dealt with Zhang Shengkang.","After all, someone who was ill shouldn't receive too much of a shock.","As these words fell, Yanshu acknowledged with a \"yes\" and hurriedly went to search through the bookshelf.","He asked curiously, \"What are you doing?\"","It was already late; surely she wasn't planning to write stories now?","Yanshu replied, \"I'm not sure where I put the manuscript about Zhang Shengkang. I want to find it so I can read it to the Empress Dowager tomorrow.\"","Yuwen Lan pulled her away, saying, \"It's already very late. You can look for it tomorrow. You've spent all day at the Palace of Benevolent Peace, you should rest now.\"","As if on cue, Yanshu yawned, finally realizing how tired she was. She agreed and followed him to bed to rest.","The next day, Yuwen Lan woke up early as usual, preparing to attend the morning court session at Qianming Palace.","His movement woke Yanshu, who lazily sat up and pushed aside the bed curtains to ask, \"Is Your Majesty leaving?\"","As she spoke, she yawned again, her eyes not fully open yet.","Yuwen Lan felt both amused and tender, leaning down to kiss her forehead, saying, \"No need to get up. It's cold outside, sleep a while longer.\"","Yanshu, spoiled by his affection, made a soft sound and was about to lie back down.","However, at that moment, Fu Hai announced from outside, \"Your Majesty, the Imperial Guard has something to report.\"","Yuwen Lan made an acknowledging sound and put on his outer robe to go to the outer chamber, asking, \"What is it?\"","Meanwhile, Yanshu, still lounging in bed, wondered what scandal the Imperial Guard had uncovered to report so early.","Could they have caught the Baihe Taoist?","No, that couldn't be right. Given the timing, the people sent out would have barely reached the Min Yue Region by now, let alone caught anyone and returned...","So who could it be?","Well, driven by curiosity, she found herself no longer sleepy, so she got up, put on her outer robe, and crept to the door to listen.","She heard the Imperial Guard report from outside, \"Your Majesty, last night when we infiltrated the Zhang residence, we discovered that after Zhang Shengkang returned home from his duties, he was intimate with a woman, who then shortly after went to his son's chamber and remained intimate with him until late into the night...\"","Yanshu: \"???\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111","paragraphs":["The sudden juicy gossip early in the morning instantly drove away all sleepiness.","Yanshu was afraid she hadn't heard clearly, so she first organized her thoughts—","The Imperial Guard said that the old scoundrel Zhang Shengkang had an affair with a woman last night, and afterward, that same woman went to his son's room to have an affair with the son?","...In other words, both Zhang Shengkang and his son had affairs with the same woman last night?","Suddenly, the system's voice popped up in her mind, [That's right.]","Yanshu: [??? What do you mean 'that's right'? I must say, I've noticed you've gotten increasingly lazy lately. Why didn't you tell me about such exciting gossip earlier???]","System: [How could telling you earlier be as thrilling as letting you know now? Gossip is best served fresh, isn't it?]","Yanshu: [...Well, you've got quite a theory there. Stop the nonsense and tell me quickly what's going on with that old scoundrel and his son? Is that woman Zhang Shengkang's concubine?]","As soon as she said this, she realized something wasn't right, [I haven't heard that the old scoundrel had any concubines. Oh right, his son just got married recently. Holy cow, could it be that this old man is having an affair with his daughter-in-law?]","But the system replied, [No, that's not it. Zhang's new daughter-in-law is the daughter of Pei Xiangzhi, the Deputy Director of the Court of Imperial Entertainments. Miss Pei comes from a scholarly family; how could she do such a thing?]","Hearing this, Yanshu became even more confused, [Then what's really going on?]","However, the system first brought up something else, asking her, [Remember that despicable thing Zhang Shengkang did last time, when he tried to frame Doctor Jiang by having someone switch the medicine he prescribed for the neighbor's child?]","Yanshu immediately nodded, [Of course I remember!]","Damn, just thinking about it still makes her blood boil!","That scoundrel Zhang, in order to frame Doctor Jiang, actually risked a child's life! Unfortunately, one of Zhang's disciples ended up taking the blame, and that old scoundrel put on a show of admitting his fault before the Empress Dowager. The Empress Dowager, being deceived, even spoke up for him, and in the end, he only got demoted and had his salary reduced.","But what did this have to do with the current gossip?","The system explained, [The woman who had affairs with both Zhang father and son is actually the wife of that disciple who took the blame for Zhang Shengkang. Back then, Zhang Shengkang used two hundred taels of silver and promised to take care of this man's wife and children as conditions to make him take the blame.]","Yanshu: [...Well, well, so that's how he's 'taking care' of her in bed? But wait, since she's his disciple's wife, how did she end up in his mansion?]","The system continued, [Actually, this Lady Cui is quite crafty herself. After her family's misfortune, thinking about her husband being sentenced to ten years of hard labor, not even sure if he would survive, and how Zhang Shengkang's silver was all sent to her husband's parents, Lady Cui was definitely unhappy and wanted to plan for herself. She knew Zhang Shengkang was wealthy, and his household didn't have any concubines, plus his wife was getting old. So she tried to seduce him, and it turned out this Zhang Shengkang was an old lecher. They hit it off immediately and started their affair.]","[Meeting outside was inconvenient, and Zhang Shengkang was particularly lustful at first, so he used his son's wedding as an excuse, claiming they needed more help managing the household, and brought Lady Cui into the mansion. This way, they could carry on their affair freely, and even now, three months after his son's marriage, he still hasn't sent her away.]","So that's how it was.","Yanshu quickly asked, [Then how did Lady Cui end up having an affair with Zhang's son too?]","The system explained, [Well, shortly after Lady Cui entered the Zhang household, Zhang Shengkang's wife, Madam Xu, discovered their affair. But Madam Xu was weak-willed and didn't dare to openly defy her husband. However, she couldn't let it go, so she secretly made things difficult for Lady Cui, trying to drive her away both openly and subtly. Lady Cui wasn't easy to bully either, and she happened to discover that Zhang's son was also a lecher who had tried to take advantage of her several times. So she simply went all in and seduced the son too, occasionally having affairs with him.]","[Speaking of last night, it was quite a coincidence. Originally, Lady Cui had made plans with Zhang Shengkang's son, but Zhang Shengkang had been on duty at the palace for several days and was extremely eager. As soon as he returned home, he sought out Lady Cui. She had no choice but to deal with the old scoundrel first before keeping her appointment with his son.]","Yanshu: [...]","This family was so chaotic that she didn't know what to say.","[But wait, isn't the son newly married? During what should be his honeymoon period, he's actually fooling around with Lady Cui?]","System: [This young lecher did behave himself for a few days right after getting married, but he couldn't resist for long since his new wife is a proper lady and not as experienced as Lady Cui in bedroom matters. So it didn't take long before he started fooling around with Lady Cui again.]","Yanshu couldn't help but feel sorry for the new wife, and asked, [Isn't this young lecher afraid his wife will find out? Also, with Lady Cui carrying on with both father and son, is Madam Xu still too afraid to do anything about it? And hasn't the new daughter-in-law noticed anything?]","The system sighed and said, [The daughter-in-law is still new to the household and isn't very familiar with everything yet, so she hasn't discovered the affairs between the scoundrel father and son with Lady Cui. Her mother-in-law, Madam Xu, knows everything clearly and has fallen ill from anger.]","Yanshu: [...She's sick but still doesn't dare to do anything? Can't really blame others then.]","Tch, what a pity for Zhang's new daughter-in-law. How did such a proper young lady from a good family end up married into this household!","The system continued, [Actually, this marriage was arranged through Zhang Shengkang's connection with the Empress Dowager. Miss Pei was both beautiful and virtuous, and there were many suitors from even more prestigious families in the capital. Pei Xiangzhi only agreed to the marriage because Zhang Shengkang had the Empress Dowager's trust and their families were of similar status. He just hoped his daughter wouldn't suffer any grievances.]","Yanshu: [...It seems Pei Xiangzhi really loves his daughter. If he ever learns the truth, won't he be furious?]","System: [Indeed. That's why the mother-in-law would rather make herself sick with worry than speak up.]","Yanshu: [Hmph, if she doesn't dare to speak up, then let others do it for her.]","Alright, now that she understood the gossip clearly, it was time to plan carefully.","Originally, she thought Zhang Shengkang was just a person of poor character, but this unexpected development made things even more interesting!","Meanwhile, in the outer hall, Yuwen Lan was still in a state of disbelief about what he had heard.","Did he hear wrong?","Did the Imperial Guard just say that Zhang Shengkang and his son both had affairs with the same woman?","How did the Zhang household become so chaotic???","Just then, Yanshu's voice came from the inner chamber, \"Your Majesty, I have something to report...\"","Yuwen Lan came back to his senses, first dismissed the Imperial Guard with a wave of his hand, and returned to the inner chamber.","Before he could steady himself, Yanshu, with gleaming eyes, fed him all the gossip about the Zhang family.","\"Your Majesty, I've figured it all out. The woman who had affairs with both Zhang father and son is actually the wife of that disciple who previously took the blame for Zhang Shengkang. Zhang Shengkang's wife knows about this but doesn't dare to intervene, and has already fallen ill from anger. Their newly wedded daughter-in-law is still in the dark about all this. We can use this to help this innocent young woman escape from her misery early.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","How did she not only figure out the truth but also come up with a solution in such a short time?","Well, his beloved consort's ideas had always been reliable when dealing with such matters, so he asked, \"What do you propose we do?\"","She then stood on her tiptoes and whispered in his ear for a while.","After listening and thinking it over, Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Handling it this way would indeed be more natural. Very well, I'll have them proceed with it right away.\"","Then he glanced at her and asked, \"It's still early, don't you want to sleep a bit more?\"","After all, with the Imperial Guard watching the Zhang family, all she needed to do was sit back and watch the show unfold.","However, she shook her head and started putting on her clothes layer by layer, saying excitedly, \"With such an interesting event, how could I possibly sleep? I'm going to write a novel while it's still early in the day.\"","Hehe, with a novel, the readers would be happy, and her biggest fan might also be energized when hearing about it. This way, the illness might recover faster!","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't be sure about the Empress Dowager's spirits, but she was certainly in high spirits right now.","Palace of Benevolent Peace.","As another three days passed, the first treatment was more than halfway through, and the Empress Dowager's condition had indeed improved significantly.","Not only did her headaches occur less frequently, but her appetite had also recovered considerably, and she could even walk around her bedchamber.","Yanshu still visited daily to check on her, and seeing this progress, she felt more at ease.","Hmm, Doctor Jiang is indeed irreplaceable.","In the afternoon, with nothing else to do, the Empress Dowager had rested well and was in good spirits. Yanshu personally served her the medicine and was chatting with her when suddenly, a herald's voice rang out from outside the hall, \"His Majesty the Emperor has arrived...\"","Everyone in the hall quickly bowed, and soon, the tall figure of the Emperor entered the hall.","The Empress Dowager was puzzled, \"Why has the Emperor come here recently?\"","Yuwen Lan sat down beside her and said, \"I was busy this morning, so I came to see how you are doing.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"I'm much better now, and with Yanshu's company, the Emperor doesn't need to worry too much.\"","Yanshu knew the Emperor's intentions and seized the opportunity to say, \"The Empress Dowager is recovering much faster than before, which shows that Doctor Jiang's methods are effective.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded and sighed, \"Indeed, the younger generation is truly impressive. I didn't expect Doctor Jiang, despite his young age, to surpass Zhang Shengkang in medical skills.\"","At this point, Yuwen Lan took the opportunity to say, \"Speaking of which, I have something to report to you, Mother.\"","The Empress Dowager responded with an \"Oh,\" and asked, \"What is it?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"This morning, Pei Xiangzhi, the Assistant Minister of the Court of Imperial Entertainments, came to the palace to accuse Zhang Shengkang and his son of incest.\"","Incest?","The Empress Dowager was genuinely shocked by this revelation and frowned, \"What? Zhang Shengkang and his son... incest? Is this true or false? With whom did they commit such acts?\"","Yanshu, \"...\"","As a modern person with limited reading, she was momentarily stunned when she heard the Emperor's words. Only now did she realize that the term \"incest\" likely referred to the father and son engaging in illicit relations with the same woman.","Tsk, the Chinese language is indeed profound!","Shame on me, shame on me.","However, the Empress Dowager, still frowning, said, \"How absurd! How could these two commit such a disgraceful act? Didn't his son just marry? What does the mother-in-law say? And since the woman is the wife of a disciple, why did she end up in the master's house?\"","Yuwen Lan continued, \"Zhang Shengkang's wife is currently ill and not managing affairs. As you said, Miss Pei, who is newly married, felt wronged and had no one to turn to, so she returned to her parents' home last night to report the matter. Pei Xiangzhi came to the palace this morning to inform me immediately.\"","\"As for the woman, it is said that she has been involved with Zhang Shengkang for a long time. To facilitate their affair, Zhang Shengkang took advantage of the recent shortage of manpower due to his son's wedding and brought the woman into the house under the pretext of helping. By the way, the woman's husband is the one who attempted to frame Doctor Jiang earlier this year. Zhang Shengkang had personally come to apologize to you and me at the time. Do you remember?\"","The Empress Dowager thought for a moment and immediately nodded, \"I remember. It's the one who switched the medicine because his pharmacy's business was affected.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Exactly.\"","The Empress Dowager thought further and said, \"Since Pei Xiangzhi has reported this to the Emperor, it must be known outside. The Emperor must handle this matter, investigate the Zhang family thoroughly, and ensure that no innocent person is wronged and no immoral person is let off.\"","The more she thought about it, the angrier she became. How could these two commit such a disgraceful act!","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"I have already ordered an investigation. Additionally, I suspect that the disciple's previous offense may have hidden motives. I have also ordered a review of the case in prison.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Good. How could this man get involved with his disciple's wife? It must be thoroughly investigated.\"","Just as she finished speaking, Fu Hai rushed in to report, \"Your Majesty, there is a new development in the prison case.\"","Yuwen Lan responded with an \"Oh\" and asked, \"What is it?\"","Fu Hai reported, \"The disciple in prison has confessed that he took the blame for Zhang Shengkang. It was actually Zhang Shengkang who ordered the switch of the medicine prescribed by Doctor Jiang. According to his confession, Zhang Shengkang, seeing Doctor Jiang's exceptional medical skills and the Emperor's trust, feared losing his position and devised this scheme to frame and slander.\"","What?","Before Yuwen Lan and Yanshu could react, the Empress Dowager angrily exclaimed, \"What a scoundrel! It was him!\"","It was infuriating that she had defended him at the time, and Zhang Shengkang had dared to exploit her trust so shamelessly!","Yuwen Lan quickly followed up, \"Indeed, a scoundrel! Not only did he find someone to take the blame and deceive us, but he also engaged in incest with his disciple's wife. His lack of personal integrity is evident, showing his despicable character! Guards, immediately arrest Zhang Shengkang!\"","Fu Hai immediately acknowledged and hurried out to instruct the guards.","In the hall, Yanshu quickly said, \"Your Majesty is wise!\"","She then secretly winked at Yuwen Lan.","Hehe, isn't this all going smoothly now!","Am I not amazing?","Yuwen Lan, [...Amazing!]","No one is as amazing as my beloved concubine!"]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112","paragraphs":["As Yanshu had predicted, by starting with the outrageous actions of Zhang Shengkang and his son, gradually revealing this man's true nature, the Empress Dowager found it much easier to accept. When the Emperor issued the order to arrest him, the Empress Dowager showed little emotional disturbance.","However, Zhang Shengkang's imprisoned apprentice, upon seeing his wife dishonored, became extremely angry. After confessing the truth about the switched medicines, he continued to reveal many unknown facts about Zhang Shengkang. He disclosed how Zhang had used his position as an imperial physician to collect disciples and amass wealth by opening pharmacies throughout the capital, colluding with medicine merchants to inflate prices, driving out other medical establishments in an attempt to monopolize the capital's medical industry. He also revealed how Zhang's pharmacies used inferior medicines while charging exorbitant fees, showing complete disregard for the lives of poor patients.","Since this was a case personally assigned by the Emperor, the Ministry of Justice didn't dare to be negligent. Upon receiving these reports, they immediately continued their investigation, uncovering more and more evidence.","Within just a few days, news about the Zhang family spread throughout the capital. Officials and commoners alike had heard about Zhang Shengkang's misdeeds, and it became the talk of the town.","Yanshu wasn't idle either. She seized this opportunity to visit the Palace of Benevolent Peace to share the biggest scandal about Zhang Shengkang with the Empress Dowager.","When she arrived, the Empress Dowager had just finished her acupuncture treatment, with Doctor Jiang carefully removing silver needles from her head and placing them back in his needle case.","Yanshu thought the timing was perfect and said to the Empress Dowager, who was lying on her couch, \"Your Highness, I heard that the Carefree Scholar has written a new story. I've just finished reading it. Would you like me to share it with you?\"","The Empress Dowager, who was feeling bored, immediately replied, \"Of course! Tell me quickly, what kind of story is it this time?\"","Yanshu sat down beside the couch and, while watching Doctor Jiang collect his needles, began, \"Coincidentally, this time the Carefree Scholar wrote about a physician. It tells of a doctor in the capital who was renowned for his exceptional medical skills. He could treat all sorts of difficult illnesses and saved countless lives, earning him the title of Divine Physician among the common people. This Divine Physician had a son and an apprentice. The son was younger but clever, though somewhat playful; in contrast, the older apprentice appeared more steady and hardworking.\"","At this point, Yanshu deliberately paused and glanced over to see Doctor Jiang's hands noticeably hesitate while collecting his needles.","In his heart, he thought, \"Could this... be about my father?\"","Seeing that he had caught on, Yanshu continued, \"This Divine Physician was broad-minded and never discriminated between his apprentice and son. In fact, he taught everything he knew to his studious apprentice, without any reservation, hoping that after completing his studies, the apprentice would follow in his footsteps to heal and save people.\"","Hearing this, the Empress Dowager nodded, \"Indeed, he was a good doctor and a good master.\"","Looking at Doctor Jiang, though he didn't pause again, he reflected in his heart that yes, his father was exactly such a person, who had placed complete trust in Zhang Shengkang. If only...","Just then, Yanshu's voice continued, \"Unfortunately, this old doctor had misjudged his apprentice. This apprentice was actually someone who coveted power and position, and because the young disciple was more talented than himself, he harbored jealousy, believing that his master was withholding knowledge from him.\"","\"After completing his apprenticeship, this person became a physician for a noble family and quickly gained the family head's favor using the skills his master had taught him. However, since his master's abilities were still superior to his own, he feared his master would threaten his position. He devised a sinister plan, secretly switching the medicine his master had prescribed, causing the patient's condition to worsen and die. He then instigated the victim's family to create a scene outside his master's clinic, falsely accusing his master of causing death through malpractice.\"","At this point, Doctor Jiang's brows furrowed slightly, while the Empress Dowager exclaimed in shock, \"Heavens! How could someone do such a terrible thing? This was to his master who had shown him such great kindness!\"","Yanshu explained, \"Because this apprentice was determined to become the most highly regarded physician in the family head's eyes. But his master's skills were always superior to his, and even though his master had no interest in seeking wealth and status, there was still the talented younger disciple to consider. He feared that when the younger disciple grew up and completed his training, he would take away his livelihood, so he forced his master to leave the capital to eliminate any future threats.\"","At this point, Doctor Jiang couldn't help but scoff inwardly, thinking that old scoundrel assumed everyone was as despicable as himself.","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but curse, \"This person truly has a heart worse than wolves and jackals! What happened next?\"","Yanshu continued, \"The old physician had saved lives his entire life, yet never expected that one day, he would be ruined by his ungrateful apprentice. He was filled with anger and grief, and his emotions turned into illness. Shortly after leaving the capital, he died coughing blood.\"","\"After his father's death, the son matured overnight and began planning revenge. He first studied medicine diligently, carefully examining all the medical books and cases his father had left behind. Then he traveled far and wide, observing various difficult cases and humbly learning from other physicians to broaden his knowledge. After several years, he too became a renowned physician.\"","At this point, Doctor Jiang paused again.","How did this Carefree Scholar know the details so clearly?","Yanshu continued, \"Meanwhile, that evil-hearted apprentice became increasingly greedy and selfish. Many times when the noble family members fell ill, though he could have cured them completely, he deliberately held back, just so they would remain dependent on him. At the same time, he used his position as the family physician to open numerous medical clinics, inflating prices to suppress competition, completely disregarding a physician's duty to save lives. He committed countless misdeeds. Fortunately, eventually, his evil deeds were discovered by the wise family head, who angrily handed him over to the authorities.\"","As she finished speaking, the Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow, but before she could say anything, Doctor Jiang, who had finished collecting his needles, bowed and said, \"Your Highness, today's acupuncture session is complete. Please remember to take your medicine later. I shall take my leave now.\"","The Empress Dowager didn't think much of it and nodded, letting him go.","Soon after, when no outsiders remained in the hall, the Empress Dowager asked Yanshu, \"The apprentice in this story is Zhang Shengkang, isn't it?\"","Yanshu feigned surprise, \"How did Your Highness guess?\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"The way he falsely accused his master is exactly the same method he used to harm Doctor Jiang, isn't it?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded and flattered, \"Your Highness is most perceptive.\"","The Empress Dowager gave a bitter smile and sighed, \"To think that I once trusted such a despicable person! I can hardly claim to be perceptive.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu hurried to comfort her, \"This is not your fault at all, Your Highness! It's entirely Zhang Shengkang's doing! Please don't be angry.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed again and said, \"I'm not angry. Such a person isn't worth my anger. Let the Emperor handle this matter as he sees fit. But speaking of which, where is his master's child now, and what is he doing?\"","Yanshu paused briefly, but instead of answering directly, she said, \"Well... I believe we'll have an answer to that very soon.\"","She then quietly asked her system, \"System, where is Doctor Jiang right now?\"","The system replied, \"Naturally, he's gone to the Qianming Palace.\"","Yanshu understood and thought that what happened next would depend on the Emperor.","In the Qianming Palace.","At that time, Yuwen Lan was reviewing memorials when Fu Hai entered to report, \"Your Majesty, Doctor Jiang requests an audience.\"","Without stopping his brush, he simply said, \"Let him enter.\"","Fu Hai acknowledged and went to call him in. Soon after, Doctor Jiang entered the hall, knelt and paid his respects, \"Your subject pays respects to Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan told him to rise and casually asked, \"How is the Empress Dowager today?\"","Doctor Jiang quickly replied, \"In response to Your Majesty, the Empress Dowager's first course of treatment has been completed, and her headache symptoms have significantly improved. She will need to continue taking medicine for another month, after which she should be fully recovered.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"You deserve great credit for this.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Doctor Jiang, who had just risen, knelt again and said, \"Your subject doesn't deserve such praise. I have come today to beg Your Majesty's forgiveness.\"","Yuwen Lan made an interested sound and finally stopped writing to look at him, saying, \"What forgiveness do you seek?\"","As he spoke, \"I originally bore the surname Xun. My father's name was Xun Ji, and our family once ran a medical clinic on Horse Street in the capital. Later, my father was falsely accused by his disciple Zhang Shengkang and forced to leave the capital. After my father's death, to evade Zhang Shengkang's persecution, I changed my name and wandered elsewhere. Eventually, I encountered the Imperial Medical Academy's recruitment exam and entered under my altered name. I have not previously disclosed this to Your Majesty, and for this, I am truly guilty beyond redemption.\"","With those words, Yuwen Lan said, \"Changing one's name to enter the palace is indeed a crime against the emperor. However, considering your contributions in healing, your offense can be pardoned.\"","Doctor Jiang was stunned and quickly kowtowed in gratitude, \"I thank Your Majesty for your magnanimity.\"","But then he added, \"However, there is one more matter I must address.\"","Yuwen Lan responded simply, \"Speak.\"","Doctor Jiang then said, \"I wish to accuse Zhang Shengkang of betraying his master and falsely accusing my father.\"","Yuwen Lan's reply was straightforward, \"Zhang Shengkang's case has already been handed over to the Ministry of Justice. You may go there to file your complaint, citing my decree.\"","Doctor Jiang felt a weight lift from his heart and quickly kowtowed in acknowledgment before standing up and departing hastily for the Ministry of Justice.","In the Palace of Benevolent Peace, Yanshu, having learned the situation through the system, felt relieved.","It was nearly noon, and the Empress Dowager had already taken her medicine. She decided it was time to take her leave.","Before she could rise, a palace maid entered to report, \"Your Majesty, Consort Wang has arrived.\"","Consort Wang?","Yanshu was momentarily puzzled. Wasn't she the one who used to patrol at night?","It had been quite a while since they last met.","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Let her in.\"","The maid complied, exiting the hall. Soon, Consort Wang entered the room.","It was said that after incurring the Emperor's wrath last year, Consort Wang had been patrolling for several months, enduring the cold from winter to almost summer. It was only after the Empress Dowager intervened that she was allowed to stop.","Since then, she had mostly feigned illness and avoided attending various banquets, so Yanshu hadn't seen her in a long time.","Upon entering the hall, Consort Wang first bowed to the two, saying, \"I pay my respects to the Empress Dowager and the Noble Consort. I heard that Your Majesty has not been well recently, and I am deeply concerned. I was afraid of disturbing Your Majesty's rest if I came earlier, so I delayed until now. Please forgive me. I wonder how Your Majesty is feeling now?\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"If you had come two days later, I would have been completely recovered.\"","Yanshu thought, \"Heh, her majesty is quite humorous.\"","Consort Wang, however, was extremely embarrassed and quickly added, \"I am ashamed.\"","Yanshu thought, \"Being ashamed is of no use. Coming after the first treatment phase is over, of course, the Empress Dowager would be upset.\"","As a loyal follower of the Empress Dowager, she could only hastily add, \"Please be at ease, Your Majesty. Doctor Jiang said you are almost fully recovered and only need to continue taking medicine for another month.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly without saying more. Yanshu, however, could hear Consort Wang's thoughts—","\"It's almost lunchtime, why is the Noble Consort still here? Everyone in the harem has been killed by her. Now that I've been seen by her again, will I have a way to live? Is she planning to find a way to kill me next? I didn't want to come but had no choice. Is the heavens deliberately trying to make me die?\"","Yanshu was puzzled, \"What do you mean everyone has been killed by her? Does Consort Wang attribute the deaths of Consort Zhou, Consort Ning, Consort An, and Consort Li to her as well?\"","She felt both speechless and amused and couldn't help but speak to Consort Wang, \"It's been a long time, Consort Wang. How have you been these days?\"","Consort Wang shivered and quickly replied, \"Thank you for your concern, Your Highness. I am well.\"","In her heart, she was terrified, \"Oh no, oh no! She actually spoke to me first. She must be planning to deal with me!\"","Yanshu listened silently and couldn't help but play a prank, \"It must have been hard for you to patrol for so long. I've always heard you weren't feeling well. Could it be that you were overworked?\"","Consort Wang shivered again and quickly said, \"I dare not. I've been weak since childhood, and recently, I've had both a cold and gastrointestinal issues, but it has nothing to do with patrolling.\"","In her heart, she thought, \"This wicked woman, does she want to pin the blame on me in front of the Empress Dowager? May the heavens curse her to a miserable end!\"","Yanshu listened silently but smiled on the surface, \"Then take good care of yourself. It's almost winter, and the weather is getting colder.\"","Consort Wang nodded frantically, but in her heart, she was already crying, \"Is she planning to make me patrol again? This woman is truly ruthless!\"","Yanshu secretly raised an eyebrow; she hadn't thought that at all.","Alas, since this woman had already labeled her as evil, no matter what she said, the other party would interpret it negatively.","She had no intention of wasting more words with her and said to the Empress Dowager, \"It's almost noon, so I won't disturb Your Majesty any longer. I'll take my leave now.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Go and rest.\"","Then she turned to Consort Wang, \"There's nothing more here. You can leave too.\"","Both acknowledged and left the hall together.","Yanshu didn't bother with Consort Wang and took a sedan chair back to Ganlu Palace. She then instructed Rendong to send the novel she had been reading to Qianming Palace.","Earlier, she had only used the novel as an excuse to prompt Doctor Jiang to file a complaint quickly. In reality, the novel hadn't been sent out.","Now that the Emperor had pardoned Doctor Jiang's crime, and Doctor Jiang had gone to the Ministry of Justice to file a complaint, she no longer had any concerns and could share the novel with the readers.","As expected, after reading the novel and combining it with the rumors in the city, the readers guessed that the villain in the story was Zhang Shengkang. They began to condemn him vehemently.","Under such pressure, the Ministry of Justice hastened to handle the case without delay.","Yanshu was very pleased.","However, a couple of days later, Rendong informed her, \"Your Highness, it's said that Consort Wang is ill again.\"","Yanshu was puzzled, \"Ill again? Is it true?\"","Could it be an excuse to avoid patrolling?","Before Rendong could answer, the system said, \"The illness is real. She's scared of you and got sick.\"","Yanshu was puzzled, \"When did I become so terrifying that I could make someone sick?\"","The system explained, \"This is called paranoia. In such people's eyes, even a falling leaf is out to kill them.\"","Yanshu thought, \"Could this be a side effect of patrolling?\"","Oh well, she couldn't be bothered. Now, she only cared about when the verdict on Zhang Shengkang's case would be announced.","The system said, \"It just came out, fresh.\"","Yanshu's eyes lit up and she quickly asked, \"Tell me!\"","The system said, \"Zhang Shengkang was sentenced to death and will be executed in half a month. His son and disciples, who helped him bully the market, were all sentenced to prison terms. His wife has been seriously ill for the past few days and may not survive the news. However, his new wife received the Emperor's permission to divorce and return to her family.\"","Yanshu nodded, \"This verdict is gratifying. That old scoundrel Zhang has finally received his due!\"","Alright, now they just had to wait for the execution of Zhang Shengkang in half a month.","After all, the Empress Dowager had already made it clear that no one would save him!","Half a month later.","After noon, the despicable Zhang Shengkang was executed. The onlookers all felt a sense of justice and returned home satisfied.","A member of the Imperial Guard rushed into the palace, presenting a letter to the Emperor, \"Your Majesty, just before Zhang Shengkang was taken to the execution ground, he handed an epistle to the eunuch, saying he wanted to give it to Doctor Xun.\"","Indeed, after Zhang Shengkang's case was thoroughly exposed, Doctor Jiang, who had been living under an assumed name for many years, also restored his true name—Xun Lan.","Thus, he was now Doctor Xun.","At first hearing this, Yuwen Lan assumed it was Zhang Shengkang's last-minute repentance, wanting to write a letter of confession to Xun Lan.","However, upon further thought, he felt something was amiss.","Would Zhang Shengkang be someone to easily repent?","Curious, he took the letter and opened it to glance at it.","It contained only a few lines—","\"Before the late Emperor's death, he was obsessed with Taoism, neglecting food and drink, but he particularly enjoyed drinking kelp soup daily. During that time, the Empress Dowager once asked me for Yuebai Powder.","Within half a month, the late Emperor passed away.","Does my junior brother know why?\"","...","After reading the letter, Yuwen Lan was initially puzzled—","He vaguely knew that \"Yuebai Powder\" was used to treat various sores.","But why did this man bring up the late Emperor's death?","And why write to Xun Lan?","As he pondered further, a sense of uncertainty crept into his heart.","He decided to set the letter aside for the moment and summoned Xun Lan to his presence.","In no time, Xun Lan arrived in a hurry, likely thinking that the Emperor was unwell, as he was carrying a medical kit.","Yuwen Lan remained composed and first dismissed the onlookers before asking Xun Lan, \"I was reading a book the other day and came across some medical matters I didn't understand. I wanted to consult you about them.\"","Doctor Xun quickly bowed his head and said, \"Please command, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan inquired, \"If one were to consume Yueqing and kelp together, what would happen?\"","Xun Lan replied, \"Your Majesty, Yueqing is an external medication and should not be taken internally. It contains mercury powder. If consumed with kelp, it could lead to poisoning.\"","Poisoning?","Yuwen Lan paused but maintained his composure, asking, \"What kind of poison?\"","Xun Lan explained, \"It would be similar to ingesting mercury, causing chest tightness, shortness of breath, and extreme fatigue. If the dosage is large, it could lead to convulsions, unconsciousness, bleeding from the mouth and gums, hematuria, and even death by hemorrhage.\"","Yuwen Lan was taken aback.","Didn't the late Emperor die with exactly these symptoms?"]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113","paragraphs":["Yuwen Lan still remembered that four years ago, after leading his army to a great victory against the Xiongrong and returning to the capital, he received news from the palace just as he was approaching the metropolitan area. The message said that the Former Emperor was gravely ill.","Without taking any rest, he immediately rode hard through the night to return to the palace. When he arrived at Qianming Palace, he witnessed that scene—","The Former Emperor, who had just coughed up blood, still had bloodstains on his robes, but had already stopped breathing—","At that time, everyone said the Former Emperor had died from weakness due to excessive Taoist cultivation and alchemy practices, neglecting food and drink until he lost control of his spiritual energy.","Could it be...","No, that possibility had barely surfaced before he immediately dismissed it.","This matter could not possibly involve the Empress Dowager!","It must be that bastard Zhang Shengkang harboring hatred, deliberately trying to drive a wedge between mother and son.","Indeed, how malicious were his intentions? Producing this letter before death—if Xun Lan had seen it, he would have been burdened with such a heavy weight, whether he spoke of it or not, it would have been a sin.","He would never have been able to live peacefully afterward.","Or as now, letting him see it, planning to sow discord between mother and son.","That dog!","Yuwen Lan silently gritted his teeth, but maintained a normal expression as he said to Xun the Imperial Physician, \"It's fine now, you may go. The Empress Dowager has half a month left in her treatment course. Take good care of her and ensure nothing goes wrong.\"","Xun the Imperial Physician, who remained unaware of what had transpired, quickly bowed his head in acknowledgment and retreated from the hall with his medicine box.","Yuwen Lan threw the letter into the incense burner, then summoned Fu Hai inside and ordered, \"Issue an imperial decree: Zhang Shengkang's crimes are heinous. His corpse shall be whipped for three days and thrown in the mass grave, with no one allowed to collect it.\"","Fu Hai quickly acknowledged the order and went to make arrangements, wondering to himself what evil deeds of Zhang Shengkang had been discovered to prompt such an order from the emperor.","In Ganlu Palace.","Yuwen Lan came late tonight; Yanshu was almost asleep when she heard the door.","Before she could get up, he had already climbed into bed and embraced her without a word.","Yanshu was still somewhat confused and mumbled, \"Your subject waited until the night watch but didn't see Your Majesty. I thought you weren't coming.\"","Yuwen Lan spoke in a low, deep voice, \"I was busy until late, that's why I've only come now.\"","After a pause, he asked her, \"How was your day?\"","Yanshu, still half-asleep, replied, \"Very good.\"","Heh, sending that dog Zhang to meet his maker today was truly satisfying. If she weren't pregnant, she would have loved to drink three hundred cups in celebration!","Yuwen Lan silently listened, then said, \"Sleep now.\"","Yanshu made a sound of agreement, shifted her position to find a comfortable spot in his embrace, and finally closed her eyes, quickly falling into dreamland.","Yuwen Lan lowered his gaze and reached out to stroke her hair.","If something were wrong, she would have known already, wouldn't she?","And just now, he hadn't detected anything unusual in Yanshu's thoughts.","So, Zhang Shengkang must have been slandering after all.","In the darkness, he too closed his eyes and fell asleep.","That night's sleep was very light, and Yuwen Lan woke before dawn.","Although there was no morning court session today, he didn't want to sleep anymore, so he got up, dressed, and went to Qianming Palace.","The cold wind along the way was sobering. After reading memorials for half a watch in the imperial study, the sky outside gradually began to show its first light.","Fu Hai had been attending nearby, just thinking about arranging the emperor's meal, when before he could move, an Imperial Guard came to report, \"Your Majesty, news just arrived from the Min Yue Region that they've captured a Taoist who appears to be the Baihe Taoist.\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound and immediately asked, \"Is he alive?\"","The Imperial Guard replied, \"The Min Yue people say they chased him into the mountains, and when he found no escape route, he jumped off a cliff. His fate is currently unknown.\"","Jumped off a cliff?","Yuwen Lan frowned, thought for a moment, and said, \"This person is full of tricks, we cannot trust this easily. Have them find the body first and confirm whether it's truly the Baihe Taoist before anything else. Also, we must not let our guard down against the Red Lotus Cult.\"","The Imperial Guard acknowledged and withdrew from the hall.","Yuwen Lan thought for a moment, then picked up the memorials again.","With so many important matters to handle, why dwell on something that happened four years ago?","Moreover, he didn't believe it.","As days passed, the capital entered the eleventh month.","The first snow had already fallen, and the weather grew increasingly cold.","Fortunately, the palace had floor heating, especially the Palace of Benevolent Peace. Fearing the Empress Dowager might catch cold, the palace servants kept the floor heating particularly warm.","Today was the final day of the Empress Dowager's last treatment course. Although Yanshu's belly was now as big as a ball, she still made a special effort to accompany the Empress Dowager for Xun the Imperial Physician's pulse-taking.","At this moment, watching Xun the Imperial Physician remove his fingers from the pulse point, she quickly asked, \"How is it?\"","Xun the Imperial Physician hastily replied, \"Please be at ease, Your Grace. The Empress Dowager's illness has been completely cured, and there's no need to worry about a relapse. However, she still needs to be careful about keeping warm and avoiding drafts during cold weather to prevent catching a cold.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu finally felt completely relieved and quickly said to the Empress Dowager, \"Congratulations, Your Grace. There's no need to worry anymore.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said to Xun the Imperial Physician, \"You have done well in treating this illness. I should reward you.\"","Xun the Imperial Physician quickly knelt and said, \"Treating patients is a doctor's heavenly duty. Moreover, Your Graces have already shown me great kindness. I dare not ask for rewards.\"","But the Empress Dowager said, \"Your not asking for rewards is your business, my giving rewards is mine. Don't be modest.\"","She then instructed the palace servants, \"Award Xun the Imperial Physician fifty taels of gold, plus a pair of deerskin gloves and a pair of cloud boots. The weather is cold now, and you need to keep warm when coming and going.\"","Hearing this, Xun the Imperial Physician could only hurriedly kowtow in thanks, his face full of trepidation.","Yanshu was so excited she almost stood up to clap—","Hmph, her boss was just this generous! When she liked someone, she'd shower them with gold and silver, how domineering!","Just then, the Empress Dowager said to her, \"Next, I'm just waiting for your child to be born. Counting the days, it should be about a month from now, right?\"","Before Yanshu could answer, Xun the Imperial Physician quickly said, \"The Empress Dowager is correct. In another half month, the royal heir will be full-term, and birth would be normal any day after that.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"We'll have to trouble you to take extra care and look after the Imperial Consort well.\"","Xun the Imperial Physician hurriedly agreed.","Just then, they saw the cotton curtain at the hall entrance being lifted, and a tall figure wearing a crane-patterned robe entered.","Everyone in the hall quickly bowed, while the Empress Dowager said, \"Why has Your Majesty come at this time?\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"I remembered today was Mother's last day of treatment, so I came to see how things were going.\"","Yanshu quickly said, \"Your Majesty need not worry, the Empress Dowager's illness has been cured.\"","Yuwen Lan breathed a sigh of relief and nodded, \"That's good.\"","Then Yanshu asked him, \"Why is Your Majesty's shoulder wet?\"","Yuwen Lan made a sound and said, \"It's snowing outside.\"","It's snowing again? Yanshu's eyes lit up.","The Empress Dowager sighed and said, \"Your Majesty is still like when you were young, not liking to use an umbrella in the snow. What if you catch a cold?\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and said, \"I came by palanquin, Mother. I only got a few snowflakes on me while walking the few steps after getting out, don't worry.\"","The Empress Dowager finally said nothing more.","Then Yanshu said with a grin, \"Snowy days are perfect for hotpot. Why don't we have lamb hotpot for dinner?\"","Ahem, since everyone present knew she was a foodie, she didn't bother pretending anymore. Besides, they should celebrate the boss's recovery today!","However, the Empress Dowager smiled and said, \"You two go ahead and eat. I'm not very fond of that taste.\"","Yuwen Lan added, \"Mother indeed doesn't care much for lamb.\"","Yanshu could only agree; if the boss didn't like it, she couldn't force it. She would just have to eat with the emperor.","Then the Empress Dowager instructed her, \"The snow makes it cold, and tomorrow will likely be icy. You needn't come over; stay in your palace. We can't have anything go wrong at this crucial time.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed.","Then she took her leave with the emperor.","Outside the hall, snow was indeed falling. They boarded the imperial palanquin together and headed for Ganlu Palace.","Yanshu was already hungry, her mind full of the delicious hot pot lamb. She couldn't help saying, \"We should have the imperial kitchen prepare six plates of lamb.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"That much? I only need two plates.\"","She paused in surprise and said, \"Oh right, there's Your Majesty too. Then let's make it eight plates.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So those six plates she mentioned earlier hadn't even included his portion?","After finishing their hotpot meal and taking a bath, they both climbed onto the bed.","Without the covering of her cotton robe, Yanshu's belly was even more prominent now, round like a watermelon.","Yuwen Lan looked at it with concern and couldn't help but ask, \"It's so big, does it hurt?\"","Yanshu made a soft sound and replied, \"It doesn't hurt now, but I wonder how painful it will be during delivery.\"","Just as she finished speaking, a bump appeared on her belly.","Her eyes lit up as she smiled, stroking her belly while talking to the little one inside, \"Baby, are you trying to tell Mommy that you'll be good and won't make Mommy hurt for too long, right?\"","After she spoke, the bump rolled to another direction.","As the birth drew near, the baby's movements became more varied and obvious, with bumps rolling around and even stretches of hands and feet, making them increasingly eager to see what the baby would look like.","Yuwen Lan couldn't resist placing his hand on her belly and smiled, \"Baby will definitely listen to Mommy.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the baby made another bump, as if responding.","Yuwen Lan's heart melted, and he added, \"Baby is a good child. It's late now, go to sleep early so your Mommy can get a good rest too.\"","Surprisingly, as if understanding their words, the little one in the belly gradually stopped moving.","Yanshu's eyes brightened, \"It seems our baby can really recognize Your Majesty's voice. Such an obedient child.\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow and said, \"Of course, my child will certainly be as clever as I am.\"","He kissed her forehead and said, \"Let's sleep now.\"","Yanshu made a sound of agreement and closed her eyes in his embrace, falling fast asleep.","That night, as snow fell silently outside the window, Yuwen Lan dreamed of the baby's birth a month later.","In his dream, he held his child, who kicked and waved, constantly smiling at him, and even called him \"Father.\"","In the dream, he thought, truly his own child, speaking earlier than others - how clever indeed!","The next day there was a court session, and Yuwen Lan rose early as usual to go to Qianming Palace.","Last night's snow had stopped, and the weather was indeed very cold.","In court, as various ministers presented their reports, Yuwen Lan asked with concern, \"Did last night's snow cause any disasters? Are there any citizens suffering from the cold?\"","The Assistant Minister of Revenue quickly replied, \"Please be assured, Your Majesty. Last night's snow wasn't heavy, so there was no disaster. This morning, the Capital Official has already set up three porridge stations and warming shelters in the city, which should address any issues.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and said, \"Not just the capital, but all areas affected by snow should follow this example. If there's a shortage of funds, you may apply to the Ministry of Revenue, but strict oversight is necessary to prevent corruption. The court's money must benefit the common people.\"","The Assistant Minister of Revenue quickly agreed.","Then the Minister of Justice stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, I received a report from the Capital Official this morning. Recently, there have been cases of pregnant women miscarrying in the capital. Some physicians found it suspicious and reported it to the Capital Official.\"","This news surprised everyone.","Someone suggested, \"Could it be due to the cold weather causing ice, making pregnant women slip and fall?\"","The Minister of Justice replied, \"This may not be the main reason. According to the Capital Official's statistics, there have only been two snowfalls recently, neither particularly heavy, so there hasn't been much ice on the roads. Moreover, most pregnant women have been staying indoors to avoid the cold, rarely venturing out, yet they still mysteriously miscarried. This matter seems quite suspicious.\"","Upon hearing this, Yuwen Lan furrowed his brow and asked, \"How many such cases have there been?\"","The Minister of Justice quickly responded, \"According to the Capital Official's report, there have been more than ten cases in the past half month.\"","More than ten cases in half a month?","That meant almost one case every day or two?","Yuwen Lan thought of someone.","He remembered Yanshu mentioning the Baihe Taoist using human placentas for alchemy...","Plus, a few days ago, the Imperial Guard reported that the Baihe Taoist had fallen off a cliff, and after he ordered an investigation, there had been no further news.","He paused, about to give orders.","However, the Minister of Justice continued, \"I recall that about four years ago, similar incidents occurred in the capital, with numerous pregnant women miscarrying within a short period. However, that was during summer, not in severe winter like now.\"","This statement startled Yuwen Lan again.","Summer four years ago...","That was around the time before the Former Emperor passed away.","At that time, the Baihe Taoist was still in the palace, spending his days accompanying the Former Emperor in his pursuit of immortality...","Could it be that he had already started using this method for alchemy back then?","Then... did the Former Emperor know about it?","While lost in thought, he heard the Minister of Justice continue, \"Your Majesty, I believe someone must be causing these evil acts behind the scenes. We should investigate thoroughly to prevent more pregnant women from becoming victims.\"","Yuwen Lan snapped back to attention and immediately ordered, \"Indeed. Command the Capital Official, Ministry of Justice, and Ministry of Punishment to investigate this matter immediately. The Capital Guard should deploy men to thoroughly search the capital. If any suspicious Taoist priests are found, arrest them immediately. I suspect the Baihe Taoist has already arrived in the capital.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone quickly agreed, not daring to be negligent."]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114","paragraphs":["Yanshu woke up and only then learned about the events of the morning court.","Surprised and angry, she, like Yuwen Lan, immediately guessed that it was the work of the Baihe Taoist.","However, she was still a bit puzzled. Wasn't the Taoist in the Min Yue Region? A few days ago, she had heard that he was chased by the Imperial Guard and jumped off a cliff. How could he suddenly appear in the capital?","Then she heard the system chime in, **Because the one who jumped off the cliff wasn't him. It was a stand-in he had prepared for himself. While the Imperial Guard was chasing the stand-in, he took the opportunity to escape from Min Yue and has already arrived in the capital.**","Yanshu widened her eyes in surprise, **This Taoist can actually find stand-ins?**","The system replied, **Didn't someone build a temple for him? Never underestimate his ability to brainwash people.**","Yanshu thought, **...You're right.**","So, this Taoist is indeed cunning and treacherous. By himself, he has caused so much trouble! Without realizing it, he has caused so many unborn lives to be harmed in the capital!","No, now that she knows, how can she stand by and do nothing?","She immediately asked the system for the location of the Taoist, wrote it down on paper, and had Rendong hurry to deliver it to Qianming Palace.","Thinking about it again, she felt a bit uneasy—knowing about this matter made her so angry, the Empress Dowager would surely be even more furious, right?","But her beloved, who had just finished his treatment yesterday, must not trigger an old illness again.","So she ordered a sedan chair to be prepared. After breakfast, she put on thick clothes and went to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","Upon arrival, the Empress Dowager was a bit surprised and asked, \"Didn't I tell you not to come yesterday? Why are you here?\"","Yanshu replied, \"The snow from last night has melted, and the ground isn't slippery. I was worried that you might be bored alone, so I came to keep you company.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"It's kind of you to think of me, but I was just about to ask someone. I've just heard that many pregnant women in the capital have had miscarriages. What's going on?\"","Yanshu explained, \"Yes, there's been such a thing. It's likely the work of that Baihe Taoist. It's said that when he was in Min Yue, he used placenta to refine some kind of elixir. When the Emperor found out, he was furious and ordered the Imperial Guard to arrest him. But the one who jumped off the cliff in Min Yue a few days ago was actually his stand-in. This person has recently escaped to the capital.\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager's brow furrowed, \"What? It's that Taoist again?\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"This man is outwardly a Taoist, but in reality, he is a rebel with extremely malicious intentions. He is also very cunning. It's said that a minister mentioned this in the morning court, saying that such an incident happened a few years ago. He must have been in the capital then, so it's unlikely to be anyone else.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly but didn't say anything more. In her heart, she was seething, **That old scoundrel is still doing such heinous things! Why didn't I kill him back then? That dog man, this is all your fault!**","Hearing this, Yanshu frowned inwardly.","The Empress Dowager used the phrase \"still doing.\"","This means that the Empress Dowager knew about the Taoist's actions back then.","Then, the late Emperor must have known too.","The system chimed in, **Otherwise, what do you think? If the late Emperor hadn't allowed it, how could a Taoist have gotten away with it in the capital?**","Yanshu was stunned and couldn't help but exclaim, **The late Emperor was the ruler of the nation! How could he have allowed that old Taoist to harm his own people?**","She paused and immediately thought of a horrifying possibility, **...Did the late Emperor also eat it?**","The system replied, **Exactly. He was obsessed with eternal life. Knowing it was a \"good\" thing, how could he not eat it?**","\"Ugh...\"","Hearing this, Yanshu felt a wave of nausea and almost vomited on the spot.","The Empress Dowager was startled and quickly asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Yanshu patted her chest and said, \"I don't know why, but I suddenly felt unwell.\"","The Empress Dowager quickly said, \"Go back and rest. Call Imperial Physician Xun to check on you right away. Be very careful these days.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed and also comforted the Empress Dowager, \"Please don't be too angry, Your Majesty. It's not a bad thing that the Taoist is nearby. The Emperor is wise and powerful, and the capital is well-guarded. He will surely catch this man.\"","Oh, it's so hard for the Empress Dowager to have such a reckless and tyrannical emperor. Such a just person must have been very angry back then.","Fortunately, that emperor is already dead. But her beloved must not fall ill again.","The Empress Dowager nodded slightly and said, \"Don't worry about me. You are the most important now. That Taoist is very cunning. Even though we are in the palace, we must not let our guard down.\"","Yanshu quickly agreed and then took her leave, returning to Ganlu Palace.","Thinking about what the late Emperor and the Taoist had done, Yanshu felt sick to her stomach, which affected her appetite at noon. She only had some porridge and then went to sleep.","When she woke up from her nap, it was already dark outside, and it was almost time for dinner.","She was still concerned about the matter and quickly asked the system, **Has the Taoist been caught yet?**","To her surprise, the system replied, **Not yet.**","Yanshu frowned, **What happened? Didn't I tell the Imperial Guard it was near Sajin Lane at the Binzhi Inn? Even the room number was given. How could they not catch him?**","The system replied, **I told you that Taoist is very cunning. He changed locations before the Imperial Guard arrived.**","Yanshu was almost exasperated. In this era, there were no communication tools, so she couldn't direct the Imperial Guard in real-time. Now that she was heavily pregnant, she couldn't go to the scene herself like last time when they caught the human trafficker. Time is of the essence now. How can they catch that Taoist immediately?","Just then, the system said, **Maybe he can be caught now.**","Yanshu was puzzled, \"What?\"","But then the system said, **But first, check if your windows and doors are closed.**","Yanshu, **???**","Before she could ask another question, she suddenly heard the hurried voice of Imperial Physician Xun outside the door, \"Please ask Consort Yanshu to close all windows and doors immediately and not allow anyone to enter or exit for the time being.\"","Yanshu was puzzled again. Why was another person telling her to close the windows?","But the next second, she heard Imperial Physician Xun say, \"I smell a medicinal odor outside, which could be harmful to pregnant women.\"","What?","Hearing this, everyone in the hall was shocked.","Fortunately, it was cold outside, so the windows and doors were already closed. Only Rendong had planned to go out to order food for her mistress, but now she didn't dare move.","Just then, another voice came from outside the door. It was Yuwen Lan asking, \"What happened?\"","Yanshu didn't dare open the door, but fortunately, Imperial Physician Xun was outside to report, \"Your Majesty, I smelled a strong smoke with a medicinal odor in the palace. It should contain something harmful to pregnant women. I was afraid the Consort would be in danger, so I hurried to report.\"","In fact, Yuwen Lan had already smelled the medicinal odor in the air as he walked over. Hearing this, he realized the seriousness of the situation and immediately told Yanshu, \"Don't go in or out for now. Close all windows and doors.\"","Then he asked Imperial Physician Xun, \"Do you know where the smoke is coming from?\"","Imperial Physician Xun replied, \"I walked from the duty room to here, and the smell became stronger as I approached the inner palace. It should be nearby.\"","Yuwen Lan immediately ordered Fu Hai, \"Immediately have the guards follow Imperial Physician Xun to search. No one is allowed to stop them.\"","Fu Hai agreed and quickly called over a dozen guards to follow Imperial Physician Xun to search the palace.","Since there were few people in the inner palace, they soon found the source of the medicinal odor.","It was the Cuiwei Palace where Consort Wang lived.","Upon hearing the report, Yuwen Lan was furious and immediately interrogated her personally.","However, Consort Wang denied it, saying, \"Please investigate, Your Majesty. I was just unwell and asked my family outside the palace to buy some moxa sticks to fumigate. I absolutely didn't intend to harm Consort Yanshu!\"","In her heart, she thought, **This Consort Yanshu is really ruthless! She framed and slandered me like this!**","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan did not easily believe her and ordered the guards, \"Bring out the item she was burning and let Imperial Physician Xun examine it.\"","The guards agreed and immediately brought out the \"moxa stick\" seized from Cuiwei Palace for Imperial Physician Xun to inspect on the spot.","Imperial Physician Xun peeled open the moxa stick and immediately saw a pile of medicinal powder fall out.","After a thorough inspection, Xun the Imperial Physician quickly determined, \"Your Majesty, this contains red peony, salvia, safflower, musk, turmeric, and other blood-activating herbs. Even if not ingested, merely inhaling the scent poses a risk of miscarriage. Although it is cold now, during dinner time, people coming and going in the hall will still allow the smell to enter, which is certainly detrimental to Consort Yi and the royal offspring.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone was shocked, and Yuwen Lan immediately turned to Consort Wang, coldly asking, \"Where did this item come from? Who instructed you to do this?\"","Consort Wang was stunned and immediately cried out, \"Your Majesty, please believe me, I truly didn't know there were such things inside. I was suffering from a long-term illness and had no other choice but to ask my family to buy some moxibustion outside the palace. I really didn't know there were so many toxic substances...\"","【Goodness, what is going on? How could there be such things in moxibustion? Could it be that Consort Yi is instructing this imperial physician to deliberately frame me?】","Yuwen Lan, however, had lost all patience and coldly ordered the guards, \"Immediately control the Wang family, prohibit anyone from entering or leaving, and ensure the source of this poison is uncovered!\"","The guards immediately complied and rushed to Consort Wang's family outside the palace.","Meanwhile, Yanshu had already learned about the developments through the system.","She pondered, 【Could it be that Consort Wang was also exploited by that Taoist?】","The system replied, 【Indeed, those moxibustion sticks actually came from that Taoist. Since arriving in the capital, he has disguised himself as a physician. A few days ago, he just happened to cure the Wang family patriarch's stomach ailment, who then regarded him as a divine doctor. That's why he bought these moxibustion sticks from him and had them sent into the palace for his daughter.】","Yanshu nodded but still felt some confusion, 【But why didn't Consort Wang see an imperial physician when she was sick? Just relying on moxibustion won't cure her!】","The system explained, 【Because she is now very afraid of you, thinking that the imperial physicians are in cahoots with you, wanting to take her life, so she has been too scared to see them.】","Yanshu, 【...】","Alright, since that's the case, she won't force it. She should focus on the issue of the Taoist instead.","【In that case, could the previous miscarriages of pregnant women in the capital also be the work of that Taoist?】","The system said, 【Not necessarily. After all, this method is costly and quite expensive. He only uses it specifically against you. For other pregnant women, he usually first investigates, then secretly sprinkles the drug powder into their well water, and bribes the nearby midwives in advance to obtain fresh placenta after the women miscarry.】","Hearing this, Yanshu couldn't help but feel nauseous.","Heh, that damned Taoist actually targeted her! This time, she must capture him!","The system then said, 【This time, it's easier. The person is currently in the second room of the west wing at the Xingyuan Pharmacy by Yongding Bridge, with freshly dyed black hair, estimated to be around forty to fifty years old.】","Freshly dyed hair?","Yanshu raised an eyebrow. As she knew, the current hair dyeing technique involved boiling black beans in vinegar juice until a black paste was formed, which was then applied to the hair. Of course, some reinforcement methods were needed afterward, but since this person dyed his hair this afternoon, there probably wasn't enough time for reinforcement...","She immediately came up with an idea, quickly wrote another letter, and had it sent to Qianming Palace.","In the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","As the sky darkened, the Empress Dowager was waiting for news.","Only when she heard that the source of the poison, Consort Wang, had been captured and Yanshu was unaffected, did she finally breathe a sigh of relief.","Dan Shuang quickly stepped forward to persuade, \"Your Majesty, you haven't had dinner yet. Since Consort Yi is unaffected, please have some food.\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"I have no appetite. The Baihe Taoist has not been captured yet.\"","After all, as long as the Taoist is not caught, it means that pregnant women in the city are still at risk.","Even unborn children are lives! How can she eat in peace?","Come to think of it, it's also her fault.","If she had eliminated that Taoist along with the person back then, how could there be such a hidden danger now?","Fortunately, not long after, the eunuch Qiao Fushun, who had gone to inquire about the news, came in to report, \"Your Majesty, I just received news from Qianming Palace that the Baihe Taoist has been captured!\"","The Empress Dowager paused and quickly asked, \"Truly captured? No mistake?\"","Qiao Fushun nodded vigorously, \"Your Majesty, please rest assured, the identity has been verified. It is said that the Taoist dyed his hair black this afternoon and disguised himself as a physician, hiding in the area around Yongding Bridge. The Imperial Guards followed the smell of vinegar directly to Yongding Bridge, surrounded the residential and commercial areas there, and conducted a thorough search. They quickly found a man in black, wearing a black hat, with a head full of vinegar smell. When hot water was poured on his head, the black hair all turned white. After confirmation, it is indeed the Taoist.\"","What?","The Empress Dowager was stunned. This method seemed a bit... cunning?","But anyway, capturing this person is good.","The heavy stone in her heart finally fell, and she clasped her hands together, chanting \"Amitabha.\"","Seeing this, everyone also relaxed. Dan Shuang stepped forward again, \"Your Majesty, can we now serve dinner? Your illness has just improved; you can't go hungry.\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"Just prepare a bowl of plain porridge.\"","Dan Shuang complied and hurried out to arrange for dinner.","The Empress Dowager was about to sit on the warm couch when she heard Qiao Fushun say, \"By the way, Your Majesty, on my way back, I just happened to meet the guards at the palace gate who came to deliver a message, saying that Madam Xu, the wife of Zhang Shengkang, passed away today.\"","The Empress Dowager's expression turned cold and said, \"Let her die. Her husband and son committed so many evil deeds. The Emperor did not sentence her to suffer while sick, which is already lenient.\"","Qiao Fushun quickly complied, then added, \"Madam Xu had someone send a letter to the palace gate before her death, requesting Your Majesty to read it.\"","Saying this, he presented a letter.","The Empress Dowager paused, finally reached out to take it, and quickly scanned it.","To her surprise, she was stunned.","The letter was not written by Madam Xu but by Zhang Shengkang.","After all, Zhang Shengkang had written her prescriptions for so many years, and she was very familiar with his handwriting.","At this moment, Zhang Shengkang wrote in the letter, \"The matter of mixing menstrual blood into the emperor's kelp soup, I have already informed Xun the Imperial Physician before my death. I sincerely hope Your Majesty will be cautious.\"","The Empress Dowager paused.","Heh, what a Zhang Shengkang!","...","After confirming the identity of the Baihe Taoist, the Imperial Guards immediately took him to the prison.","It was already late at night, and Yuwen Lan also breathed a sigh of relief, preparing to rest in Ganlu Palace.","After capturing the foolish Consort Wang, the crisis had been resolved, and Ganlu Palace could now be entered and exited.","Before he could get up, the Imperial Guards reported, \"Your Majesty, the Taoist says he has a secret about the late emperor that he wants to report to you.\"","Yuwen Lan paused.","After a moment, he nodded, \"I will see him.\"","Just as he had always wanted to see what the Taoist who harmed the late emperor looked like now.","With that, he got up and left.","Not long after, Yuwen Lan met the Taoist in the prison.","The man's face showed no signs of aging, and apart from the slightly ridiculous hair after losing its color, his appearance was indeed much younger than before.","But he only felt disgust.","Why did the late emperor trust such a person?","At this moment, before he could speak, the Taoist smiled first, \"Your Majesty has finally come. Since you are so gracious, I will offer a secret to you.\"","Yuwen Lan remained expressionless and said, \"What secret?\"","The Baihe Taoist smiled and said, \"Your Majesty, don't think that the late emperor was killed by me. At that time, I lived and ate with the late emperor, and our diets were the same. Except for one thing, the late emperor drank a bowl of kelp soup every day. Later, I was fine, but the late emperor vomited blood and died. Do you know why? The one who poisoned the late emperor was someone from the palace!\"","Yuwen Lan did not show any reaction but coldly asked, \"You lived and ate with the late emperor. So, did the late emperor also eat the pills you refined from human placenta?\"","The Baihe Taoist was stunned and then smiled, \"Your Majesty is indeed smart. Yes, I was loyal to the late emperor. Such a precious thing should naturally be offered to the late emperor first.\"","Yuwen Lan narrowed his eyes.","Just at this moment, he heard a voice from behind, \"Enough.\"","All eyes turned to the door, where they saw the Empress Dowager standing.","Before anyone could bow, the Empress Dowager had already approached Yuwen Lan, glanced at him, and then addressed the Baihe Taoist, \"You, who once lured the late Emperor into persecuting civilians, committing such heinous acts, now on the brink of death, still seek to frame others?\"","The Baihe Taoist paused, then said to Yuwen Lan, \"Does Your Majesty really bear to see the late Emperor die without knowing the truth?\"","\"Silence,\" Yuwen Lan coldly commanded. \"On the brink of death, you still spout lies. Guards, cut out his tongue and sever his tendons. Announce to the world, execution at noon tomorrow, in public.\"","Then, bowing his head to the Empress Dowager, he said, \"This place is bloody, please return to the palace, Mother.\"","The Empress Dowager hesitated but had to agree, and they left the prison together.","In the deep winter night, the biting cold air stung the lungs.","The Empress Dowager did not get into the carriage but said to Yuwen Lan, \"I have something I wish to tell Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan, however, gently replied, \"It's late, Mother. Please go back and rest. Whatever it is, we can discuss it tomorrow.\""]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115","paragraphs":["The Empress Dowager knew that Zhang Shengkang wouldn't have written just that one letter to her.","Since he mentioned Xun the Imperial Physician, it was highly likely that he had indeed written a letter to him as well.","However, reviewing recent events, she hadn't noticed anything unusual about Xun the Imperial Physician.","To be safe, she immediately sent someone to investigate, and discovered that before Zhang Shengkang's execution, he had given a letter to the prison guard, who then handed it to the Imperial Guard.","The Empress Dowager was well aware that the Imperial Guard answered to the Emperor, and would certainly report any discoveries to him immediately.","Having just witnessed the Emperor's reaction to the Taoist priest, and now hearing him speak to her this way, she understood that the Imperial Guard probably hadn't given that letter to Xun the Imperial Physician, but rather to the Emperor.","The Emperor already knew.","This was the child she had raised, and she understood him well.","His response to her now was probably just his way of avoiding the issue.","But now, things had reached this point, and there were no other options left.","So the Empress Dowager continued, \"This is a matter of great importance. Even if Your Majesty doesn't believe what that evil Taoist said today, others have already heard it. This matter cannot wait until tomorrow.\"","After a pause, Yuwen Lan finally replied, \"Then let's discuss this back at the palace.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded at his words and finally boarded her carriage.","Yuwen Lan followed closely behind, and their carriages, mother and son, headed one after another toward the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","In Ganlu Palace.","When news arrived that the evil Taoist had been captured, Yanshu finally breathed a sigh of relief.","However, at the same time, there were still things she couldn't understand.","With that Taoist's abilities, he could have easily escaped to the Min Yue Region, so why did he deliberately come to the capital to provoke trouble?","Wasn't he afraid of being captured and beheaded?","Or perhaps this Taoist was trying to hide in plain sight? Thinking the most dangerous place would be the safest?","Then the system chimed in, [You're overthinking it. He actually just wanted to rebel, doing everything he could to harm the royal family. Even if he had to die, he wanted to do his utmost to disrupt the court, preventing the Emperor from sleeping peacefully. He hoped to cause a major incident that would shake the foundation of the Great Liang dynasty.]","Yanshu: [Heh.]","This evil Taoist priest had quite ambitious goals, but now he's been put in his place, hasn't he?","But speaking of which, this old Taoist was truly cunning - surely he couldn't escape from the imperial prison again?","The system responded, [That's impossible now. The Emperor just ordered his tendons to be cut and his tongue to be removed. There's no way he could cause any more trouble.]","Yanshu breathed a sigh of relief, [That's good then.]","But come to think of it, if they'd already cut his tendons, why did they also cut out the Taoist's tongue?","System: [Because the Emperor said this old Taoist was spreading malicious rumors.]","Malicious rumors?","Hearing this, Yanshu became curious again and quickly asked, [What kind of malicious rumors? What else did this old Taoist do?]","The system replied, [The old Taoist just told the Emperor that the Former Emperor was killed by someone in the palace, not by him.]","Hearing this, Yanshu scoffed, [That's ridiculous! Who in the palace would dare kill the Former Emperor?]","The system clicked its tongue, [Emmm...]","Yanshu paused, suddenly feeling something was off, [...What's with those ellipses? ...Don't tell me it really was someone from the palace?]","System: [Correct.]","Yanshu's eyes widened, [Th-then who did it? Who would be so bold?!!]","System: [Who do you think in the palace would be that bold?]","Yanshu froze.","...Could it be her number one boss?","After all, besides the boss, she really couldn't think of anyone else.","The system said, [Correct again.]","Yanshu: [What???]","...","In the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","After traveling through the cold wind, mother and son had now returned to the hall.","After dismissing everyone else and closing the doors, the Empress Dowager sighed and finally said, \"I know that Your Majesty may have heard rumors about the Former Emperor's death. Rather than letting others tell you, it's better if I tell you myself.\"","Yuwen Lan said, \"Mother, you don't need to explain...\"","Before he could finish, the Empress Dowager shook her head and said, \"No, I never intended to hide this matter. Since it has been brought up, I might as well tell you everything. The longer we delay, the harder it will be for me.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan fell silent for a moment, then nodded, \"Please continue, Mother.\"","The Empress Dowager gathered her thoughts and said, \"Back then, the Former Emperor was deceived by this White Crane Taoist, becoming obsessed with pursuing immortality, completely neglecting the people's suffering. I and the court officials tried to persuade him, but it was useless. It would have been one thing if he just ignored state affairs - I could handle those for him. But one day, that Taoist convinced him to use unborn children for his elixir, and he actually agreed.\"","\"Where could they find so many unborn children? Moreover, the alchemy required large quantities, so that Taoist used the most vicious method. During that period, pregnant women in and around the capital were miscarrying every day. Those were all human lives, the lives of our people!\"","At this point, the Empress Dowager had become emotional, her eyes glistening with tears as she continued, \"But the Former Emperor turned a deaf ear to it all. Not only did he allow it, but he deliberately prevented the Imperial Guard from investigating. He was clearly that Taoist's accomplice, completely unworthy of being an emperor!\"","\"I am also a mother who has lost her own flesh and blood. I understand the pain of those pregnant women. Moreover, as the empress of Great Liang, how could I watch this happen without taking action? But no matter how I tried to persuade him, the Former Emperor wouldn't budge. Yet I still had to protect his reputation, preventing the court officials and common people from knowing, to avoid shaking the Yuwen family's rule.\"","At this point, the Empress Dowager closed her eyes, took a deep breath, and looked at Yuwen Lan again, \"Fortunately, by then you had grown into an adult. You had the responsibility of a ruler and a benevolent heart, capable of bearing great responsibility. So I took action, trading his one life for the peace of our people. Looking back now, my only regret is letting that Taoist escape back then, allowing him to take so many more lives over these years.\"","As she finished speaking, Yuwen Lan quickly said, \"No, this is not your fault, Mother. You did everything you could, and you did nothing wrong.\"","The Empress Dowager shook her head and said, \"Your Majesty need not say such things. From the moment I took that action, I knew this day would come. I never intended to hide or escape punishment - I just wanted to wait until the empire was stable before explaining the truth to you.\"","But Yuwen Lan shook his head again, \"No, he deserved his fate. You bear no guilt.\"","He was the emperor whom the people relied upon, and now he was also a father, about to welcome his own child.","Regardless of his role, he could not tolerate anyone harming such innocent young lives.","So even now, hearing the truth from the Empress Dowager, his resolve wouldn't waver in the slightest.","Therefore, he continued, \"The law applies equally to nobles and commoners alike, let alone the Former Emperor who, as a ruler, abused his power to commit evil - that's an even greater crime. So this is not your fault at all.\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager looked at him and said, \"That Your Majesty can treat me this way shows that I didn't raise you in vain.\"","Then she sighed and added, \"But back then... I had considered raising the King of Liaodong's child.\"","Yuwen Lan quickly replied, \"No, even then, Mother, you did nothing wrong. It was I who wasn't honest enough, causing you worry.\"","After all, weren't those misunderstandings caused by the Former Emperor and that Taoist?","Finally, he could only say, \"Let's not speak of past matters.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"Very well, we won't speak of it. Everything is good now, especially how Your Majesty can always see ahead clearly, which gives me great comfort.\"","However, she then changed her tone and continued, \"But this is still the crime of regicide, and today when that Taoist spoke of it, others heard.\"","Yuwen Lan quickly said, \"They won't dare speak of it. If Mother is worried, I can...\"","\"That's not necessary.\"","The Empress Dowager quickly waved her hand and said, \"They are loyal to Your Majesty, why harm innocent people for my sake? That would only make others lose faith in Your Majesty - you must always remember the lesson of the Former Emperor.\"","She sighed again and said, \"Everyone must die eventually, and I have lived long enough.\"","No...","Before Yuwen Lan could speak, there was a creaking sound as the hall doors were pushed open from outside, and Yanshu rushed in, crying out, \"No, don't!\"","In an instant, she had hurried before them.","This startled the Empress Dowager, and Yuwen Lan also looked surprised.","Before they could ask anything, she was already kneeling before them with tears streaming down her face. \"Please, Your Majesty, don't blame the Empress Dowager. The Former Emperor deserved his fate - the Empress Dowager was merely eliminating a threat to the people! She did it not only for the common folk but also for you. If the Former Emperor had continued to be deceived by that evil sorcerer, who knows what other atrocities he might have committed? You might not have even inherited the throne...\"","At these words, the Empress Dowager exclaimed in surprise, \"Yanshu, how did you come to know about this?\"","Yuwen Lan tried to speak, but before he could, Yanshu turned to him tearfully, \"Your Highness has suffered too much - you cannot be so cruel to her! Though she may not be your birth mother, she has raised you all these years and worked tirelessly to secure your place on the throne. Her grace knows no bounds! Do you know why you only received news of the Former Emperor's illness when you returned from the northwestern campaign? It was because the Empress Dowager wanted to ensure your smooth succession without any complications! Every move she made was for you and for the empire. How can you treat her this way now?\" She broke down sobbing.","Seeing her distress, the Empress Dowager momentarily forgot her confusion and hurriedly instructed the Emperor, \"Quick, make her stop crying - she's too delicate for this!\"","She pulled Yanshu into her embrace, consoling her, \"My dear child, I know your loyalty, how you care for me. The Emperor treats me well too, please don't be sad...\"","Yuwen Lan finally had a chance to speak, sighing, \"I never meant to blame Mother. Please stop crying.\"","But Yanshu, still nestled in the Empress Dowager's arms, looked at him through tear-filled eyes, \"But I just heard the Empress Dowager say she's lived long enough.\"","At these words, Yuwen Lan paused, looking toward the Empress Dowager.","The Empress Dowager also froze before sighing, \"Even if His Majesty doesn't blame me, I truly have lived long enough. I've experienced everything life has to offer...\"","But Yanshu shook her head vigorously through her tears, \"You haven't tasted sweetness yet - all you've known is bitterness!\"","In her heart, she grieved: betrayed by her husband, losing her own child, single-handedly holding together an empire for that foolish husband, while the Former Emperor continued to sabotage everything...","Then finding true love but being unable to be together, only able to gaze at Master Qi from afar, not daring to speak more than a few words...","What a wretched life - her beloved mentor had suffered too much!","Though Yanshu was grief-stricken, she hadn't completely lost her senses, so she kept these angry thoughts to herself.","But Yuwen Lan heard everything.","In this moment, his heart was filled with unprecedented bitterness.","Indeed, though he had become Emperor, he had never brought any joy to the mother who raised him.","The luxuries of palace life probably meant nothing to her anymore, which was why she had decided to confess everything to him, even at the cost of her life...","Swallowing his pain, his eyes reddened as he said, \"It's my fault. All these years, I never truly tried to understand Mother's feelings. But I've grown up by your side since childhood - if you leave me too, won't I be an orphan?\"","At these words, the Empress Dowager's eyes also welled with tears. She sighed and said, \"Nevertheless, this is still the crime of regicide. My presence in the palace will always be a liability. If Your Majesty cannot bear to let me end my life, perhaps you could send me to guard the imperial tombs, or to practice cultivation at the Yuzhen Temple.\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then shook his head.","Before he could speak, Yanshu cried out, \"Your Highness, you're still so young - why punish yourself this way? What's the point of guarding those tombs? And the Yuzhen Temple is no place for you! Even if you're tired of palace life, you deserve to live for yourself for once!\"","Her tears flowed freely again, distressing the Empress Dowager who quickly pulled out a handkerchief to wipe them away herself.","At this moment, Yuwen Lan spoke, \"I think Qi Shuguang is a good man. Why don't I send Mother to be with him, so he can keep you company?\"","What?","Both women froze at these words.","The Empress Dowager stared at him in shock for a long while before asking, \"What did Your Majesty say?\"","Yanshu had completely forgotten to cry, her tear-filled eyes barely remembering to blink as she thought in amazement, [\"...Heavens, he... he knows about this too?!\"]"]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116","paragraphs":["\"What... what did Your Majesty say?\"","Upon hearing Yuwen Lan's sudden words, the usually composed Empress Dowager was so shocked she began to stutter.","Yanshu also stared at him with equal astonishment.","Yuwen Lan paused before continuing, \"Mother, since you've grown weary of palace life, why not find someone suitable to spend the rest of your life with? Mr. Qi used to teach me, and since then, I've known him to be truly talented and learned. From our recent interactions, I can see even more clearly his noble character. Among all the people I've met, only he is worthy of you.\"","After these words, both women remained shocked.","The Empress Dowager thought to herself, [... He truly thinks Mr. Qi and I are a match?]","Yanshu pondered, [Does the Emperor really think highly of Mr. Qi? But he seemed to reject Mr. Qi before...]","Yuwen Lan, [...]","Well, the past is the past, and now is now...","At this moment, Yanshu quickly spoke up, \"Your Majesty is wise! I also believe Mr. Qi is of noble character and thoughtful nature. Moreover, the academy's environment is pleasant. If Mr. Qi could take care of the Empress Dowager, both Your Majesty and I would be at ease.\"","Hehe, regardless of what the Emperor's true intentions were, this was a rare opportunity. As a devoted shipper, she had to help push the Empress Dowager and her idol together!","After all, this might be their last chance.","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager paused again, chiding gently, \"This child...\"","But in her heart, she wondered, [Could I... really be with him?]","Yanshu nodded vigorously in her mind, but then the Empress Dowager sighed, saying, \"How could that be possible? I am the Empress Dowager, with so many eyes watching my every move...\"","Before she could finish, she suddenly stopped, surprised at having spoken her thoughts aloud.","Yanshu quickly responded, \"That's not a problem at all! Your Highness always wears a veil when leaving the palace, and none of the academy's students have ever seen your face. You could simply assume a different identity!\"","The Empress Dowager was taken aback, \"But... how would that work?\"","Yuwen Lan spoke up, \"As long as you can be happy, I will arrange everything.\"","The next day, news spread of the white crane sorcerer's capture. People learned that not only had he plotted rebellion and harmed common folk, but he had also posed as a physician and encouraged Consort Wang's family to send poison into the palace, which had poisoned the Empress Dowager.","The Emperor was furious and had the sorcerer executed at noon that day, much to the public's satisfaction.","However, this did not restore the Empress Dowager's health.","As days passed, her condition worsened, and even the miraculous physician Xun Lan was helpless.","During the old year's final day and the new year's first day, visitors who came to pay their respects couldn't see the Empress Dowager's face, only smelling the medicinal herbs in the palace.","Everyone worried, hoping that Consort Yi would soon give birth to a prince to bring some joy to the Empress Dowager.","In the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","It was the third day of the new year. After dealing with New Year's visitors during the day, Yanshu and Yuwen Lan came to the Palace of Benevolent Peace at night.","After dismissing the attendants, only three people remained in the hall.","They saw that after a period of bone manipulation surgery, the Empress Dowager's features had changed somewhat.","Those who saw her daily might not notice, but those who visited less frequently would notice that her nose bridge, cheekbones, and eye shape were different from before.","Soon, old acquaintances would no longer recognize the Empress Dowager.","Seeing Yanshu's pregnant belly, the Empress Dowager worried, \"You're so close to your due date, why are you still moving about? What if you suddenly go into labor?\"","Yanshu rubbed her belly and smiled, \"The imperial physician said walking around at this time is good for delivery. We're in the palace anyway, and the midwives and wet nurses are all ready. If I go into labor, so be it.\"","The Empress Dowager laughed, \"It's rare to see someone so carefree about this. But that's good - those with peace of mind are blessed.\"","Yanshu thanked the Empress Dowager with a smile, then Yuwen Lan asked, \"Mother, how have you been these days? Can you endure the bone manipulation surgery?\"","The Empress Dowager replied, \"I am well, Your Majesty need not worry. Consort Yi is the priority now - she must not be neglected.\"","Yuwen Lan responded, \"Rest assured, Mother. I will ensure both mother and child are well protected.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded and said, \"It's late, you should return to rest. It's cold outside, do be careful.\"","They agreed and left the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","As mentioned earlier to the Empress Dowager, walking was beneficial for labor at this time, so Yanshu didn't want to take a sedan chair and planned to walk back to Ganlu Palace.","Yuwen Lan accompanied her.","The air was somewhat humid tonight. Yanshu looked up at the sky, seeing heavy clouds obscuring the stars. Her eyes brightened as she said, \"Looks like it might snow again? Hehe, then we can have hotpot tomorrow night!\"","Yuwen Lan found it amusing and said, \"If you want to eat it, can't you have it any day? Why wait for snow?\"","Yanshu giggled, \"Because snow creates the perfect atmosphere for hotpot...\"","Before she could finish, she suddenly stopped.","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow, \"What's wrong? Why did you suddenly stop talking?\"","She stood still for a moment, then looked at him in disbelief, \"I... I think I'm going into labor...\"","Indeed, she had just felt a warm flow from her abdomen that wouldn't stop - this symptom seemed to be the legendary water breaking...","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan was startled and quickly called out, \"Someone, prepare the sedan chair!\"","But Yanshu stopped him, \"No, I can't move anymore. If I move, more amniotic fluid will flow out, and the baby will be in danger...\"","\"What?\"","Yuwen Lan paused, then without further thought, picked her up in his arms and rushed toward Ganlu Palace.","Although they had prepared thoroughly beforehand, only when the contractions actually began did Yanshu understand how painful childbirth could be.","Damn, it was really too painful. If it weren't for the system constantly reminding her in her mind not to scream to avoid losing strength and causing difficult labor, even showing her many frightening examples, she might have cried out.","Fortunately, she had eaten well at dinner, had three midwives guiding her, and had done well in her prenatal training. After enduring contractions for almost half the night, she finally gave birth to the baby.","It was a boy, pink and white, with a loud cry. When weighed, he was exactly six jin and six liang - an auspicious number.","Seeing both mother and child safe, Yuwen Lan was overjoyed. When the midwife wrapped the little one in swaddling clothes and handed him to him, he barely dared to move.","This was his baby, his child, the new life created by him and his beloved.","His life finally had continuation.","He bent down to kiss Yanshu's sweat-dampened forehead, saying softly, \"Thank you for your hard work.\"","Yanshu wearily opened her eyes and asked, \"What time is it?\"","Yuwen Lan replied gently, \"Dawn is approaching. Get some good rest. I'll watch over the baby.\"","Yanshu agreed and closed her eyes contentedly.","In her drowsy state, she suddenly realized something―","It seemed that since the contractions began, she hadn't heard anyone else's thoughts?","Huh, what was going on?","Had her mind-reading ability disappeared?","Or was she simply too exhausted?","However, having gone through a sleepless night, she was too tired and sleepy to think about this matter now, and finally fell asleep.","While Yanshu was resting, Yuwen Lan personally carried the baby to the Palace of Benevolent Peace.","The Empress Dowager, having worried all night after hearing about Yanshu's labor, was both surprised and delighted to see her son bringing her grandson personally.","Carefully holding the little one in her arms, the Empress Dowager could hardly take her eyes off him, examining him closely while exclaiming, \"The precious one looks exactly like Your Majesty did as a child. Look at these eye creases - they'll surely become big eyes. And these earlobes - they take after his mother, signs of a blessed life.\"","Yuwen Lan leaned in to look too, nodding as he listened.","Just then, the little one who had been sleeping soundly opened his eyes.","Mother and son were startled, thinking the baby would cry.","But the little one just quietly looked at them, without any fuss.","When he had looked enough, he closed his eyes and went back to sleep.","The Empress Dowager carefully handed the baby back to Yuwen Lan, saying softly, \"Now that I've seen him, I can rest easy. Your Majesty should take him back soon, lest he wakes up hungry.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded slightly and responded in a low voice, careful not to disturb the little one.","Unexpectedly, the Empress Dowager continued, \"Consort Yi has repeatedly rendered great service to Your Majesty, and she deserves proper rewards. In my opinion, she has a compassionate heart, a broad mind, and can distinguish right from wrong. Now that she has given birth to your first son, she is worthy of the position of Empress.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled, \"Mother, please rest assured. Tomorrow I will issue an imperial decree, and when both mother and child complete their full month, we shall hold the investiture ceremony.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"In that case, I can be at ease.\"","The emperor she had raised would surely treat his loved ones well, unlike that person from before.","The next morning, as promised, an imperial decree was issued: for the merit of bearing a son, Consort Yi would be elevated to Empress. Her father Zhong Rong was promoted to Duke Zhongyi, her mother was granted the title of First-Rank Noble Lady, and her brother became the Heir of Duke Zhongyi.","After the third-day celebration, the emperor personally named his firstborn son Yuwen Heng, signifying the perpetuation of the Yuwen clan's glory.","Simultaneously, he was established as the Crown Prince.","As days passed and the first month of the year ended, spring breezes began caressing the branches in the capital, and the weather turned warm.","Taking advantage of the gentle spring weather and coinciding with the full-month celebration of the Empress and the Crown Prince, the palace held both the grand ceremony for establishing the Empress and investing the Crown Prince.","Court officials and common people were all excited—the Great Liang Dynasty now had an Empress and a Crown Prince, bringing vitality to both court and common life.","However, not long after, news came of the Empress Dowager's passing, and the emperor ordered national mourning to express grief.","By mid-February, early spring flowers were blooming on the sunny hillsides.","Qi Shuguang stood beneath a tree, watching an approaching figure, struggling to contain the emotion in his eyes as he said, \"Welcome, my lady.\"","The Empress Dowager had already removed her veil and smiled at him, saying, \"We're family now, no need for such formalities from now on.\"","Qi Shuguang smiled in agreement and took her hand, leading her to where wildflowers bloomed abundantly.","Shouldn't human life be like these mountain flowers—as long as one lives, one should strive to bloom brilliantly?","Meanwhile in the palace, Yanshu, who had witnessed these scenes through the system, couldn't hold back her tears.","Oh my, her idol and the boss had finally reached this point—it was so difficult, so moving!","After crying for a while, she was about to wipe her tears when she looked down and saw her baby staring at her with pouting lips, seemingly about to cry.","Yanshu paused, wondering what was wrong. Had the little one secretly wet himself?","But when she checked the swaddling clothes, they were completely dry.","Besides, the little one had just finished nursing, so he shouldn't be hungry.","She asked, \"Baby, why are you looking at Mother like that?\"","Of course, the little one couldn't answer her yet, only gazing at her with his grape-black eyes, appearing quite aggrieved.","Yanshu: \"...\"","Alas, being a first-time mother without her mind-reading abilities, she really couldn't guess what this milk-drinking baby was thinking.","Well, since the little one wasn't crying, she might as well continue enjoying her favorite couple's story.","Having finished crying from being moved earlier, she now felt content—the Empress Dowager boss had finally gotten together with her idol, and they could support each other for the rest of their lives.","After smiling fondly for a while, she looked down again to find her baby grinning at her.","Yanshu became excited, \"Baby can smile?\"","Upon hearing this, the little one paused, then smiled at her again.","Mother and son shared a moment of joy, and Yanshu suddenly realized something—perhaps the little one was sensing her emotions?","When she had tears in her eyes earlier, he pouted; now that she was smiling, he smiled too?","Ah! Upon this realization, she was startled—could it be that her lost mind-reading ability had transferred to her son?","Thinking of this, her eyes widened with joy as she exclaimed, \"This is amazing!\"","As she spoke, the little one smiled again.","Yanshu became even more convinced.","It must be true!","Because the baby was still young, he probably couldn't understand people's thoughts, but he could sense their happiness.","This way, as he grew older and more aware, he would be able to discern people's good and bad intentions, and protect himself!","How wonderful!","Yanshu was overjoyed and began showering her baby with kisses.","Just then, Yuwen Lan entered the hall.","Seeing her like this, he curiously asked, \"What's happening?\"","She replied, \"Nothing special, just that our baby is so clever, I'm happy.\"","Ahem, better not tell him about the baby's mind-reading abilities, or her own past mind-reading powers might be exposed.","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan was also pleasantly surprised—so his mind-reading ability really was hereditary?","He deliberately asked, \"How is our baby clever?\"","Yanshu responded, \"Baby and I are connected heart-to-heart—when I'm happy, he's happy.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Indeed clever!\"","He then took the chubby little one into his arms and smiled, \"Is our baby that amazing?\"","The little one grinned at him in response.","Yuwen Lan felt his heart melt with tenderness as he bent down to kiss the baby's milk-scented cheek.","Yanshu proudly commented from the side, \"Our baby is really extraordinary!\"","Yuwen Lan hummed in agreement and kissed her milk-scented cheek as well, saying, \"Just as extraordinary as you.\""]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117","paragraphs":["As days passed by, the little Crown Prince Yuwen Heng of Great Liang grew day by day.","The little one was quite clever, learning to smile before two months old, and by three months, he could already babble in conversation with others.","Of course, Yanshu deserved the most credit for this achievement. Since her confinement period, being bored, she would chat with the baby daily, telling him all sorts of gossip. Watching his mother's mouth move constantly, the little one naturally learned quickly.","For instance, tonight, as Yuwen Lan emerged from the bathhouse, he witnessed mother and son engaged in parent-child communication on the bed—","Yanshu said, \"My dear child, I heard that in the recent Imperial Academy examinations, the Jiangning Communications Commissioner's youngest son didn't study properly and ranked last, even getting caned by the teacher. How embarrassing! You mustn't be like him in the future.\"","Baby: \"...ah...ah.\"","Yanshu continued, \"I heard the Deputy Minister of Personnel's son argued with his mother, and the next day when he went out, he fell and knocked out his front teeth. His looks are ruined now, and he'll probably have trouble finding a wife. You must never argue with your mother in the future!\"","Baby: \"...ah...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","The baby was still so young, yet this was how mother and son communicated daily?","Before he could speak, Yanshu placed the little one in his arms, saying, \"Your Majesty, please watch the baby while I take a bath.\"","Yuwen Lan was more than willing and nodded in agreement, carefully holding his chubby son.","Now it was time for father-son bonding.","Yuwen Lan carefully examined his son in his arms, noticing that after not seeing him for just one day, the little one seemed to have grown bigger, with bright eyes clearly taking after him.","But good looks alone weren't enough, so he seriously began, \"Heng, as the heir to Great Liang, you must always remember the words of the sages.\"","The little one looked at him with dark eyes, responding earnestly, \"...ah...ah.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded with satisfaction, \"Good attitude.\"","He cleared his throat and began reciting to the little one, \"If the Son of Heaven is not benevolent, he cannot protect the four seas; if the feudal lords are not benevolent, they cannot protect their ancestral temples; if officials are not benevolent, they cannot protect their clan temples; if common people are not benevolent, they cannot protect their four limbs.\"","The little one paused, then after a moment said, \"...ah...\"","Yuwen Lan continued, \"One who shares in the people's joy will find the people sharing in their joy; one who shares in the people's worries will find the people sharing in their worries. To share joy with all under heaven, to share worries with all under heaven - yet never to achieve kingship, such a thing has never happened.\"","After finishing this passage, he noticed the little one just staring at him blankly, without responding for a long time.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","...What did this mean?","After some thought, he decided his son's attitude was probably correct - after all, the words of the sages shouldn't be taken lightly, and should be listened to seriously and solemnly.","So he continued, \"The gentleman preserves benevolence in his heart and propriety in his conduct. The benevolent person loves others; the courteous person respects others. Those who love others are constantly loved by them; those who respect others are constantly respected by them.\"","After finishing this passage, he looked down again, only to see the little one blink a few times before gradually closing his eyes, not opening them again even after waiting a while.","He had fallen asleep.","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Just then, Yanshu, fresh from her bath, entered the hall and glanced at father and son, exclaiming, \"Your Majesty is amazing, putting the baby right to sleep! Hehe, this must be the result of prenatal education!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","So it turned out that all those prenatal education sessions from the grand academicians and Imperial Academy instructors were actually meant to be lullabies for the baby?","Ah, the trials of being a father.","But... it was good that the little one was asleep.","He carefully placed the baby in the small bed beside their own, tucked him in carefully, and gently patted his belly. Only after ensuring the little one was sound asleep did he withdraw his hand.","Then, he suddenly lifted Yanshu by the waist and quickly carried her to their bed.","Yanshu was startled and didn't have time to cry out before being caught in his kiss...","Mmm...","Now, their time together had finally begun...","As several more days passed, when spring was in full bloom in the capital, the little Crown Prince reached his hundredth day.","Though it had only been a hundred days, the baby had already more than doubled his initial weight, becoming white and chubby like a little winter melon.","Of course, the little one was much more active than a winter melon. When excited, he would wave his arms and kick his legs with strength, and his little voice was quite loud.","However, due to the Grand Empress Dowager's passing, the Emperor decided not to hold a formal celebration. Nevertheless, since the hundredth day was still an important milestone, a few close relatives and friends were invited to the palace for a gathering.","The first to arrive were from the Empress's family at Duke Zhongyi's Mansion - the Crown Prince's maternal grandmother Madam Zhu and great-grandmother Old Madam Li.","Madam Zhu hadn't seen her little grandson for some time, and for Old Madam Li, this was her first time meeting her great-grandson. Upon entering the hall, both were immediately drawn to the little one.","The little one was particularly accommodating to his grandmother and great-grandmother, not only showing them bright smiles but also allowing his grandmother to hold him. Usually, only his mother and wet nurse could hold him in the palace, and even palace maids like Renchun and Lianxin had to rely on luck - one wrong move could trigger a bout of crying.","At this moment, Madam Zhu bounced her grandson in her arms and praised, \"The little Crown Prince has gained good weight, clearly easy to feed.\"","Just as she finished speaking, the little one looked at his grandmother and made an \"ah\" sound, both sweet and clear.","This delighted the grandmother immensely, and she said, \"Is the little Crown Prince talking to me?\"","The little one made another \"ah\" sound, seeming quite ready for conversation.","Old Madam Li watched longingly and came forward to touch the Crown Prince's chubby little hand, sighing, \"For this old woman to shake hands with the Crown Prince today, my life has been worthwhile.\"","Yanshu quickly said, \"Listen to what you're saying, Grandmother. Heng is your great-grandson, why so formal?\"","Just as she finished speaking, the little one also chimed in with, \"Ah... @#%¥#&*...\"","He actually babbled quite a string of sounds.","Yanshu's eyes lit up, and she laughed, \"Look, Grandmother, Heng wants to chat with you!\"","Old Madam Li was also deeply honored and quickly said to the baby, \"Very well, very well, this old woman humbly accepts Your Highness's command.\"","This made everyone in the hall burst into laughter.","After the laughter subsided, the Grand Princess, Ankang County Lord, and other royal relatives arrived, and Old Madam Li and Madam Zhu tactfully stepped aside.","Today the little Crown Prince was the center of attention. After the Grand Princess and her daughter led everyone in paying respects to Yanshu, they all gathered around the little prince.","Like his maternal grandmother Madam Zhu, when the Grand Princess saw her little nephew, she couldn't help but praise, \"My, the Crown Prince is truly easy to feed, look at this little body, how enviable!\"","The little one was also very accommodating to his great-aunt, opening his mouth to make an \"ah\" sound.","The Grand Princess praised again, \"Such a clever little Crown Prince, already knowing how to chat with people?\"","Everyone joined in the praise.","However, the Grand Princess then sighed, \"If only the Grand Empress Dowager were still here. She would have been so happy to see the Crown Prince being so clever.\"","At these words, everyone felt melancholic, and Yanshu could only put on a regretful expression.","Ankang County Lord quickly consoled, \"The Grand Empress Dowager's spirit in heaven must be blessing His Majesty, the Empress, and the little Crown Prince.\"","At this, everyone hurriedly agreed.","Just then, Fu Hai entered the hall carrying a brocade box, announcing, \"Your Highness, this is a congratulatory gift for the Crown Prince from Songhe Academy. His Majesty requests your review.\"","Songhe Academy?","Yanshu's heart stirred, but her expression remained unchanged as she said, \"Thank you for your trouble, Chief Steward.\"","She then had Renchun accept it.","Although there was no formal hundred-day celebration this year, the court officials all remembered the Crown Prince's hundredth day and had already sent congratulatory gifts, so this gift from Songhe Academy wasn't out of place.","However, everyone was curious about what gift this world-renowned academy would present to the little Crown Prince.","Fortunately, Yanshu was generous enough to have it opened immediately.","Inside the box was an intricately carved peach pit strung with red thread, meant to ward off evil spirits for the little prince.","Additionally, there was a copy of \"Mencius.\"","When Yanshu picked it up and opened it, she immediately smelled the clear scent of ink.","The text wasn't printed but handwritten, with neat and careful calligraphy that showed the writer's dedication.","Yanshu wondered in her heart if this might have been personally written by the Grand Empress Dowager.","The system said, \"That's right, this book was indeed handwritten by the Empress Dowager, and the peach pit was personally carved by your idol. The red string on it was also hand-twisted by the Empress Dowager herself.\"","Yanshu was deeply moved, imagining the beautiful scene of the two great figures - one reading and writing, the other carving the peach pit and twisting the red string.","Oh, this must be what it means to envy love more than immortality - they finally found their happiness!","Around her, everyone was praising how creative and meaningful the gift was, while Yanshu winked at her baby and whispered in her heart, \"Look, this is from Grandma and Great-Uncle for you, they've been thinking of you all along!\"","Though the little one heard his mother's voice and didn't quite understand the meaning, he still happily waved his chubby arms and kicked his little legs.","On the first rest day after the little prince's hundred-day celebration, as spring warmth arrived, the Emperor and Empress changed into casual clothes and took their baby out of the palace.","The carriage headed towards Pine Crane Mountain in the outskirts, and during the swaying journey, the little prince went from excited to heavy-eyed, and eventually fell fast asleep.","When he woke up from his satisfying nap, he found himself in an unfamiliar new place.","There were no grand palaces here, but neat houses; no exotic flowers and trees like in the imperial garden, but comfortable little flowers and grass.","Most importantly, a kind grandmother was holding him, examining him carefully with eyes full of love.","Seeing him awake, grandmother's eyes brightened as she called him tenderly, \"Heng'er, you're awake?\"","The little one didn't know yet that there were very few people in the world who could call him \"Heng'er.\"","However, he felt this voice was very familiar, as if he had heard it somewhere before, giving him an inexplicable sense of security.","So the little one opened his mouth, showing his pink gums, and greeted grandmother with an \"Ah... ah.\"","Grandmother was also delighted, kissing his forehead and saying, \"Good child, just like your father when he was little.\"","Though he still couldn't understand, he knew grandmother was chatting with him.","Mmm, he liked it when people chatted with him, especially when they smiled.","So he opened his mouth and smiled again.","He accidentally put too much effort into it and giggled out loud, causing the adults around to exclaim in delight, coming over to hold and kiss him.","Mmm, the little prince thought, he liked this place where everyone's love surrounded him like sunshine, making him feel warm all over.","It was wonderful indeed."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 2","Although there were wet nurses in the palace, Yanshu always insisted on nursing her little one herself after giving birth.","The bond between mother and child grew deeper each day, and their nursing time became the most intimate moment between them.","However, this meant she had to be careful with her diet, avoiding foods that could cause inflammation or were too cooling.","Compared to before, her diet had become much simpler.","Of course, for the sake of her adorable little one's healthy growth, these restrictions were bearable. However, the little one became increasingly curious about food, gradually becoming unsatisfied with just milk and showing intense interest in what adults were eating.","Especially when seeing adults eat, the baby would immediately become fixated, not only staring intently but sometimes even drooling.","This was truly amusing, but alas, the little one was still too young and could only drink milk for now.","However, as the baby grew day by day, their abilities increased too, from initially kicking around happily to gradually being able to grab things.","For instance, on this day during their mother-child bonding time, while Yanshu was holding the baby and humming a tune, she suddenly felt thirsty. She picked up her teacup for a sip to moisten her throat, but before it reached her lips, the chubby baby suddenly reached out.","Fortunately, she was quick enough to move the cup away, or the baby's little paws would have surely dipped into her tea.","However, the tea still spilled onto her dress hem.","Rendong and others were startled and quickly came forward asking, \"Your Highness, were you scalded?\"","Before Yanshu could answer, the chubby baby suddenly giggled, completely unaware of their mischief.","Yanshu was both amused and exasperated. She told Rendong she was fine, put down the teacup, and said seriously to the little one, \"Baby, you mustn't grab Mommy's cup, it's very dangerous.\"","The little one thought Mommy was just chatting and immediately responded carelessly with \"Ah... woo...\" while grinning.","Yanshu shook her head and decided to tell the baby, \"Once there was a playful child, just like you, who grabbed their mother's teacup, and their little hand got burned and blistered, making them cry very loudly...\"","Perhaps because the story was too long, the baby paused for a moment before chattering again, \"Ah... @#¥%#@&*...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Thinking it wasn't scary enough, she continued seriously, \"There was another child who always tried to grab adults' food. One time they got a terrible stomach ache and lost all their cute baby fat, and none of the aunties, sisters, or grandma liked them anymore...\"","The baby stared at mommy blankly for a moment, then babbled again while excitedly waving their little arms, seemingly saying, \"Don't worry, Mommy, my baby fat is very solid, it won't go away!\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Well, it seemed intimidation wasn't working, so she switched to heart-to-heart communication, sighing, \"Mommy is only drinking tea, which is bitter and you wouldn't like it. Since I'm nursing you, I can only eat bland food, which isn't very tasty either. You don't know how much Mommy is suffering.\"","After she finished speaking, she noticed the baby had finally stopped smiling and was just staring at her blankly, making an \"ah\" sound that might have been meant as comfort.","Oh? Had it finally worked?","Encouraged, Yanshu couldn't help but continue talking to her son—","\"Baby, I heard there's a new lamb barbecue shop on East Street. Their lambs come from northern pastures, the meat is tender with no gamey taste, freshly slaughtered and grilled daily. That tender lamb meat sizzling on charcoal, sprinkled with cumin, salt, and chili powder, it's absolutely delicious! Mommy could eat a whole leg of lamb and twenty lamb skewers without getting full. It would be even better with two grilled flatbreads – those breads brushed with lamb fat, grilled until golden and crispy outside, then split open with a knife and stuffed with lamb skewers. One bite gives you that crispy exterior, fragrant interior, and juicy tender lamb meat. It's absolutely amazing!\"","After she finished, she noticed the baby was stunned, forgetting even to make their usual \"ah\" sound.","But Yanshu was already lost in her daydream and continued, \"Oh right, and there's the knife-cut noodles on Cotton Market Street. Those noodles are thin, smooth, and chewy, topped with a spoonful of meat sauce and mixed together – it's incredibly delicious! I could easily eat three bowls now!\"","After these words, the baby finally recovered and started babbling again.","Then they heard mommy say, \"You want to eat too, don't you? We'll go out to eat someday!\"","The baby made a loud \"ah\" sound and started excitedly kicking their legs and waving their arms.","But then Yanshu paused and suddenly said, \"...Oh right, you can't eat meat yet, nor noodles. We'll have to wait until after you're weaned to go eat.\"","She felt quite regretful, after all, if the baby couldn't eat, she couldn't either.","Seemingly sensing her emotions, the baby paused, then suddenly pouted, babbling disapprovingly.","Yanshu sighed and said, \"Being unhappy won't help, we have to think about your health. Once you turn one year old and we wean you, it'll be fine. It's just eight months away, that'll go by quickly.\"","What? Eight months?","Hearing this, everyone in the hall sighed for the little prince—","After all, he was only four months old now, and eight months was twice as long as he had been alive. The little Crown Prince would have quite a wait ahead of him.","But just as they were thinking this, the little Crown Prince suddenly burst into loud tears, seemingly expressing his dissatisfaction.","It was about feeding time anyway, so Yanshu dismissed everyone, opened her clothes to nurse the baby, and comforted him while feeding, \"Don't be impatient, baby. As they say, hope gives us motivation. Let's focus on drinking milk for now, grow up quickly with good nutrition, and the lamb legs and knife-cut noodles will come eventually.\"","The baby continued making small whimpering sounds while nursing, still appearing quite disgruntled.","As days passed, when the little Crown Prince turned six months old, he could finally eat some rice porridge.","On his first try, the baby was very excited, finishing half a bowl of rice porridge in the blink of an eye, making \"ah ah\" sounds to chat with his mother while eating, as if saying, \"This is delicious! I want to eat more tomorrow!\"","This continued for several days with the same enthusiasm and no discomfort, showing an excellent appetite.","The wet nurses and palace maids couldn't help but praise that babies who eat well grow well, and with such a good appetite, the little Crown Prince would surely grow up strong and healthy.","The little one was also very happy, and as time passed, he tried more and more supplementary foods. His body indeed grew stronger and more robust, becoming increasingly adorable.","That's why no matter how busy his father was during the day, he would return to the central palace early every evening to personally hold the little one.","Of course, this was also his mother's happiest moment.","Mainly because Yanshu increasingly discovered that the Emperor was truly a master at putting the baby to sleep.","As the little one grew bigger, his energy levels increased, making it difficult to get him to nap during the day. Usually, it would take her or the wet nurse half a day to get the baby to sleep.","But the Emperor was different. Once the baby was handed to him, within the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, the little one would be sound asleep, so deeply that even thunder wouldn't wake him – it was quite miraculous.","For instance, this evening, as soon as Yuwen Lan entered the hall, Yanshu immediately handed the baby to him, saying, \"Your Majesty, I've been waiting. He's all yours now. I'm going to take a bath.\"","With that, she went to the washroom to enjoy her flower petal spa.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","He looked down at the baby in his arms and said, \"Look how Heng'er has worn your mother out, making her so eager to leave.\"","The baby made an \"ah\" sound, happily grinning at his father while showing off the two white baby teeth that had just emerged on his lower gums.","Yuwen Lan's heart melted with love. He bent down to kiss the baby's cheek and said, \"Heng'er seems to have gained some weight again. You must have been eating well lately.\"","The baby responded, \"#¥%...&\"","Yuwen Lan nodded again, \"Indeed, but a man of great character cannot merely focus on eating. He must also dedicate himself to studying.\"","The little one responded with incomprehensible babbling, \"@#$%$#&*&...\"","The tiny child hadn't yet realized that his father was about to give him another lesson.","Although the little one fell asleep at the first mention of the sage's teachings, Yuwen Lan wasn't discouraged. He believed in persistence, thinking that even if the child couldn't understand, the gradual influence, like spring rain nurturing the earth, would eventually show results.","Look how far they'd come - they'd progressed from the \"Mencius\" all the way to the \"Han Feizi.\"","He was full of confidence.","Clearing his throat, he began, \"Safety and danger lie in right and wrong, not in strength and weakness. Survival depends on substance, not numbers.\"","The little one babbled, \"@#$@*&*...\"","His expression had grown serious.","Yuwen Lan continued, \"Don't burden your mind with cleverness, nor yourself with selfish desires. Entrust order and chaos to law and strategy, and right and wrong to reward and punishment.\"","The little one mumbled, \"$@#...\"","His voice growing fainter.","Yuwen Lan pressed on, \"The masses assist with their strength, those nearby bond with sincerity, those far away are drawn by reputation, and the respected lead with authority.\"","The little one had stopped talking, his eyelids growing heavy.","Yuwen Lan persisted with one more line, \"One with talent but no authority, though worthy, cannot control the unworthy. Thus, a foot-long piece of wood placed atop a high mountain overlooks a thousand-foot ravine - not because the wood is long, but because its position is high.\"","The little one had fallen asleep.","Yuwen Lan nodded, feeling that his efforts were indeed showing progress.","After all, the little one had improved from falling asleep after three sentences to lasting four sentences.","The child showed promise.","As days passed, considering the little one's development, when the baby reached ten months, Yanshu stopped nursing.","After all, the little one was eating solid foods well and had a wet nurse, so she decided not to force herself to continue.","However, as the capital had grown cooler in late autumn, she couldn't take the little one out anymore, so she had the imperial kitchen roast a leg of lamb for a feast.","Hehe, after ten months of restraint, she could finally return to her days of hearty eating!","The imperial chef's skills were exceptional. The freshly roasted lamb leg, marinated beforehand and sprinkled with cumin and chili, had a crispy exterior that carried a subtle honey sweetness - truly delectable.","While she ate with gusto, the little one beside her grew increasingly agitated. Watching his mother devour the meat made him terribly hungry. He let out loud \"ah-ah\" cries and nearly stood up from his little wooden chair.","He was using all his might to express - \"Mother! What delicious food is this! Let your baby have a bite!!!\"","Yanshu felt guilty, but since the lamb was roasted rather than minced, the little one couldn't eat it. She could only give him a lamb bone to appease him.","The inexperienced little one happily accepted it and began gnawing away.","As he gnawed, he babbled on.","The meaning was probably -","This hard-to-bite thing is so special.","But why does it seem like I'm not getting anything to eat no matter how much I gnaw?","Grown-up food is so strange."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119","paragraphs":["As the days went by, the Little Crown Prince of Liang Country gradually celebrated his first birthday, learned to walk, and could clearly call out \"daddy\" and \"mommy.\"","His little body grew taller, and the soft baby fat on him became more solid, making him look less like a little pumpkin.","With the weather warming up again, early summer arrived, and Yanshu and Yuwen Lan took the little one to visit Grandma.","Little Heng'er slept on the carriage as usual, waking up when the carriage came to a halt.","Stepping out of the carriage, he saw the familiar and comfortable courtyard, and dear Grandma waiting for him at the gate.","Mommy smiled and encouraged him, \"Heng'er, walk to Grandma by yourself.\"","The little one nodded and trotted over to Grandma, calling out \"Grandma, Grandma\" with his sweet baby voice.","His adorable voice could melt anyone's heart.","Grandma couldn't stop smiling, bending down to scoop the little one into her arms, saying, \"Heng'er is good, Heng'er is so smart.\"","Little Heng'er giggled and echoed, \"Smart...\"","This made Grandma laugh even more, unable to resist kissing his chubby cheeks.","Then, the little one reached into the small pocket on his chest, fumbling around until he pulled out a sweet potato candy and handed it to Grandma, saying, \"Grandma, candy.\"","Grandma was surprised and asked, \"Is this for Grandma?\"","Little Heng'er nodded vigorously.","Yanshu explained beside them, \"This morning, when Heng'er heard we were coming to see Grandma, he put on his pocket, already planning to share with you.\"","This warmed the Empress Dowager's heart, and she quickly took the candy, smiling at her grandson, \"Then Grandma thanks Heng'er. Grandma will keep this candy and eat it slowly.\"","Little Heng'er hummed in agreement and reached into his pocket again, pulling out two milk-flavored fruit candies and offering them to Grandpa, saying, \"Grandpa, eat.\"","Qi Shuguang was taken aback, feeling honored, \"Are these for me too?\"","Yanshu quickly added with a smile, \"Since Grandma and Grandpa are together, if there's Grandma's, there's naturally Grandpa's. Please take them.\"","Qi Shuguang agreed and accepted the candies.","The little one was very happy, struggling to get down from Grandma's arms and walking into the courtyard on his own.","While the adults exchanged greetings, Little Heng'er curiously looked around, soon spotting the white, fluffy little rabbits in the corner.","The little one, already quite knowledgeable, pointed at them with his chubby hand, saying, \"Bunny...\"","This made Grandma's eyes light up, \"Heng'er knows rabbits?\"","Yanshu explained with a smile, \"I had some children's books drawn and let Heng'er look at them every day. There are also some rabbits and cats in the imperial garden that Heng'er often plays with, so he can tell them apart.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"That's very good.\"","Then, the little one trotted over to a corner, plucked a green, oily little grass, and held it in his chubby hand, saying, \"Feed bunny.\"","The Empress Dowager couldn't help but laugh, \"Heng'er even knows how to feed the bunnies? What a clever little one.\"","The clever Little Heng'er, intent on feeding the bunnies, had already trotted over to the rabbit cage.","Yuwen Lan and Yanshu quickly followed.","After all, who wouldn't like to feed such cute bunnies?","While the family of three was busy feeding the rabbits, the Empress Dowager picked some fresh vegetables from the garden and washed them clean with clear spring water. So, after feeding the rabbits, the family started feeding themselves.","The freshly picked cucumbers were crisp and sweet, and the apricots were soft and fragrant. Yanshu praised as she ate, \"Mother really knows how to grow vegetables. The vegetables here taste especially good.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"The vegetables grown with mountain spring water naturally taste different. But I'm just an amateur; he's the one who does the actual work. I just help out occasionally.\"","Yanshu quickly added, \"Mr. Qi is indeed skilled in everything. Truly impressive!\"","Hehe, it had been a year and a half since they left the palace. The Empress Dowager's complexion had clearly improved, indicating a comfortable life, which made Yanshu, a CP fan, very pleased.","As she was feeling happy, she saw her son, who had been playing with Grandpa, walk over with a flower in his chubby hand, saying to her, \"Mommy, flower.\"","Yanshu's heart warmed, and she quickly took the flower, kissed the little one's cheek, and said, \"Thank you, my little darling. You're Mommy's precious baby.\"","Little Heng'er giggled.","Meanwhile, Yuwen Lan said, \"Did you forget about Daddy, Heng'er?\"","The little one had given something to everyone today except him.","Was he not important in the little one's heart?","Upon hearing this, Little Heng'er paused.","This question seemed a bit difficult for a one-and-a-half-year-old.","Seeing this, Yanshu quickly explained to her son, \"What should Heng'er give Daddy?\"","Finally understanding, Little Heng'er walked up to Daddy, opened his arms, and said, \"Hug...\"","Yuwen Lan raised an eyebrow. Everyone else got gifts, but he only got a hug?","Of course, who could resist such a cute little one? He bent down and picked up the little one.","Then, the little one hugged his head and kissed his cheek.","Yuwen Lan was stunned, but Yanshu laughed, \"So Heng'er wants to give Daddy a kiss?\"","The Empress Dowager also laughed, \"What a clever little one.\"","Little Heng'er giggled.","The laughter echoed in the adults' ears like a clear spring in the mountains.","Yuwen Lan also smiled and returned the kiss to the little one.","Well, what a clever little one, just like his mommy.","The family of three spent a pleasant afternoon on the mountain. After dinner, they said their goodbyes and left.","With the courtyard quiet again, the Empress Dowager planned to clean up the dishes, only to find Qi Shuguang already squatting by the water basin, washing them.","She quickly walked over and said, \"Today's meal was prepared by you, let me wash the dishes.\"","He replied, \"Your hands are delicate, let me do it.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"What's delicate about it? It's not like it was in the past.\"","Qi Shuguang said, \"Whether now or in the past, you've always been the same in my heart. Let me handle these rough chores.\"","The Empress Dowager paused, then sighed, \"You're just flattering me. I'm clearly old.\"","He said, \"Nonsense, you're not old at all. Just right in my heart.\"","This man, he's getting better and better at saying things that make one blush.","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"Smooth talker.\"","Qi Shuguang didn't say anything, just continued washing the dishes with a smile.","After a while, the Empress Dowager said, \"By the way, the academy will have a field break soon. Let's go back to Langya this year.\"","Qi Shuguang paused, \"Why think of going to Langya?\"","The Empress Dowager sighed, \"You've been away for two years, it's time to pay respects to your parents. Langya isn't far, if we hurry, we can make a round trip in about half a month.\"","He said, \"Half a month of travel might be too tiring for you.\"","The Empress Dowager immediately raised an eyebrow, \"How could I be tired? You just said I'm not old. Or, do you not want me to pay respects to your parents?\"","Qi Shuguang quickly said, \"How could that be?\"","The Empress Dowager said, \"Then let's go back. I've been in the capital for so many years, I'd like to see more of the world.\"","Hearing this, Qi Shuguang finally nodded, \"Alright, let's go back. I'll make arrangements tomorrow.\"","So it was decided. A few days later, when the academy had its field break, the two of them set off for Langya.","With ample time, Qi Shuguang drove the carriage himself, with Yuwen Lan's arranged guards following closely for safety. They traveled leisurely, stopping to enjoy the scenery and local delicacies, having a wonderful time.","Yanshu was very envious. She wanted to travel and taste the world too!","So, during the evening family time, she seriously told her son, \"Baby, you have to study hard and take good care of the house for us in the future. Mommy also wants to travel with Daddy!\"","Little Heng'er, wearing his pajamas and lying next to his mother, nodded understandingly with his sweet baby voice, \"Mm-hmm.\"","Meanwhile, Yuwen Lan, who was leaning on the bed reading, quietly breathed a sigh of relief.","Fortunately, now she was considering taking him along on the trip.","\"Are you planning to take me along as well?\" Yuwen Lan asked, feigning ignorance.","To his surprise, Yanshu replied, \"Of course! I don't know how to drive a carriage.\"","Yuwen Lan was taken aback. \"???\"","So, after all that, she just wanted him to be the coachman?","The Little Crown Prince of Liang Country was growing bigger and smarter by the day.","For instance, after experimenting and observing, he finally realized that bones were not as tasty as meat. Hence, the next time his mother ate a lamb leg, he was no longer content with gnawing on the bones.","However, now that the little one had about a dozen teeth, he could also enjoy meat. Meals like minced meat mixed with rice, shrimp paste, fish paste, and noodle slices were all within his dietary repertoire.","Thus, he could now join the adults for all three daily meals.","Moreover, the little one had recently started eating with his own little spoon. In just a month, he had progressed from smearing food all over his face to accurately placing it in his mouth.","Truly a little master of dining.","Of course, the little one was also at an age of intense curiosity, showing interest in all foods he had yet to try.","For example, during lunch one day, there was a dish of boiled fish, which Yanshu had specially ordered. As soon as the dish was served, the little one's eyes were immediately drawn to it.","He thought, \"That dish looks so bright and beautiful, and it smells so fragrant. It must be delicious.\"","However, why was his mother eating it herself and not giving him any?","He stretched out his chubby little hand, pointing at the boiled fish and said, \"Fish...\"","To his surprise, his mother replied, \"This fish is spicy, Little Heng'er can't eat it. Just eat what's in your own bowl. Today's meat paste is also made from fish.\"","The little one paused, then remembered that he hadn't finished his own meal and continued eating.","But after a while, he looked up again and saw the boiled fish, and the thought of it resurfaced.","That fragrant fish, he really wanted to try it too!","But his mother didn't give him any. What should he do?","The little one thought for a moment, then took advantage of his mother talking to Rendong and reached out with his little spoon to scoop some from his mother's bowl.","Rendong, keeping a watchful eye, immediately called out, \"Little Crown Prince!\"","He was about to stop the little one.","When Yanshu turned around, she saw her son holding a small spoon with spicy broth and about to put it in his mouth.","She was about to stop him too, but then thought, \"Let him try it first.\"","So, everyone refrained from intervening, watching as the little one brought the spoon to his mouth and licked it with his little tongue.","Time seemed to stand still for a few seconds, then the dining table was filled with loud wails.","His tongue!","The little one felt that his tongue was in pain!","Sob, sob, sob. His mother was right. Grown-up food was so scary!"]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120","paragraphs":["Traveling south from the capital, after savoring local delicacies and admiring scenic views along the way, the Empress Dowager and Qi Shuguang finally arrived in Langya.","The couple didn't forget the purpose of their journey and immediately went to pay respects to their parents upon arrival.","The Qi Family's ancestral graves were located halfway up the mountain, with the family's old house - where Qi Shuguang grew up - situated at the foot.","Since they were already there, the Empress Dowager naturally wanted to take a look, so she suggested, \"It's still early, why don't we stay at the house for a few days?\"","To her surprise, Qi Shuguang seemed hesitant.","The Empress Dowager noticed this and raised an eyebrow, asking, \"What's wrong? Afraid I'll embarrass you in front of your neighbors?\"","Qi Shuguang responded with an awkward smile, \"No, I'm worried I'll embarrass you.\"","\"Oh?\" the Empress Dowager arched her brow. \"How so?\"","He explained, \"When I resigned from my official position and returned home years ago, the neighbors assumed I had been dismissed for some wrongdoing. Then, remaining unmarried for so many years made them view me as an unfilial son. In short... I'm not exactly well-regarded in the village...\"","After hearing this, the Empress Dowager paused, looking at him with complex emotions. \"So in the end, it's all because of me?\"","As Qi Shuguang tried to protest, she took his hand and said, \"You've done nothing wrong. There's no reason you can't return to your own home. Don't worry.\"","With that, she headed down the mountain.","Upon reaching the Qi Family's old residence, the Empress Dowager surveyed the property. The houses were built with gray bricks, and the courtyard was spacious, indicating the family's former middle-class status.","Though long uninhabited, the property wasn't overgrown with weeds but rather well-maintained.","Qi Shuguang explained, \"When I was teaching at the academy, I would return here during holidays. Even these past two years while I've been in the capital, my colleagues and students would help maintain the place.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, teasing him, \"I see. So you're not as terrible as the neighbors make you out to be?\"","Qi Shuguang laughed, \"I'm grateful my wife doesn't find me wanting.\"","After their playful exchange, they prepared to clean the dust inside and outside the house.","The courtyard had an ancient, tranquil charm, with tall trees surrounding the buildings, making it cool and pleasant. Staying for a few days would make for a nice summer retreat.","Before they could begin cleaning, a woman peeked in through the gate. Upon seeing Qi Shuguang, she exclaimed in surprise, \"I thought there were thieves! Fourth Brother, aren't you supposed to be in the capital? Why are you suddenly back?\"","Qi Shuguang was startled but quickly smiled and greeted her as Third Sister-in-law, explaining, \"The academy is on summer break, so we came back to visit Father and Mother's graves.\"","The Third Sister-in-law nodded, then turned her curious gaze to the Empress Dowager, asking, \"And who might this be?\"","Qi Shuguang cleared his throat and smiled, \"This is my wife.\"","The Empress Dowager smiled as well, quickly addressing the Third Sister-in-law, \"Hello, Sister. I'm his wife, my maiden name is Guan.\"","Since leaving the palace, she naturally couldn't use her original surname Zhou, so she had adopted her mother's surname, which was what she used in the capital as well.","The Third Sister-in-law beamed, \"So you're my sister-in-law! Oh my, Fourth Brother, why didn't you tell us when you got married!\"","Before Qi Shuguang could respond, the Empress Dowager smoothly interjected, \"It's our fault. We should have informed the family, but the capital is so far away. We took this opportunity during the summer break to come back.\"","The Third Sister-in-law nodded, \"So sister-in-law is from the capital too? That's wonderful!\"","She continued excitedly, \"Our Fourth Brother finally getting married is such joyous news! We must celebrate properly!\"","The Empress Dowager eagerly agreed, \"Sister is absolutely right. That's what we had in mind too. No time like the present - why don't we invite everyone over for drinks today?\"","The Third Sister-in-law happily replied, \"That's perfect! I'll go spread the word!\"","She added, \"Don't worry, sister-in-law. I'll call the other sisters-in-law and nieces-in-law to help out!\"","With that, she hurried away excitedly.","Watching this scene, Qi Shuguang, who hadn't been able to get a word in, smiled at the Empress Dowager, \"You seem to get along better with her than I do.\"","The Empress Dowager raised an eyebrow, \"That's what we call adapting to local customs.\"","Thanks to the villagers' help, by evening, the once-quiet Qi Family courtyard was bustling with activity.","The tables were laden with homestyle dishes, and the wine was homemade sorghum liquor brought by neighbors. Though simple, it was honest and flavorful.","Naturally, everyone was curious about the new Qi Family bride's background, and they took the opportunity amid the festivities to inquire.","\"Sister-in-law, what does your family do in the capital?\"","\"Looking at your refined manner, you must be from an official's family?\"","The Empress Dowager responded graciously, \"You're too kind. My father was indeed an official, but he passed away long ago. I have no family left now. I was previously married and widowed for many years. Then through a matchmaker, I met him and we got together.\"","Upon hearing this, everyone understood - the new Qi Family bride was a widow.","However, the village didn't care much about such matters, and besides, the new bride was both beautiful and dignified. What did it matter if she was a widow?","The most important thing was that their village's most troublesome bachelor had finally married!","Everyone was delighted, and several of the sisters-in-law encouraged the Empress Dowager, \"That's wonderful, just focus on living well together. Try to give the Qi Family an heir - that would put Uncle and Aunt's spirits at ease.\"","Qi Shuguang tensed at these words, about to speak, but the Empress Dowager smoothly replied, \"I'm afraid I'm not as blessed as you sisters. I'm getting on in years and probably can't bear children anymore.\"","The sisters-in-law nodded, showing some disappointment, then asked, \"Do you have any children from before?\"","The Empress Dowager smiled, \"I have a son who is quite filial.\"","Qi Shuguang quickly added, \"He's very good to me too.\"","The sisters-in-law nodded and didn't pursue the matter further.","After all, women of a certain age couldn't bear children even if they wanted to. Besides, all the meat and fish on the table had been bought from various households with the new bride's money - she was clearly well-off. Fourth Brother hadn't done badly for himself.","Just then, the tipsy Third Brother slurred to Qi Shuguang, \"You finally get married and you couldn't find someone younger...\"","Before he could finish, his wife, the Third Sister-in-law, snapped, \"What's it to you? What's so good about young women? They'd just be waiting for you to die young!\"","This retort left the Third Brother speechless and sent everyone into fits of laughter.","The Empress Dowager couldn't help laughing too, and smoothed things over, \"They say young couples grow old together - Third Brother and Sister are such straightforward people!\"","The Third Sister-in-law then turned to her husband, \"Serves you right with no money and no skills, stuck farming all your life! If you were like Fourth Brother, you'd probably want a young wife too?\"","This thoroughly frightened the Third Brother, who quickly shook his head, \"No, no, I wouldn't dare!\"","Everyone burst into laughter again as the festivities continued with great merriment.","As night fell and stars appeared in the clear sky, the farmhouse feast came to an end.","After cleaning up, Qi Shuguang and the Empress Dowager cuddled in the courtyard to enjoy the cool evening air.","The wine had left the Empress Dowager feeling soft and relaxed, and she rested her head on his shoulder as he held her.","A sweet fragrance drifted on the cool night breeze, and she asked, \"What's that smell?\"","Qi Shuguang replied, \"It's the scent of harvest.\"","The Empress Dowager nodded, \"It's lovely.\"","After a pause, Qi Shuguang added, \"The villagers are farmers who speak plainly. Don't take offense.\"","The Empress Dowager laughed, \"Why would I? Having no pretenses makes them easier to get along with.\"","She sighed, \"Other men all want young wives, but you spent half your life alone, bore the label of being unfilial, and ended up marrying a widow like me.\"","He nuzzled her forehead with his cheek, saying, \"You're the one who didn't mind taking me, a man past forty with nothing to his name except these old country houses.\"","She smiled, \"How can you call this a country house? It's a paradise. I love it here. Let's come back every year and stay for a while.\"","He nodded, \"Of course.\"","Anything you like is fine with me.","Back in the capital, at the Imperial Palace.","Ever since getting burned by chili peppers, the little prince had behaved himself for quite a while. During meals, he no longer dared to eye the adults' dishes and obediently ate from his own bowl.","However, despite his young age, the little fellow was quite caring.","For instance, one evening during dinner, when Father happened to return home early, Mother specially ordered the royal kitchen to prepare spicy eel, one of Father's favorite dishes.","As soon as the dish was served, the little one immediately spotted the red chili pepper slices in it.","In that instant, memories of that night when he got \"bitten\" by chilies flashed before his eyes.","The little one was startled and quickly waved his small wooden spoon at his father, saying, \"Hurts...\"","Yuwen Lan was initially confused and hurriedly asked, \"What's wrong, Heng'er? Where does it hurt?\"","The little one stuck out his tiny red tongue and said, \"Mouth... hurts...\"","Huh?","Yuwen Lan grew even more confused and leaned in to check his son's mouth, asking worriedly, \"What's wrong, Heng'er?\"","Yanshu laughed beside them and explained, \"It's nothing. The other day I was eating boiled fish with chilies, and he was curious to try it. I told him it was spicy, but he wouldn't believe me. He sneaked a taste when I wasn't looking, and now he knows what spicy means.\"","Hearing this, Yuwen Lan couldn't help but smile and told his son, \"It's alright, Father isn't afraid of spicy food.\"","He patted the little one's head gently and said softly, \"Good boy.\"","Just as he reached for the eel with his chopsticks, the little one suddenly burst into tears, shaking his head frantically, \"Father... spicy... no...\"","Yuwen Lan was speechless.","His son was this worried about him getting burned by the chilies?","Deeply touched, he had no choice but to put down his chopsticks and say, \"Alright, don't cry, darling. Father won't eat it then.\"","Upon hearing this, the little one finally calmed down and stopped crying.","The father, feeling warmth in his heart, bent down to kiss his son's forehead.","However, when he turned his head, he discovered his wife eagerly enjoying the delicious spicy eel.","Yuwen Lan asked puzzled, \"Why doesn't he cry when you eat chilies? Isn't he worried about you getting burned?\"","Yanshu, while enthusiastically eating, replied, \"Oh, it's nothing. I told him that day that I would fight the chilies and destroy them all to protect His Majesty and him.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","Meanwhile, their round-faced little one broke into a smile, waving his small wooden spoon and exclaimed, \"Mommy, amazing!\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\""]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121","paragraphs":["As the sweltering summer approached, the weather grew increasingly hot, and the palace had already switched to lightweight summer attire.","Children, in particular, were especially susceptible to the heat. Yanshu had the knitting bureau make several cool summer outfits for her baby, exposing his chubby arms and legs, making the little one feel much more comfortable.","This, however, further accentuated the chubbiness of the child's figure, making him look exceptionally cute and adorable.","But as the child grew older and more capable, he also became more restless, climbing all over the palace every day, quite mischievous, which was quite exhausting for Yanshu.","Fortunately, there were plenty of hands in the palace. Seeing that the child was now older, she felt it was time to resume her career in writing novels.","Woohoo, ever since giving birth, she could only produce one novel every two months. She felt terribly guilty towards her readers.","However, the child was still young, and although there were wet nurses and attendants to take care of him, the little one often sought her out for various things, wanting to be held. Yanshu had no choice but to ask Rendong to accompany the wet nurse and take the child to the Imperial Garden to play.","Not long after, the emperor in Qianming Palace faintly heard a childish voice outside the hall.","As there was no pressing business at the moment, he felt a stir in his heart and quickly got up to go outside.","Sure enough, he saw his little son pulling the wet nurse's hand, trying to enter the palace, while the wet nurse and Rendong looked troubled and were coaxing the little one not to disturb him.","However, upon seeing his figure, no one could stop the child anymore. The little one sweetly called out \"Daddy\" and, with a chuckle, toddled towards him.","Yuwen Lan was also pleasantly surprised and quickly bent down to scoop his son into his arms, asking, \"Why are you here, Heng'er?\"","Rendong quickly explained, \"Your Majesty, the empress is busy with important matters. She originally asked us to take the little prince to the Imperial Garden to play, but the little prince only took a few steps before insisting on coming to see you. He even pointed the way and insisted that we bring him here.\"","This was true. Despite his young age, the child already knew many things, such as the directions to the Central Palace, Qianming Palace, and the Imperial Garden. If he wanted to go somewhere and the adults didn't take him, he would definitely throw a tantrum.","Yuwen Lan naturally understood this and did not blame Rendong and the others. Instead, he gently asked his son, \"Heng'er, did you miss Daddy, so you came to find him?\"","The little one vigorously nodded his round head and said, \"Miss Daddy, play...\" while pointing towards the Imperial Garden.","This sweet voice melted everyone's hearts. What could Yuwen Lan refuse? He immediately agreed, \"Alright, then Daddy will take Heng'er to the Imperial Garden to play.\"","With that, he carried the child to the Imperial Garden.","As the weather was hot, other places were not cool enough, so Yuwen Lan directly took the child to the edge of Taiye Pool.","The vast water surface, dense willows, and gentle breeze made this place very cool.","Moreover, the lotus flowers were in full bloom on the lake, which was also very pleasing to the eye.","As soon as the child arrived, he was immediately attracted by the lotus flowers in the lake, pointing at them with his chubby fingers and saying, \"Flowers... Mama.\"","Yuwen Lan understood; his son wanted to pick a lotus flower to give to his mother.","It was rare for the child to be so filial from a young age. How could the father not support this? He immediately ordered the attendants, \"Pick a lotus flower.\"","The attendants immediately complied, rowing a boat to the middle of the lake and picking a beautiful lotus flower.","Yuwen Lan personally handed the lotus flower to his son, who smiled very happily, showing his white little teeth.","Yuwen Lan kissed the child's face and then asked, \"What will Heng'er give Daddy?\"","He remembered that last time at the Empress Dowager's place, when he asked this, the child gave him a sweet kiss.","He thought this time would be the same, but instead, the child thought hard and then plucked a petal from the lotus flower in his hand, offering it to him.","He said very seriously, \"Daddy... here.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","He gave his mother a whole flower, but only a petal to him?","He asked in confusion, \"Why not give Daddy a kiss?\"","The child replied, \"Man, kiss wife.\"","What?","Yuwen Lan widened his eyes and quickly asked again, \"What did Heng'er say?\"","The child repeated seriously, \"Man, kiss wife.\"","Seeing Yuwen Lan's puzzled expression, Rendong and the others were inwardly sweating, so they explained, \"Your Majesty, the little prince probably means that a man can only kiss his wife...\"","[Goodness, how did the little prince say what the empress usually tells him? I hope the emperor doesn't get angry.]","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He finally understood what his son meant.","And it was his wife who taught him that.","...Why did the child have to tell him this at such a young age?","Just then, the child in his arms said to him again, \"Daddy... man.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He didn't need Rendong to translate this time; he understood.","His son was saying that he was also a man.","...Not bad, at least the child could distinguish between men and women.","He nodded seriously and said, \"Yes, Daddy is also a man. So Daddy kisses your mother, my wife.\"","Upon hearing this, Rendong and the wet nurse were inwardly exclaiming—","The emperor was truly a rare good man in the world!","A model for all men!","The child in his arms also nodded seriously, trying to imitate his mother's usual praise by giving a thumbs-up. However, the action was too difficult, and after struggling for a while, he simply extended his whole chubby hand and said, \"Daddy, good!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded solemnly and said, \"So Heng'er should also learn from Daddy. By the way, do you remember what you learned from the Analects yesterday?\"","The child actually nodded.","This surprised Yuwen Lan, who immediately asked enthusiastically, \"Then what do you remember?\"","The child said, \"Don't hit wife.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","This meant... not hitting one's wife?","...What was his wife teaching every day?","He had to suppress the urge to raise his eyebrows and asked his son patiently, \"It was Daddy who taught Heng'er, 'Seek the Way, adhere to virtue, rely on benevolence, and enjoy the arts.' Do you remember?\"","The child was stunned.","Yuwen Lan then recited, \"When three people walk together, there must be one who can be my teacher. Choose the good and follow it, correct the bad...\"","Before he could finish, the child's eyelids began to droop, blinking as if he was about to fall asleep.","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","He had been teaching for over a year, and the child still fell asleep whenever he heard the classics?","He quickly changed the subject, \"Alright, it's still early, not time to sleep yet. Let's play with Daddy, Heng'er.\"","He was worried that if the child fell asleep now, he might not sleep at night.","Pointing to the water, he said, \"Heng'er, look, what's that?\"","The child followed his finger and his eyes lit up, saying, \"Fish.\"","Yuwen Lan smiled and asked, \"Is it fun?\"","The child said seriously, \"Yummy...\"","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","As a model father who personally took care of the child every day, how could he not understand that the child meant \"delicious\"?","The child was still pointing at the water with a serious expression, saying, \"Eat fish, baby, eat fish...\"","Yuwen Lan, \"...\"","Alright, besides falling asleep whenever he heard the classics, his son was still very smart.","Yes, that's right.","Like his mother.","After staying in their hometown for a few days and visiting their former colleagues and students at the academy, the time for the summer vacation was almost over.","Qi Shuguang and his wife prepared to return to the capital.","As before, the couple planned to enjoy the journey by eating and sightseeing along the way.","To allow his wife to appreciate different scenery, Qi Shuguang specially planned another route.","One day, passing by Lanling, Qi Shuguang took his wife to visit an old friend—Gu Hongbai, the famous scholar from Lanling who had attended the Great Scholars Forum in the capital.","Upon seeing him, Gu Hongbai and his wife were very happy, especially when they saw that he had gotten married and brought his wife along. They immediately prepared a banquet to entertain them.","At this time of year, schools across the country were on summer break, so Gu Hongbai's academy was also empty, which was perfect for the four of them to enjoy their drinks and conversation.","Madam Gu was a straightforward person. After a couple of drinks, she first congratulated Qi Shuguang and his wife, expressing her heartfelt emotions, \"Old Qi, you've waited a lifetime for a heart's desire, and finally, the heavens have been kind to you.\"","Qi Shuguang nodded eagerly, \"Thank you, Sister-in-law. You're right; the heavens have been kind to me.\"","He then looked at the Empress Dowager with deep affection.","Gu Hongbai, sitting beside him, laughed and added, \"Old Qi, just you wait. I've calculated—your good days are far from over. Live well, aim to reach your eighties or nineties, and you'll have another four or five decades of happiness ahead!\"","Upon hearing this, the Empress Dowager looked surprised and asked, \"Mr. Gu, do you also practice fortune-telling?\"","Before Gu Hongbai could respond, Madam Gu interjected, \"He's just talking nonsense, Sister-in-law. Don't take him seriously. But Old Qi has done so many good deeds; he certainly deserves good fortune.\"","Qi Shuguang then turned to the Empress Dowager, saying earnestly, \"My lady, you are my good fortune.\"","The Empress Dowager blushed, slightly embarrassed, and chided, \"Look at you, making Mr. and Madam Gu laugh at us.\"","Madam Gu quickly shook her head, \"How could we laugh? We're old friends! There's nothing to laugh about.\"","She then turned to her husband, \"But look at how well Old Qi expresses himself.\"","Gu Hongbai raised an eyebrow, \"Is that so? Didn't he just say that one line? How many love poems did I write for you back then? If you string them together, they could circle this mountain! Should I write another one for you now?\"","This made Madam Gu blush even more. She chided, \"Are you drunk? With the students away these past few days, you've become so unruly. At our age, talking about love poems...\"","Perhaps the alcohol had gone to his head, but Gu Hongbai immediately retorted, \"What do you mean, 'our age'? We're still young!\"","He then chuckled, \"With such a wonderful life with you, who would want to grow old?\"","Madam Gu blushed even deeper and quickly fed him a piece of food, saying, \"Eat up...\"","Beside them, Qi Shuguang and the Empress Dowager exchanged smiles and began to serve each other their favorite dishes.","Yes, with such a wonderful life, who would want to grow old?","Let the years continue.","If we could do it all over again, I would hope to meet you in the prime of our youth.","That way, our companionship could be even longer."]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122","paragraphs":["Lanling City.","On an early summer noon, the sun blazed high in the sky, cicadas chirped vigorously in the trees, and pedestrians were sparse on the streets.","It was lunchtime, and the aroma of food wafted from restaurants and homes along the street.","Especially from the \"Welcome Inn\" restaurant behind him, where the kitchen was at its busiest, various fragrances had been drifting from the chimney for nearly half an hour.","\"Hmm, stir-fried diced chicken, crispy pork tenderloin, Dong'an chicken, sweet and sour fish, braised pork knuckle, Taibai duck...\"","Eighteen-year-old Gu Hongbai silently recited the menu in his mind, thinking that the kitchen fires must be burning strong today, as all these aromas seemed perfectly cooked!","He thought to himself that once he succeeded in his mission, he would definitely come to properly enjoy a feast here.","After these thoughts, he quietly swallowed and silently moved his fortune-telling stall a bit to the side.","He was here for important business, how could he let such food distract his mind?","Today was Gu Hongbai's fifth day setting up his fortune-telling stall.","And from the first day until now, he hadn't served a single customer.","Of course, it wasn't that no one had approached him, but rather that he had found excuses to turn away anyone who came.","Because:","First, he didn't actually know how to tell fortunes;","Second, and most importantly, he had set up this stall solely to catch another glimpse of the girl in red who had ridden past on horseback five days ago. How could he waste time fortune-telling and risk missing her?","So never mind an empty stomach - even if he fainted from the heat, he would stand his ground until that lady in red appeared again!","However, today the heavens seemed particularly harsh, even hotter than previous days, and the willow leaves by the roadside looked ready to curl from the heat.","Gu Hongbai suspected that if the sun continued like this, even his hair would start to curl.","But even if it did curl, he wouldn't give up.","Fortunately, persistence paid off. After half an hour, right when the sun was at its most fierce, the sound of hoofbeats suddenly rang out from down the street.","Gu Hongbai quickly looked up to see a young lady on horseback, her graceful figure exactly the one he had been thinking about for days.","In that moment, all his hunger and discomfort vanished, but he faced an extremely important question―","How should he make her acquaintance?","Actually, after first seeing her that day, he had pretty much figured out her identity―the daughter of the Chang family, a martial arts household in Lanling.","After all, what other family in Lanling City had women who rode horses?","However, the Chang family associated with various martial arts schools and jianghu heroes. Never mind someone like him - even the teachers at the academy had no connection to the Chang family. He'd heard that Master Chang had five sons before finally having this precious daughter, whom he cherished like the apple of his eye. If he rashly went to their door professing his admiration for their precious daughter, he would likely be thrown out.","So after much thought, he felt his only chance was to make the acquaintance of Miss Chang directly.","And now, the opportunity he had waited days for was right before him, but unfortunately, she was on horseback.","At her current speed, she would pass by him in the blink of an eye...","At this critical moment, Gu Hongbai caught sight of several people stepping out of the restaurant, led by the notorious local bully Pang San, who had just collected protection money from him two days ago.","A quick idea struck him, and he immediately walked quickly toward Pang San, deliberately colliding with him head-on.","He had used all his strength, causing Pang San's chest to hurt. Pang San immediately started cursing, \"Which blind fool dares to bump into your Master Pang?\"","Upon seeing who it was, he cursed again, \"So it's the worthless fortune teller who dares to bump into me? Didn't learn your lesson from two days ago? Today I'll let you taste your Master Pang's fists!\" He grabbed Gu Hongbai's collar, ready to throw a punch.","But just then, a red figure descended from above, delivering a kick straight to Pang San's big head. In the blink of an eye, Pang San was thrown to the ground, the impact seeming to shake the street.","\"Well, well, Pang San, it's been a few days since I taught you a lesson, and you dare to bully the weak again?\"","The young lady's clear voice rang out, and before him was her face, as beautiful as a lotus after rain.","Only after Pang San had kowtowed three times promising never to bully anyone again and fled clutching his head and rubbing his waist did Gu Hongbai finally come to his senses.","He saw the heaven-sent lady looking at him with concern, asking, \"Are you hurt, young sir?\"","Gu Hongbai quickly shook his head and said, \"Thanks to your timely appearance, miss, you saved me from that villain. I am deeply grateful for your kindness and will never forget it. May I ask where you're from? I must visit with gifts another day to properly thank you.\"","The young lady smiled graciously and said, \"You're too kind. My surname is Chang, given name Ruyu, and I live at the Chang Manor in the east of the city. I'm glad you're unharmed - it was nothing, really no need for thanks.\"","With that, she mounted her horse again and rode on.","East City Chang Manor, Chang Ruyu.","Gu Hongbai silently repeated the name, thinking his guess had been correct.","Good.","He straightened up, packed away his fortune-telling stall, and leisurely returned to the academy.","That night, as the air cooled, Gu Hongbai lay in bed planning his future marriage proposal when he heard his dormitory mates discussing the Chang Manor in the east of the city.","\"I heard the Chang family in the east is accepting marriage proposals these days!\"","\"The Chang family? You mean the most powerful martial arts family in the area? I heard Madam Chang had five sons before finally having a daughter, and they cherish her even more than their sons. I wonder what kind of marriage selection process they're using?\"","\"For a martial arts family, naturally it's a martial arts competition! They announced the conditions a few days ago - I heard you have to defeat the young lady's five brothers to qualify.\"","Silently listening, Gu Hongbai thought, \"...\"","Defeat her five brothers?","Looking down at his own physique...","Any one of his potential brothers-in-law could probably kill him...","In the darkness, his roommates suddenly heard their usually quiet companion ask, \"Has anyone tried?\"","Someone immediately answered, \"Quite a few! Not just from around Lanling, but from Jiangnan, Jiangbei, Shandong, Shanxi, and even as far as the northern frontier and Yunnan, but without exception, none could defeat the Chang family's five sons.\"","\"Good!\"","This outburst surprised everyone.","Gu Hongbai realized his slip and tried to explain, \"How could such a fine lady be allowed to marry so far away?\"","But this didn't stop his dormmates' teasing―","\"Brother Gu, you haven't fallen for Miss Chang, have you?\"","\"No offense, but you're no match for the Chang brothers with your build!\"","\"Let me give you some advice - hurry and find a martial arts master to train you these days, maybe you'll still have a chance...\"","Gu Hongbai remained silent.","...Did they think he hadn't considered learning martial arts?","If reason hadn't told him it was impossible, he would have found a master long ago.","Hmph, he refused to believe those martial artists could love Ruyu more sincerely than he did!","After quietly observing for several days, Gu Hongbai discovered that regardless of where these men came from, none could defeat his five formidable potential brothers-in-law.","This meant that no one had yet been selected as a potential son-in-law by his future parents-in-law.","Somewhat relieved, he chose an auspicious day and carefully selected gifts that, while not extravagant, showed sincere intention, then gathered his courage to visit the East City Chang Manor.","As the area's renowned martial arts family, the Changs had always been known for their righteousness, frequently involving themselves in acts of chivalry and standing up against injustice over the years.","Therefore, they often received visitors expressing gratitude.","However, they had never received a young man like Gu Hongbai before.","Particularly noting his scholarly appearance, they quickly inquired and discovered he was a student at Crane Lake Academy, the most prestigious school in Lanling.","It was well known that Crane Lake Academy ranked among the nation's finest, with its students consistently achieving top scores in various examinations, indicating this young man must be quite scholarly indeed.","Given this, Madam Chang, who had always held educated people in high regard, immediately began to view him differently.","Of course, seeing his polite manner and proper conduct, Master Chang was also quite impressed with him.","Gu Hongbai also knew well the principle of quitting while ahead. After expressing his gratitude, he immediately bid farewell and left the manor, never once revealing his thoughts about their daughter throughout the entire encounter.","Of course, he hadn't caught a glimpse of Miss Chang who had been haunting his dreams.","However, unexpectedly, just as he was about to return to Crane Lake Academy, he heard someone calling out to him from behind.","That crystal-clear voice made him start. Gu Hongbai quickly stopped and turned around, only to find it was the very lady he had most hoped to see.","Ahem, could it be that the Chang family elders had taken a liking to him and thus sent their daughter to chase after him?","Although Gu Hongbai considered himself quite excellent, he still maintained his rationality and thought this unlikely.","So he quickly stood at attention and asked, \"What can I do for you, Miss Chang?\"","Chang Ruyu replied, \"That day when I beat up Pang San, it was only because I couldn't stand him bullying others, not because I wanted anything from you. Why did you specially come to thank me?\"","Ahem, finally another chance to speak with her!","Gu Hongbai suppressed his excitement and said seriously, \"I certainly understand that your actions that day were chivalrous, but wouldn't I be failing as a person if I didn't come to thank you? So you did what you did, and I'm thanking you for what I should - there's no conflict there.\"","After speaking, he gave her his best sunny smile, showcasing his handsome features.","He noticed that the lady did indeed pause slightly at the sight.","Oh?","Gu Hongbai thought to himself, [How about that, my lady? Have you fallen for me? As they say, true scholarly refinement naturally shines through - surely I'm far better than those rough fighters.]","Just as he was secretly feeling pleased with himself, he heard the lady say, \"But you're setting up fortune-telling stalls while studying - it must be hard for you. How can you waste money like this?\"","Gu Hongbai: \"...\"","Although... he wasn't actually short of money! His father was a successful candidate in the imperial examinations and owned hundreds of acres of good farmland...","Before he could speak, he saw her stuffing a money pouch into his hands, saying with a smile, \"Take this, and don't set up stalls anymore. It's not easy to get into Crane Lake Academy - you should focus on your studies and strive to achieve scholarly honors soon to repay your teachers and parents.\"","With that and a carefree laugh, she mounted her horse and rode away.","Gu Hongbai stood there dazed, bewitched by that smile, until her figure disappeared from view.","When he finally came to his senses and looked down at the money pouch in his hand, he suddenly felt anxious.","He had gone there to gain her favor, how did he end up taking money from her?!","Wait, my lady! Your husband isn't the type to live off women!!!"]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 7","After all his careful planning and effort to finally meet the girl of his dreams, who would have thought she would mistake him for a poor student scamming people on the streets.","At present, Gu Hongbai found himself in quite a predicament.","Concealing the truth was certainly wrong, but if he were to explain the real situation to her, he feared it would ruin the good impression he had built with the Chang family elders.","So...","After much deliberation, Gu Hongbai decided to keep quiet for now.","A few days later, his dormitory mates noticed that the recently peculiar Gu Hongbai, after stopping his fortune-telling business down the mountain, had taken up gathering mushrooms, white fungus, and lingzhi in the mountains.","Puzzled by his behavior and assuming his family had fallen on hard times, they privately collected some money to give to him.","\"Though this isn't much, it should help Brother Gu for a while. You were the top scorer in the previous prefectural exam, and with the institutional exam approaching, if you prepare well, you'll surely become a government student. Then you won't have to worry about making a living anymore.\"","Gu Hongbai: \"...\"","Touched by their gesture, he politely declined their money and said, \"I appreciate everyone's kindness, but I have money. If any of you have spare time, you could help me gather mushrooms and white fungus, and lingzhi would be especially welcome.\"","Everyone: \"???\"","A few days later, the East City Chang Manor received another batch of mountain products, including mushrooms, white fungus, and some lingzhi.","These were said to be from the mountains behind Crane Lake Academy, seemingly carrying an scholarly air that made them particularly special.","Needless to say, these were again from that young scholar.","More importantly, he had specifically arranged for these to be delivered to Chang Ruyu, saying it was a small token of gratitude for her kindness.","Chang Ruyu was initially surprised, then amused—","Why was this young scholar busy setting up fortune-telling stalls and gathering mountain products instead of focusing on his studies?","She shook her head and simply had the kitchen store everything, thinking nothing more of it.","However, a few days later, she unexpectedly saw him again on the street.","He was wearing the same cyan straight-collared robe, with his slim figure so different from her father, brothers, and relatives.","This time, Gu Hongbai didn't need to devise any schemes as Chang Ruyu stopped her horse and jumped down to greet him, \"Are you fortune-telling again?\"","Though his heart was pounding, Gu Hongbai maintained a casual demeanor as if this were a chance encounter, expressing surprise before saying, \"Oh, Miss Ruyu, you misunderstand. I'm here to buy clothes today. Since hearing your words last time, I haven't set up my stall again.\"","He coughed slightly and ventured to ask, \"What brings Miss out today?\"","Chang Ruyu replied with her usual frankness, \"I just visited relatives in the south of the city.\"","Then she asked, \"Were those mushrooms and white fungus from you?\"","Gu Hongbai nodded, \"Yes, it was a small token of gratitude for Miss's kindness...\"","He specifically emphasized, \"I gathered them all myself.\"","But she replied, \"Why aren't you focusing on your studies instead of gathering these things? Please don't do this anymore.\"","Gu Hongbai obediently agreed, then quickly took out a money pouch from his chest and handed it to her, saying, \"I've been carrying this with me, hoping to return it when I met you. Now that we've finally met, please take it back. I... actually don't lack money.\"","Chang Ruyu didn't take it, and after some thought said, \"Let's consider this payment for your dried goods. Don't gather anymore in the future; focus on your studies. If you want to repay me, earn a good academic title and bring honor to our Lanling.\"","With that, she gave a carefree smile and gracefully mounted her horse to leave.","As Gu Hongbai watched her depart, he silently vowed in his heart—","Wait for me, my lady, I will definitely bring honor to you!","In the following days, his dormitory mates noticed that Gu's family crisis seemed to have passed, as he no longer told fortunes or gathered mountain products.","Instead, he threw himself into his studies, rising early and sleeping late, studying by lamplight, nearly to the point of tying his hair to the beam to stay awake and pricking his thigh with an awl to keep from dozing.","His fellow students were relieved and remarked, \"At this rate, Brother Gu will surely top the institutional examination.\"","Gu Hongbai responded confidently, \"Thank you for the kind words. If it comes true, I'll treat everyone to a feast!\"","Everyone: \"...Brother Gu, how many meals have you promised now? Perhaps you should keep a notebook to avoid forgetting?\"","Gu Hongbai waved his hand dismissively, \"What's a few meals? If I succeed, I'll treat you all for a whole month!\"","Everyone applauded his generosity.","But then, a fellow student said, \"By the way, have you heard the latest news about the Chang family's martial arts marriage selection?\"","Hmm?","Upon hearing this, Gu Hongbai immediately asked, \"What's the latest news?\"","The student replied, \"The Chang family's sons are all exceptionally skilled, and after nearly a month, they still haven't found a suitable candidate. They've injured quite a few people, so Old Master Chang has ended the selection and plans to marry his daughter to his nephew instead.\"","Nephew?","Gu Hongbai jolted and quickly asked, \"What nephew? What does he do?\"","The student answered, \"Isn't it Zhao Kaihong, the second young master of the South City Zhao Family Escort Agency?\"","Upon hearing this, Gu Hongbai froze, suddenly remembering that day when he met Ruyu on the street and she mentioned visiting relatives in the south of the city...","...Could it have been that Zhao fellow's family?","This won't do!","How could Ruyu marry someone else?!!","A few days later, Chang Ruyu received a letter.","Opening it, she found only a short sentence: \"I hear that Zhao Kaihong, the second young master of the South City Zhao Family Escort Agency, is a regular patron of the Yihong House's top courtesan. Miss Chang should think carefully.\"","Chang Ruyu: \"???\"","To be honest, she had never particularly liked Zhao Kaihong and hadn't even thought about marriage. It was only because the martial arts selection hadn't found a suitable candidate that her father had grown anxious and turned his attention to the Zhao family.","Her father thought the Zhao family was good enough since they were distant relatives and they knew each other well, but she had grown up with Zhao Kaihong and had always disapproved of his arrogant behavior.","If what this letter said was true, she would have a reason to refuse...","However... who had written this letter?","Chang Ruyu examined the letter carefully again, noting that the handwriting was as beautiful as iron paintings and silver hooks.","...Hmm, among all her family's relatives, few could write so beautifully...","She suddenly thought of someone.","Could it be... that young scholar?","With this question in mind, Chang Ruyu visited Crane Lake Academy for the first time.","After sending word, she soon met the young scholar.","She noticed that he seemed to have grown even thinner since she last saw him.","She wondered if he had no money for food again and had grown thin from hunger.","At that moment, the young scholar bowed to her and said, \"It's my great honor that Miss Chang has come here.\"","Hmm? Chang Ruyu thought, he doesn't seem surprised that I've come to find him?","So she got straight to the point, \"I have something to ask you. A few days ago, I received a letter saying Zhao Kaihong is involved with the top courtesan at Yihong House. Did you write it?\"","To be honest, Chang Ruyu wasn't entirely sure about this.","She just felt that among all the people she knew, only he could produce such beautiful handwriting.","And if it wasn't him, she wouldn't have suspected anyone.","However, to her surprise, he immediately admitted without any hesitation, \"Yes.\"","Chang Ruyu paused.","After a moment, she asked, \"Then do you know that spreading gossip behind others' backs is not what a gentleman would do?\"","He nodded again very frankly and said, \"I do.\"","Chang Ruyu raised an eyebrow, \"Then why did you write it?\"","He replied, \"When I was setting up my stall on the street, I heard about this person's character. Then a few days ago, I heard your father intended to take him as a son-in-law... I simply couldn't bear to see such a person become your husband, so I resorted to this ungentlemanly act.\"","At these words, Chang Ruyu was stunned.","After another moment, she thought to ask, \"Why can't you bear to see him become my husband? What does my marriage... have to do with you?\"","But he replied, \"Because there is someone in this world who truly loves you.\"","As the words fell, Chang Ruyu blushed for the first time in her life and stammered, \"W-what are you saying?\"","Gu Hongbai coughed lightly and said, \"A gentleman should not speak improperly, so there are some things I dare not say rashly. However, I hope miss understands that besides your family, if there's anyone who most wishes for your happiness, it would certainly be me.\"","Chang Ruyu was stunned.","Her mind went blank for a long while, forgetting what she wanted to say...","A few days later, people in the city heard news that the pending marriage arrangement between East City Chang Manor and South City Zhao Family Escort Agency had suddenly been called off.","As for the reason, few knew, but many began to gossip about the Chang family's daughter Ruyu.","Some said that the young lady was usually too flamboyant and skilled in martial arts, making ordinary men hesitant to marry her.","Others said that the Chang family's martial arts marriage competition conditions were too harsh, which was why they couldn't find a husband for their daughter in a month. Now that things fell through with the Zhao family, perhaps ordinary men would be too afraid to marry her.","The blame fell on Master Chang – why did he let his daughter learn martial arts? If she had no such skills, she might have been married off long ago.","Now what? Would this beautiful flower of a lady end up unmarriageable?","Of course, Chang Ruyu paid no mind to these comments, continuing to ride horses in fine clothes, remaining bright and passionate as ever.","Actually, after the Zhao family incident, there were still suitors who came to propose, but she showed little interest in any of them.","As for the reason...","She couldn't quite explain it herself, but somehow, that young scholar's image kept appearing in her mind.","Tsk, what was happening to her?","Fortunately, after a few more days, new news spread through the city—","This year's provincial examination's top scholar came from Crane Lake Academy.","This joyous news spread quickly, and soon everyone in Lanling City knew about it.","Chang Ruyu naturally heard about it too.","While feeling proud, she secretly wondered if that top scholar might be that young scholar.","When she returned home, she heard her parents discussing this matter, and her mother specifically remarked to her, \"What a coincidence, it turns out the top scholar who brought glory to our Lanling is that young scholar you saved on the street, what was his name again...\"","\"Gu Hongbai.\"","Her father deliberately cleared his throat and said, \"That's a good name, sounds scholarly.\"","But Chang Ruyu was stunned.","It was really him?","He passed the examination?","After her initial shock, a hint of joy unconsciously crept onto her lips, impossible to suppress.","A few days later, the Chang Manor received unexpected visitors.","Master Chang looked at the name card and realized it was the Distinguished Scholar Gu from the west city, coming to visit with his son.","Scholar Gu had a high reputation locally, and Master Chang, surprised, quickly ordered servants to welcome them into the house.","When they met, before Master Chang could speak, Scholar Gu took the initiative and said, \"I only recently learned that your daughter Miss Ruyu once saved my unworthy son. I've come rather late to pay my respects, which was quite discourteous. I hope your family can forgive us.\"","What?","Ruyu had saved Scholar Gu's son?","The Chang family was stunned and quickly looked at the young man beside Scholar Gu, only to realize he was the young scholar who had visited before – the one who had just won top honors in the provincial examination, Gu Hongbai.","Chang Ruyu, in particular, was completely stunned.","How was it him?","Her eyes remained fixed on him in surprise, momentarily forgetting proper etiquette.","Meanwhile, the adults continued their polite exchange.","Master Chang said, \"Actually, your son had already come to thank us personally before, but we didn't know then that he was your son. We were quite negligent, and we hope you can forgive us.\"","Scholar Gu quickly smiled and said, \"That was only proper of him, you're too kind...\"","He coughed and continued, \"Speaking of which, I've brought my son here today for another matter.\"","The Chang family master hurriedly asked, \"Please, do tell.\"","Then he heard the other party say, \"We can never repay your daughter's great kindness, so I would like to formally propose marriage on behalf of my son, hoping to join our two families.\"","As the words fell, Chang Ruyu was stunned.","She blushed for the second time in her life.","On their wedding night, the red candles burned bright.","After bidding farewell to relatives and friends at the banquet, Gu Hongbai came alone to the bridal chamber.","The moment he opened the door, he saw his dream girl sitting on the edge of the bed in her red wedding dress, waiting for him.","He tried to suppress his excitement, closed the door, and walked quickly to the bedside.","Then he quietly cleared his throat and called out in his most pleasant voice, \"Wife.\"","As his words fell, the bride at the bedside looked up at him, but before responding, she said, \"There's something I need to ask you.\"","\"Since you were the son of a distinguished scholar, why were you setting up a fortune-telling stall on the street that day?\"","Gu Hongbai: \"...\"","Tsk, he'd thought she'd forgotten about that.","What should he do now?","Would he be able to sleep tonight?"]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 8","With the Little Crown Prince in the palace, time seemed to pass especially quickly.","As the scorching summer and golden autumn passed in succession, when the people of Da Liang welcomed the new year, their Little Crown Prince also turned two years old.","The two-year-old little one had grown bigger, looking increasingly sturdy with his round face. Wearing the small dragon robe specially made for him by the Imperial Weaving Bureau, he looked particularly adorable.","The little fellow's legs had become quite steady, and he would run around the palace all day, rarely falling. His speech was also very clear, and people could understand whatever he said.","On New Year's Day, the little one accompanied his parents to receive royal relatives and ministers who came to offer New Year greetings. He was both cute and gracious, politely thanking anyone who praised him, showing his excellent upbringing.","So it was obvious who had swept the snow.","When the family of three got off their carriage, they saw the divine couple waiting at the entrance. The little one sweetly called out to his grandparents and ran towards the Empress Dowager.","Yanshu hurriedly asked her idol, \"Uncle, why are you so diligent, sweeping all the snow on the mountain path?\"","Qi Shuguang smiled and said, \"I went down the mountain this morning to buy some vegetables, and swept the snow beforehand, fearing my wife might slip.\"","Hearing this, Yanshu's heart melted again—aww, her idol was so good to her boss, they were so sweet!!!","As they spoke, her child had already rushed into his grandmother's arms, calling out sweetly, \"Grandmother.\"","The Empress Dowager was so happy that crow's feet appeared at the corners of her eyes. She quickly took her little grandson into her arms and kissed him twice, then couldn't help but remark, \"It's only been a few days, but Heng'er seems to have gotten heavier? Next time I might not be able to carry you anymore.\"","It was meant as praise, but unexpectedly, the little one in her arms quickly replied, \"No need to carry me, Grandmother. Heng'er can walk by himself.\"","Saying this, he struggled to get down.","The Empress Dowager was puzzled and quickly held onto the little one's hand.","Before she could ask anything, the little one said to her, \"Heng'er is hungry, haven't eaten yet.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Because the little one usually had such a good appetite and grew so fast, Yanshu had intentionally controlled the child's food portions. Whenever the little one asked why he couldn't eat more, she would explain that eating too much might make him too fat, and then he wouldn't be cute anymore.","So, was the little one saying this now because he thought grandmother was calling him fat and wouldn't feed him?","...This child, should they call him clever or silly?","The Empress Dowager was amused by her grandson and kissed his forehead again, saying, \"Grandmother will always have food for Heng'er. Don't worry, snacks are all prepared for you. Come, let's go inside to eat.\"","Hearing this, the little one immediately beamed with joy, skipping along while holding his grandmother's hand as they went inside.","Yanshu and Yuwen Lan exchanged glances, both showing amused yet helpless expressions, and followed them inside.","While the mountain wilderness was cold and white with snow, the room was warm and filled with laughter.","After tasting various snacks made by grandmother and various delicacies made by grandfather, the little one, satisfied with his round belly, bid farewell to his grandparents along with his parents.","\"Grandmother, Grandfather, Heng'er will come again!\" the little one said in his sweet voice, very seriously.","The Empress Dowager quickly nodded with a smile and said, \"Good, good, then next time grandmother will make snacks for Heng'er again, and have grandfather cook chicken and fish stew for you, alright?\"","The little one nodded vigorously saying yes, then followed his parents out the door and onto the carriage back to the palace.","Of course, he was still tightly holding onto the chestnut cakes that grandmother had wrapped for him.","These were from grandmother, and neither father nor mother could take them away.","On the fourth day of the New Year, after the Little Crown Prince had enjoyed a feast at his grandmother's, on the fifth day, the little one followed his mother to Duke Zhongyi's Mansion to visit his maternal grandparents.","Compared to the quiet mountain cottage, Grandma's house was much more crowded, with not only Grandma and Grandpa, but also the white-haired Great-grandma and the young, handsome Uncle.","So it was even more lively.","Of course, to avoid trouble, today mother and he came in casual clothes specifically, so there was no need for grand ceremony.","After they were welcomed inside, Grandpa had the main gate closed, and the little one began playing around at Grandma's house.","In just half a day, the little one had convinced Grandpa to fish two fish from the pond for him and caught two of Great-grandma's white cats.","More importantly, the little one had again eaten his fill of delicious food.","Unlike grandmother who was skilled at making snacks, Grandma's specialty was various flour-based foods like buns and pancakes.","Although the mansion's kitchen had put forth their best effort to prepare a table full of delicacies today, the little one's favorites were still Grandma's handmade meat buns and chive pockets.","According to mother, these were also what she loved to eat most when he was still in her belly, so it was evident that the little one had half of Ande's blood flowing through him, which was quite inspiring.","Unfortunately, the little one was still young and didn't understand what Ande was, he only knew that Grandma's meat buns and chive pockets were absolutely delicious, and before he knew it, his little belly was round and full again.","Just like yesterday, when it was time to leave, the little one again carried a small bundle filled with delicacies from Grandma's house.","On their way back to the palace, they found his father, who had been missing him, waiting in the central palace.","Yuwen Lan first hugged his little one, then asked, \"Did our little one have fun at Grandma's house today?\"","The little one immediately showed his white little teeth in a smile and said, \"Fun!\"","Yuwen Lan's heart softened, and he asked again, \"What did our little one do at Grandma's house today?\"","The little one answered in his sweet voice, \"Seven buns.\"","As he spoke, he patted his round little belly with his chubby hand, and specifically explained, \"Meat buns.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Well, looking at that little belly, he really did eat quite a lot.","However, why does this little one only think about eating all day?","He's not at all like how I was as a child, only interested in reading.","Perhaps he takes after his mother more.","Just as he was thinking this, he caught sight of the little bundle in his son's arms, so he asked, \"What's this?\"","Hmm, it still smells warm and fragrant?","As soon as he finished speaking, the little one quickly pushed the small bundle into his hands, saying seriously, \"This is for Father Emperor, buns, big buns!\"","Yuwen Lan made an \"oh\" sound, somewhat surprised, \"There's some for me too?\"","Yanshu laughed from the side, \"Of course, my mother always remembers what Your Majesty likes to eat. Before we left, she specially steamed some large vegetarian buns for Your Majesty, filled with chives, eggs, and glass noodles, and even added dried shrimp. Please try them while they're hot.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Mm.\"","It was thoughtful of his mother-in-law, these were indeed his favorites.","He quickly unwrapped the bundle and started eating while the buns were still warm.","Mmm, the warm big buns were soft in his hands, and with one bite, they were indeed full of the fragrance of flour and incredibly savory.","He nodded while eating, \"Your Grandma's cooking skills are indeed excellent, little one.\"","Before Yanshu could say anything, the little one on the side giggled, \"Good, good!\"","Buns are the best!","In the blink of an eye, the seven-day New Year holiday passed, and this year's various important matters were put on the agenda as all departments in the court resumed normal operations.","However, while immersing himself in state affairs, Yuwen Lan was also concerned about his child.","Watching the child grow day by day, only knowing about eating, drinking, and playing – how could this do?","Although the little one was just two years old now, princes traditionally began their education at three, so there was only one year left. If things continued like this, would the little one be able to learn when the time came?","This was his Crown Prince after all...","With these concerns in mind, after finishing his work that day, Yuwen Lan returned to the central palace early.","Before it was time for the meal to be served, he entered the hall to find the little one nestled in his mother's arms, looking at a book together with her.","Of course, the little one couldn't read characters yet, so to be precise, the mother and son were reading together, with Yanshu reading the words on the book aloud for the little one to hear.","Seeing this scene, Yuwen Lan was initially very pleased.","It seemed that not only was he aware of the seriousness of the matter, but his wife also knew and was actively teaching their son to read.","However, after listening for a while, he discovered that his wife wasn't reading the teachings of the sages to their son.","Instead, it was something like a storybook—","\"It is said that many years ago, there was a wealthy dye house owner in Qingzhou City...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"???\"","He immediately frowned and asked, \"What is this?\"","His wife replied, \"A storybook, of course.\"","Yuwen Lan asked, \"...Did you write this?\"","\"No, no,\" Yanshu quickly shook her head. \"I haven't written much lately. This was written by a new talented author in the capital. I read it and found it quite good!\"","Well, as a passionate enthusiast of story manuscripts, she wasn't just an author but also a reader. It was quite enjoyable to read the masterpieces of other skilled writers in her spare time!","However, Yuwen Lan didn't seem to understand her perspective and instead asked, \"What is our little one doing?\"","Yanshu replied, \"...Reading the story manuscript with me.\"","Wasn't that obvious?","But it seemed someone wasn't too pleased. He picked up the little one and said with a serious expression, \"You are the Crown Prince of Great Liang, heir to the great enterprise. You're already two years old now, considered a big child. You should be learning useful things, understand?\"","The little one nodded innocently, \"I know.\"","Somewhat satisfied, Yuwen Lan proceeded, \"Then let father help you review what you learned the other day. The wise find joy in water, the benevolent...\"","\"Find joy in mountains...\"","Before he could finish, the little one suddenly chimed in with his baby voice.","Yuwen Lan was stunned.","What did his son just say?","...Was it \"find joy in mountains\"?","Not quite sure, he tried again, \"The wise...\"","\"Move...\"","\"The benevolent?\"","\"Are still...\"","\"The wise?\"","\"Joy...\"","\"The benevolent?\"","\"Long life.\"","After this back-and-forth between father and son, the little one had answered everything correctly.","Yuwen Lan was pleasantly surprised – had his son really learned it all?","Yanshu proudly exclaimed, \"Wow, my baby is a genius!\"","She quickly kissed the little one's chubby cheeks.","The little one giggled and repeated, \"Genius!\"","Three lively days passed, and on the fourth day of the new year, which happened to be the little one's second birthday and while the court was still on holiday, Yuwen Lan and Yanshu found some time to take their little one to pay New Year respects to grandmother.","It had snowed a few days ago, and Yanshu had been worried about the mountain roads being too slippery for carriages. However, when they arrived, they discovered that the snow on the path had already been cleared.","This was the back mountain of Songhe Academy, where only her mentor and idol lived. During the New Year holiday, all the teachers and students of the academy had already returned home."]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 9","After the initial joy, Yanshu also had some doubts. Was her son really remembering the Classics and Analects that his father taught him, or was it due to some other... reason?","Cough, after all, her son had telepathy...","Perhaps he was just repeating what he heard his father thinking in his mind?","With such doubts, the next day, while Yuwen Lan was away, she decided to test him again.","So she smiled and said to the little one, \"Mommy wants to play a game with you, okay?\"","The unsuspecting little one nodded innocently and cutely, \"Okay.\"","Yanshu coughed and began to recite.","\"The wise are not...\"","Of course, with her limited knowledge, she couldn't recite the Classics and Analects as fluently as her son's father, so she had specifically looked up a few books of wisdom beforehand and was now reading from them.","The words had barely left her mouth when the little one immediately responded, \"Worried.\"","Oh, the little one got it right again!","Yanshu's eyes lit up and she quickly continued, \"The brave are not...\"","The little one immediately said, \"Afraid.\"","She didn't dare to celebrate too soon and quickly changed to another book, randomly finding a sentence, and even covered the following words with her hand as she tried to ask the little one, \"The gentleman is harmonious but not?\"","Heng'er, \"Partial.\"","Yanshu, \"The petty man is partial but not?\"","The little one, \"Harmonious.\"","Yanshu, \"Poverty does not lose righteousness?\"","The little one, \"Prosperity does not, leave, the way.\"","Yanshu, \"!!!\"","Again, all correct!","For safety, she decided to try one more sentence, \"Those who love others?\"","The little one, \"People, always, love, chicken.\"","Yanshu, \"Those who respect others...\"","The little one, \"People always respect chicken.\"","Although there were a few unclear pronunciations, the little one got them all right!","This showed that the son really remembered what his father taught, even though he often fell asleep after a few sentences, the gradual influence really worked.","Yanshu was very excited. After all, her son was only a two-year-old baby!","Never did she expect that such a genius son could come from her, who didn't like studying and spent all day reading novels! This was simply too moving!","\"My baby is so good!!!\"","The mother hugged her little treasure and kissed him again and again.","The little one was also kissed and giggled, showing his white little teeth and said, \"Baby good good!\"","The mother and son laughed together for a while, the scene was very warm.","Of course, as an excellent mother, Yanshu immediately realized that just laughing was not enough. Although the little one had talent, he also needed continuous effort.","So she immediately conducted positive guidance and said to the little one, \"Since my baby is so good and remembers what daddy taught, let's have roast lamb for lunch to reward you, okay?\"","\"Lamb!\"","The little one immediately clapped and said happily, \"Heng'er likes to eat lamb!\"","So that noon, the Empress in the Central Palace and the little Crown Prince enjoyed a sumptuous roast lamb feast.","Of course, after the big meal, Yanshu remembered another important matter.","With her son now two years old, from being able to sense her emotions when he was still in swaddling clothes, to now being able to accurately experience others' joys and sorrows, she could almost confirm that the little one had telepathy.","However, being so young, the little one probably couldn't distinguish his special ability, so she, as a mother, also needed to guide her son well.","She tried calling in her heart, \"Baby?\"","The little one playing with the nine-link ring looked up at her and said, \"Hmm.\"","Yanshu tried, \"Did you hear mommy calling you?\"","The little one nodded, \"Hmm, mommy called baby.\"","Yanshu was relieved.","This showed that her son indeed had telepathy, and the little one currently couldn't distinguish the difference between the words in people's hearts and the words spoken out loud.","She then said to her son, \"Besides mommy, if others don't speak out loud to you, just listen quietly and don't answer, okay?\"","The little one seemed a bit confused and thought for a while, asking, \"Why?\"","Yanshu said, \"Because others can't hear the words in people's hearts like you, this is a special ability that only you have. If others find out, they might want to take it away.\"","The two-year-old little one, currently in a very possessive phase, immediately hugged himself with his chubby little hands and said seriously, \"Can't take!\"","Yanshu quickly comforted, \"Daddy and mommy will protect you, so no one can take away your ability, but you also shouldn't let others find out, okay?\"","The little one nodded understandingly.","Yanshu stroked the little one's head and sighed inwardly. Having such a powerful ability from a young age wasn't an easy thing.","She would certainly protect her child well, but she was also afraid that if the wrong people found out, they might use the innocent child for evil.","Fortunately, the current palace environment was good, with everyone around being kind and honest.","As the child grew older and understood right from wrong, everything would be fine.","Seeing that her efforts were not in vain, Yuwen Lan became even more motivated to educate his son. He continued to use the gradual influence method, teaching his son a few wise sayings every night and trying to explain them in a way that a child could understand.","Of course, with the busy court affairs, he still mostly had to spend time with his son in the evenings, reviewing what was learned the previous day and teaching a few new sentences.","However, the little one, as before, often fell asleep after hearing no more than five or six sentences, sleeping very soundly.","Yuwen Lan believed that this must be because the little one was tired from playing during the day.","And he wasn't worried at all, after all, his son had been sleeping like this since he was born, and he still remembered everything he should.","Anyway, it's a matter of accumulation, his son is doing great.","However, speaking of which, the Empress Dowager had been \"dead\" for over two years, and the mourning period was almost over. Since his son was so outstanding, maybe...","Have another one or two more?","Of course, after witnessing the birth of his eldest son last time, he had deeply realized that childbirth was still a difficult task for women, so regarding this matter, he still had to consider Yanshu's opinion.","Late at night, with such expectations, the monarch entered the Central Palace.","As usual, his beloved wife and son were snuggling in bed reading novels.","His wife and son both looked freshly bathed, with pink faces and slightly damp hair.","Especially the little one in his clean nightclothes, looking exceptionally cute.","Seeing him come, the little one was also very happy, bouncing over to greet him, \"Heng'er greets father.\"","Yuwen Lan's heart softened, and he quickly picked up the little one, asking gently, \"What did my baby do today? Do you miss daddy?\"","The little one nodded seriously, \"Baby misses daddy, and eats, plays.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Putting daddy first, baby is a filial child.\"","As he thought this, he couldn't help but wonder, if they had another child, would it be as cute as the little one?","He didn't know if the little one wanted a brother or a sister?","Just as he was thinking this, the little one in his arms suddenly said, \"Brother, sister.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Could it be that the little one heard what he was thinking?","Oh, right, he almost forgot, his son seemed to have inherited his telepathy.","Tsk, back then, even Yanshu couldn't hear his thoughts and had to touch her stomach to do so, but the little one could hear it right away?","Hmm, indeed a smart child, perfecting his telepathy to such a level.","While he was silently proud, Yanshu was also secretly pondering—","Hearing her son's words, did that mean someone wanted a second child?","Hehe, actually, she wanted one too.","During the New Year's festival, some ministers' family members brought their little granddaughter to pay their respects, and the pink and tender little girl was so adorable.","If she had a daughter, she would dress her up every day, combing her hair into beautiful braids, wearing pretty little dresses...","Thinking of this, she wanted a daughter even more!!!","And Yuwen Lan, who overheard quietly, also nodded in his heart.","Yes, now that they already had a son, if heaven could bless them with another daughter, that would be even better.","So he asked the little one, \"Do you want a brother or a sister, baby?\"","The couple looked at their son together.","The little one thought for a while and giggled, \"Want sister.\"","Yanshu, \"???\"","Yuwen Lan, \"???\"","What? The son wanted a sister?","At this moment, the little one repeated very seriously, \"Heng'er wants a sister.\"","Yanshu, \"......This is something even Mother can't do.\"","As she said this, she glanced at Yuwen Lan, who immediately responded, \"Then Father definitely can't do it either.\""]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter Ten","The Little Crown Prince's wish was indeed a bit of a challenge for his father and mother.","However, although having a sister might be difficult, having a younger sister seemed quite possible.","Of course, Yanshu knew that the gender of a child couldn't be determined by desire alone, but there's a saying that human effort can influence outcomes, so she decided to prepare thoroughly.","Thus, she first called upon the System.","【System, do you have any secret recipes for having a daughter?】","System, 【...Hasn't anyone told you that the gender of a child mainly depends on your husband? I'm afraid I can't help with that.】","Yanshu, 【...Life is so boring, a little fun wouldn't hurt. I just want to express my urgent desire, like some people praying before an exam.】","After all, she had already experienced a time-travel and possessed such a powerful System. So, even if she temporarily indulged in a bit of superstition, as long as it increased the chances, it was worth a try.","System, 【...You do have a point. But I really don't have any secret recipes. Seeing how articulate you are, I can chat with you for a bit. You know, before the Eldest Princess conceived her daughter, she had a particular fondness for grapes. Ankang county lord, before conceiving her daughter, loved peaches, and the Grand Princess, before conceiving Ankang county lord, was very fond of honeydew melons.】","Yanshu, 【...】","Grapes, peaches, honeydew melons?","These were all summer fruits. But now it was only early spring. There were no greenhouses back then, and the imperial fruit storehouse only had oranges, apples, and pears left over from last autumn. Where could she find these fruits?","She felt a bit discouraged, 【Is there any way to have a daughter without eating these? Just to boost my confidence.】","System, 【...You're quite demanding. How about something practical? Just go ask the imperial physician.】","Yanshu's eyes lit up. Right, why hadn't she thought of that earlier?","Since she was preparing for pregnancy, it would be good to have the imperial physician check her health and adjust her body!","She immediately summoned Xun the Imperial Physician.","Soon, Xun the Imperial Physician arrived in a hurry with his medical box.","Unexpectedly summoned, he thought something urgent had happened in the imperial harem and asked anxiously, \"Is there something wrong with Your Majesty?\"","To his surprise, Yanshu smiled and said, \"I'm not unwell. I'm planning to have another child and want you to help me adjust my body. If you could increase the chances of having a daughter, that would be even better.\"","Xun the Imperial Physician, \"......\"","Well, he had seen many who wanted sons, but a queen who wanted a daughter this much was the first.","He quickly agreed, \"I obey, but there's no absolute guarantee in determining the gender of a child. Please be prepared, Your Majesty.\"","Yanshu nodded eagerly, \"Understood, understood.\"","She then turned to the little one beside her and said, \"See, baby, Mama has done her best. If I can't have a sister this time and it's a brother instead, don't be upset, okay?\"","But the little one insisted, \"I want a sister!\"","Yanshu, \"......\"","Xun the Imperial Physician, \"......\"","It was indeed a bit too much to ask, Little Crown Prince.","After a diagnosis by Doctor Jiang, Yanshu was found to be generally healthy, though slightly yin-deficient and damp-cold, requiring some adjustments. Thus, Yanshu began her days of drinking medicine again.","This time, not only did she drink it herself, but she also made Yuwen Lan drink with her.","After all, in determining the gender of a child, the man played a more significant role.","Although Yuwen Lan found it amusing, seeing her so enthusiastic, he could only cooperate. After all, for the sake of their child, he could endure the bitter medicine.","Yanshu, though a foodie, really disliked the bitter taste. But for a lovely little daughter, she had to swallow it with a pinched nose.","Her little foodie baby, unaware of the truth, saw his mother drinking large gulps of the dark, hot soup and thought it was something delicious. He stood on tiptoe by the table, anxiously asking, \"What is Mama drinking?\"","Yanshu, her face contorted from the bitterness, could only laugh and say, \"Mama is drinking medicine.\"","The little one, though over two years old, had been in excellent health since birth and hadn't been sick much. So, the concept of \"medicine\" was foreign to him.","Hearing his mother say this, the little one still didn't understand and curiously asked, \"Can I taste it?\"","Yanshu, \"......\"","This little glutton was indeed her own child.","Unable to refuse, she used a spoon to dip a bit of the leftover medicine and said, \"Here, taste it.\"","The little one, without any hesitation, licked it.","Immediately, his little face scrunched up, and he frowned, saying, \"Bitter, bitter......\"","Yanshu quickly handed him a cup of water to rinse his mouth, saying, \"Now you know, medicine isn't tasty. You must keep healthy and drink less medicine in the future.\"","The little one nodded and even worried about her, saying, \"Mama, don't drink medicine.\"","Yanshu, moved, hugged the little one and kissed him, saying, \"Mama is drinking medicine to give you a little sister. I endure the bitterness for that.\"","But as she finished speaking, the little one frowned and said, \"I want a sister.\"","Yanshu, \"......This, Mama really can't do, my dear. How about this, when the little sister is born, you two can discuss if she can be the sister and you the brother?\"","The little one, not quite understanding, nodded, \"Mm-hmm.\"","Rendong, \"......\"","This mother and son duo were truly one of a kind.","Thanks to Yanshu's persistence, as summer approached in the capital, she was once again with child.","This time, unlike her previous pregnancy, she didn't experience morning sickness and had a great appetite. As summer fruits began to appear, she indulged in cherries, lychees, grapes, and more, making her skin glow with moisture.","Her little one also enjoyed the same diet as his mother, making his skin exceptionally good. The mother and son looked so fair and radiant that it was enviable.","As before, upon learning of her pregnancy, her mother from Duke Zhongyi's Mansion visited the palace several times, each time bringing homemade meat buns, large vegetable boxes, etc. Not only did Yanshu enjoy them, but her little one also had several delicious meals, making his little belly round and full.","The little one was very happy. As he watched his mother's belly grow day by day, he gradually understood that there was a baby inside, the sister he wanted. So, he called to his mother's belly, \"Sister......\"","Yanshu, \"......\"","Yuwen Lan, \"......\"","At first, the couple thought the little one would forget about the sister, but months had passed, and he still remembered.","This could be a problem. If the second child was born and the little one still called it sister, others might think the Crown Prince was a fool.","Yanshu expressed her concerns to her husband.","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"Indeed, we need to have a serious talk with the little one about this.\"","He then led the little one to him and said gently, \"Baby, you're growing up now, a little man, right?\"","The little one nodded, \"Little man, don't hit wife.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"......\"","Yanshu, \"......\"","The little one's associative thinking was quite strong.","Of course, there was an urgent matter to address, so the father continued to explain to his son, \"Besides not hitting your wife, there are many other things to pay attention to.\"","The little one blinked his big eyes and asked, \"What?\"","Yuwen Lan guided, \"For example, Heng'er is the first child of your father and mother, the eldest brother.\"","Yanshu quickly added, \"Daddy is right. In the future, you'll also be the eldest brother. Being the eldest brother is very powerful, you can play with your younger brothers and sisters.\"","At this, the little one's eyes lit up and said, \"Play climbing trees, catching birds, fishing!\"","Yanshu quickly nodded, \"Yes, yes, you can do all that with your younger siblings. So being a big brother is great, right?\"","The little one nodded, \"I want to be the big brother!\"","Yuwen Lan nodded, \"You'll soon be a big brother. When the baby in Mama's belly is born, you'll be the big brother.\"","The little one looked at his mother's bulging belly and smiled with his little white teeth, saying, \"Baby.\"","Hee hee, thinking about it this way, the little one realized that having younger siblings was actually quite nice, and so gradually forgot about the sister matter, focusing all his attention on calling the baby in his mother's belly \"Little Treasure,\" filled with anticipation.","As days passed, the baby in Yanshu's belly began to move, especially when hearing the voice of his brother, becoming even more lively.","The Little Crown Prince also grew more fond of greeting the baby inside through his mother's belly, and if he could feel the baby move, he would become even more excited.","Yanshu took the opportunity to guide, \"Wow, Little Treasure really likes Little Crown Prince brother, she only gets this happy when he talks.\"","Hearing this, the Little Crown Prince became even happier and quickly said to the belly, \"Little Treasure, come out and play.\"","Yanshu kissed her son's forehead and smiled, \"Soon, when it gets cold, Little Treasure will come out to play with you.\"","As the days went by, by late November, as the capital entered winter, Yanshu was about to give birth.","With the experience from last time, the palace's preparations this time were even more sufficient. Midwives, wet nurses, and doctors like Xun the Imperial Physician and Doctor Jiang were all on standby. As soon as the Empress showed signs of labor, they immediately sprang into action.","Yanshu had heard that the second birth was usually faster than the first, and this time she found it to be true, but along with the faster labor, the pain also intensified.","She remembered when she gave birth to the Little Crown Prince, she was still chatting and laughing with Rendong in the first half of the night, but this time she was in so much pain that she couldn't speak.","Outside the delivery room, Yuwen Lan was also anxiously waiting with the Little Crown Prince.","Nearly a year had passed, and the Little Crown Prince was about to turn three.","The little one had become more sensible, tightly holding his father's hand, not saying a word.","Seeing that it was late, the wet nurse stepped forward to suggest, \"It's getting late, how about letting the Crown Prince go to rest first?\"","But the little one shook his head, \"I want to wait for Mama to come out.\"","Yuwen Lan asked his son gently, \"Heng'er, are you not sleepy?\"","The little one shook his head, \"I insist, I want to wait for Mama and Little Treasure.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded and asked the wet nurse to step back.","The hall was somewhat quiet when Yuwen Lan suddenly heard the little one say, \"Mama is in pain.\"","Yuwen Lan stroked the little one's head and sighed, \"Yes, Mama was in the same pain when she gave birth to you, so you must always be filial to Mama, understand?\"","The little one nodded, and after a while, he said, \"A man, loves his wife.\"","Yuwen Lan, \"......Mm.\"","His wife giving birth was so difficult, of course, he would cherish her dearly.","Anyway, whether this time it was a boy or a girl, he wouldn't let her go through such pain again.","Fortunately, father and son didn't have to endure for long. At a certain moment, a faint cry of a baby suddenly came from the room, followed by Lianxin rushing in to report the good news, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, the Empress has given birth to a little princess, both mother and child are safe.\"","Both mother and child are safe!","Yuwen Lan finally breathed a sigh of relief and then quickly told his son, who was tightly holding his hand, \"Mama is fine, Heng'er has a little sister.\"","The little one also smiled and clapped his hands, \"A man, loves his sister!\"","Yuwen Lan kissed the little one's forehead and hummed in agreement.","These were the most precious people in his life, and he loved them all."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 11","At the break of dawn, the back courtyard of the Mansion of the Guardian General was already bustling with activity.","Sixteen-year-old Zhou Ruolan opened her eyes, awakening from her slumber.","It felt like emerging from a long dream; in the blink of an eye, she had returned to her days as a young maiden.","Indeed, she was no longer the Empress Dowager of Great Liang who had passed away.","Instead, she was once again Zhou Ruolan, the eldest daughter of the Guardian General's family, known by her original name.","Hearing faint commotion coming from outside, she gathered her thoughts, pulled aside the bed curtains, and called for her maid to inquire, \"What's happening?\"","The maid quickly replied, \"I heard that the young master snuck out of the academy last night to drink, and the steward caught him and brought him back. Madam is currently scolding him in the courtyard.\"","It was that good-for-nothing brother Zhou Yucheng again.","Zhou Ruolan temporarily set aside her thoughts and got out of bed, saying,","\"Help me dress, I'll go take a look.\"","The maid responded and hurriedly began her work.","When Zhou Ruolan stepped out of her room, the sky had grown a bit brighter.","But her brother Zhou Yucheng was still kneeling in the courtyard, while their mother, Madam Zhou, stood nearby, alternating between scolding and crying.","Zhou Ruolan walked up to them and, without a word, raised the horsewhip in her hand and began striking Zhou Yucheng.","Zhou Yucheng, who had been merely enduring the verbal lecture, was caught off guard by the sudden whipping and began crying out in pain. Madam Zhou was also startled and quickly moved to stop her, asking, \"Ruolan, what are you doing?\"","Zhou Ruolan calmly replied, \"He did wrong, and I'm helping you discipline him.\"","Madam Zhou stammered, then hurriedly said, \"The whip is too harsh, be careful not to hurt him too badly.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Zhou Yucheng began wailing even louder than before.","Zhou Ruolan said coldly, \"Without severity, he won't learn his lesson. At such a young age, he already dares to go out drinking and visiting courtesans. Never mind our family's reputation, but if we let this slide, what will become of him in the future? How many times have you given him these mild scoldings since he was young? Has he ever improved? To be frank, Zhou Yucheng has you figured out completely. Every time he makes a mistake, you scold him a bit, he cries a little, and you soften your heart. Then he does it again, and worse than before. Mother, if you want to discipline him, you must steel your heart and give him a proper thrashing, correct his bad habits all at once.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhou Yucheng was frightened and quickly crawled to Madam Zhou's feet, crying for help, \"Elder Sister must be possessed, Mother! She's trying to whip me to death!\"","Before he could finish speaking, Zhou Ruolan delivered two more lashes, angrily saying, \"Shut your mouth! You're supposed to be a man, but what can you do besides cause trouble for the family? Now you have parents to protect you, but who will keep you in line after they're gone?\"","The hatred from both her past and present lives combined, making her show no mercy as she whipped that good-for-nothing brother until he was rolling on the ground crying out in pain. This scene frightened Madam Zhou, but seeing that she couldn't stop her daughter, she had no choice but to hurry to the front courtyard to find her husband.","Thus, after finishing with her worthless brother, Zhou Ruolan went to face her father.","Having just heard his wife's tearful complaint, Guardian General Zhou Pengze sternly asked his daughter, \"I hear you defied your mother just now. What exactly happened?\"","Zhou Ruolan sighed and said, \"Father is busy with court affairs daily and has no time to discipline Yucheng, while Mother is too soft-hearted. But excessive kindness breeds disaster. Yucheng is only fourteen, yet he already dares to sneak out to drink and visit brothels. If we don't discipline him strictly now, what will become of him? Unlike you, Father, he was born in peaceful times, lying back and enjoying the peaceful days that our ancestors paid for with their lives. He doesn't understand how difficult life can be or the principle of staying vigilant in times of peace. If this continues, should he make a grave mistake one day, even Grandfather's and your merits might not be able to save him.\"","After hearing this, the General was quite surprised that his young daughter could speak with such foresight.","He stroked his beard, looked her up and down, and finally nodded, \"You speak truly. I have been negligent in his education. From now on, Yucheng will be in your charge. No matter what, you must correct his bad habits as soon as possible.\"","Zhou Ruolan quickly agreed.","When Zhou Yucheng heard the news, his legs went weak.","Indeed, after that whipping's deterrent effect, Zhou Yucheng behaved much better for the next few days.","Because he discovered that his sister seemed to have become a different person, being particularly harsh with him, whipping him for the slightest mistake without mercy, and even their mother couldn't stop her.","Though Madam Zhou felt heartache, she could do nothing but send someone to deliver medicine for her son's wounds.","However, seeing that her son didn't dare misbehave anymore, she was ultimately relieved.","In mid-March, when spring was in full bloom in the capital.","With her father's birthday approaching in a few days.","As a gesture of filial piety, Zhou Ruolan planned to go to the market to buy a set of scholar's four treasures as a birthday gift for her father, so she made a special trip out that day.","When the carriage reached the front of Academy Street, it suddenly stopped, and then she heard the sound of gongs and drums.","The driver craned his neck to look and reported to her, \"Miss, today is the Imperial Examination announcement ceremony, and it seems the road ahead is blocked.\"","Zhou Ruolan made a sound of acknowledgment, finally realizing that she had stumbled upon the day of the palace examination results announcement.","This was a grand occasion for the court, so she said, \"Then we'll wait.\"","Hearing the drums and gongs getting closer, she couldn't help but lift the carriage curtain to look. The street was crowded with people, all craning their necks to catch a glimpse of the new imperial scholars.","Logically, there should be many familiar faces among them.","After all, in her previous life, most of these people had entered the court and assisted her in managing state affairs.","For instance, the top scholar riding the white horse with red flowers in his cap at the front was He Chengyin, who would later become Princess Yuwen Hui's consort.","She smiled faintly and looked further back, seeing the second-ranked scholar, about twenty-five or twenty-six years old, who would later become Lu Kaihe, the Minister of Works.","Looking further back at the third-ranked scholar following the second, she saw another young man, but when she clearly saw his features, she froze.","This was him at barely twenty years old, tall as a bamboo, with eyes like flowing light, seeming even more elegant and otherworldly than when she first met him in her previous life.","Zhou Ruolan stared blankly, almost calling out his name.","Shu Guang...","Yes, it was him.","The man who had accompanied her through several decades of her previous life, in whose arms she had closed her eyes for the last time...","As if reuniting after a long separation, at this moment, she quietly gazed at his appearance, almost bringing tears to her eyes.","As if by some spiritual connection, across the dense crowd, he suddenly cast his gaze in her direction.","Their eyes met, and they silently looked at each other until his horse gradually moved forward, and he could no longer look back at her.","Zhou Ruolan came back to her senses and finally lowered the carriage curtain, but slightly furrowed her brow.","Strange, she remembered that in her previous life, he had participated in the palace examination two years later.","How was he here in this year's examination?","Following tradition, on the third day after the palace examination results announcement, the royal family held a celebration banquet at Changchun Garden to entertain the new imperial scholars.","By afternoon, Changchun Garden gradually became lively, but the guests arriving at the garden were not just the new imperial scholars.","It turned out that today, besides the celebration banquet at Qushui Garden, there was another banquet across the lake at Huifang Garden, hosted by the Empress to entertain the royal clan members and noble ladies for spring appreciation.","Of course, everyone knew that currently in the court, the Princess, the Second Prince, and the Third Prince were all of marriageable age, and the Emperor and Empress wanted to take this opportunity to find suitable matches for their children.","Therefore, all the young ladies who came to the garden today were carefully dressed, each trying to catch the Empress's attention and find chances to speak with her.","However, just after Zhou Ruolan had paid her respects to the Empress, she was pulled aside by Princess Yuwen Hui.","\"Ruolan, today my royal parents are arranging my marriage. Quick, come with me to see if the top scholar is truly handsome or not.\"","Having grown up together and being naturally forthright, among all the noble ladies, only she was most favored by Yuwen Hui and considered her best friend.","As the beloved daughter of the founding Emperor and Empress, Yuwen Hui was pampered and thus outgoing and passionate.","This scene, which truly violated proper etiquette, had also occurred once in her previous life.","However, at that time, Zhou Ruolan had thoroughly discouraged Yuwen Hui, but this time, she nodded and agreed to go along with her.","Taking a pleasure boat across the lake, they soon arrived outside Qushui Garden.","Although Yuwen Hui was naturally vivacious and energetic, she still knew proper etiquette, especially since her royal father was present in the garden today. Therefore, she only dared to peek quietly through the flower-patterned window from outside the wall.","Of course, although there were dozens of people in the garden today, the Top Scholar was easily distinguishable from others due to his distinct attire and his seat being closer to the Emperor, making him immediately recognizable.","After observing for a while, Yuwen Hui nodded with satisfaction, \"This He Chengyin looks quite decent.\"","Zhou Ruolan tried hard to suppress her smile as she congratulated her, \"Congratulations, Your Highness.\"","As she spoke, she also deliberately glanced through the wall several times.","Although his attire wasn't as eye-catching as the Top Scholar's, she still recognized him instantly.","Just like the other day, he maintained that same elegant and otherworldly demeanor.","No one else could compare to him.","She thought to herself that with his scholarly abilities, he was actually no less accomplished than He Chengyin, so perhaps he had deliberately held back this time?","While lost in her thoughts, Yuwen Hui's voice suddenly reached her ears, \"Hmm? Ruolan, who are you looking at?\"","She quickly feigned shyness and withdrew her gaze, lowering her head as she said, \"Just... looking around, Your Highness, please don't tease your humble servant.\"","But Yuwen Hui insisted on teasing her, wiggling her eyebrows and chuckling, \"Don't be so formal with me, tell me, have you perhaps taken a fancy to one of the young lords?\"","Zhou Ruolan refused to say anything.","Yuwen Hui then stretched her neck to look again, pondering, \"I think the Third Scholar is quite handsome too, though a bit thin.\"","Zhou Ruolan pretended to be startled and quickly covered Yuwen Hui's mouth with her hand, saying shyly, \"Please stop, Your Highness.\"","Yuwen Hui laughed, \"What's wrong with that? If you like him, I can ask Father Emperor to arrange your marriage too. Though I heard his family isn't wealthy or noble, as long as you don't mind.\"","After giggling for a while, Yuwen Hui remembered something and became more serious, saying to her, \"But speaking of marriage, don't you want to marry into the royal family and become my sister-in-law? Today, Mother Empress plans to look for potential princesses for my second and third brothers.\"","Zhou Ruolan quickly responded solemnly, \"Your humble servant is not worthy of such honor and dares not aim so high. I only wish to live as a common citizen.\"","Seeing this, Yuwen Hui sighed and said, \"Well then, I suppose my second and third brothers are the unfortunate ones. Someone with your wonderful personality cannot be found anywhere else in this garden today.\"","Zhou Ruolan quickly lowered her head again, saying, \"Your Highness flatters me.\"","As they spoke, she caught a glimpse of someone's skirt disappearing behind a nearby tree. Her heart steadied, and she said, \"It's getting late, we should head back now, lest someone sees us.\"","Yuwen Hui nodded and left with her."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter Twelve","When Zhou Ruolan and Yuwen Hui returned to Huifang Garden, the evening banquet was about to begin.","Naturally, everyone wanted to be closer to the Empress, but not everyone could fulfill their wish. However, Zhou Ruolan was pulled by Yuwen Hui and managed to sit not far from the Empress.","The garden, which had been filled with the chatter of birds and swallows, now saw everyone gathered before them, and Empress Guo's gaze first fell upon Zhou Ruolan.","\"It's been a while since I last saw you, Ruolan. You seem to have grown taller? You're becoming a young lady.\"","Zhou Ruolan quickly lowered her head to respond, \"Thank you for your kind words, Your Majesty.\"","With so many people present, the Empress spoke to her first, leaving the other ladies feeling sour. The Empress then asked her, \"Why didn't I see you earlier?\"","Before Zhou Ruolan could answer, someone else spoke up, \"I saw someone from afar by the lake earlier, it looked like Miss Zhou. Was I mistaken?\"","Anyone who had been to Changchun Garden knew that the other side of the lake was Qushui Garden, where the Emperor, princes, and new scholars were today. Normally, female guests were not allowed to go there freely. If Zhou Ruolan had indeed been there earlier, it would be quite intriguing.","So, as soon as these words were spoken, everyone turned to look at her.","Yuwen Hui was also quite nervous, secretly cursing Yao Huiqin for being so meddlesome. How could she recognize Ruolan from such a distance?","What should they do now? Should she help Ruolan cover it up with a lie?","But instead, Ruolan said, \"Miss Yao probably wasn't mistaken. When I entered the garden today, the wind was strong, and my handkerchief was blown away. I just went to look for it.\"","The tumultuous waves of the palace from her previous life were still etched in her mind. She naturally hadn't forgotten that Yao Huiqin was the Consort who had killed her child and tried to push her own son to the throne.","Of course, she later met her fate of being banished to the cold palace and given a white silk to die, along with her entire clan.","Given another chance, this woman still wanted to target her.","However, it also suited her intentions.","With those words spoken, Yao Huiqin quickly pretended to laugh and nodded, \"I see, I thought I was mistaken.\"","Zhou Ruolan didn't say anything more to her but quickly stood up to apologize to the Empress, \"I acted rashly earlier, please forgive me, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Hui quickly added, \"Mother, it's not Ruolan's fault. We all had to pass by the lake when we entered the garden. Ruolan's handkerchief was blown away by the wind. If she hadn't gone to retrieve it, people would have gossiped even more.\"","She also shot a fierce glance at Yao Huiqin.","Hmph, this Yao girl is really annoying! Does she think that by suppressing Ruolan, she has a chance to marry into the royal family?","Not a chance!","Hearing her daughter say this, Empress Guo said to Zhou Ruolan, \"It's a minor matter, no need to be so nervous. Sit down.\"","However, compared to before, her tone was noticeably colder.","Seeing this, many people felt a sense of schadenfreude.","Zhou Ruolan felt it wasn't enough yet.","Fortunately, her cousin Zhou Shulan, who was always jealous of her, was also present today.","Hopefully, she wouldn't disappoint.","Sure enough, as soon as she thanked the Empress and sat down, Zhou Shulan spoke up, \"Thank you for your mercy, Your Majesty. Actually, Ruolan is very sensible. Usually, when my uncle is busy with his duties, she helps my aunt manage the household. My younger brother is young and immature, these days it's all thanks to her guidance that he's made progress.\"","This piqued Empress Guo's curiosity and she asked Zhou Ruolan, \"How do you discipline your brother?\"","Zhou Ruolan followed her cousin's lead and honestly replied to the Empress, \"Your Majesty, I don't have any special methods. I just whip him with a horsewhip.\"","What? A horsewhip... whip him?","Seeing her say this so calmly, all the ladies were shocked.","Empress Guo's expression also changed, and her gaze towards Zhou Ruolan grew colder.","After that, she didn't speak to her again.","Cousin Zhou Shulan was quite satisfied with this outcome.","Zhou Ruolan herself was also satisfied.","Meanwhile, across the lake in Qushui Garden, the Rong'en Banquet was also underway.","Each batch of new scholars was the hope of the court, especially this year with more young people, which was quite pleasing. The founding Emperor also set aside his dignity for once, engaging in a flowing water wine party and enjoying wine with these talents.","Delicious dishes were continuously served, and the palace servants were busy. During this time, Second Prince Yuwen Sheng quietly slipped away to a secluded spot.","Someone immediately whispered something to him.","After listening, Yuwen Sheng frowned—","The Zhou girl had actually incurred his mother's displeasure?","Why was this girl different from before?","He had thought she was meticulous and steady, but it turned out she was also so foolish?","But the Zhou family was still a force he needed. Moreover, the girl was bright and poised, fitting for the position of Princess Consort...","After some silent consideration, Yuwen Sheng still instructed the person who came to him and then returned to the banquet as if nothing had happened.","He thought he was acting undetected, but he didn't know that as soon as he got up earlier, someone had already written down his actions on a piece of paper and secretly passed it to Third Prince Yuwen Cheng...","As the bright moon slowly moved westward, the time was getting late, and the evening banquet in Huifang Garden was also drawing to a close.","Empress Guo got up first and left, and after everyone had bowed, they dispersed.","Taking the opportunity, Yuwen Hui quickly pulled Zhou Ruolan to the side, apologizing, \"Ruolan, I'm sorry for tonight. I caused you to be misunderstood by my mother. I didn't expect Yao Huiqin to follow us!\"","Zhou Ruolan comforted her, \"Your Highness, you're too polite. This is also what I should do. However, Yao Huiqin probably wasn't trying to target the princess, but rather wanted to embarrass me.\"","Yuwen Hui still looked indignant and snorted, \"This ugly girl thinks that by suppressing you, my mother will look upon her favorably? I definitely won't let her succeed! She's bullying you, which means she's bullying me. Watch how I deal with her!\"","Zhou Ruolan smiled again, \"Your Highness is wise, but you really don't need to be angry about this.\"","The Empress Guo doted on this daughter immensely. Since Yao Huiqin had offended the apple of the Empress's eye today, it was unlikely she would have an easy time entering the royal family, whether as a wife or a concubine.","Yuwen Hui was still concerned about her and said, \"But how will it be if my mother misunderstands you? Especially at this time. My mother actually liked you a lot and wanted you...\"","Before she could finish, Zhou Ruolan quickly said, \"Your Highness, don't worry. The Empress is kind-hearted and benevolent and definitely won't mistreat me because of a small matter. Besides... I have no intention of climbing the social ladder or attaching myself to influential figures.\"","Yuwen Hui sighed, \"Alright, it seems you really don't want to join the Yuwen Family... Ruolan, I owe you this time, and I will definitely repay you well in the future.\"","Zhou Ruolan thanked her with a smile and then bowed, \"It's getting late, I should take my leave.\"","Yuwen Hui felt reluctant and said, \"Why don't you stay tonight? I'll be accompanying my mother here for the night, you can stay with me and we can chat.\"","She politely declined, \"Thank you for your kind offer, Your Highness, but I'm afraid my family will worry.\"","After a pause, she added, \"However, my father's birthday is coming up, and we'll be hosting a few banquets at home. If Your Highness is gracious, I would dare to invite you.\"","Yuwen Hui immediately nodded, \"Yes, yes, as long as you send me an invitation, I will definitely come.\"","Alas, in a few days, my father and mother will be arranging my marriage, and then I won't be able to go out so freely.","Having made arrangements with Yuwen Hui, Zhou Ruolan left Changchun Garden.","She had spent some time talking, and most of the guests had already left. Now, there were only a few carriages left outside the garden.","Zhou Ruolan scanned the carriages and noticed one that was clearly not from a noble family but looked like one rented from the market.","She silently pondered for a moment, then boarded her own carriage and headed home.","As the wheels rolled, Changchun Garden slowly faded into the distance. However, after traveling for a while, there was a sudden \"crack,\" and the carriage came to a stop.","Her maid Zi Zhu was startled and quickly lifted the curtain to ask the coachman, \"What's the matter?\"","The coachman replied, \"I don't know what we ran over earlier, but the wheel got bent.\"","\"What?\"","Zi Zhu complained to the coachman, \"Uncle Zhao, what's wrong with you? It's dark out, how are we supposed to get the lady back to the mansion?\"","Just as she finished speaking, another carriage's sounds came from behind.","The sound of horses and wheels approached, followed by a man's voice, \"May I ask what happened?\"","Zi Zhu lifted the curtain and peeked out, then quickly reported to her, \"Miss, it seems to be the official who entered the garden today.\"","Zhou Ruolan had already known the answer from the familiar voice, so she said, \"Then ask properly and see if he can give us a ride.\"","After they returned to the mansion, they would send someone to pick up the coachman.","The maidservant agreed and quickly asked the other party, \"May I know the honorable name of the official? We are from the Mansion of the Guardian General. Our carriage broke down here due to a malfunction. If it is convenient for the official, could you possibly give us a ride back to the city?\"","As the words fell, Ruolan listened carefully inside the carriage, only to hear the young voice say, \"My surname is Qi, and I am a scholar who attended the Enron Banquet today. If the lady feels at ease, please feel free to step into my carriage.\"","Upon hearing this, the maidservant immediately thanked the other party and helped Ruolan down from the carriage.","Before getting on the carriage, Zhou Ruolan raised her eyes and looked.","The man had already stepped out of the carriage and stood by the side, and under the good moonlight of tonight, one could discern the even younger eyebrows and eyes than in her memory.","She turned sideways and bowed to him, saying, \"Thank you for your help, Official Qi.\"","The other party also quickly bowed to her and said, \"It's just a small favor, Miss, you're too kind. Please get on the carriage.\"","She agreed and boarded the carriage with Zi Zhu.","Qi Shuguang then sat on the carriage frame with the coachman.","The carriage moved on, continuing towards the city.","Compared to their own carriage, this rented one was a bit cramped and swayed quite a bit.","But Ruolan only felt warmth in her heart.","She could guess that tonight, Yuwen Sheng might have come out to \"help\" her.","But because of his presence, Yuwen Sheng did not appear.","After a while, they had entered the city, and the road gradually became lively, slowing down the carriage's speed.","Through the carriage curtain, Zhou Ruolan asked, \"May I know where Official Qi is from? Judging from your attire, you should be the new top scholar, right?\"","She heard the voice outside the curtain answer, \"You flatter me, Miss. I am from Langya County, Mizhou Prefecture.\"","The clear voice seemed to carry a hint of a smile.","Ruolan also gently tugged at the corners of her lips.","Langya, what a wonderful place!","She had recalled the scent of wheat she smelled every time they returned to that quiet village in her previous life.","Her thoughts returned to the present, and while Zi Zhu wasn't paying attention, she quietly slipped off the sandalwood bracelet on her wrist and placed it in his sash bag.","After a while, they finally arrived at the Mansion of the Guardian General.","Stepping down from the carriage, Zhou Ruolan bowed to the man and thanked him.","\"Official Qi, I have no way to repay your kindness today.\"","The young man quickly bowed and said, \"Miss, you're too kind. Tonight was just a small favor, please don't dwell on it.\"","Zhou Ruolan then said, \"In five days is my father's birthday. If Official Qi does not mind, I sincerely invite you to our humble home.\"","After speaking, she bid farewell to the other party and turned to step into her family's mansion.","Zi Zhu hurriedly followed and whispered to her along the way, \"Why did the lady invite that official to attend Master's birthday banquet? Is it to thank him?\"","Zhou Ruolan smiled and said, \"Otherwise? If we had given him money, do you think he would have taken it?\"","Zi Zhu nodded and said, \"That's true. That official seems to be a man of noble character, he definitely wouldn't take money. I just wonder if he will come. He doesn't seem to be from a noble family.\"","Ruolan, however, smiled and said, \"Whether he comes or not depends on him, but whether we invite him or not depends on us.\"","If he recognizes that wooden bracelet, he will definitely come."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 13","Five days passed swiftly, and it was time for the Guardian General's birthday celebration.","In truth, Guardian General Zhou Pengze was barely in his forties, so he didn't arrange for any grand festivities. He merely invited a few relatives and colleagues to his residence for a gathering.","Nevertheless, Zhou Ruolan woke up early to assist her mother in welcoming the guests who arrived at their residence.","The sixteen-year-old young lady was as radiant as a begonia in bloom, and her every movement displayed such natural grace that all the guests couldn't help but praise her.","Before long, Zi Zhu came running to her, saying, \"Miss, Young Master Qi has arrived.\"","Young Master Qi?","Her heart steadied as she told her mother, \"Mother, the benefactor who helped me return home the other day has arrived. I'll go welcome him.\"","Madam Zhou had already heard about this matter and nodded, \"Go quickly, and don't be remiss in your duties.\"","Zhou Ruolan acknowledged and headed to the front courtyard.","When she arrived, she saw that Qi Shuguang had just entered the hall. He wore a bamboo-green robe that wasn't particularly luxurious compared to others, yet his bearing set him apart.","Perhaps it was because most of the guests today were military officials, but as a scholar among them, though he appeared somewhat thin, he had an otherworldly presence.","She quietly observed him, and when she approached, she hurriedly introduced him to her father, \"Father, this is Young Master Qi who helped me return from Changchun Garden that day.\"","Upon hearing this, General Zhou quickly greeted Qi Shuguang, \"So it's Official Qi, please forgive my discourtesy.\"","In the past few days, the court had successively announced appointments for the new imperial scholars, and General Zhou had heard that this Third Place Scholar had been appointed as an Imperial Lecturer in the Hanlin Academy, surely destined for a brilliant future.","Qi Shuguang replied, \"I don't deserve such courtesy. I've boldly come to disturb you today to wish the General happiness as vast as the Eastern Sea and longevity like the Southern Mountains. I've brought a humble gift, though it's hardly worthy.\"","He then presented his gift.","General Zhou quickly ordered someone to accept it and smiled, \"I should be the one thanking Official Qi. Please, have a seat. I'm a military man, and there aren't many formalities in my household, so please don't feel constrained.\"","As he finished speaking, Zhou Ruolan, standing beside her father, also smiled and said, \"Yes, please don't stand on ceremony, Official Qi.\"","Qi Shuguang quickly agreed, wearing a gentle smile.","General Zhou secretly raised his eyebrows.","A father knows his daughter best, and this was the first time he had seen his daughter being so friendly toward an outside man.","However, if he hadn't seen it with his own eyes today, he wouldn't have known that the new Third Place Scholar was so young.","He appeared to be not even twenty?","I wonder if he's married yet...","Just as he was about to ask, an announcement came from outside that Princess Changping had arrived.","Immediately, all guests, both men and women, went out to welcome her.","Seeing everyone so nervous, Yuwen Hui giggled and said, \"Everyone, please don't be so formal. I'm just here to chat with Ruolan and wish General Zhou a happy birthday.\"","This made General Zhou extremely anxious, and he quickly said, \"This humble servant thanks Your Highness for your kindness.\"","Yuwen Hui nodded, and as her gaze wandered, she spotted a somewhat familiar figure among the male guests.","She exclaimed in surprise, \"Isn't this... the Third Place Scholar?\"","Qi Shuguang hurriedly bowed again, \"Your humble servant Qi Shuguang pays respects to Your Highness.\"","Yuwen Hui glanced at Zhou Ruolan, then addressed everyone, \"Everyone may rise. I'm going to chat with Ruolan.\"","She then pulled Ruolan toward the back courtyard.","Naturally, Yuwen Hui wanted to know why Qi Shuguang was here.","Zhou Ruolan pretended to be shy and told her about that night's events.","After hearing the story, Yuwen Hui immediately exclaimed, \"Your carriage broke down on the road, and he happened to pass by? Isn't this fate? I must say, you two look quite well-matched.\"","Zhou Ruolan didn't tell her that the carriage breaking down on the road had another reason.","But since both of them had returned safely, this must indeed be fate's arrangement.","She only responded shyly again, \"Your Highness, please stop teasing me.\"","Just then, new guests arrived to pay their respects to Yuwen Hui, and their conversation paused.","Although the celebration wasn't grand, there were still dozens of guests at the residence today.","Zhou Ruolan accompanied Yuwen Hui to meet some people, and when Yao Huiqin appeared with her mother, her heart steadied.","That woman had indeed come.","Yuwen Hui could barely hide her disdain—","This Yao woman had just recently tried to trip up Ruolan, how dare she show her face here today?","She truly had the thickest skin in the world.","However, before long, she understood why this Yao woman had the nerve to come to the Zhou residence.","It turned out her second brother, the Second Prince Yuwen Sheng, had also come today.","Just as when they had greeted her earlier, upon hearing the announcement, everyone in the residence went out again to welcome him.","Everyone respectfully bowed their heads, except for Yao Huiqin, whose face was covered in an undisguisable blush as she kept stealing glances at the Second Prince.","Yuwen Hui understood then that this woman must have set her sights on her second brother, which was why she had the nerve to come to the Zhou residence.","Hmph, what wishful thinking.","Yuwen Hui suppressed her contempt and casually asked her second brother Yuwen Sheng, \"Second Brother, why have you come as well?\"","Yuwen Sheng coughed and said, \"I was passing by the Zhou residence and saw many carriages outside. Then I remembered it was General Zhou's birthday today, so I came to take a look.\"","He then addressed everyone, \"Please don't be nervous, I'll just stay for a short while.\"","He told everyone to rise and entered the hall accompanied by the hosts.","The Zhou family naturally wouldn't dare to be negligent and immediately ordered for the feast to be served.","Thus, everyone followed and took their seats at the banquet.","Yuwen Hui hadn't come today for the feast, so after eating for a while, she pulled Ruolan out to the courtyard.","After complaining about the Yao woman's thick skin and chatting about other matters for a while, they gradually heard the sound of men's voices and cheering.","Yuwen Hui craned her neck to look and saw that in a pavilion by the lake nearby, several young men were playing touhu (arrow throwing game).","Among them, there was one notably thin figure who was immediately recognizable.","Yuwen Hui's eyes lit up, and she quickly pulled Zhou Ruolan forward, \"It seems they're playing touhu? Let's go take a look.\"","Zhou Ruolan didn't refuse.","She had also recognized that among the young men playing touhu was Qi Shuguang.","She had been worried that he might feel constrained on his first visit to their residence, but it seemed he was getting along quite well with the others.","Her heart relaxed, and she followed Yuwen Hui.","Yuwen Hui was determined to play matchmaker today, and upon reaching the pavilion, she volunteered to join the touhu game, insisting that Ruolan join as well.","As it happened, among these young men, almost all were Zhou Ruolan's cousins, either from her father's side or mother's side.","Therefore, she wasn't shy and joined everyone in the game.","After several rounds, everyone was having great fun, their laughter filling the garden, which attracted others to join.","Zhou Shulan and Yao Huiqin appeared beside them at some point, asking, \"May we join in as well?\"","The young men were very open-minded and readily agreed, distributing several arrows to them.","Thus, the touhu group grew larger.","The game continued, and it was soon Zhou Ruolan's turn again.","Her aim was actually quite good, and at this moment, she raised the arrow to take aim.","Just then, a figure wearing a royal blue dragon robe appeared not far away.","It was none other than Yuwen Sheng.","At this moment, everyone was watching Zhou Ruolan's movements.","Only Yao Huiqin, who had been harboring her own intentions, was the first to notice Yuwen Sheng's figure.","She vaguely saw that the Second Prince seemed to be watching Zhou Ruolan's movements as well.","She knew that Zhou Ruolan's aim was very good, having hit the target with all three arrows earlier.","Now, as she watched Zhou Ruolan raise another arrow, about to throw it,","Her heart filled with jealousy, so she hid her own arrow in her sleeve and quietly moved closer to Zhou Ruolan, attempting to use her dress as cover while trying to poke Zhou Ruolan's leg with the arrow.","However, at that very moment, Zhou Ruolan suddenly stepped forward.","And the arrow hidden in Yao Huiqin's sleeve struck Zhou Shulan instead.","The sudden pain caused Zhou Shulan to lose her balance and fall forward.","Instinctively, she grabbed onto her cousin Ruolan's sleeve.","However, it didn't help, and she continued to fall forward, pulling her cousin Ruolan down with her.","In the blink of an eye, Zhou Ruolan instinctively reached out toward the young man across from her.","He simultaneously extended his hand, steadying her before she could hit the copper kettle.","Zhou Shulan, however, was not so fortunate. She fell heavily to the ground with such force that it produced a dull thud.","Everyone was startled and rushed to help her up, only to find that a large bump had already formed on her forehead, and her dress was covered in dust, making her look quite disheveled.","Zhou Shulan had never suffered such humiliation before, and combined with the genuine pain from the fall, she immediately burst into tears.","Seeing this, Zhou Ruolan turned to confront Yao Huiqin, \"Miss Yao, why did you cause my cousin to fall?\"","Yao Huiqin hastily tucked the arrow into her sleeve while defending herself, \"I didn't do anything! Miss Ruolan, you must be mistaken.\"","Before she could finish speaking, Yuwen Hui grabbed her arm and demanded, \"What's this? Why are you hiding an arrow in your sleeve? You used this to trip someone just now, didn't you?\"","Startled, Yao Huiqin quickly tried to defend herself again, \"Your Highness, please understand, I merely placed it there absent-mindedly. I have no grudge against Miss Shulan, why would I want to make her fall?\"","Yuwen Hui nodded with a sneer, \"Indeed. If you have no grudge against Shulan, then you must have been trying to harm Ruolan? After all, Ruolan was closest to you - why else would you have moved so close to her?\"","Yao Huiqin was frightened and hurriedly protested, \"No, no, I bear no ill will toward Ruolan either...\"","Before she could finish, Yuwen Hui interrupted, \"Oh, so you weren't trying to harm Shulan or Ruolan - perhaps you were attempting to harm me instead? Guards, seize her!\"","This thoroughly terrified Yao Huiqin, who immediately fell to her knees and began repeatedly kowtowing.","\"Please spare me, Your Highness! I absolutely had no such intention...\"","The scene descended into chaos as Zhou Shulan's and Yao Huiqin's crying mingled together.","Observing this situation, Zhou Ruolan finally spoke up, \"We apologize for alarming Your Highness today. Our Zhou family has failed in our duties as hosts. Please calm your anger.\"","She then instructed the maids, \"Help Sister Shulan back to change her clothes.\"","The maids acknowledged the order and led the disheveled Zhou Shulan away from the scene.","Zhou Ruolan then turned to Qi Shuguang and said, \"Thank you, Lord Qi. If not for you, I would have fallen as well.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Yuwen Hui shot Yao Huiqin a fierce glare before quickly adding, \"Indeed! Lord Qi has helped you twice now, Ruolan. You should really think about how to properly thank him.\"","Before Qi Shuguang could respond, Yuwen Sheng, who had been standing outside the pavilion the entire time, flicked his sleeves and walked away."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 14","After the second prince left, Yuwen Hui stayed at the Zhou mansion for another half day.","Of course, she didn't forget her main task. After playing with Ruolan, she returned to the palace in the evening and immediately reported to her mother about what happened during the arrow-throwing game earlier that day.","\"Mother, you don't know how wicked that Yao girl is! When Ruolan was about to throw her arrow, she secretly crept up close and deliberately hid an arrow in her sleeve. I was right beside Ruolan at the time - she must have been trying to harm either Ruolan or me. I could have ended up limping back today, or worse, I might have fallen and hit my face on the bronze vessel!\"","Upon hearing this, Empress Guo became very angry and immediately summoned a palace lady-in-waiting, ordering, \"The Yao family has failed to properly educate their daughter. Punish her with copying the Women's Rules and Precepts one hundred times and thirty strikes to the face. Such a girl must never be allowed to enter the Yuwen family.\"","The lady-in-waiting complied and immediately left the palace to carry out the order at the Yao residence.","Empress Guo sent her daughter to rest, then summoned her eldest son Yuwen Sheng and said, \"I think the Minister of Works' granddaughter, Xu Ruoling, is quite suitable. Tomorrow I will report to your father and have her arranged as your primary consort.\"","Yuwen Sheng hesitated upon hearing this. \"But...\"","Before he could finish, Empress Guo interrupted, \"I know what you want to say. I originally thought Zhou's Ruolan was good, but from what I saw that day, she falls far short of my expectations. Her temperament is somewhat rash and impetuous - not suitable for a primary wife.\"","After she finished speaking, Yuwen Sheng still seemed unwilling and was about to say something, but his mother continued, \"Most importantly, your behavior today was particularly reckless. It's one thing for Hui to go, but what business does a prince have attending their celebration? Since when did the Zhou family become worthy of having a prince attend their birthday festivities?\"","Yuwen Sheng was stunned, and his mother continued, \"Don't think others can't see through your intentions. You know your father's temperament - once he becomes suspicious of you, even though you're my eldest son, I won't be able to protect you.\"","At these words, Yuwen Sheng's heart skipped a beat.","Indeed, he wasn't his mother's only son - there was also the fifth prince.","That fifth prince was particularly good at winning their parents' favor...","Gritting his teeth secretly, he could only say, \"Yes. I will follow mother's arrangements.\"","A few days later, news came from the palace that the Emperor and Empress had arranged marriages for both the second prince and Princess Changping.","Yuwen Hui's husband would be He Chengyin, the new top-ranking scholar.","And Second Prince Yuwen Sheng's primary consort would be Xu Ruoling, granddaughter of the Minister of Works.","When the dust settled, Madam Zhou felt quite regretful and couldn't help but say angrily, \"What's wrong with our Ruolan? Just because we happened to meet that Yao girl that day, it cost Ruolan such a great opportunity. If only we hadn't invited the Yao family!\"","Zhou Ruolan, however, felt relieved.","Xu Ruoling was the one who had given birth to Princess Yuwen Yan for Yuwen Sheng in her previous life. Though not a bad person, she had poor health and passed away three years after giving birth to Yuwen Yan.","Now that neither she nor Yao Huiqin would enter the palace, Consort Hui's son, Yuwen Lan, would become the crown prince in the future.","Although Yuwen Sheng hadn't been a particularly wise ruler in her previous life, it was worth noting that the other princes were even worse in character. Most importantly, only if he ascended to the throne would Yuwen Lan be able to inherit the empire in the future.","Living this life again, she would not sacrifice her own happiness, but she would still do what she could to ensure the people's peace and stability.","However, now that the biggest crisis had been resolved, it was time to attend to her own matters.","As her mother finished speaking, she looked at her father and said, \"What's important now is that the Second Prince personally visited our mansion that day, surely intending to build a good relationship with father. What are father's thoughts on this?\"","General Zhou stroked his beard and said, \"His Majesty is currently in good health. If I were to act rashly, it would likely arouse the Emperor's suspicion.\"","Zhou Ruolan nodded and said, \"Father's words are reasonable, but His Majesty will eventually grow old. We should still think of our own interests.\"","Upon hearing this, Madam Zhou, finally understanding the implications, was startled and hurriedly said, \"Oh dear, could we have offended the Second Prince? He is, after all, the Empress's eldest son.\"","Following her mother's words, Ruolan added, \"That's one concern, and although the Second Prince's marriage has been arranged, there's still the Third Prince. If he also approaches father...\"","These words made General Zhou's heart tighten—","Indeed, during this morning's court session, the Second Prince had been somewhat cold towards him, while the Third Prince had actively sought conversation...","Although His Majesty had not yet named an heir, the Second Prince was indeed the most legitimate candidate.","While he hadn't actively sought to ally with the Second Prince through marriage, he also didn't want to be viewed as an enemy.","As a mere military general, how dare he get involved in the princes' struggle for succession?","If the Third Prince truly had designs on Ruolan...","There was only one solution.","Before he could speak, Ruolan said, \"Father must understand that the best solution now is to quickly arrange a marriage for me.\"","General Zhou nodded.","Madam Zhou sighed and said, \"But this is a lifelong matter, how can we rush into it?\"","Although there had been many suitors showing interest in recent years, she had been focused on the royal family and hadn't carefully considered any of them.","Now in such a hurry, who should they choose for their daughter?","Their daughter smiled shyly and said, \"I actually have someone in mind.\"","\"Who?\" Madam Zhou immediately asked.","Zhou Ruolan replied bashfully, \"The new third-ranking scholar Qi Shuguang. I think he has excellent character.\"","Upon hearing this, Madam Zhou immediately expressed her disapproval, \"Though that young man is decent-looking, his family isn't from the capital and has no influence...\"","Zhou Ruolan reminded her mother, \"In our current situation, the lower my marriage status, the safer it will be for the Zhou family.\"","General Zhou nodded.","Suddenly he looked up at his daughter and said, \"Could it be you've had your eye on that young man for some time?\"","His daughter smiled sweetly and said, \"Father is most perceptive.\"","Madam Zhou glanced at her and sighed, \"You'll have to follow wherever your husband goes, whether he's wealthy or poor. His family isn't well-off - aren't you afraid of living a hard life? Can you handle it?\"","Zhou Ruolan smiled again, \"I'm not afraid.\"","Indeed, in her previous life she had enjoyed all the glory and wealth, but what did it get her?","Weren't her best days those quiet times spent with him in the mountains?","Madam Zhou didn't know her daughter's thoughts and assumed love had addled her brain, saying, \"Just don't regret it later.\"","Ruolan certainly wouldn't regret it.","However, what followed surprised Madam Zhou.","She had assumed that the young Qi, coming from a humble background, wouldn't even have a house in the capital, and she had planned to buy one for her daughter. Unexpectedly, despite his young age, Qi Shuguang had already saved up money and purchased a residence in the capital during his visit for the imperial examinations.","Though not as grand as the General's mansion, it was complete with all necessities, and he even had a Hanlin Academy Scholar accompany him to propose marriage, which gave quite a good impression.","Most importantly, both her daughter and husband were satisfied, so for the sake of the bigger picture, Madam Zhou had to agree.","However, a humble background had its advantages - Madam Zhou thought that at least her daughter would have autonomy and wouldn't be bullied by in-laws.","With her daughter's marriage settled, Madam Zhou's only remaining concern was her son.","Recently, after being whipped by his sister, Zhou Yucheng had improved considerably. Madam Zhou thought that with this future son-in-law's scholarly excellence guiding him, her son might improve even more.","So all things considered, her daughter's marriage wasn't bad at all.","August in the capital was the golden autumn season.","Amidst the fragrance of osmanthus flowers, the Mansion of the Guardian General was holding a wedding.","Finally marrying the girl he loved, Qi Shuguang naturally spared no effort in making the wedding grand and lively, with music and festivities drawing many onlookers.","Some people remarked that the General's daughter, being one of the capital's foremost noble ladies, was marrying beneath her station to a minor court lecturer with no background.","Others said, don't look down on the third-ranking scholar just because his current position is low - he serves the emperor daily, and with true talent and learning, it's very easy to gain the emperor's recognition. The groom's future is boundless!","Of course, the bride in the sedan chair couldn't hear any of this.","Even if she could, Zhou Ruolan wouldn't have cared at all.","She only knew that the man riding the horse leading her bridal sedan was the one she had cherished through two lifetimes.","Each hoofbeat of his horse, leading her every step, seemed to echo every day they had longed for each other in her previous life.","In that previous life, she had to thank her children for fulfilling her wishes in her later years.","She still remembered that moment of farewell when she had sighed, wishing heaven would grant her another chance to marry him properly and bear his children.","Unexpectedly, that day had finally come.","Under her bridal veil, her lips couldn't help but curl into a constant smile.","Arriving at their new home, after paying respects to heaven and earth, the newlyweds finally entered their chamber.","With the merry guests temporarily shut out, the door closed, the groom Qi Shuguang lifted the red veil.","After gazing at that face he had longed for day and night, he finally called out, \"My wife.\"","Zhou Ruolan responded, and with a smile, called back, \"My husband.\"","\"At last, in this life, I can properly be your wife.\"","As her words fell, he had already taken her hand, saying with a smile, \"Thank you for walking this path with me once again.\"","She nodded with a smile, saying, \"And thank you for taking care of me once more.\"","...","Their newlywed bliss and devotion to each other went without saying.","After dispelling the imperial family's suspicions, the Zhou family found peace, and the couple focused entirely on their own life together.","Zhou Ruolan managed their household affairs wholeheartedly, making their home prosperous.","Qi Shuguang dedicated himself to his official duties, and with his talents and experience from his previous life, gradually gained the emperor's recognition and trust, becoming a court favorite.","In their second year of marriage, they had a child.","It was a boy, and Qi Shuguang, overjoyed, specifically named him Chengbo.","When Ruolan heard that name, tears welled up in her eyes.","Bo was the name of her child from her previous life who never had the chance to grow up.","She was touched that he remembered and comforted her this way.","Both children looked very much like her, often making her feel as if her lost treasure had returned.","Regardless, in this life, her family was stable, and she would never let anything happen to her flesh and blood again.","Two years later, Emperor Gaozu passed away, and Qi Shuguang, now a Hanlin Academy Scholar, was responsible for drafting the imperial edict.","As in the previous life, several princes eyed the throne hungrily, and crisis loomed.","Fortunately, with his and father-in-law Zhou Pengze's support, Second Prince Yuwen Sheng successfully ascended to the throne.","Yuwen Sheng named his wife Madam Xu as empress and his eldest daughter Yuwen Yan as princess.","However, not long after, Empress Xu passed away.","Coincidentally, Consort He gave birth to the crown prince Yuwen Lan, and with the support of officials like Qi Shuguang, Yuwen Sheng made her the new empress and named Yuwen Lan as crown prince.","Empress He was kind-hearted, and though not forceful in nature, she had a clear sense of right and wrong and was deeply grateful for the support of Qi Shuguang and others, extending her trust to Ruolan as well.","Of course, with Ruolan's frequent guidance and care, her health remained good, avoiding the early demise of her previous life.","Having experienced the chaos during his ascension, Yuwen Sheng understood that both the Qi and Zhou families were his loyal subjects.","Combined with Qi Shuguang's genuine talent and learning, at Empress He's suggestion, he appointed him as Imperial Tutor to guide Crown Prince Yuwen Lan.","Under Qi Shuguang's careful instruction, the little crown prince gradually grew up.","One day, during the Imperial Tutor's rest day, the six-year-old crown prince, struggling with a difficult problem, suddenly decided to visit his tutor's home.","The Qi couple was surprised and hurried to receive him properly.","Ruolan personally made many snacks to serve him.","The little crown prince particularly loved his teacher's wife's baked treats, especially the taro puffs and chestnut cakes.","Watching him, Ruolan couldn't help but reflect that this child was just like in her previous life.","In this life, with her occasional guidance, Empress He's health was good, and she should be able to raise Yuwen Lan to adulthood herself.","Although she couldn't raise the little one herself in this life, being his teacher's wife at least included the character for \"mother,\" so in a way, she was still playing a maternal role.","After being warmly hosted by the Imperial Tutor and his wife, the satisfied little crown prince prepared to return to the palace.","Before boarding his carriage, the little crown prince suddenly turned back to Ruolan and said, \"Teacher's wife...\"","Ruolan started, quickly responding, \"Yes, Your Highness?\"","The little one asked seriously, \"May I come again for snacks?\"","Ruolan quickly nodded and smiled, \"Of course you may. As long as Your Highness doesn't mind, I can make snacks for you anytime.\"","The little crown prince nodded and added with a smile, \"I cannot drink sheep's milk, please remember not to use any.\"","What...","Ruolan was stunned.","The little crown prince continued, \"I wish you, the Imperial Tutor, and my senior brother well.\"","With that, he boarded his carriage back to the palace, leaving the couple bewildered.","The crown prince's words seemed beyond his years.","Qi Shuguang and Zhou Ruolan exchanged glances, both considering the same possibility—","Could it be... the crown prince also...","If so, that would be even better."]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 15","From the moment the Little Princess was born, the Little Crown Prince immediately stepped into the role of being a big brother.","Not to mention that he had stayed up with Father the first night waiting for his sister's birth, the next day, the first thing the little one did after waking up was to run to Mother's chambers to see his sister.","The little one had been sleeping in the side palace since not long after Mother became pregnant with his sister.","Now, as the little brother came to Mother's chambers, he saw his sister sleeping peacefully in her swaddling clothes, looking even prettier than when she was born last night.","The little one leaned over the bed and looked carefully for a while, then carefully moved closer and puckered his lips to kiss his adorable sister.","Yanshu felt deeply touched and stroked her son's head, also giving him a kiss.","The little one giggled and snuggled into Mother's embrace, predictably earning himself several more kisses.","However, the milk-scented little sister just pursed her lips slightly, without even opening her eyes, and continued sleeping soundly.","The little one found it strange and asked Mother, \"Why isn't sister waking up?\"","Yanshu smiled while stroking the little one's head, saying, \"Sister used a lot of energy to be born last night, she must be very tired.\"","Understanding now, the little one nodded and said in his childish yet mature voice, \"Sister worked hard.\"","Just then, palace servants brought in breakfast, and the nursemaid said, \"Please have your breakfast first, Little Crown Prince.\"","The little one made a sound of agreement and pitter-pattered to the dining table.","After carefully eating three small buns and drinking a bowl of pumpkin porridge, the little one hurriedly ran back to Mother's bedside.","He saw his sister still sleeping soundly in her swaddling clothes, not having changed position at all.","The little one felt disappointed and asked, \"Why won't sister play with me? Doesn't she know I'm waiting for her?\"","Yanshu had to comfort him again, \"Sister is still very small, and in these first days after being born, she needs to sleep a lot. It's not that she doesn't want to play with you, she's just too tired.\"","The little one sighed and said, \"Sister is so lazy.\"","Yanshu was amused and told the little one, \"All babies are like this. When you were little, you also slept all day.\"","But the little one protested, \"I wasn't lazy, I worked very hard.\"","Then he started swaying his head and recited, \"Spring sleep unaware of dawning, Everywhere I hear birds singing, After storm in night hours deep, How many petals now lie in heap?\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Very good, after his father finished teaching him the Four Books and Five Classics, he had now started teaching Tang poetry.","She was very supportive of this behavior, so she quickly clapped and praised, \"You're amazing! You're such a capable big brother. When sister wakes up, I'll tell her to learn poetry from her brother. Remember to come recite poetry for sister every day, this way, sister can become as smart as you.\"","The little one nodded vigorously, \"Yes yes, I learn poetry from Father every day.\"","Yanshu quickly gave her son another kiss on his forehead, \"You're wonderful, and Father is wonderful too!\"","Hehe, speaking of the importance of marrying a scholarly husband - now husband teaches son, son teaches daughter, and she wouldn't need to worry about the children's studies at all.","After making this arrangement with Mother, the Little Crown Prince diligently learned poetry from Father every day, and then carefully recited it to his sister.","Hard work pays off - watching his sister grow day by day, she finally stopped sleeping so much, and stayed awake for longer periods.","The milk-scented little girl loved her brother the most. Whenever brother came, she would watch him intently, her grape-like eyes unwilling to even blink.","As days passed by, gradually, the little girl could make sounds too. Whenever brother talked to her, she would open her cherry-like little mouth and keep making \"ah, ah\" sounds along with him.","This excited the little one greatly, and he hurriedly told Mother, \"Sister is learning poetry with me!\"","Yanshu quickly nodded in encouragement, \"That's right, sister especially likes her brother, you should talk to sister more often.\"","The little one felt very accomplished, and in his excitement started singing nursery rhymes he had just learned.","The little sister was very supportive, actually giggling out loud.","The big brother felt even more accomplished and ended up performing everything he knew for his sister all at once.","After the performance, both big brother and little sister were tired.","Sister closed her eyes for a nap, while big brother went to eat some fruits and drink some tea.","When little sister woke up from her nap, she saw her big brother seriously eating snacks.","The little sister stared in fascination, her dark eyes fixed straight on her brother's mouth, not even blinking.","As she watched, she opened her little mouth and started making \"ah\" sounds, very seriously trying to talk to her brother.","After listening, the little one said in his childish voice, \"Sister wants to eat snacks too.\"","Saying this, he actually took another piece of snack from the plate with his chubby hand to give to his sister.","Yanshu quickly stopped him, \"You're a good brother, but sister is too young now, she has no teeth and can't eat snacks.\"","But the little one was very worried, \"But sister is hungry.\"","Yanshu smiled and said, \"Then we'll give her milk, that's all she can eat right now.\"","Saying this, she took the little girl into her arms and began feeding her.","Probably because she was really hungry, the little girl ate very seriously, with loud gulping sounds that were quite captivating.","The little one watched for a while, suddenly forgetting the snack in his hand as he remembered when he used to drink milk.","...Oh no, he was actually getting hungry for it.","Fortunately, Yanshu quickly noticed the little one's expression and hurriedly instructed, \"Big brother has grown up now, and can't drink milk like sister anymore, or he'll turn back into a baby.\"","Hmm? Turn back into a baby who can't walk, can't talk, and can't eat snacks?","The little one silently weighed his options, suddenly feeling that the snacks and roasted lamb leg in his hand smelled better, so he had to suppress his current craving and nodded, \"A man doesn't drink milk.\"","Then he went back to eating his snacks.","By the time the little one finished his snacks, sister's little tummy was also full.","Yanshu burped the little girl and placed her on the couch for the siblings to chat and play.","However, not long after, the little girl's face turned red, and she started straining with \"mm\" sounds.","The little one quickly told Mother, \"Sister needs to poop!\"","As soon as he said this, Rendong the nursemaid and others quickly gathered around, and they heard a series of gurgling sounds.","When they opened the little one's diaper, sure enough, the Little Princess had made quite a mess.","Everyone quickly started washing the little girl's bottom and changing her diaper, while Yanshu laughed from the side, \"Eating and then pooping, our girl really has a straightforward gut.\"","The little girl, who was now feeling comfortable, made an \"ah\" sound and started laughing along.","Rendong asked curiously, \"How did the Little Crown Prince know the princess needed to poop?\"","Yanshu said, \"Maybe he still remembers from when he was little, babies usually clear their bowels after drinking milk.\"","But in her heart, she knew that her little one probably understood his sister's needs through mind-reading.","Speaking of which, since her little one had mind-reading abilities, would their girl also have some special abilities?","As they say, children grow up without worry. As the harsh winter passed and spring arrived, the hundred-day-old girl had already grown to over ten pounds.","The little one was easy to feed just like her brother had been, and thus was equally chubby and rosy.","However, compared to her brother, the little girl's features clearly resembled her father more.","Like her brother when he was little, the little girl loved to babble, loved to chat with people, and loved to giggle, making her absolutely adorable.","Her father loved her to his very core.","Everyone in the palace knew of the king's doting on the Little Princess. No matter how busy he was with state affairs during the day, even if he only had meal times free, the king would rush back to the central palace by carriage to see his little daughter, holding and kissing her, barely able to let go.","The Little Princess also loved her father, especially when father held her and tenderly called her \"Xuan'er.\"","Yes, this was the name her father had personally chosen for her - Yuwen Xuan, meaning to live without worries and for everything to go smoothly.","Not satisfied with just visiting his daughter during the day, at night, father would chat with his milk-scented little daughter and tiger-like son, the three of them cuddling on the big bed, nothing could be happier.","For this, everyone envied the Empress.","Yanshu also felt she was quite enviable.","Her husband was busy with state affairs during the day, but still loved to take care of the children at night, which was truly remarkable.","This way, she wouldn't mind having a few more children.","At the very least, if her children all possessed superpowers, she could feel more at ease taking her husband out for leisure travels when they grew up.","Yes, that would be a sure win.","As his little sister grew day by day, the little brother wasn't idle either.","Having turned three, the Little Crown Prince had officially started his studies.","Though he naturally retained his playful and active nature, thanks to the solid foundation his father had laid for him since young, the little fellow showed remarkable progress.","The Grand Tutor and other imperial tutors all praised him, and the court officials were greatly encouraged—","With such a talented heir apparent, the future of the Great Liang dynasty was secured!","Of course, while her brother embarked on his scholarly journey, the little sister wasn't idle either. At three months old, the little girl had reached the stage where she enviously watched adults eating.","During family mealtimes, the little girl would cry out impatiently, and needless to say, she would reach out trying to grab chopsticks and bowls.","Compared to her brother when he was young, the little girl seemed even more eager.","Perhaps it was because now she had to watch her parents and brother eating at the table while she could only stare and drool.","Seeing this, her brother felt sympathetic and quickly translated for their parents, \"Sister wants to eat too.\"","Having experience from the first child, how could Yanshu not understand? But she could only earnestly tell her little daughter, \"Darling, it's not time yet. We'll feed you rice porridge in another month, please be patient, my girl.\"","However, the little girl couldn't understand and continued reaching for her bowl.","The nursemaid had to quickly step forward and say, \"Let this servant take the princess for a walk. Please, Your Majesty and Your Highness, continue with your meal.\"","That was the only solution, otherwise nobody would be able to eat. Yanshu asked the nursemaid to carry the little girl out.","Fortunately, the weather was warm, so viewing flowers outside wouldn't be bad.","But after just a few bites, they heard the little girl's frustrated cries from outside.","It was as if she was protesting, \"Not only do Father, Mother, and Brother eat delicious food without sharing, but they even drove me out!!!\"","This made everyone at the table pause.","Before Yanshu could speak, Yuwen Lan put down his chopsticks, stood up and said, \"I'll go keep Xuan'er company. You all continue eating.\"","Yanshu said, \"...Thank you for your trouble, Your Majesty.\"","Yuwen Lan gave a slight nod and went out to quickly take his crying daughter into his arms.","Everyone who witnessed this couldn't help but marvel at how well His Majesty treated the Empress.","Yanshu also marveled at how much this man truly loved their daughter.","Silently hearing everyone's thoughts, their son wondered, [Does Father love me too?]","Yuwen Lan, who was holding his daughter, thought in response, [I love you both, equally!]","After all, they were both his precious children, how could he not?"]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 16","After the little princess had been fussy about food for nearly a month, Her Majesty's father, the Emperor, had carried her for almost a month. During dinner time, Yanshu would feed their son first, while Yuwen Lan would carry his little daughter around outside.","After enduring this routine, finally, after four and a half months, the little girl was ready to start eating solid food.","On the first night of introducing solid food, the whole family sat around the dining table to witness this exciting moment.","Especially the doting father Yuwen Lan, who personally held his little daughter on his lap while Yanshu fed her.","The little girl's eyes lit up at the sight of the bowl, and when she saw her mother holding a small wooden spoon, she became even more excited, reaching out with her chubby little hands trying to grab it. It took Yanshu quite some effort to finally get the first spoonful of rice porridge into the little princess's mouth.","The whole family eagerly watched as the little girl smacked her lips a couple of times before swallowing the porridge, then happily made two \"ah\" sounds.","It was as if she was announcing that she had finally eaten something other than milk.","Everyone else was delighted too, especially Yuwen Lan.","Having waited so long for this day, he could finally sit down and properly enjoy a meal with his wife and children.","Just like her brother when he was little, the little girl had a good appetite. She accepted everything from rice porridge to egg yolk and fruit puree, never refusing anything. She would always finish the portions prepared for her by the adults, growing healthy and chubby, much to everyone's satisfaction.","However, as the little one grew day by day, she became increasingly clever.","Gradually, the little girl became dissatisfied with the bland rice porridge. She would often spit out the porridge fed to her, anxiously trying to grab the adults' bowls while babbling away.","Her mind-reading brother translated from the side, \"Sister wants to eat our dishes.\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","This little girl, how did she become so clever so quickly?","However, having already raised one child, Yanshu had a bright idea. She used chopsticks to let the little girl taste a bit of non-spicy soup from their dishes.","The little girl smacked her lips a few times, clearly delighted.","Yanshu then fed her another spoonful of rice porridge.","The little girl smacked her lips again, swallowing somewhat hesitantly.","But when her mother quickly gave her another taste of soup, it successfully dispelled her doubts, and the little girl became excited again.","Yanshu continued feeding her spoonfuls of porridge, and whenever the little girl showed signs of doubt, she would quickly offer some soup.","With this strategy, they successfully managed to feed the little girl until she was full.","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","His wife always had the best solutions.","However, their son, who had been watching, couldn't help but say, \"Mother is tricking sister...\"","Yanshu: \"...\"","She quickly explained to her son, \"Mother isn't tricking sister. Sister is too small, her teeth haven't fully grown in yet, and eating adult food could be dangerous for her. Mother can't let sister be in danger, so this is the only way to feed her.\"","The little boy seemed to understand and looked sympathetically at his chubby little sister, saying, \"Poor sister, soup isn't as good as meat.\"","Yuwen Lan nodded from the side, \"When Xuan'er grows up, she can eat meat with her brother.\"","But as soon as he finished speaking, the little boy picked up a salt and pepper shrimp and said, \"I'll save this tasty shrimp for sister.\"","Yanshu quickly smiled and said, \"Sister will have to wait many more days before she can eat shrimp. We'll make new ones for her then, you eat this one.\"","Inwardly, she was very pleased - her son was such a good brother!","From the side, Yuwen Lan also nodded and said, \"Heng'er cares for his sister and is a good elder brother, but as the Crown Prince, he must also remember to care for all the people of the realm.\"","The little boy obediently nodded, \"I understand.\"","Just then, the little girl, who was full of soup, opened her mouth and started babbling along.","Her brother immediately translated for their mother, \"Sister says she likes today's food and wants it again tomorrow.\"","Yanshu: \"...No problem, daughter, you can have all the soup you want.\"","Yuwen Lan: \"...\"","Poor little daughter, grow up quickly.","Since starting school, the three-year-old brother had become increasingly steady, while the six-month-old sister remained playful as ever.","The little girl seemed to have a wild spirit, unable to stay indoors and always wanting to go out to play.","Every day after eating, she would point outside and make \"ah ah\" sounds to the adults, indicating it was time to take her out to play.","Especially every morning when her brother had to go to class, the little girl would get as excited as if she were going to class herself.","Thus, every morning there was a peculiar sight in the palace: the milk-scented little bundle of joy, the little princess, sitting in a specially made cart, being pushed by adults to send her little brother, the Crown Prince, to the study.","Of course, with the tiger-headed brother bouncing along in front, and the chubby, delicately beautiful sister behind, they couldn't be more adorable.","However, when they reached the study door, brother would wave and say, \"Goodbye, sister,\" before entering the study.","The little sister would pause, make an \"ah\" sound, and then start crying.","Wuwuwu, why wouldn't brother play with her anymore? Why did brother run away by himself?","The little girl would cry very sadly.","The wet nurses and palace maids, afraid of disturbing the Crown Prince's studies, would quickly push her away.","She would only forget about it when she saw something like a cat or dog, or when they took her to watch the goldfish in the pond.","As days passed by, once the little princess developed the ability to crawl, she was no longer content to sit in her little cart.","Yanshu felt that this little girl was just as mischievous as her brother had been when he was young.","She would crawl all over the palace, and quite quickly at that.","Especially when she heard the palace servants announce \"His Majesty arrives,\" the little girl would crawl faster than anyone.","Thus, whenever Yuwen Lan stepped into the hall, she was always the first one he saw.","Moreover, the little girl would keep calling out in her sweet voice, \"Dada, dada...\"","Which meant \"Father,\" and it made the daughter-doting emperor so happy he could hardly contain himself.","Indeed, what father wouldn't be moved when such a soft, fragrant, and adorable little person affectionately called them \"Father\"?","Yuwen Lan would quickly pick up his little daughter, kiss her repeatedly, and softly ask, \"Did Xuan'er miss Father?\"","Unable to speak properly yet, little Xuan'er would giggle and snuggle in her father's arms, her little mouth calling out \"Dada...\" a few more times while sucking on her finger.","Yuwen Lan's heart melted completely. He nuzzled his little daughter's head and asked softly, \"Is Xuan'er hungry? Shall we eat some meat?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, his son nodded and said, \"Yes, this subject would like to eat lamb leg!\"","Indeed, after attending the study for over half a year, the little Crown Prince had become quite proficient in using respectful language when speaking to adults.","Yuwen Lan ruffled his son's head and ordered, \"Then let's have the imperial kitchen roast two lamb legs.\"","Fu Hai quickly went to relay the order, and an hour later, the family was enjoying freshly roasted lamb legs.","While the parents and brother heartily ate the crispy-outside-tender-inside lamb meat, the little princess was enthusiastically gnawing on a meatless bone.","...This scene looked somewhat familiar.","The little girl was babbling away while gnawing on her bone.","Her brother quickly translated, \"Sister says hers is different from ours.\"","Yanshu told the little girl, \"All little ones gnaw on these, your brother did too when he was small, right, son?\"","The little Crown Prince made agreeing sounds, while secretly thinking to himself that being grown up was better.","After all, lamb bones really weren't as good as lamb meat.","As more days passed, the little princess turned one year old.","The old year passed, and the people welcomed the new year.","On the afternoon of the third day of the New Year, the children accompanied their parents to Songhe Mountain to pay New Year respects to their grandparents.","The little girl could walk now, and despite the cold winter weather, it didn't dampen her enthusiasm for activity. As soon as they got out of the carriage, she started toddling around on her own.","Yuwen Lan, worried, held his little daughter's hand in his, afraid she might fall.","After walking a few steps, they saw Grandpa and Grandma waiting at the courtyard entrance.","Their son happily called out \"Grandma, Grandpa!\" and ran towards them.","Just then, Niuniu also broke free from her father's hand and ran up, her little voice sweet and tender as she called out, \"Grandma,\" \"Grandpa\"...","The Empress Dowager, having finished hugging her grandson, came over to embrace her granddaughter. Her eyes crinkled into crescents with joy as she kissed the little girl repeatedly, exclaiming in delight, \"Xuan'er hasn't visited many times, yet she still remembers her Grandma and Grandpa?\"","Yanshu smiled from the side, \"She follows her brother's lead.\"","However, in her heart, she too found it surprising. She had to admit, her little girl had always been particularly quick with words, learning many terms of address without needing to be specifically taught.","After spending most of the day at their grandparents' home, two days later, Yanshu took the siblings to visit their maternal grandparents.","Surprisingly, the little girl could immediately call out \"Grandma,\" \"Grandpa,\" and \"Uncle\" correctly.","Mind you, while the little girl had seen her maternal grandmother quite a few times, she had rarely met her maternal grandfather and uncle.","Even with her brother's guidance, how could she recognize everyone so quickly?","And she hadn't mistaken anyone either.","The Zhongyi family was also quite amazed by this.","\"How is the little princess so clever, recognizing everyone at once?\"","To this, Yanshu could only say, \"Perhaps she learned it from her brother.\"","But in her heart, something felt off.","So she immediately called out to the system, asking, [System, does my daughter have some special ability? How is she so accurate at recognizing people?]","The system replied, [That's right, to celebrate you, my host, having a precious daughter, I gifted a sub-system to Niuniu.]","Yanshu: [...What? A sub-system?]","Did this mean her little girl had a Melon Eating System too???","The system explained, [Correct, what else could my sub-system be? But don't worry, currently Niuniu's is an infant sub-system, pure and harmless, very healthy. It just teaches her to recognize people and such, consider it early education.]","Yanshu: [!!!]","Could it really work like this?","My system is truly amazing!!!"]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 17","(Reading note: The male lead is the Empress Dowager's biological son, now named Zhou Lan, and the female lead is now named Li Shu.)","The phone alarm had been ringing by her pillow for nearly a minute before Li Shu finally managed to open her eyes with difficulty.","The once four-person dormitory was now eerily quiet with just her remaining.","With graduation approaching, her roommates had all moved out, either for internships or full-time jobs. Only she remained, unable to attend interviews because she stayed up late writing novels, which led to her inability to wake up the next day.","It wasn't that she wanted to stay up late; mainly, it was because thousands of readers were online daily demanding updates. She couldn't bear to let them down, so she had no choice but to grit her teeth and keep writing.","Staying up until two or three in the morning had become the norm. The next day, after getting enough sleep, she would start thinking about the new chapter, and time passed day by day in this cycle of writing.","In the blink of an eye, it was already late May, with graduation coming next month.","Although her current writing income was decent, if she didn't find a proper job, her parents would likely force her to move back home.","Home itself wasn't scary; what was scary were all those neighbors and relatives!","It was bad enough that they constantly compared husbands and children, but since she turned twenty, these relatives had been competing to set her up on blind dates. If she really went home, she'd be driven crazy.","So she really wanted to find a job, but struggled to find the time.","Fortunately, Professor Qi from her department had recommended her for a position yesterday. The Huarui Group was establishing a media company and was currently hiring. She tried submitting her resume and surprisingly received an interview invitation quickly.","So, no matter how sleepy she was now, she had to go.","At 10 AM, in the conference room on the fifteenth floor of the Huarui Building, the new CEO Zhou Lan glanced at his watch, feeling slightly impatient.","He had already interviewed several candidates for the planning and publicity position but wasn't quite satisfied with any of them. He was even considering leaving.","Of course, it wasn't just him – everyone else in the conference room had started to zone out, and various thoughts began flooding into his ears.","[Tsk, who is that male celebrity who secretly got married, had two kids, and is now forcing his wife to quietly divorce him so he can pursue a rich woman? That author called Carefree Meatball is such a cliffhanger master!!! Are they trying to kill us with suspense!!!]","[It's only 10 AM, still 35 hours until Carefree's latest chapter, how am I going to survive this difficult day...]","[I'm so late to the party, why did I only discover this treasure of an author, Carefree Meatball, yesterday!!! Stayed up all night but still haven't caught up to the latest chapter, don't want to work, just want to read the novel!!!]","\"...\"","There were currently four people in the conference room, and except for him, the other three were all thinking about this Carefree Meatball...","Zhou Lan mentally frowned.","He knew that \"Carefree Meatball\" was currently a dark horse author ranking in the top ten bestsellers on a certain novel website. They had written a novel called \"Let Me Tell You About My Years of Entertainment Industry Gossip,\" which was currently trending across the internet.","Come to think of it, he had glanced at that novel. While it wasn't particularly outstanding in terms of storytelling or literary merit, the subject matter was quite novel, focusing mainly on entertainment industry exposés. What was peculiar was that every story written would be followed by real cases being exposed online a few days later, with irrefutable evidence.","So many readers speculated that Carefree Meatball might be a famous paparazzi in the country.","But Zhou Lan had people investigate, and such speculation proved false. Even the paparazzi were currently searching everywhere for this author, wanting to know their true identity.","To be honest, Zhou Lan was quite curious too.","Just as his mind was wandering, the conference room door suddenly opened, and the next interviewee arrived.","He snapped back to attention and took a look. This time it was a young woman, probably no more than 24 years old.","Judging from her walk, she seemed uncomfortable in high heels – likely a fresh university graduate.","Tsk, her bangs were even sticking up a bit...","Clearly hadn't woken up early this morning.","He looked down at her resume again – sure enough, a fresh graduate from S University's Chinese Department, majoring in Chinese Language and Literature.","A fresh graduate...","Zhou Lan had almost no hope left.","Then he heard the HR manager say, \"Please introduce yourself.\"","The girl then said, \"My name is Li Shu, I'm 22 years old, studying Chinese Language and Literature at S University's Chinese Department, graduating with a bachelor's degree this year. Um... I saw your company was recruiting for the planning and publicity position, found it interesting, so I wanted to give it a try.\"","As she spoke, she was thinking to herself, [Is this okay to say? Well, that's what Baidu taught anyway.]","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","She needed Baidu to teach her?","Must be her first interview.","Beside him, HR continued, \"Miss Li, do you have any previous experience in corporate planning?\"","Zhou Lan looked up to see the girl pause for a second or two before saying, \"...No.\"","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","Well, just like her blank resume, at least this girl was honest.","Just as he was thinking this, he heard the girl hurriedly add, \"Wait, does writing promotional copy for a Taobao shop count? I did that for my roommate, and her business wasn't bad... I just forgot to put it on my resume.\"","This sparked some interest from HR, who then asked, \"May I ask what kind of Taobao shop your roommate runs? What category of business?\"","Zhou Lan also looked at her.","After all, many online shops now had considerable business. If she had managed to promote an online shop well during her student years, that would show some capability.","However, she replied, \"Um, she mainly runs a service for picking up express deliveries, takeout food, cafeteria meals, and other errands.\"","HR: \"...\"","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","Had to admit, it did sound quite busy.","At this point, he had even less hope, but HR cleared their throat and continued trying, \"So, besides this, Miss Li doesn't have any other work or internship experience?\"","Li Shu: \"Um... um...\"","She was hesitating internally, wanting to ask \"Does writing web novels count?\" Ugh...","Zhou Lan: \"???\"","Writing web novels?","So she's also an online writer?","Just as he was surprised, he heard her mentally reject the idea, [No, if I mention it, they might ask for my pen name? They might even want to see what I write... No way, that would expose my identity! I absolutely can't let them know who I am.]","Zhou Lan quietly raised an eyebrow –","From her tone, her pen name seemed quite impressive?","Then, he heard her sighing her own name in her thoughts, [Li Shu, oh Li Shu, you must keep your identity tightly under wraps. Once exposed, forget about the paparazzi camping outside your door, all those scumbags and nasty women you've written about will come after you! Especially that recent scumbag Yang XX who secretly got married, had two kids, and is now forcing his original wife to divorce...]","Zhou Lan: \"???\"","Secretly married, two kids, forcing the original wife to divorce...","Yang XX???","How did this girl know?","Could she be... Carefree Meatball???","After being silently shocked for a while, Zhou Lan thought for a moment and suddenly asked, \"Since Miss Li majored in Chinese Language and Literature, have you written anything during your four years in university?\"","When he finished speaking, he saw the girl look toward him at the sound of his voice. She didn't immediately answer his question, but first exclaimed internally –","[This man... is so fucking handsome!!!]","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","Ahem, although he often heard such exclamations, since the previous interviewees today were all male, this girl was the first one.","And... her feelings were quite intense.","However, as a well-mannered man who had experienced the tumultuous world, he was very clear-headed and wouldn't be easily swayed by his own appearance.","But could this girl please remove those two words before \"handsome\" when expressing her admiration?","It doesn't sound very polite.","Of course, coming back to the main point, the most important issue now was her.","He really hadn't expected that this seemingly young girl in front of him would turn out to be Carefree Meatball, the author currently on everyone's lips who was causing such a stir in the entertainment industry?","Was she really... just a college student?","While he was pondering this, he heard the girl think to herself, [One minute, I want his complete information!]","Zhou Lan: \"???\"","Who was she talking to?","Before he could figure it out, the system in Yan Shu's mind had already started explaining, [Haven't I already dug up this guy's information for you? He's Zhou Lan, the precious son of Huarui Group's chairwoman Zhou Ruolan, remember?]","Li Shu couldn't help but exclaim \"Holy crap!\" upon hearing this. [You mean this is that Zhou Lan, the youngest CEO who ranked in the top ten of Asia's richest people list just last month?]","System: [That's right, it's young master Zhou himself, genuine and guaranteed.]","Zhou Lan, who had been quietly listening, found this somewhat strange.","He wasn't wearing any brand labels today, and no one had introduced him earlier. How did this girl suddenly recognize him?","Though come to think of it, he had attended some events before, so if she had seen any related news reports, it would make sense that she recognized him now.","However, the girl was still in shock.","Although Li Shu knew that Zhou Lan was the son of Huarui Group's chairwoman Zhou Ruolan, and that this young CEO was currently the face of Huarui Group, she never imagined that on her first interview, she would encounter the man himself.","His looks were seriously way beyond those self-proclaimed top celebrity actors who desperately bought trending topics on social media!","How could someone be both so wealthy and so handsome?","Being cautious, she double-checked with the system again, [Is this the same Zhou Lan who once weighed over 400 pounds because he went through a self-destructive phase of drinking sodas and eating junk food during his parents' divorce, but then lost over 200 pounds in anger when no girls liked him during puberty?]","System: [Yep, that's him. Looking at his appearance now, he's maintained his figure quite well over the years.]","Yan Shu: [...Indeed, just goes to show every chubby person is a potential stock worth investing in.]","Zhou Lan: \"???\"","What was going on??","How on earth did she know all of this?!!"]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 18","That afternoon, Li Shu received a job offer call from Huarui Media.","\"Is this Miss Li Shu? I'm pleased to inform you that you've been accepted by Huarui Media Group. Please report to the HR department on the fifth floor of Huarui Building tomorrow morning at 9 AM.\"","...","After hanging up the phone, Li Shu was somewhat incredulous.","Based on how the morning interview went, she felt the company seemed to place great importance on work experience.","However, her biggest experience in recent years had been in following celebrity gossip and writing web novels. To protect her online identity, her answers during the interview hadn't been very satisfactory.","Later, when that legendary chubby Young Master Zhou asked if she had any works to show, she hesitated for a while and could only mention the second prize she won in a writing competition for her university journal.","It was obvious that he wasn't very satisfied with that answer.","She had felt somewhat regretful, which led her to devour an entire bucket of spicy chicken wings for lunch, before routinely opening her computer to start writing her update.","Well, only food and her readers would never let her down, so she couldn't let them down either.","But unexpectedly, Huarui actually approved her application?!","Hmm, so they preferred inexperienced fresh graduates like her?","Regardless, this was good news. Li Shu was very happy. After hanging up, she immediately ordered some barbecue takeout, then continued writing.","Tomorrow would be her first day at work, so she had to improve her efficiency and try to sleep early, otherwise she might work herself to death.","The next morning, Li Shu arrived at her new company right on time.","The first day was full of tedious procedures, and it took her a full hour to complete all the paperwork.","After walking around in high heels all morning, she could finally sit at her own workstation. She let out a quiet sigh of relief and, while waiting for her computer to boot up, couldn't resist secretly taking out her phone to check the comments on today's new chapter.","She saw readers already asking if the scumbag who abandoned his wife and child for a rich woman was the popular celebrity Yang XX.","Li Shu thought to herself, \"Wow, they figured it out so quickly?\"","Then she heard the system say, [Your novel has become the new gossip compass. The paparazzi have been investigating everywhere since yesterday to get first-hand information. Over a hundred people barely slept all night, and one of them has already tracked down Yang XX's original wife. That sister has seen what you wrote and is now considering posting her own exposé to denounce that scumbag.]","Li Shu's eyes lit up – this was great news!","The strength of that lady alone wouldn't be enough, but with the paparazzi joining in, there would be plenty of attention.","The rest would be up to the parties involved. She hoped this woman would hire a good lawyer and fight for proper alimony and shared property to start her new life.","Just then, her computer finished booting up. She put away her phone contentedly and started working.","Although she had no formal work experience before, she was smart and eager to learn. She would definitely do fine.","Before she knew it, lunch time had arrived. Today, in the cafeteria, elevators, corridors, and lobby, everyone was discussing one thing―","It turned out that the modern Chen Shiming, the ungrateful scumbag in Xiao Yao Wan Zi's latest chapter, was actually the popular celebrity Yang XX.","This was the atmosphere in which Zhou Lan entered the company.","He silently listened to all the discussions along the way, and his mind couldn't help but ponder an important matter―","After that girl Li Shu left the company yesterday, he had people quietly investigate her background, but they didn't find anything unusual.","That girl was indeed just a college student, with no connections to any other companies.","But how did she know so much?","Driven by this mystery, he decided to press the elevator button for the twelfth floor, where the planning department was located.","Stepping out of the elevator, Zhou Lan walked inside, hearing greetings from colleagues returning from lunch, as well as various gossip discussions―","[Damn, I've followed so many of his dramas and variety shows, never thought he was such a scumbag! His reputation is ruined!!!]","[Tsk tsk, this shows you shouldn't randomly create public personas in the entertainment industry. Who would have thought that the devoted lover we see on TV was actually this kind of person?]","[Finally got to see this drama unfold! Wonder who Xiao Yao will expose next?]","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","Well, he was actually quite curious about who she would expose next too.","Soon, he reached the area near her office.","Through the glass wall, he could see her typing somewhat aimlessly on her computer.","He quietly moved a few steps closer and heard her thinking, [Who should I write about today?]","[Maybe I should dig into the scandalous history of Wang XX, the ex-husband of rich woman Zhao X whom Yang XX is trying to get close to? After all, he used insider trading back then and scammed quite a lot of money from stockholders.]","Zhou Lan quietly raised an eyebrow. Wang XX was already in his fifties, how did this girl in her twenties know about his past?","Just then, he heard her thinking, [Oh right, this Wang XX even pursued Zhou Lan's mother, Madam Zhou Ruolan, back then! After failing to win her over, they met at a business venue, and that old bastard tried to kidnap little chubby Zhou to threaten his mother. Fortunately, Madam Zhou Ruolan discovered it in time, so little chubby Zhou didn't fall into his hands. Although it didn't succeed, this incident should be exposed too!]","Zhou Lan: \"???\"","Wait, by \"legendary chubby\"... did she mean him?","And such a thing happened back then?","Even he didn't know about it, so how did she know?","Li Shu really hadn't expected that after just one day at work, before she'd even fully mastered the office software, she would become the president's secretary the next morning.","Yes, her workstation had been moved to the sixteenth floor, right outside the president's office.","It was now ten minutes past nine in the morning, and she sat at her desk, dumbfounded for a full five minutes.","Damn, how did all this happen?","Were personnel transfers in this company always this casual???","Of course, the president's secretary position paid much better than her previous role, and she wasn't against it, but she faced several problems―","First, she had never been a secretary before. If chubby President Zhou saw how clumsy she was, would he fire her?","Second, with Boss Zhou right in front of her, would she still have time to write during lunch breaks? Would Zhou discover her identity?","Nearby, Zhou Lan: \"...\"","Did she really have to call him that?","Of course, although he knew she had no experience and might struggle a bit, his most important task right now was to solve the mystery of this girl.","Being closer meant he could hear more clearly.","And so began their close-quarters working relationship.","Although this girl wasn't great at writing documents or making coffee, he patiently taught her everything himself.","Well, it was hard to tell who was whose secretary.","But that wasn't important. What mattered was that after two days, he still hadn't made much progress on solving the mystery.","This girl was quite focused during work hours, and when she had free time, apart from thinking about what to write and what to eat for lunch, there wasn't anything unusual.","However, this made him even more confused.","Because during this time, he had learned two more different pieces of gossip from her thoughts, each one extremely secretive and explosive.","How was this happening?","No, this approach wasn't enough.","The wall clock showed there were two hours left before getting off work. Zhou Lan thought for a moment, then suddenly sent a message to the girl outside through the office software: [Need to work overtime tonight, please wait.]","She immediately replied: [Understood.]","Zhou Lan then got back to work.","As time passed, when he finally pulled himself away from work, the sky outside had already darkened.","He quietly looked through the glass wall and saw the girl typing on her computer.","Judging by her typing speed, she was probably writing a new chapter of her novel.","Being a polite person, he waited a while until she finished a section, then notified her to print a document.","Then, he personally went out to tell her, \"I'm sorry for keeping you so late. It's getting late, let's go get dinner together.\"","Li Shu politely replied, \"No need to be so courteous, President Zhou. This is all part of my job.\"","But in her mind, she couldn't help thinking, [Treating me to dinner? Is this boss really so generous? Well, this is a good chance to see what rich people eat, it'll be good material for my writing.]","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","The way she put it, it was as if rich people ate something other than normal food?","He put on a sincere expression and said, \"It's no problem, I need to eat too. Why don't we go together?\"","With that, he started walking ahead.","The young lady hesitated for a moment before following him with light, quick steps.","Not far downstairs, there happened to be a Cantonese restaurant with a nice ambiance and decent food.","Although it was dinner time, since it wasn't a holiday, there were still tables available.","The two of them sat down as the waiter led the way.","Zhou Lan was something of a regular here. He casually glanced at the menu before ordering a steamed grouper, a seafood medley, and two vegetable dishes.","Li Shu observed this and thought to herself, \"So rich people eat Chinese food too. I thought it would be like those CEO novels with 1982 vintage wine and premium steaks.\"","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","She was overthinking it. Although he had spent a few years abroad, he had always maintained an authentically Chinese palate.","Before long, the dishes arrived, and Zhou Lan asked, \"Cantonese cuisine is quite light, suitable for dinner. I hope it suits your taste?\"","Li Shu quickly smiled and replied, \"It's perfect, I think so too.\"","Suddenly, a realization dawned on her—","Oh right, this handsome guy had lost weight from over 200 pounds, so he probably doesn't want to gain it back. Generally, people who want to maintain their figure need to eat high-protein, low-fat foods like steamed fish. Western food wouldn't really work.","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","He couldn't help wanting to ask her if she could please stop bringing up the over-200-pounds thing.","But then, she suddenly seemed to remember something important and mentally gasped—","[Oh right! They say obesity during puberty might affect that particular area in men... I wonder if Little Fatty Zhou is okay down there?]","[Damn, it would be such a shame if such a handsome man had problems with that!!!]","While Li Shu was lost in these thoughts, the man across from her suddenly spluttered, spraying a mouthful of tea."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 19","Seeing the devastatingly handsome boss in front of her suddenly spitting out tea and coughing uncontrollably.","Li Shu was startled and quickly handed him a tissue, asking with concern, \"Chairman Zhou, are you alright?\"","Zhou Lan took the tissue to clean himself up, trying hard to compose himself before finally managing to say, \"I'm fine.\"","However, internally he was furious, almost wanting to prove to her right then and there whether he had \"problems\" or not.","This girl, what on earth was she thinking?","And who on earth told her that he used to weigh over 400 pounds?!","But he couldn't express any of these emotions. He could only wait until he fully recovered before saying \"excuse me\" and then asking her, \"What do you usually do at school?\"","Li Shu answered, \"I spend most of my time in the dorm or library.\"","Zhou Lan tried asking, \"Don't you go out to have fun?\"","Li Shu shook her head, \"I rarely go out, there's quite a lot of schoolwork.\"","In her heart though, she sighed. How could she have time? As they say, writing web novels is as deep as the sea - she had already given all her time to her readers, she didn't even have time for dating.","Wait, come to think of it, now that she's working, maybe after finishing this book, she could take a break and try dating or something. From her observations these past two days, there were quite a few young handsome guys in the company.","Zhou Lan, who was quietly listening, raised an eyebrow - just the other day she was saying he was handsome, and now she's interested in others?","Before he could say anything else, he saw her sneaking a glance at him while getting food, secretly thinking to herself, [Come to think of it, this guy seems to be single... How is someone so handsome and rich still without a girlfriend?]","[Tsk, could it be that weighing over 400 pounds back then really affected that aspect?]","Zhou Lan's eyebrow twitched, and he quickly interrupted, \"By the way, many colleagues at the company have been reading a novel lately, I think it's called 'Let Me Tell You About My Years of Entertainment Industry Gossip,' have you read it?\"","As he spoke, he pretended to casually look at her, waiting for her reaction.","Li Shu indeed froze for a moment, surprised in her heart, \"What? He reads my novel too?\"","On the surface, she could only nod and say, \"Oh, I've heard of that book, seems like many people are reading it.\"","Zhou Lan continued asking, \"Everyone's trying to guess the author's identity now. I'm quite curious too - how does she know so many inside stories, and they're all accurate?\"","As he watched her, he heard her secretly feeling proud in her mind, [Of course! With my Statistics, how could I worry about material? As they say, if you don't want others to know, don't do it in the first place. As long as someone does something, I'll definitely know about it.]","Zhou Lan quietly frowned -","\"Statistics\"?","What kind of thing was that?","Could it be some kind of special ability like his mind-reading?","Just as he was thinking this, he suddenly paused.","Hmm? Why does this scene feel familiar - him repeatedly testing a girl, and coming to the same conclusion?","But there were no such scenes in his memory, it just felt familiar somehow...","Perhaps he had dreamed it before?","While he was lost in thought, he suddenly heard the girl ask, \"By the way, Chairman Zhou, I've been wanting to ask you something.\"","Zhou Lan came back to his senses and made an acknowledging sound, \"Go ahead.\"","\"How do you maintain your figure? Do you have any good methods? Could you share them?\"","Zhou Lan answered, \"There's nothing special, just try to do some cardio every week, do some moderate muscle exercises before bed, and eat less high-calorie, high-fat, high-sugar foods. That's basically enough to avoid gaining weight.\"","Then he emphasized one more point, \"Also, don't stay up late.\"","As soon as he said this, Li Shu suddenly remembered something important -","Oh right, she hadn't finished writing tomorrow morning's update yet, she needed to hurry back and continue grinding!","She quickly wiped her mouth and said, \"I'm about done eating.\"","Zhou Lan nodded, \"Then let's go, I'll drive you. Are you still living in the S University dorm?\"","Li Shu quickly shook her head, \"I found a small apartment near the company the day before yesterday. I've already moved out of school, mainly because the school is quite far from here, to save some time.\"","Zhou Lan didn't say much, just nodded, \"That's good. I'm driving anyway, I'll give you a lift.\"","Li Shu politely declined, \"It's not far, I can walk.\"","Zhou Lan's expression turned serious, \"It's late, young women should be careful about safety. Besides, you're technically working overtime tonight, so I'm responsible for your safety.\"","With that, he took her to the underground parking lot and drove off.","Li Shu's new home really wasn't far, less than two miles by car.","However, the apartment was converted from an old factory, and the surrounding environment wasn't very good. When they were about 200 meters away, the car couldn't go any further.","Li Shu quickly said to Zhou Lan, \"I can get off here, the road ahead is too narrow for cars.\"","Zhou Lan peered ahead and saw that the alley was deep and the street lights seemed dim.","He frowned slightly, \"Which building do you live in?\"","\"Building 3, Room 505,\" she smiled, unbuckling her seatbelt, \"Goodbye, Chairman Zhou.\"","She opened the car door and got out, walking towards the small path.","Zhou Lan didn't leave immediately, watching the direction the girl had gone, wondering how far Building 3 was and if it would be safe for her to go in alone.","Just as he was thinking this, he suddenly heard a phone vibrate.","It wasn't his phone, as his was on him.","Following the vibration sound, he found a phone under the passenger seat, with a white case with gold edges, decorated with a cartoon lucky cat and four large characters saying \"Get Rich and Prosper\"","Zhou Lan, \"...\"","There was no need to say whose phone this was.","This girl...","He simply turned off the engine, opened the door, and went after her.","Actually, Li Shu was feeling a bit nervous too.","Because she was in a hurry to find housing, she had quickly decided on this single apartment after just looking online, only to find it less than ideal after living there for two days.","It was noisy, the external facilities often broke down, and the surrounding environment was basically like an urban village.","Fortunately, she had only paid three months' rent, so she could manage for three months and move when the lease was up.","As luck would have it, the street lights were broken tonight, and after passing Building 1, the path ahead was pitch black.","She was about to take out her phone for light when she realized after searching her bag that her phone was missing.","Oh no! Where did she lose it?","She quickly tried to remember, she seemed to have checked the time in Zhou's car earlier, could she have forgotten to put it back in her bag?","She thought about going back to get it, but then realized he must have left already.","So now she could only go home first and use her computer to send him a message through the office software, asking him to bring it to the company tomorrow.","Li Shu had no choice but to continue walking in the dark, but after a while, she suddenly heard footsteps behind her.","Somehow, she felt those footsteps were coming for her. She was startled and quickly sped up, entering Building 3's entrance and rushing up to the fifth floor.","Unexpectedly, the footsteps followed her up.","And they sounded like they belonged to a man.","She was certain there were no male tenants on this floor, so whoever was coming definitely didn't live on the fifth floor.","She became scared and quickly fumbled for her keys to open the door, but perhaps due to nervousness, she couldn't find them.","Meanwhile, the footsteps were getting closer.","In an instant, all sorts of scenes of stalking and home invasion crimes she had seen before flooded her mind.","Li Shu panicked and grabbed the cleaning lady's broom handle by the door for self-defense.","However, at the same time, she heard a familiar voice, \"Li Shu?\"","She froze - this voice... hadn't she just heard it?","In the corridor light's illumination, the visitor's silhouette gradually became clear, that impeccably handsome face and that perfect model-like figure...","She finally recognized him as her boss, Zhou Lan.","She was extremely embarrassed and quickly tried to put down the broom.","However, she accidentally hit the electrical wire on the wall, and the shoddy wire seemed to come loose from the wall to the ceiling, bringing down the light bulb with it, which fell straight onto his head.","\"Fatty! I mean, Chairman Zhou!!!\"","Zhou Lan lay on Li Shu's sofa, unconscious for a full ten minutes.","The pain was secondary; mainly, his mind was suddenly filled with flashing images -","He was an emperor, and she was his concubine...","At that New Year's Eve banquet, their first encounter...","She bit him...","Then forcefully kissed him...","She even took an assassin's dagger for him, getting wounded in the process...","She was hemophobic, yet always loved to watch excitement...","She helped him manage various state affairs...","She cured his illness...","They covered each other's eyes...","Their children, Heng'er and Xuan'er...","They supported each other sweetly throughout life, until they passed away peacefully of old age...","Yes, Zhou Lan finally remembered everything - he was once an emperor...","And she was his one and only empress.","...","However, beside the sofa, that girl was still asking him with a panicked face, \"President Zhou, are you alright?\"","Zhou Lan didn't know whether to laugh or cry. After a while, he could only sigh and say, \"Does this have to happen every time?\"","Indeed, as his memories returned, he also remembered how she bit him in their previous life.","It really hurt.","However, Li Shu, who didn't understand the situation, looked increasingly confused and scratched her head, saying, \"What do you mean... has to happen every time?\"","She was startled internally, [Oh no, did the bump make him stupid? Or did he get electrocuted by the light bulb?]","[Damn, what should I do? Should I take him to the hospital?]","[Oh no, if he really became stupid, would I have to take responsibility?]","[Well, considering how good-looking he is, I wouldn't mind taking responsibility, hehe.]","Zhou Lan: \"...\"","Well, it seemed that up until now, only he had remembered.","But...","Thank goodness he remembered!","Earlier during dinner, she was actually thinking about dating someone else???","While he was lost in complicated thoughts, the girl asked again, \"President Zhou, are you really okay?\"","Zhou Lan finally spoke, \"I'm not feeling well.\"","Li Shu was startled, \"If it's that bad, let me take you to the hospital?\"","Zhou Lan looked at her weakly, \"That won't be necessary, but I'm afraid I'll need to spend the night here.\"","Li Shu: \"???\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 20","Li Shu could hardly believe her ears. \"Mr. Zhou, what did you say? You want to sleep here?\"","The man leaning on the sofa looked at her weakly, \"I can't leave right now.\"","After thinking for a moment, she suggested, \"Should I call an ambulance to take you to the hospital?\"","But the man declined, \"It's probably not serious enough for the hospital, and that might cause news headlines.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","Afraid of making headlines, so he wants to stay here?","Finding it hard to understand, she continued, \"But... this is just a small rundown apartment that rents for about a thousand yuan a month...\"","Before she could finish, the man sincerely said, \"I don't mind.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","She wasn't worried about him minding.","Her concern was that besides a small open kitchen and a tiny bathroom, it was just one large room. The bed and sofa were only separated by a sheer curtain - how would they manage sleeping arrangements?","As if reading her mind, he added, \"It's fine, I'll take the sofa.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","How could she let a CEO worth hundreds of billions sleep on her sofa while she took the bed?","That wouldn't sit right with her conscience.","After some thought, she suggested, \"How about you take my bed, and I'll find a hotel room.\"","But the man weakly replied, \"Your apartment isn't very secure, and I'm not feeling well. What if something happens while I'm here alone?\"","He glanced at her and added in a soft voice, \"Are you that opposed to my staying?\"","Li Shu: \"It's not that I'm opposed... it's just... a single man and woman staying together...\"","The man actually gave a light chuckle and said, \"In my condition, I doubt I could do anything.\"","Li Shu: \"...I'm more worried about what I might do...\"","After all, having such a handsome man lying weakly before her...","She froze after speaking, realizing she'd accidentally said her thoughts out loud.","Zhou Lan chuckled again, followed by a light cough, \"Well, we're both single anyway...\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","Why did his words suddenly create such an ambiguous atmosphere, making her blush?","No, no, she had to stop talking. If this continued, who knows what might happen.","But the problem was, she hadn't finished her chapter update yet!","Her readers were more important! No longer bothering with politeness, since the bed, wardrobe, and computer desk were inside, she told the weakened man who refused to go to the hospital on her sofa, \"Then I'll have to trouble you to make do with the sofa for tonight. I still have some schoolwork to finish.\"","Zhou Lan made a sound of agreement, but reminded her, \"Don't stay up too late, get some rest early.\"","Li Shu quickly nodded, \"Alright, and please let me know if you feel unwell again.\"","She grabbed a blanket to cover him, then hurried to turn on her computer.","At midnight, after Li Shu had finally finished her update and gone to bed, Zhou Lan lay on the sofa, unable to sleep.","His headache was long gone, but his mind was filled with memories of their past life.","He remembered their reluctant parting in their previous life, when she said if there was a next life, she would marry him again.","Unexpectedly, they had truly reunited in this life.","Thank heavens.","But there was still one problem - how to make her remember?","He had taken a hit to remember, but for her... he definitely couldn't bear to let that happen to her.","Well, perhaps it was up to fate.","Besides... even if she couldn't remember now, it didn't matter, as long as he remembered.","Early the next morning, Li Shu woke up before her alarm. She saw that Zhou Lan was already up, with the blanket she had given him neatly folded on the sofa.","She quickly asked, \"Mr. Zhou, are you feeling better?\"","Zhou Lan made an affirmative sound, \"Yes. I'll drive you to the company first, then go home to change clothes.\"","Li Shu breathed a sigh of relief, agreed, and after getting ready, they left together.","Fortunately, where she had gotten out of the car last night was a legal parking zone, and Zhou Lan's car was still safely parked by the roadside overnight.","She opened the car door and got in, unaware that someone was hiding in the roadside bushes, taking several photos of her at the perfect moment.","After arriving at the company, Zhou Lan headed home while she took the elevator up to her floor, turned on her computer, and got busy. Soon after, Zhou Lan arrived.","She stood up and greeted him as \"Mr. Zhou,\" noticing he was freshly dressed, his hair still slightly damp, emanating a faint fragrance from his recent shower.","For a moment, she couldn't help but let her mind wander...","Zhou Lan, who secretly noticed this: \"...\"","Was she developing feelings for him?","Well, it seems good looks do have their uses.","Zhou Lan had a morning meeting and left his office after grabbing some documents. With nothing urgent to do, Li Shu finished her work and continued writing her new chapter.","As the morning passed and lunch approached, her system suddenly chimed with a notification: [You're about to become famous.]","Li Shu: [What???]","What did that cryptic message mean?","System: [Check the trending topics.]","Li Shu quickly grabbed her phone to look, and as soon as she opened Weibo's trending page, a headline jumped out at her: \"Huarui Group's Young Master's Girlfriend Appears\"","Huarui Group's Young Master?","Were they talking about Chubby Zhou?","He... had a girlfriend?","In that moment, Li Shu felt a chill in her heart and instinctively clicked on the headline.","She first saw several similar photos showing a young couple walking to a luxury car, getting in, and driving away.","The man was clearly her boss, Chubby Zhou, and as for the woman...","Li Shu looked down at her outfit today and was shocked to realize it was her!","[What's going on???]","System: [Last night when Zhou Lan drove you home with your phone, he parked by the roadside, right? Some paparazzi happened to see it, and they waited all night to finally catch you two coming out of the building and getting in the car.]","Li Shu: \"...\"","The paparazzi had been waiting there since last night?","This would be impossible to explain away now.","She quickly checked her phone again and saw the headline: \"Zhou Lan, the diamond bachelor and new CEO of Huarui Group, ranking in Asia's top ten richest, spent the night at an apartment and left early next morning with a young woman, suggesting cohabitation.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","Looking further, the comments section had exploded with users asking who she was and why such a wealthy billionaire would spend the night in such an ordinary apartment building.","...","Turning off her phone screen, Li Shu felt extremely nervous.","She regretted not bringing a change of clothes this morning - now that her colleagues had seen the trending topic, wouldn't they realize she was the one who \"spent the night\" with the boss?","System: [It's too late, they've already figured it out. Check the latest top comment.]","What?","Li Shu was startled and quickly reopened her phone. Sure enough, there was a new top comment saying, [Hey, doesn't this girl's outfit look like Huarui's new CEO secretary?]","The replies below were all trying to dig up information about her role as the CEO's secretary.","Li Shu: \"...\"","This was...","Feeling an indescribable panic, she quietly closed Weibo and clicked on her latest chapter posted this morning, only to find readers already asking if she had any gossip about Huarui's CEO Zhou Lan and wanting to know who his rumored girlfriend was.","Li Shu: \"...\"","Great.","Talk about karma - who would have thought that after writing so much gossip about others, one day she'd be writing about herself?","But she was just an ordinary person, she couldn't handle this much attention!!!","Suddenly, an idea struck her - wait, what about her boss, Chubby Zhou? He was the male lead after all! With his wealth, surely he would pay to suppress the trending topic?","At the very least, he should clarify things with the media?","Just as she was thinking this, she heard the elevator ding, and the male lead in question walked in while on the phone, making occasional sounds of agreement.","Unlike his usual work calls, his attitude seemed relaxed, and he even had a smile on his face.","Most notably, as he passed by her desk, Li Shu faintly heard a woman's voice on the other end of the call.","Hmm... who could he be talking to?","Just then, he finished his call and looked at her, asking, \"Any plans for the morning?\"","His lips still curved in a slight smile, his mood seemingly quite good.","Li Shu suddenly felt an inexplicable complexity in her heart. After thinking for a moment, she simply nodded and said, \"There is indeed something...\"","Zhou Lan stopped and looked at her, \"What is it?\"","Li Shu cleared her throat and said, \"Please don't get angry first, but... I was photographed by paparazzi this morning while riding in your car, and they also know about you staying at my place last night... It's already trending on social media.\"","After she finished speaking, she was feeling anxious, but to her surprise, the man simply responded with a calm \"Oh, I already knew about that.\"","Li Shu: \"??? When did you find out?\"","Why wasn't he surprised?","Zhou Lan showed her his phone and said, \"My mother just called to tell me.\"","What, his mother?","So that means the Chairwoman knows too???","Li Shu was so shocked that she started stammering, \"Then, then, then Chairwoman Zhou must be very angry?\"","But Zhou Lan said, \"Not at all. My mother just told me that I need to take responsibility for you.\"","Li Shu's eyes widened, \"What, what, what responsibility?\"","If anyone should take responsibility, shouldn't it be her? After all, she was the one who caused him to get hit by that light bulb...","But then, unexpectedly, the man in front of her smiled and said, \"I told my mother I want to marry you.\"","What???","Li Shu was completely stunned, looking at him in disbelief, \"Why do you want to marry me?\"","He smiled at her and said, \"Because I like you.\"","What???","Li Shu was dumbfounded again.","From the time she came to Huarui Media for her interview, they hadn't known each other for even a week, and he's saying he likes her?","Is this how rich people express their feelings, so abruptly?","However, something flickered in her mind, like a scene where he had said similar words before.","It was the same face, but his appearance seemed somewhat different...","What was going on?","Had she dreamed about this?","While Li Shu was puzzled, the man beside her spoke up, \"Don't doubt it. Everything I'm saying is true. I really like you, and I really want to marry you, if you're willing.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","She suddenly didn't dare to speak, even suspecting if this was some kind of romance scam―","The man in front of her, one of the ten wealthiest men in Asia, actually wanted to marry her???","Although she was indeed quite pretty, and many boys had confessed to her since she was young, but this was Chubby Zhou!!!","Weren't rich people like him supposed to be interested in models and actresses?","Or at least arrange some kind of family alliance marriage?","Why did he like her?","To be safe, she quietly confirmed with her internal system again, [This is really Zhou Lan, right? Not someone impersonating him to scam me?]","Zhou Lan, who silently heard this: \"...\"","Zhou Lan didn't rush her for an answer. After his confession, he went to deal with the trending topic.","Soon enough, the trending topic disappeared.","Li Shu felt slightly relieved, but still couldn't calm down.","To be honest, just as a person, Zhou Lan was indeed her ideal type, and she had made up her mind to have a relationship this year.","But she really hadn't expected to end up with her boss!","Being wealthy wasn't a problem, but he was perhaps a bit too wealthy!","And he wanted to marry her right away...","It was too sudden.","How could a billionaire be so innocent in love?","This was too absurd!","...","What Li Shu hadn't expected was that something even more absurd was about to happen. At the end of the workday, their group's chairwoman, Chubby Zhou's mother, Zhou Ruolan, suddenly appeared in the office and cordially invited her to dinner.","Li Shu couldn't refuse and had to go along.","Initially, she felt quite uncertain, but to her surprise, Madam Zhou was extremely kind and friendly towards her.","Her words were also very sincere―","\"As long as it's true love between you two, I have no objections. Zhou Lan has been independent since he was young. I was busy with business before and couldn't take care of him much, so he learned to cook and do laundry by himself. Later, he spent a few years abroad and took good care of himself. In recent years, he's been busy with work and hasn't had any scandals. You're the first girl he's ever admitted to liking. His lifestyle should be acceptable, but if you find out you've been deceived, come to me first, and I'll definitely teach him a lesson. Being my child, above all else, means being honest. In my life, I despise nothing more than dishonest men.\"","These words filled Li Shu with respect, and she wanted to nod in agreement― with such principles, no wonder she became the chairwoman, she was practically her idol!","However, before she could say anything, Madam Zhou continued, \"As for the wedding, we can invite your family here for the ceremony, or we can hold it in your hometown. Either way is fine, it's mainly up to you two.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","They were already discussing the wedding?","Although she really liked Madam Zhou, some things needed to be clarified first...","But before she could speak, her phone suddenly rang in her bag.","Li Shu took it out and saw it was one of her mother's friends from her hometown, Aunt Zhang.","While she was hesitating whether to answer, Zhou Ruolan smiled and said, \"Go ahead and answer it, we can continue our conversation later. I specially came back today, so I'm in no hurry to leave.\"","Li Shu could only nod and say \"excuse me\" before walking outside the private room to answer the call, \"Hello, Aunt Zhang.\"","\"Hello, Li Shu. I'm not calling for anything special, just that your mother asked me to keep an eye out for job opportunities for you a while back, and our unit just started accepting applications for civil service positions. I wanted to remind you, would you like to come back and apply?\"","Li Shu quickly responded politely, \"Thank you, Aunt Zhang, but I've already found a job here, so I won't be coming back.\"","Aunt Zhang immediately replied, \"Oh, you found a job? Is it a state-owned enterprise or a private company? I hear private companies there are very demanding. You're so young, what if you don't have time to find a partner? Besides, being in a strange city, you never really know people. I think you should come back.\"","Before Li Shu could respond, Aunt Zhang continued, \"Oh, remember my nephew I told you about? He bought another house this year, a big three-bedroom, over 120 square meters, with a garage! And he has a stable job. Why don't you come back and meet him...\"","On this end of the phone, Li Shu wanted to roll her eyes.","This nephew of Aunt Zhang only had a high school education and got a job as a driver at some company through connections a few years ago. Never mind his salary, but most importantly, he had already been divorced once due to domestic violence, though they thought people didn't know about it.","How little must Aunt Zhang think of her to try to set her up with someone like that?","On the other end of the phone, Aunt Zhang was still enthusiastically praising her abusive nephew, but Li Shu had lost patience and interrupted, \"Thank you for your kindness, Aunt Zhang, but I'm actually seeing someone, and we'll probably get married this year or next.\"","There was a pause on the other end, \"You're seeing someone? Who is it? Why haven't your parents mentioned anything?\"","Li Shu: \"Oh, no one special, just my boss. Nothing much, just a Fortune 500 company CEO.\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137","paragraphs":["Extra Chapter 21","After hanging up the phone, Li Shu returned to the private room, having already made up her mind.","She said somewhat shyly to Mrs. Zhou Ruolan, \"Thank you very much for your trust, Chairman Zhou, but it might be a bit early to discuss the wedding. I haven't even told my family yet.\"","Zhou Lan raised an eyebrow from the side - was this her way of saying yes?","Mrs. Zhou Ruolan smiled and said, \"Of course, properly speaking, I should visit your parents first. When would they be available? Also, from now on, there's no need to be so formal by calling me Chairman Zhou - just call me Aunt Zhou.\"","Li Shu: \"...Aunt Zhou.\"","Well, as expected of a Global Fortune 500 company's chairwoman - such efficiency! Already wanting to visit her parents?","While she admired this, if they really did visit, wouldn't it frighten her parents?","So she quickly thought of a solution, \"You're too kind, Aunt Zhou. It's just that my home is quite far away. However, I'm having my graduation ceremony in a few days and plan to invite my parents to visit. If it's convenient for you, perhaps we could all have dinner together then.\"","\"Of course that would be convenient. Please let me know when they arrive.\"","Mrs. Zhou Ruolan agreed very promptly.","Li Shu nodded, already planning to call her family later.","However, before she could make the call, just after returning to her small apartment from dinner, her parents called first.","\"Shu dear, we just heard from Aunt Zhang that you're dating someone over there, and he might be a scammer? What's going on?\"","Her parents sounded very worried.","Li Shu remained calm, \"Aunt Zhang must have been frightened. I'm not dating any scammer. It's my boss, and he's quite nice. You know about Huarui Media, right? It's just that Aunt Zhang doesn't believe my boss is wealthy.\"","However, her parents were still very surprised, \"What's going on? You're dating your boss? Is this real?\"","Li Shu replied directly, \"Of course it's real. Why would I lie to you about this? By the way, I have my graduation ceremony in a few days. Would you like to come and witness it, and meet my boss and his mother?\"","Although their family wasn't as wealthy as Zhou Lan's, they could certainly afford plane tickets.","However, after hearing this, her parents couldn't even wait a few days. They bought plane tickets right after hanging up and arrived in her city the next afternoon.","Li Shu: \"...\"","Apparently, it wasn't just Chairwoman Zhou Ruolan who was efficient - her parents were too.","While she was certainly happy to see her parents, Zhou Lan was even more eager than her upon hearing the news. He immediately arranged a dinner and notified his mother, Mrs. Zhou Ruolan.","Thus, on the first evening of Li Shu's parents' arrival in City S, they met one of the main purposes of their visit - their daughter's boyfriend Zhou Lan, who was rumored to be worth billions.","They also met his mother, Mrs. Zhou Ruolan, who was reportedly China's wealthiest businesswoman.","To their surprise, both mother and son were very humble, polite, and cultured.","Zhou Lan was practically flawless in his presentation. Mrs. Zhou Ruolan was also very sincere, taking the initiative to tell them, \"As a mother, I can see that Zhou Lan truly cares for Li Shu, and I'm very fond of her too. Of course, we are a single-parent family, which is my regret. I've always tried my best to guide him to develop a good character, and I hope you won't discriminate against him for this.\"","These words were somewhat heartbreaking, and Li Shu's parents quickly responded, \"You're too modest, Chairman Zhou. We don't care whether it's a single-parent or two-parent family, as long as the young people are sincere in their relationship.\"","Ever since receiving Aunt Zhang's call, the couple had been very anxious, but now after meeting them in person, they could finally relax.","Huh, that Aunt Zhang - she must have really looked down on their daughter to insist that Li Shu had met a scammer.","A few days after their pleasant first meeting, it was time for Li Shu's graduation ceremony.","Li Shu was very happy that her parents could attend in person. To her surprise, Zhou Lan also brought his mother, Mrs. Zhou Ruolan, to join her group of family and friends.","Although they tried to keep a low profile, they still caused quite a stir.","Her classmates gathered around to ask, \"Are those two in your family group the chairwoman and CEO of Huarui Media?\"","Li Shu coughed slightly, \"Yes, that's them.\"","Everyone showed surprised expressions. Who would have thought that the formerly most reclusive girl in class would have such prestigious guests at her graduation?","Someone carefully asked, \"That online rumor about... the young master Zhou's girlfriend, was that you?\"","Li Shu coughed again, \"Yes, it was.\"","\"Ahhhh...\"","Screams erupted from the crowd.","All the girls were excited, especially her three closest dormitory roommates, who grabbed her hands and jumped excitedly, \"Shu, Shu, Shu, you're amazing! When are you having your wedding? You must invite us!!!\"","Before Li Shu could respond, a voice suddenly came from behind, \"No problem, we'll definitely send you all invitations when the time comes.\"","As the voice finished, Zhou Lan appeared before them.","The crowd held their breath for a moment before erupting again.","\"Ahhhh, they're really getting married!!! Our Shu is marrying into a wealthy family!!!\"","...","Li Shu pulled Zhou Lan aside and asked with a red face, \"What are you doing? They were just joking.\"","Unexpectedly, Zhou Lan looked serious, \"I wasn't joking. They can all come if they want to.\"","Li Shu coughed, \"...I only just agreed to date you, who said anything about marriage...\"","Zhou Lan looked very serious, \"Any relationship not aimed at marriage is just playing around.\"","Li Shu: \"...\"","Well, now it seemed like she was the one playing around.","Her face felt hot, and her classmates were still teasing them. She quickly pulled him away, \"Let's go take photos. Your photography skills must be pretty good, right?\"","Zhou Lan made a sound of agreement, \"I won some photography awards back in school...\"","...","After sixteen years of hard study, she had finally graduated. Li Shu was very happy and took many photos with her parents, classmates, boyfriend, and even her boyfriend's mother. Suddenly, she spotted Professor Qi talking to someone nearby, so she quickly went over to express her gratitude, \"Professor Qi, thank you for your guidance and care these past few years, and for the job recommendation you gave me the other day. I've successfully joined the company now.\"","Professor Qi was only in his fifties, approachable and elegant in demeanor, and was a teacher she particularly respected.","Hearing her words, Professor Qi quickly smiled and said, \"No need for thanks. I wish you all the best as you enter society.\"","After he finished speaking, Li Shu was about to bring her parents over to meet Professor Qi.","However, before she could move, she saw her boyfriend's mother, Mrs. Zhou Ruolan, walk up and look directly at Professor Qi, calling out, \"Qi Shuguang?\"","Professor Qi also froze, looked at her for a while, and called out, \"Ruolan...\"","Li Shu's eyes widened -","\"Ruolan\"...","This form of address seemed quite unusual.","Could these two have some history?","She quickly called out to her system, [What's going on between Chairman Zhou and Professor Qi? Did they know each other before?]","The system replied, [They more than just knew each other - they dated in university. To be precise, Professor Qi was Zhou Ruolan's senior by two years. Professor Qi was famous in their department as a talented scholar, admired by many young women, while Zhou Ruolan was the campus beauty, pursued by countless young men. They made a perfect match, talented scholar and beautiful lady, but then something happened to the Zhou family, and Zhou Ruolan was forced into an arranged marriage for family reasons. Professor Qi was studying abroad at the time, and so they missed their chance. Later, Zhou Ruolan divorced and raised her son alone, focusing on her career, while Professor Qi remained in another city, and they never contacted each other.]","After hearing this, Li Shu couldn't help but exclaim, [Isn't this the legendary reunion after many years apart? It's so touching! Now Professor Qi is single, and Chairman Zhou is single too, can't they rekindle their old flame? Think about it - a powerful businesswoman and a learned professor, oh my goodness, this couple is perfect!]","Zhou Lan, who had secretly overheard: \"...\"","It was all destined!","Even in another lifetime, she would still be a devoted shipper of couples.","After the graduation ceremony, Li Shu's parents left City S contentedly.","Li Shu found a new place to live and moved.","This time, after careful inspection, she chose an apartment in a proper residential complex with complete facilities and guaranteed security.","She didn't have many belongings to begin with, so after packing up her clothes and books, Zhou Lan drove over to help her move.","Although there weren't many large items, after cleaning and arranging everything, a whole day had passed.","As evening approached, Zhou Lan suggested, \"Let's go out to eat something.\"","Li Shu, lounging lazily on the sofa, replied, \"I'm too tired. Let's just order takeout.\"","She took out her phone to open the food delivery app.","However, Zhou Lan said, \"Takeout isn't healthy. I noticed there's a supermarket downstairs. Let me buy some ingredients and cook for you.\"","Well, although they had met the parents, the marriage wasn't officially settled yet, so he still needed to make a good impression.","Fortunately, in this life, he had learned to be an excellent cook.","Upon hearing this, her eyes lit up, \"Yes, yes! I'll go shopping with you.\"","She suddenly bounced up from the sofa.","Zhou Lan raised an eyebrow, \"Weren't you tired?\"","She coughed slightly, \"No matter how tired I am, I can't let you go alone. Such a handsome boy walking around outside could be dangerous.\"","Zhou Lan laughed, ruffled her hair, and they went together.","After buying groceries, he took charge of cooking while Li Shu helped wash the vegetables.","She watched in amazement as he skillfully chopped vegetables, fired up the stove, and even managed to flip the wok professionally. When the food was served, her eyes widened in delight—","She hadn't expected his cooking skills to be so good! The Yu-Shiang pork strips, home-style tofu, and boiled beef were almost restaurant quality.","It was definitely much better than takeout!","\"How is it? Does it suit your taste?\" Zhou Lan asked.","Li Shu couldn't stop eating and kept nodding, \"It's delicious! You're amazing, I had no idea you could cook so well!\"","Zhou Lan hummed in agreement, \"During those years abroad, I couldn't get used to their food, so I had to cook for myself. I gradually got better at it. In the future, just tell me what you want to eat, and try to avoid takeout.\"","Li Shu nodded, \"Then I won't hold back!\"","She thought to herself, she hadn't made a mistake with this boyfriend - not only was he handsome and wealthy, but he could cook so well! What a catch!","Zhou Lan, silently listening nearby, thought to himself...","So, being handsome and wealthy wasn't important; what mattered was being able to cook.","This must be a foodie's unique standard for choosing a partner.","Fortunately, he could cook.","By the time they finished dinner, it was completely dark outside.","Since Zhou Lan had cooked, Li Shu volunteered to wash the dishes.","It was very hot, and remembering how he had been sweating while cooking, she suggested, \"Would you like to take a shower?\"","She hadn't thought much of it, but Zhou Lan's eyes suddenly darkened, and he softly agreed before heading to the bathroom.","When Li Shu finished washing the dishes, he had just come out of the bathroom.","He emerged bare-chested.","Li Shu was stunned.","So men really could have abs!","After secretly drooling, she managed to ask, \"Why... why are you like this?\"","While speaking, she couldn't help but get distracted, wanting to touch...","Zhou Lan looked at her with dark eyes, \"I washed my clothes while I was at it.\"","Li Shu made an \"oh\" sound, barely maintaining her scattered thoughts, and asked, \"But how will you go home later?\"","Before she finished speaking, the man suddenly came close and asked, \"Can I stay tonight?\"","In Li Shu's vision, all she could see was his well-defined physique. She swallowed again before saying, \"I guess so...\"","Actually, she wasn't even sure what she was saying anymore...","Of course, none of that mattered, because the next moment, she was in his embrace.","Then, she was lost in a kiss.","In their previous life, she had kissed him first, so this time it was his turn.","The kiss was gentle, passionate, and dizzying.","Li Shu's mind had turned to mush, but she vaguely felt that this sensation seemed familiar...","When was it?","However, as she was struggling to remember, Zhou Lan's gentle voice came to her ear, \"Shu, will you marry me?\"","Li Shu nodded.","She thought to herself that since he was good at everything, marriage would be quite profitable.","Zhou Lan smiled and carried her to the bed.","As they moved, he heard her inner thoughts, [Hmm, it's quite necessary to verify things before marriage.]","Zhou Lan, \"...\"","Well, it was finally time to teach her a lesson.","...","That night was full of ups and downs, and Li Shu fell asleep exhausted in his arms.","She had a dream filled with scenes from her previous life.","He was the emperor, and she was his empress...","The next morning, when Li Shu woke up, she smelled food cooking.","Zhou Lan came to the bedside, saw her staring blankly at the ceiling, and asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Li Shu looked at him and said, \"I had a dream.\"","\"What dream?\"","\"I dreamed about our previous life, where you were the emperor and I was your consort...\"","\"Empress.\"","Zhou Lan smiled, \"You finally remember.\"","Li Shu looked at him in surprise, \"You remember too?\"","Zhou Lan nodded.","Li Shu suddenly understood, \"No wonder...\"","No wonder he was so insistent on marrying her.","She hugged him immediately, exclaiming, \"Thank heavens for letting us meet again.\"","And thankfully, he was still just as handsome.","Especially in that aspect, there weren't the initial struggles of their previous life - it was quite good from the start.","Zhou Lan, \"...\"","As long as you're satisfied.","He bent down to kiss her, unable to control his desires.","Well, it was the weekend after all...","However, before things could progress, she said, \"Wait, something's not right.\"","He froze and quickly asked, \"What's not right?\"","She frowned, \"Didn't we agree in our previous life that if we came back, you would be the woman and I would be the man? Why am I still the woman?\"","Zhou Lan, \"???\"","\"Did we ever say that?\"","But she was very certain, \"Yes! When I was in terrible pain giving birth to Xuan'er, I said next life you should give birth to the child, and you agreed...\"","Zhou Lan, \"...\"","\"Maybe heaven forgot. It's okay, we'll wait for the next life. There will always be a chance.\"","Then he continued kissing her.","Now that the lovers had recovered their memories from their previous life, their romance became even more skillful.","At the end of the year, Zhou Lan and Li Shu held a grand wedding in Li Shu's hometown.","After returning, they also held a thank-you banquet, which attracted numerous paparazzi reports.","Now that everything was official, Aunt Zhang no longer dared to say anything. Feeling embarrassed, she didn't show her face to Li Shu's parents for quite a while.","Of course, Li Shu didn't care about these trivial matters.","Because she was completely immersed in joy.","When she was crowned empress in their previous life, they couldn't hold a grand ceremony because the empress dowager was \"ill.\" In this life, she finally fulfilled her wish.","After the wedding, the couple began their honeymoon.","One evening, the newlyweds received a video call from Mrs. Zhou Ruolan.","\"Son, Li Shu, now that your wedding has been completed perfectly, I can rest assured. I have something I want to tell you...\"","Before she finished, Zhou Lan smiled at his mother on the screen and said, \"Mom, I know. You've worked hard all these years, it's time for you to find someone to spend the rest of your life with.\"","On the other end of the call, Mrs. Zhou Ruolan was surprised, then smiled and nodded.","After saying goodbye to her son and daughter-in-law, she made another call.","\"Shuguang, it's Ruolan. Are you free tonight? Let's have dinner together.\"","\"Alright.\"","...","In their second year of marriage, Li Shu gave birth to a boy who looked just like their son from their memories and had the same lovely personality.","They didn't rack their brains for a name, directly naming the little one Zhou Heng.","When their little one was three years old, his parents gave him a little sister, named \"Zhou Xuan.\"","Little Xuan'er was equally adorable, and her favorite thing was to sit in her stroller while seeing her brother off to kindergarten.","One day, in the crisp autumn air under golden sunlight.","Heng'er and Xuan'er accompanied their parents to the airport to welcome their grandparents back from their trip.","Along the way, under the high sky and floating clouds, the wind gently caressed the leaves, and birds sang by the roadside.","The two little ones joined in, singing nursery rhymes.","Their mother looked back at them, unable to suppress a smile.","Thank you, Heaven, for giving their family a chance to reunite.","Now, let us continue this joyful journey of life together!","The End"]}]);
